1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Joseph Thorne, a third son of the patentee, married Mary Bowne, daughter of John Bowne in 1690 and lived in Flushing. He traded in land, selling a tract of 60 acres to Paulas Amerman of Flatbush in 1696 for the sum
2 CONC  of f 55 (supra Liber B1, page 321). Joseph remained in Flushing throughout his life and died there "the 3rd month 1727". Three of Joseph's sons, including Israel, the eldest, moved during the period of 1725-50 to the Nine Partner
2 CONC s Patent (northeast of Poughkeepsie, Duchess County) where they became active in the Quaker movement.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Thorne, Sr
2 CONT *BIRTH	Jan 1642 Flushing, Queens County, New York, USA
2 CONT *DEATH	3 May 1727 (aged 85) Woodbridge, Middlesex County, New Jersey, USA
2 CONT *BURIAL	 Quaker Meeting House Cemetery Flushing, Queens County, New York, USA
2 CONT
