1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Thomas moved to New Jersey, settling on the sought branch of Pennsuaken Creek near the Colestown Cemetery. He married Letitia Hinchman in 1727 and lived in a 'hip-roofed house' on the hill-side to the south of thie
2 CONC r later homoe.  IN 1742 they built a substantial birck house on the 'plantation which consisted of 200 and odd acres." At his death Letitia carried on the farm with the aid of slaves for eleven years.
2 CONT
