1 NAME Mary? "Grace" /Hedger/
2 GIVN Mary? "Grace"
2 SURN Hedger
2 _MARNM Roe
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1677
2 PLAC Flushing 
2 ADDR
3 STAE Province of New York
3 CTRY Colonial America
1 DEAT
2 DATE BEF 1 SEP 1702
2 ADDR
3 STAE Province of New Jersey
3 CTRY Colonial America
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mary Hedger (daughter of Thomas Hedger and Elizabeth Burton) was born 1677 in Flushing, now Queens, New York, United States, and died before 01 Sep 1702 in Flushing, now Queens, New York, United States, when her hu
2 CONC sband John ROE, son of David Roe and Mary Pearsall, remarried to the widow Grace Ward.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2.  John Roe-2(David-1) was born in 1672 in Flushing, now Queens, New York. He died on 12 Mar 1711 in Gloucester Twp, Gloucester, NJ.
2 CONT
2 CONT The name of John Roe's first wife is unknown ['''some have it as Mary Hedger'''] His second wife was Grace (...) Ward, widow of William Ward of Upton, Gloucester County, NJ. The second marriage took place between Sept. 1, 1702 and
2 CONC  April 2, 1710. The widow of John Roe lived in Evesham Township, Burlington County, NJ for a number of years, but returned to Gloucester County before her death. She died intestate before January 25, 1758, the date of her probate.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children mentioned in John Roe's will: John, b. about 1694; m. Elizabeth ? (Sikes or Sykes?); Children - Benjamin; Deborah; Susanna; Uriah; Henry, b. 1705; ;m. Hannah Cheesman.
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://longislandsurnames.com/getperson.php?personID=I0676&tree=Roe
2 CONT
2 CONT >John Roe's first wife ____Hedger, mentioned previously, was mother of all his children [except Henry b 1705 & Jemima] . John Roe, father of Henry Roe m. 2nd Grace (Mills) Ward (1st m. to _____Hedger), widow of William Ward of Upt
2 CONC on, N. J., (widowed on 21 Aug 1702).
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of John Roe & his 1st wife are:
2 CONT
2 CONT * John Roe 
2 CONT * ii.Benjamin Roe.
2 CONT * iii.Susanna Roe.
2 CONT * iv.Deborah Roe.
2 CONT * vi.Elizabeth Roe.
2 CONT
2 CONT -----
2 CONT
2 CONT notes
2 CONT
2 CONT John Roe son of David Roe of Flushing, NY bought land in Gloucester County, N.J., Oct 1, 1696, and another tract, Oct 5, 1696; removed to New Jersey before March 1, 1967-8, when he is mentioned as a resident of Gloucester County. 
2 CONC April 2, 1710, when his wife Grace was baptized to the First Presbyterian Church of Philadelphia. She is called Grace Roe wife of John of Cohanzy, from which it appears that he then resided in Salem County, NJ. He returned to Glou
2 CONC cester Township, Gloucester Co., NJ, before August 10, 1711, when his will was made. He died before Oct. 9, 1711, when the inventory of his personal estate was taken
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT * http://www.sweenyfiles.com/2010/11/descendants-of-david-roe.html?m=1
2 CONT * Brief record of certain descendants of David Roe of Flushing, Long Island, New York : including John Martindale of Philadelphia
