1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Biography'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * William Lupton, b. March 14, 1714 at Bucks Co., Pa., to Joseph Lupton, Jr. and Mercy Twining.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Relocated from Solebury to the Sheandoh Valley, Frederick Co., Virginia 1740-42; 
2 CONT
2 CONT *  William would return to Buckingham MM and married his step-sister, Grace Pickering, July 8, 1743-45. They settled on Apple Pie Ridge. Lord Fairfax granted William 316 acres of and in 1752. He would receive an additional 225 acr
2 CONC es of adjoining land. William's land was located where the Back Creek and Opequan watersheds meet.
2 CONT
2 CONT * William helped establish the Upper Ridge Meeting House, also referred to as Lupton's Meeting House.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of William and Grace: (All born Frederick Co., Va.)
2 CONT
2 CONT # Samuel Lupton, b.1746, married Sarah Smith
2 CONT
2 CONT # Isaac Lupton, b.1748, married Elizabeth Kirk
2 CONT
2 CONT # Joseph Lupton , b. 1752, married Susan Boyer
2 CONT
2 CONT # William Lupton, b.1754, married Bathsheba Allen
2 CONT
2 CONT # Asa Lupton, b. 1757, married Hannah Hanke
2 CONT
2 CONT # Jesse Lupton, b.1760
2 CONT
2 CONT # Marcy Lupton Horseman, b.1762, married William Horseman
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Notes: ( Hopewell MM)''':
2 CONT
2 CONT 1745 8 month 7, certificate requested for William Lupton for him and wife to Hopewell Monthly Meeting " in Orange County, Va." Samuel Eastburn and John Schofield to inquire.
2 CONT
2 CONT At this meeting was reported the marriage of William Lupton and Grace Pickering. They had made requests (1) 6 o. 5. 1745 (2)7 mo. 2, 1745, favorable report on William Lupton.  Certificate signed for him.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source''': An American Family
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source''':Hopewell Friends History, 1734-1934, Frederick County, Virginia: By Joint Committee of Hopewell Friends, Hopewell Monthly Meeting (Society of Friends)
2 CONT
