1 NOTE {geni:about_me} . Samuel Lupton was born in Frederick County on June 22, 1746, and died in 1829. Samuel married Sarah Smith, daughter of James and Mary (Capon) Smith Sr., of Hampshire County, Va., June 18, 1772. Samuel inherited h
2 CONC is father's farm on Upper Apple Pie Ridge. After Samuel's death, the farm was inherited by his daughter, Rachel Lupton, who married John Bond. Their brick house still stands on the west side of Apple Pie Ridge Road (Route 739) nea
2 CONC r Gold's Hill, on the original land granted to Rachel's grandfather, William Lupton.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Link:http://www.frostandgilchrist.com/getperson.php?personID=I10408&tree=frostinaz01'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ___________________________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT . Samuel, b. 22/4m/1746; m. 18/6m/1772 at Hopewell Sarah SMITH, daughter of James of Hampshire Co., Va. [44]; Samuel & Sarah's daughter Betty Lupton m. 9/5m/1792 at the Ridge school house Thomas ALLEN, son of Joseph and Ruth[45]; 
2 CONC Samuel & Sarah's daughter Rachel Lupton m. 1/10m/1800 at the Ridge John BOND, son of John and Margaret, dec'd.[46]; Samuel & Sarah's son Samuel [Jr] m. 25/10m/1804 at Hopewell Leah WALKER, daughter of Lewis and Sarah Walker; Leah 
2 CONC m(2) 12/4m/1810 Isaac STEER. [47] Samuel & Sarah's daughter Grace Lupton m. 4/11m/1807 at Upper Ridge William BROWN, son of Daniel and Miriam of Hampshire 
2 CONT
