3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 8 FEB 1811
2 ADDR
3 STAE Ohio
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Biography'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Born November 9, 1754 in Frederick co., Virginia, the 4th of seven children born to William Lupton and Grace Pickering. ( Hopewell Friends History , page 476, gives birth date as 11 month, 9 day, 1754)
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married Bathsheba Allen on 11-4-1779 at Smith Creek, Virginia. 
2 CONT
2 CONT *1805:  Built a sawmill on Smith's Creek,  Leesburg, Ohio
2 CONT
2 CONT *  Died August 2, 1811, Highland, Ohio.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Lupton family of Virginia was divided into the Quaker Luptons of Apple Pie Ridge, originated by William's first cousin David Lupton and the Presbyterian Luptons, originated by William's and David's uncle, John Lupton of Mound 
2 CONC Hill.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.anamericanfamilyhistory.com/Lupton%20Family/LuptonJoseph1718.html
2 CONT
2 CONT  A mass migration of Quaker families left their southern homes  due to their opposition to slavery and in part to the continuing persecution of Quakers in the south. The early Quakers were aware of the increasingly hostile atmosph
2 CONC ere in the southern states during this time period. The Northwest Ordinance of 1787 stated that slavery or any type of servitude, other than as payment for crime, would not be allowed north of the Ohio River and  east of the Missi
2 CONC ssippi River. The Treaty of Greenville in 1795 opened the territory for settlement. The land was fertile and resources plentiful. William and Bathsheba relocated to Leesburg, Ohio between 1798 and 1800, part of the migration.
2 CONT
2 CONT William's wife, Bathsheba, is credited with organizing the meetings of Friends in Frederick, Co., Ohio, but William's name is found on many documents and rolls of the Friend's Meeting histories, leading this writer to believe he w
2 CONC as also very active in church affairs.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: [ A Short History of Leesburg; compiled by J. Lester Seel ]  http://www.leesburgohio.org/HistoryofLeesburg.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT Source:[ Hopewell Friends History 1734-1934; Compiled from official records by a Joint Committee of Hopewell Friends] http://books.google.com/books?id=9zUkpoA7Xl0C&printsec=frontcover&source=gbs_ge_summary_r&cad=0#v=onepage&q&f=fa
2 CONC lse Added by D. Glenn Oct. 8, 2014
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Birthplace is Frederick, VA per geni.com match
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Link''':https://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=131121805
