2 CONT BOWNE LINEAGE
2 CONT
2 CONT History and Genealogy of the Cock, Cocks, Cox Family By George William Cocks, John Cox
2 CONT
2 CONT JOHN BOWNE was b. Matlock, Derbyshire, England. 9th of Third month (? Mar. or May) 1627 and bapt. in Matlock parish church 29th same month, son of Thomas Bowne, bapt. there May 25, 1595. Thomas Bowne with his children John and Dor
2 CONC othy came to New England in the latter part of 164S or early in 1649. In October 1650 John, leaving behind his father and sister, returned to England, and again arrived in Boston in May 1651. In June of the same year he visited Fl
2 CONC ushing, L. I., In company with his brother-in-law Edward Farrington (who had m. his sister Dorothy, probably during his absence in England) and seems to have been much pleased with the place, as he removed thither shortly after to
2 CONC  live. On the 7th of May, 1656, he m. Hannah Feake, b. (supposed) at Watertown, Mass., about 1637, and after living for a time at Greenwich, Conn., and New London, came to Flushing, with her mother, brothers and sisters, before 16
2 CONC 49. She was dau. of Lieut. Robert Feake and Elizabeth (Fones) Win- throp his wife, (see Feake Lineage).
2 CONT
2 CONT John Bowne was born in Matlock, Derbyshire, England, on Wednesday, May 9, 1627, and died in Flushing, Long Island, New York, on December 20, 1695. Hannah Feake was born in Watertown, Middlesex, Massachusetts, in June, 1637, and di
2 CONC ed in London, England, on January 31, 1677/8. They were married in Flushing on Wednesday, May 7, 1656. She took the name Hannah Bowne. He is the son of Thomas Bowne. She is the daughter of Robert and Elizabeth (Fones) Feake. They 
2 CONC had eight children:
2 CONT
2 CONT i.	 John Bowne was born in Flushing on March 13, 1656/7, and died in Flushing on August 30, 1673.	
2 CONT
2 CONT ii.	 Elizabeth Bowne was born in Flushing on October 8, 1658. She married first John Priar and second Samuel Titus, son of Edmund and Martha (Washborne) Titus.	
2 CONT
2 CONT iii.	 Mary Johanna Bowne was born in Flushing on January 6, 1660/1. Married Joseph Thorne in 1679
2 CONT
2 CONT iv.	 Abigail Bowne [#295]: She was born in Flushing on February 5, 1662/3, and died in _____ on June 16, 1688.	
2 CONT
2 CONT v.	 Hannah Bowne was born in Flushing on April 10, 1665. She married Benjamin Field in 1691.	
2 CONT
2 CONT vi.	 Samuel Bowne was born in Flushing on September 21, 1667. He married first Mary Beckit on October 4, 1691, in Falls of Delaware; they had ten children: Samuel, Thomas, Esther, Hannah, John, Mary, Robert, William, Elizabeth, an
2 CONC d Benjamin. He married second Hannah Smith on December 8, 1709, in Flushing; they had five children: Sarah, Joseph, Emy, Benjamin, and Elizabeth. He married third Grace Cowperthwait on November 30, 1734; they had no children. More
2 CONC  details available in EQG.	
2 CONT
2 CONT vii.	 Dorothy Bowne was born in Flushing on March 29, 1669.	
2 CONT
2 CONT viii.	 Martha Bowne was born in Flushing on August 17, 1673. She married Joseph Thorne in 1695.	
