1 NOTE Hannah Feake Bowne, who had received "the gift of the ministry", sailed from New York for England on March 24, 1675 on a religious visit; her husband remaining at home; but he joined her in London on November 13, 1676.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah had a violent attack of fever in London and died on November 30, 1677 at the home of their friends, John and Mary Elson, at the Peel Meeting place, in St. John Street, London, England.  It is recorded in the register of Fri
2 CONC ends in Devonshire House, London, "age about 40."  During John's absence from Flushing, his father Thomas died at "aged upwards of 82."
1 NOTE
2 CONT
2 CONT John and Hannah (Feake) Bowne became Quakers.  Hannah died
2 CONT while on a
2 CONT religious pilgrimage to England.
2 CONT ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
