2 CONT Wherefore, it is our opinion that come connivance would be useful that the conscience of men, at least, ought ever to remain free and unshackled.  Let every one be unmolested as long as he is modest, as long as he does not disturb
2 CONC  others or oppose the government.  This maxim of moderation has always been the guide of the magistrates of this city, and the consequence has been that from every land people have flocked to this asylum.  Tread thus in their step
2 CONC s and we doubt not you will be blessed.  
2 CONT
2 CONT The Directors of the West India Company
2 CONT Amsterdam Department
2 CONT Abraham Wilmandonk
2 CONT David Von Baerle"
2 CONT
2 CONT This document has particular historic interest because it was one of the first official proclamations of religious liberty for any part of America.  With this decree, the persecution of Friends on Long Island ceased.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Bowne left Amsterdam in April 1663 and after a visit to England and a journey to the island of Barbados, returned to his home at Flushing, where he arrived on January 30, 1664.
2 CONT
2 CONT George Fox stayed at the Bownes house during his visit to America in 1672 where he preached to a large meeting under the oak tree opposite the house.
