1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Bowne-10
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel Bowne (1667 - 1745)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Samuel Bowne===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 21 Sep 1667 in Flushing, Long Island, New York
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of John Bowne Sr. and Hannah (Feake) Bowne
2 CONT
2 CONT Brother of John Bowne Jr., Elizabeth (Bowne) Titus, Mary (Bowne) Thorne, Abigail (Bowne) Willets, Hannah (Bowne) Field, Dorothy (Bowne) Franklin, Martha Johanna (Bowne) Thorne, John Bowne [half], Amy (Bowne) Hallett [half] and Rut
2 CONC h Bowne [half]
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Mary (Becket) Bowne — married 4 Aug 1691 (to 21 Aug 1707) in Flushing, Long Island, New York
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Hannah (Smith) Bowne — married 8 Dec 1709 (to after 26 Sep 1720) in Flushing, Long Island, New York
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Grace (Burling) Bowne — married 14 Nov 1735 (to 30 May 1745) in Flushing, Long Island, New York
2 CONT
2 CONT Father of Samuel Bowne, Thomas Bowne, Hannah (Bowne) Lawrence, John Bowne, Mary Bowne and Robert Bowne
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 30 May 1745 at age 77 in Flushing, Queens, New York
2 CONT
2 CONT Profile last modified 6 Dec 2021 | Created 9 Feb 2011
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel Bowne was a New Netherland settler.
2 CONT Join: New Netherland Settlers Project
2 CONT Discuss: NEW_NETHERLAND
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel was a Friend (Quaker)
2 CONT Samuel Bowne, son of John Bowne and Hannah Feake, was born 21 Sep 1667 at Flushing, Long Island.[1] He died at Flushing 30 May 1745 (aged 77).[2][3][4] Samuel was buried at Old Bowne Family Burial Ground, Flushing.[4] Samuel Bowne
2 CONC  was a Quaker minister. His father had been granted 1000 acres of land in Bucks County, Pennsylvania by William Penn, and Samuel Bowne met Mary Becket there before returning to marry and live in his father’s home at Flushing, Long
2 CONC  Island.
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel married:[3][4]
2 CONT
2 CONT (1) Mary Becket on 4 October 1691,[5][6]
2 CONT Bowen, Samuel (1667-) & 1/wf Mary Becket (-1707); 4 Aug [Oct] 1691; Flushing, LI[7]
2 CONT (2) Hannah Smith on 8 December 1709,[5][6][8] and
2 CONT (3) Grace (Burling) Cowperthwait on 14 November 1734/5[6]
2 CONT Samuel, born in 1667, son of John Bowne, married Grace Cowperthwait in 1735. He died in 1745.[5][9]
2 CONT The following entry for Samuel Bowne was recorded in the death register of the Flushing Meeting of the Society of Friends:[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT "Samuell Bowne of fflushing Deceased at his hous in ye 3 mo: ye 30 dy: 1745 in ye 78 year of his age a man Serviseable in his Day bore a publick testemony in meetings & his hous always open for ye Entertaining of ffriends”
2 CONT Note: The third month of the Old Style calendar corresponds to May, rather than March.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Samuel Bowne and Mary Becket
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel and Mary had the following children:[6]
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel Bowne, b. 29 Jan 1693, Flushing, Queens Co., LI, NY; d. 31 Mar 1769, Flushing, Queens Co., LI, NY (Age 76 years)
2 CONT Thomas Bowne, b. 29 Jan 1694/95; d. 28 Mar 1762; m. 1716 Hannah Underhill b. 23 Mar 1690; d. 2 May 1761
2 CONT Esther Eleanor Bowne, b. 20 Feb 1695, Flushing, Queens Co., LI, NY; d. Sep 1759, Bordentown, Burlington, New Jersey (Age 64 years)
2 CONT Hannah (Bowne) Lawrence, b. 31 Jan 1697, Flushing, Queens Co., LI, NY; d. 1 Jul 1748, Flushing, Queens Co., LI, NY (Age 51 years); 4 Aug 1717 m. Richard Lawrence, b. 1691 Flushing NY; d, 1784 Flushing
2 CONT John Bowne, b. 11 Sep 1698; d. 4 Apr 1757; m. 1738 Dinah Underhill, b. 20 Seo 1705; d, 1 Feb 1770
2 CONT Mary Bowne, b. 21 Aug 1699, Flushing, Queens Co., LI, NY; d. 3 Apr 1773 (Age 73 years)
2 CONT Robert Bowne, b. 1700; d. 1743; m. 6 Nov 1724 Margaret Latham, d. 2 Apr 1773
2 CONT Elizabeth Bowne, b. 11 Aug 1704, Flushing, Queens Co., LI, NY
2 CONT Children of Samuel Bowne and Hannah Smith
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel and Hannah had the following children:[6][10]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah Bowne, b. 30 Jul 1710, Flushing, Queens Co., LI, NY
2 CONT Joseph Bowne, b. 25 Feb 1712, Flushing, Queens Co., LI, NY
2 CONT Amy Bowne, b. 17 Oct 1715, Flushing, Queens Co., LI, NY
2 CONT Benjamin Bowne, b. 1 Jun 1717, Flushing, Queens Co., LI, NY
2 CONT Elizabeth Bowne, b. 26 Sep 1720, Flushing, Queens Co., LI, NY
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ James E. Hazard Index, The Records of New York Yearly Meeting of the Religious Society of Friends at Friends Historical Library, Swarthmore College.; Call Number N 452; Volume 3.1; Page 123; ID 65877
2 CONT ↑ Thompson, Benjamin Franklin. The History of Long Island, from Its Discovery to the Present Time. Vol. II. Gould, Banks & Co. New York. 1843. Of the Family of John Bowne, pp. 385-90
2 CONT ↑ 3.0 3.1 The Fones Family, Page 6; Art Reierson; reprinted by Higginson Book Company, Salem MA.
2 CONT ↑ 4.0 4.1 4.2 4.3 Samuel Bowne Find A Grave: Memorial #136231676
2 CONT ↑ 5.0 5.1 5.2 Thompson, Benjamin Franklin. The History of Long Island, from Its Discovery to the Present Time. Vol. II. Gould, Banks & Co. New York. 1843. pg. 388
2 CONT ↑ 6.0 6.1 6.2 6.3 6.4 Encyclopedia of American Quaker genealogy, by ... v.3. Hinshaw, William Wade, 1867-1947. p. 42
2 CONT ↑ Torrey, Clarence Almon. New England Marriages Prior to 1700. Genealogical Publishing Co. Inc. Baltimore. 1785. pg. 88
2 CONT ↑ James E. Hazard Index, The Records of New York Yearly Meeting of the Religious Society of Friends at Friends Historical Library, Swarthmore College.; Call Number N 452; Volume 3.1; Page 35; ID 65787
2 CONT ↑ James E. Hazard Index, The Records of New York Yearly Meeting of the Religious Society of Friends at Friends Historical Library, Swarthmore College.; Call Number N 452; Volume 3.1; Page 89; ID 65790
2 CONT ↑ Long Island Genealogy Samuel Bowne b 1667 2nd marriage Hannah Smith, Pearsall family-accessed June 2019
2 CONT Thompson-Stahr, Jane. The Burling Books: Ancestors and Descendants of Edward and Grace Burling, Quakers (1600-2000). Baltimore: Gateway Press, 2001. pp 53-56
2 CONT Thompson, Benjamin Franklin. The History of Long Island, from Its Discovery to the Present Time. Vol. II. Gould, Banks & Co. New York. 1843. The History of Long Island...
2 CONT Children of Hannah Feake and John Bowne are: i. John Bowne, b. March 13, 1656; d. 1673. ii. Elizabeth Bowne, n. October 08, 1658; d. October 14, 1721; m. (1) Samuel Titus; m. (2) John Prior, November 02, 1678.; iii. Mary Johanna B
2 CONC owne, b. January 06, 1660, Flushing Long Island New York; d. 1728, Woodbridge, New Jersey; m Joseph Thorne, 1680, Flushing Long Island New York. iv. Abigail Bowne, b. February 05, 1662; d. June 16, 1688; m. Richard Willits, March 
2 CONC 25, 1686. v. Hanna Bowne, b. April 10, 1665. vi. Samuel Bowne, b. September 21, 1667; d. May 30, 1745; m (1) Mary Beckett, August 04, 1691, Flushing Long Island New York; m. (2) Hannah Smith, December 08, 1709, Flushing Long Islan
2 CONC d New York; m (3) Grace Cowperthwaite, November 14, 1734, Flushing Long Island New York. vii. Dorothy Bowne, b. March 29, 1669; d. 1690; m. Henry Franklin, 1689. viii. Martha Johanna Bowne, b. August 17, 1673; d. August 01, 1750; 
2 CONC m. Joseph Thorne, November 09, 1695. Flushing, Long Island, New York.
2 CONT See also:
2 CONT
2 CONT Friends Historical Association. SAMUEL AND MARY BOWNE, OF FLUSHNG, AND THEIR FRIENDS. Author(s): Mary Bowne, Samuel Bowne and Allen C. Thomas Source: Bulletin of Friends' Historical Society of Philadelphia, Vol. 7, No. 3 (FIFTH MO
2 CONC NTH (MAY), 1917), pp. 85-91. Published by: Friends Historical Association Stable. URL: Samuel and Mary Bowne, of Flushing, and their Friends : Accessed: 06-09-2019.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT https://books.google.com/books?id=g4DTAAAAMAAJ&pg=PA87&lpg=PA87&dq=samuel+bowne,+mary+becket&source=bl&ots=mXDGG-DSzg&sig=lx7ra5vF-3aRh6nBM7-ESbXwyZk&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwjP3oHDxJfRAhUJ7IMKHSOrCkMQ6AEIIjAD#v=onepage&q=samuel%20bo
2 CONC wne%2C%20mary%20becket&f=false
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel, sixth child and second son of John and Hannah (Feake) Bowne, was 
2 CONT
2 CONT born in Ekishing. Long Island, September 21, 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1667, (Hed May 30, 1745. He was a minister 
2 CONT
2 CONT among Friends. October 4. 1691, he married 
2 CONT
2 CONT (first) at Philadelphia Meeting, Mary, daugh- 
2 CONT
2 CONT ter of Captain Becket, who died August 21, 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1707. She bore him ten children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT i. Samuel, referred to below. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Thomas, born April 7, 1694, married, March 7. 1715, Hannah, daughter of John Underhill. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. Eleanor, April 20, 1695. married, October 9, 1718, Isaac Homer, of Mansfield, Burlington county, New Jersey. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. Hannah. March 31, 1697, married, April 6, 1717, Richard Lawrence. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. John, September II. 1698, died 1757; married, 1738, 
2 CONT
2 CONT Dinah Underhill. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. Mary, October 21, 1699, married, January 14, 1720. John Keese. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 7. Robert, January 17, 1701, died before July 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3, 1746, when his daughter Mary married 
2 CONT
