2 CONT # Susannah (Thorne) Okeson
2 CONT
2 CONT “ “When William Thorne's name next appears on the Flushing records, twelve years after his first visit, it is as a signer of the Remonstrance, in which signing he is joined by his son, William Jr., a child of his marriage to Susan
2 CONC nah Booth, whom he had married while at Lynn. In addition to William Jr., born circa 1639, their children included John (b 1640-43), Joseph (b 1642-46), Samuel (b 1648-55) and Susannah (Lockerson) (b circa 1645).“
2 CONT
2 CONT * Source: the [http://thorn.pair.com/williamthorne1/d48.htm Thorne Family Website]
2 CONT
2 CONT no confirmation of last name - I have left Booth here, but proof would be nice.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Source: [http://books.google.com/books?id=sdgUAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA18&lpg=PA18&dq=william+thorne+hallett&source=bl&ots=nazJYb2B4k&sig=0b6ptPTETsKcozLCfsTbYe3xMk8&hl=en&ei=4aJLTKmNLMGB8gbQhdEz&sa=X&oi=book_result&ct=result&resnum=1&ved=
2 CONC 0CBIQ6AEwAA#v=onepage&q=william%20thorne%20hallett&f=false Google Books]
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married to Susannah Booth about 1636 in England. Susannah Booth was born before 1617 in England. She died in 1675 in Flushing, Long Island, NY. She was buried in 1675 in Quaker Cemetery, Flushing, NY. Philip V. Thorne Notes
2 CONC : 
2 CONT
2 CONT Susannah Booth Thorne's exact parentage is unknown. There was an Ensign John Booth who came with Reverend John Youngs to New Southold on Long Island. He resided on Shelter Island. Youngs was a militant puritan with strong anti Qua
2 CONC ker feelings. In more than one instance Booth sided with the quakers against Youngs. Given this bent towards religious tolerance and given the fact the Reverend Youngs group was from Southold in Suffolk County, England (next to Li
2 CONC ncolnshire) we have some circumstantial evidence tying the Booths and Thornes to the same general area. There was a very large and very ancient Booth family in Great Grimsby an old seaport and military site at the mouth of the riv
2 CONC er Humber, Lincolnshire. Travelling inland from Grimsby, not far from the Humber River lies the City of THORNE. Thorne is located in South Yorkshire and is less than 35 miles from Grimsby and is less than 60 miles from where Gunby
2 CONC  was formerly situated. Further it's only about 80 miles south towards London to Southold (John Youngs and John Booth) 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Gary Wayne Williams of Indiana, a Thorne/Booth descendant, gives Susannah's father as Nicholas Booth, without documentation. William Thorne and Susannah Booth had the following children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 i. William Thorne.  3 ii. Joseph Thorne.  4 iii. John Thorne.  5 iv. Susannah Thorne.  6 v. Samuel Thorne.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT A puritan, born in England - among the first of the English settlers to cross the Atlantic to the New world
2 CONT
