2 CONT
2 CONT In 1638 he possibly arrived on the ship "Confidence" which sailed from Southampton, England with the emigrants for Massachusetts Bay. he was admitted as a freeman in Lynn, Massachusetts. He was the combination of Father and signer
2 CONC s of the Remonstance. He followed the pathway to Flushing in order to escape the religious intolerance of his earlier New England associations. He was a proprietor of Jamaica and was appointed as a Magistrate of Flushing. 
2 CONT
