1 NOTE In 1656, William Hallett, Sheriff of Flushing, was sentanced for allowing (Baptist) conventicles in his house, contrary to law; to be removed from office; to pay a fine of 50 pounds Flemish and to be banished, meanwhile to be impr
2 CONC isoned until the same be paid.  A petition was presented by his neighbors, asking for the remittal of the sentance, which was done except the fine.
