1 DEAT
2 DATE 1698
2 ADDR
3 CITY Hempstead
3 STAE Province of New York
3 CTRY Colonial America
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} William was the son  of William Thorne,Sr. and Susannah Booth (Hallett). Married Winnifred Linnington September 4, 1662. Some records give his birth as Massachusetts, however his parents came to America in the year
2 CONC  1638 on the ship Confidence.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://thorn.pair.com/thorn/thornlineage/WilliamThorne1.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. William Thorne was born about 1636 in Lynn, Essex, MA. He died about 1699 in New York. Presumably in Hempstead, LI, NY
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married to Winnifred Linnington (daughter of Henry Linnington) on 4 Sep 1662. Winnifred Linnington died in 1713. She was buried on 20 Feb 1713 in Grace Church, Flushing. William Thorne and Winnifred Linnington had the follo
2 CONC wing children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT +7 i. William Thorne. 
2 CONT
2 CONT +8 ii. John Thorne. 
2 CONT
2 CONT +9 iii. Elizabeth Thorne. 
2 CONT
2 CONT +10 iv. Hannah Thorne. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 11 v. Denton Thorne was born about 1673. He died about 1698. 
2 CONT
2 CONT +12 vi. Richard Thorne. 
2 CONT
2 CONT +13 vii. Sarah Thorne. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 14 viii. Abraham Thorne was born about 1681. The name of Abraham Thorne appears on the muster roll of Capt Joshua Cornell's, Dutchess Co., militia. 
2 CONT
2 CONT +15 ix. Margaret Thorne. 
2 CONT
2 CONT +16 x. Joseph Thorn.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Some claim that [https://www.geni.com/people/Sarah-Thorne/6000000006441319866 Sarah Denton] was the mother of the Thorne children, but this has been disproved by many genealogists. The only proof was a son named Denton. However, t
2 CONC here are many documents claiming Susannah Booth as the mother of all the children. This includes some of the children naming their children after her. No real proof gives evidence to Thorne having married Denton at all.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
