1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT From https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Thorne-123
2 CONT
2 CONT Susannah Thorne was born about 1645[1] to William Thorne and Susannah Booth,[2] presumably in Flushing, New Netherland.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 10 July 1667, John Ockeson and she were entered into a bond to be married.[3][4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Susannah is believed to have died around between 25 March 1694/5 and 15 April 1696 (O.S.), for on the former date she was party, with her husband, to a conveyance in Madnans Neck, while on the latter date her husband conveyed land
2 CONC  on his own.[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT Note on Her Taken Name, Ockeson, Etc.
2 CONT
2 CONT For those not familiar with this family, the spelling of "Ockeson" name was given very rough treatment during this period in Long Island -- different members of the family and different official documents, list them as Ockeron, Lo
2 CONC ckerson, Locussum, Casson, Cassum, Kissam, as well as probably other spellings. The names of descendants diverged
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Source ===
2 CONT
