1 TITL Captain
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://books.google.com/books?id=PZsyAQAAMAAJ&pg=RA1-PA176&lpg=RA1-PA176&dq=Rapalje+Nova+Scotia&source=bl&ots=t8gmoS3Mu6&sig=zgtj48wTkLKMnkPDhDirIVH9ll8&hl=en&sa=X&ei=bG25VIe3M_jfsATi9YLQDA&ved=0CCYQ6AEwAw#v=onepa
2 CONC ge&q=Rapalje%20Nova%20Scotia&f=false 
2 CONT
2 CONT Stephen was a Captain in the British militia and evacuated Long Island in 1783 at the end of the American Revolution. Married (1) Sybil Sands on 27 Jul 1746 in St George's Church, Hempstead, LI, NY. Married (2) Janetje Lefferts-Ra
2 CONC palje, daughter of Jacobus and Jane Lefferts after 1759. Janetje Lefferts-Rapalje was born on 21 Jun 1729. She died on 13 Mar 1795 in Granville, Nova Scotia.
2 CONT
2 CONT ~• from : https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/84277779/stephen-thorne
2 CONT
2 CONT ==details==
2 CONT He was married to Sybil Sands (daughter of Edward Sands and Mary Cornell) on 27 Jul 1746 in St George's Church, Hempstead, LI, NY. Sybil Sands was born on 13 Sep 1727 in Sand's Point, Long Island, NY. She died on 1 Mar 1759 in Hem
2 CONC pstead, Long Island, NY. Captain Stephen Thorne "Loyalist" and Sybil Sands had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT child+272 i. Edward Thorne.
2 CONT child+273 ii. Stephen Thorne.
2 CONT child274 iii. Joseph Thorne was born about 1752 in Flushing, Long Island, NY. He was baptized on 29 Jul 1756. He died unknown. Unmarried and was a physician.
2 CONT child+275 iv. Philip Thorne.
2 CONT child+276 v. Richard Thorne.
2 CONT child277 vi. Sybil Thorne was born in 1762 in Hempstead, Long Island, NY. She died on 3 Apr 1807 in Granville, Nova Scotia. She was buried in Karsdale Cemetery, Annapolis, Nova Scotia.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married to Janetje Lefferts-Rapalje (daughter of Jacobus Lefferts and Jane) after 1759. Janetje Lefferts-Rapalje was born on 21 Jun 1729. She died on 13 Mar 1795 in Granville, Nova Scotia. Captain Stephen Thorne "Loyalist" 
2 CONC and Janetje Lefferts-Rapalje had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT child+278 i. James Thorne.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Other Sources==
2 CONT * https://www.thornfamily.net/williamthorne1/d4395.htm
2 CONT ** (explains offspring)
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Changes in Domicile==
2 CONT As a Loyalist, Stephen was compelled to leave Manhattan at the end of the Revolution. Indeed, he died in Nova Scotia but some of his children returned to the United States and [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000218
2 CONC 834064833 one son (Stephen) was never deported.] He, himself may have returned as well as we see in the 1800 census of Manhattan that there were two Stephen Thornes listed: A Stephen  with his  wife in Ward 7 and a Stephen with wi
2 CONC fe and young children in Ward 3.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Karsdalle, Annapolis Cpunty, NS==
2 CONT Karsdale is a community in the Canadian province of Nova Scotia, located in Annapolis County. It is situated on the west bank of the Annapolis Basin.
2 CONT Note that a nearby geographical name reflects the presence of the Thorne family > '''''Thorne's Cove'''''.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===AI Overview===
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Thorne's Cove in Karsdale, Nova Scotia'', is historically significant as a settlement of Black Loyalists. The settlement likely began with the purchase of fish lot #16 by Edward Jackson in 1785, including 100 acres. Edward Jacks
2 CONC on and his family were part of the Black Loyalists who had a strong connection with the James family. They arrived in Nova Scotia and Edward acquired another fish lot, #17. Thorne's Cove was also a connecting point along Thorne's 
2 CONC Cove Road, connecting the cove to other settlements like Delap's'''''††''''' Cove. The settlement had no specific church, with many Baptists likely being adherents of the Fundy Section African Baptist Church on the other side of t
2 CONC he North Mountain."
2 CONT
2 CONT > Note: Delap's'''''††''''' Cove > Delap is an in-law surname to the Thorne family, Both <Thorne> & <Delap> are non-Afro-American lines. For more on other Nova Scotia Black Loyalist settlements, see: https://www.geni.com/projects/
2 CONC Birchtown-Nova-Scotia/45756
2 CONT - 
