1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ancestry.com
2 CONT
2 CONT Re: WICKES, SMITH, DAVIDS, TOWNSEND, BURTON, GISBORNE
2 CONT  zanasearch   (View posts) Posted:	19 Jul 2003 09:11AM Classification: Query Edited: 22 Nov 2006 10:28AM Sorry I am not of much help. I have not searched the Wicks for many years and below is all the information I have. My materna
2 CONC l 9th. great grandfather is John WICKS b. 1602 in Staines, Middlesex, England the son of Robert WICKS and Sarah married Mary b. 1607 in England and died 1689. John died Nov 1675 in Warwick, Kent, RI.
2 CONT
2 CONT John and Mary had the following children: 1.	Elizabeth b. 1622 in Staines, Middlesex, England, married first to John SMITH (Justice John Smith) the son of John SMITH and Ruth DAVIDS, she married second to Richard TOWNSEND. Elizabe
2 CONC th died 1689 possibly in Great Egg Harbor, Gloucester Co., NJ. (Elizabeth and John are my maternal 8th. great grandparents). 2.	Hannah b. 1634 in Staines, Middlesex, England, married first to William BURTON and second to Richard H
2 CONC arris, she died 20 Feb 1714. 3.	Mary b. 1635 in Staines, Middlesex, England and married Francis GISBORN. 4.	John b. 1650 in Warwick, Kent, RI, married Rose TOWNSEND and died 1689.
2 CONT
2 CONT WICKES/WICKS
2 CONT
2 CONT My maternal 10th. great grandfather is Robert WICKES, b. 1570 in Staines, Middlesex, England the son of Richard WICKS and Florence. He married Sarah who was born about 1574 in Staines, Middlesex, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert and Sarah had the following children: 1.	Thomas b. 1600 in Staines, Middlesex, England, m. Elizabeth and he d. 26 Jan 1648. 2.	John b. 1602 in Staines, Middlesex, England, m. Mary and died Nov. 1675 in Warwick, Kent, RI (th
2 CONC ese are my 9th. great grandparents). 3.	William b. 1604 in Staines, Middlesex, England, d. 23 Oct 1642. 4.	Robert b. 1606 in Staines, Middlesex, England.
2 CONT
