2 CONT ↑ William1 Carpenter of Providence, Rhode Island, in Zubrinsky, Eugene Cole. Carpenter Sketches: Links to Sketches And Articles Representing the Most Current and Reliable Scholarship Concerning Early Generations of the Carpenter F
2 CONC amilies of Rehoboth, Massachusetts, and Providence, Rhode Island and Their Ancestors. (Carpenters' Encyclopedia of Carpenters, 2008)
2 CONT page 11.
2 CONT 'HANNAH BURTON, d. probably Pawtuxet (Providence) before 1 Dec. 1724 (not mentioned in husband’s will), dau. of William and Hannah (Wickes) Burton' sources follow
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Burton-3041
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah Burton was the daughter of William and Hannah (Wickes) Burton. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT She married Timothy Carpenter who was born born at Pawtuxet, Rhode Island about 1643-8, son of William Carpenter and Elizabeth Arnold. [1] [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Her father William Burton wrote his will on March 20, 1703, with a codicil added on July 8, 1713. In it he names among his children, Hannah Carpenter. [3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Timothy died at Providence, Rhode Island on August 19, 1726. [1] [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Timothy Carpenter, by his will dated December 1, 1724: left bequests to:
2 CONT
2 CONT * son Timothy
2 CONT * daughter Ethalenah Sweet
2 CONT * daughter Elizabeth Williams
2 CONT * daughter Hannah Arnold
2 CONT * granddaughter Hannah Carpenter alias Hannah Arnold, among others. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT As wife Hannah is not mentioned in the will, she likely died before December, 1724.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT * Ethalenah born ___ ; married Daniel, son of John Sweet 2d, who was born 1657. The family had their home at Sweet's Cove Warwick, Rhode Island. [1]
2 CONT * Elizabeth born about 1676; married Peleg, son of Daniel and grandson of Roger Williams. [1]
2 CONT * Hannah born ___; married December 9, 1709; Elisha, son of Israel and Mary (Barker) Arnold. [1]
2 CONT * Timothy born about 1680; died on August 2, 1749; married ?Mehitable Fraser. [1]
2 CONT * William was drowned at Pawtuxet Falls, October 29, 1708; young man, unmarried. [1].
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT * Carpenter, Daniel H. History and Genealogy of the Carpenter Family in America: From the Settlement at Providence, R.I., 1637-190, Marion Press, 1901, p. 318-9
2 CONT * Chamberlain, Mildred M. Early Rhode Island Settlers in: Roots, Volume 13, Rhode Island Genealogical Society, Warwick, Rhode Island, 1987, p. 75
2 CONT * Austin, John Osborn. The Genealogical Dictionary of Rhode Island: Comprising Three Generations of Settlers who Came Before 1690, Albany, NY, 1887. Reprint: Genealogical Publishing Com, Baltimore, Maryland
