1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 2.  John Roe-2(David-1) was born in 1672 in Flushing, Queens, New York. He died on 12 Mar 1711 in Gloucester Twp, Gloucester, NJ. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===family===
2 CONT
2 CONT The name of John Roe's first wife is not certain; some have her as Mary (or unknown) Hedger, daughter of Thomas Hedger and Elizabeth Burton of Flushing.
2 CONT
2 CONT His second wife was Grace (...) Ward, widow of William Ward of Upton, Gloucester County, NJ. The second marriage took place between Sept. 1, 1702 and April 2, 1710. He married to Grace  on 01 Sep 1702 in Long Island, Queens, NY.Sh
2 CONC e was born in 1676 in New Jersey.
2 CONT
2 CONT The widow of John Roe lived in Evesham Township, Burlington County, NJ for a number of years, but returned to Gloucester County before her death. She died intestate before January 25, 1758, the date of her probate. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children mentioned in John Roe's will: John, b. about 1694; m. Elizabeth ? (Sikes or Sykes?); Children - Benjamin; Deborah; Susanna; Uriah; Henry, b. 1705; ;m. Hannah Cheesman. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://longislandsurnames.com/getperson.php?personID=I0676&tree=Roe
2 CONT
2 CONT >John Roe's first wife ____Hedger, mentioned previously, was mother of all his children. John Roe, father of Henry Roe m. 2nd Grace (Mills) Ward (1st m. to _____Hedger), widow of William Ward of Upton, N. J., (widowed on 21 Aug 17
2 CONC 02).
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===notes===
2 CONT
2 CONT John Roe son of David Roe of Flushing, NY bought land in Gloucester County, N.J., Oct 1, 1696, and another tract, Oct 5, 1696; removed to New Jersey before March 1, 1967-8, when he is mentioned as a resident of Gloucester County. 
2 CONC April 2, 1710, when his wife Grace was baptized to the First Presbyterian Church of Philadelphia. She is called Grace Roe wife of John of Cohanzy, from which it appears that he then resided in Salem County, NJ. He returned to Glou
2 CONC cester Township, Gloucester Co., NJ, before August 10, 1711, when his will was made. He died before Oct. 9, 1711, when the inventory of his personal estate was taken
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
