1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Biography'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Born: Sept.,8 1690 at Newton, Bucks, Pa., to Stephen and Abigail (Young) Twining. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage: Sept.10, 1713. Their intentions to marry were first brought to Middletown Monthly Meeting,1713, and they were cleared to marry. They would marry Sept 10, 1713 at the home of Mercy's father. The clearness committee was no
2 CONC t aware the couple had engaged in "unchaste relations" prior to their wedding. When their first child was born before nine months, the committee spoke to the couple. Joseph presented a paper condemning their actions to the MM. It 
2 CONC was read, accepted and recorded in the MM minutes.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT # William: b.1713-1714
2 CONT
2 CONT # Sarah: b. 1716- 1717
2 CONT
2 CONT # Joseph: b. 1717-1718
2 CONT
2 CONT # Elizabeth: b. 1722
2 CONT
2 CONT # John: b. 1725
2 CONT
2 CONT Relocated: To Solebury Township. Certificates read and approved for removal from Middletown Monthly Meeting. by Buckingham Monthly Meeting for Joseph and Nathaniel Lupton and wives.
2 CONT
2 CONT Died: May 25, 1726 ( unknown location). Family legend says, for unknown reasons, Joseph and Mercy relocated to England and she died there. Unable to find any records or information  to confirm this.
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Link''': http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~paxson/lupton/Lupton.index.html
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Link''': http://www.anamericanfamilyhistory.com/Lupton%20Family/LuptonJosephMercyTwining.html
2 CONT
2 CONT D. Glenn-2015
