2 PLAC Apple Pie Ridge,Frederick County,Virginia
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The Lupton family settled along Apple Pie Ridge near Winchester in Frederick County, Va., during the colonial period. Represented are farmer and landowner Joseph Lupton (1718-1791); his son, farmer, millwright and 
2 CONC Quaker leader David Lupton (1757-1822); David's sons Joseph (1781-1825); David (1786-1814), a merchant in Alexandria, Va.; Nathan (1792?-1843), a merchant in Winchester, Va.; Jonah H. (1795-1870), farmer and horsebreeder; and Joel
2 CONC  Lupton (1804-1883), farmer, millwright and manufacturer; and Jonah's son David P. Lupton (1846-1918) of "Springdale," Frederick County.
2 CONT
2 CONT SCOPE AND CONTENT INFORMATION
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Lupton (1718-1791) settled a large tract near Bobb's March in Frederick County and became a major landowner. His land records in this collection, covering the period 1759-1800, trace the title to a number of tracts in the c
2 CONC ounty obtained from various parties. Joseph's son David Lupton (1757-1822) established the Quaker or Apple Pie Ridge branch of the family in Frederick County. He was a prominent farmer, millwright and Quaker leader. His correspond
2 CONC ence, 1795-1822, largely focuses on family, fellow Quakers and on land dealings in Ohio. Among the more frequent or prominent correspondents are James Chenoweth (bearing a design for the internal mechanism of a grist mill); Philad
2 CONC elphia merchant and Quaker leader Samuel Rowland Fisher; Phineas Janney, an Alexandria merchant and Lupton's son-in-law; David Lupton (1786-1814), also a merchant in Alexandria; and Joseph Steer, a millwright and Quaker kinsman at
2 CONC  Millgrove, Ohio
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Citation''': Lupton Family Papers, Mss1 L9747a FA2, Virginia Historical Society, Richmond, VA
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Link''':http://ead.lib.virginia.edu/vivaxtf/view?docId=vhs/vih00004.xml#bioghist_1.1
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Link''':http://www.anamericanfamilyhistory.com/Lupton%20Family/LuptonJoseph1718.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Information compiled by D. Glenn
