1 NAME Isaac /Lupton/
2 GIVN Isaac
2 _MARNM Lupton
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1798
2 PLAC Virginia
2 ADDR
3 STAE Virginia
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1857
2 ADDR
3 STAE Indiana
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ISAAC LUPTON deceased who was one of the earliest settlers of Sheffield Township this county was a Virginian by birth born in the year 1798 When twelve years old he was taken by his parents to Ohio where he was rea
2 CONC red to farm work and received his education in the pioneer schools of that State 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1824 in company with two of his brothers Jonathan who had a wife and family and Allen he came to Tippecanoe County the three brothers living in this county until their death Allen was a blacksmith by trade which occupation he f
2 CONC ollowed at La Fayette 
2 CONT
2 CONT Isaac Lupton was married in Sheffield Township and after his marriage he settled on the Richardsville Reserve entering fifty four acres of land from the Government Here he built a hewed log house 20 x30 feet in size which in its d
2 CONC ay was considered one of the best dwellings in Sheffield Township This old house where all his children were born and reared is still standing being now about sixty years old 
2 CONT
2 CONT Here he lived until his death which occurred January 11 1857 his wife having preceded him to their better home in March 1852 They were noted throughout the county for their hospitality and were honored and beloved by all who knew 
2 CONC them Mr Lupton was quite a hunter in early life and when a lad of twelve years in Ohio he had killed a bear Game and wild animals were still plentiful when he first settled in this county and here he found ample opportunity to eng
2 CONC age in this pastime In his political views he was a Democrat casting his first presidential vote for Jackson
2 CONT
2 CONT To Isaac Lupton and his wife were born seven children but two of whom are now living Mary wife of Levi Dodson a carpenter and contractor of Chicago Illinois and Allen 
2 CONT
2 CONT The latter is the only one of his father's family living in Tippecanoe County and is numbered among the leading citizens of Sheffield Township He grew to manhood on the old homestead and was educated in the schools at Wyandotte He
2 CONC  participated in the raid after the rebel General Morgan He married Mrs Sarah Graham Peppin a native of Indiana and this union has been blessed with two sons Mark and Arthur By her first marriage Mrs Lupton has four daughters Ella
2 CONC  Nancy Flora and Lillie Mr Lupton lives on the old Peppin homestead of 152 acres well improved a substantial two story residence built in 1876 a good barn and other valuable improvements In politics he is a Democrat He has served 
2 CONC his township as trustee for four years which office he filled to the entire satisfaction of his constituents He is a man of genial disposition and cordial manners and honorable in all his dealings and has gained the confidence and
2 CONC  respect of the entire community where he has spent his life. BIOGRAPHICAL SKETCHES 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Isaac Lupton (1798 VA- 1857) moved to Ohio at age 12, where he killed a bear the same year. He was educated in the pioneer schools and came to Indiana with his two brothers in 1824. He was married in Sheffield township (wife not n
2 CONC amed) and she died in 1852. He settled on Richardville Reserve and built a hewed log house 20 x 30 ft. He had seven children: Mary (b. 1833), Allen (b. 1840, and five others who were not named because they were deceased by then (1
2 CONC 888).
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Link:''' https://www.ancestry.com/boards/thread.aspx?mv=flat&m=804&p=localities.northam.usa.states.indiana.counties.tippecanoe
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Isaac Lupton m. Catherine Lupton March 17, 1831, Tippecanoe County, In (per Indiana State marriages). I believe she was the widow of one of his brothers. Perhaps Baker is her maiden name?
2 CONT
2 CONT I do show that Isaac Lupton had a brother, Jonathan, b. 1787, married 1 Feb 1814 to Catherine Stephens, married in Clinton Co., Ohio. I have no other info re Jonathan. According to Hopewell MM, Va, Jonathan Lupton was dis., mcd, 2
2 CONC 7 Aug 1814.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Link: '''https://www.ancestry.com/boards/thread.aspx?mv=flat&m=804&p=localities.northam.usa.states.indiana.counties.tippecanoe
2 CONT
