1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mildred Morris, wife of Bro. Harrison Morris, died on August 12, 1852, in Henry County, KY, after a painful illness of near twenty years.  She had been an affectionate wife for near thirty years.  In 1835 she was b
2 CONC aptized into the fellowship of the Hillsboro Church in this county, of which she remained a most devoted member while she lived,  by Bro. J. A. McGuire.
2 CONT
2 CONT She lived to see six out of seven children engage in the service of the Lord, one only a few days before her death.  Two have gone before to that “better country.”  After a life of about 47 years it may indeed be said of her, “non
2 CONC e knew her but to love her, or named her but to praise.”
2 CONT
2 CONT Western Recorder Newspaper (Southern Baptist)  September 1, 1852
