1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Thornton Morris, (February 15, 1828 – February 15, 1852) son of Harrison and Mildred Morris of Henry County, KY, at the house of a friend in Shelby County, KY.  His health had been delicate for several years; and o
2 CONC n a visit with a relation he was taken with hemorrhage of the lungs which soon terminated in death, at about the hour in which he was twenty-four years old.  When quite a youth, he professed hope in Christ, and became a member of 
2 CONC the Baptist Church at Hillsboro.
2 CONT
2 CONT He has left a kind father, a dear afflicted mother, a number of brothers, the church at large and numerous relatives and friends to mourn their loss.  Interment was in the Morris Cemetery #1.
2 CONT
2 CONT Western Recorder Newspaper (Southern Baptist)  March 19, 1852
2 CONT
2 CONT
