1 OCCU Politician. He served as a member of the Illinois State House of Representatives. He also fought in the War of 1812, and his name is on a cenotaph for veterans of that war at Evergreen-Washelli Cemetery, Find A Grave Memorial #131
2 CONC 860583.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John Denny (1793–1875), fought in the western battles of the War of 1812 and later served in the Illinois state legislature, elected as a Whig. (He eventually traveled west with the Denny Party, but stayed on in Or
2 CONC egon's Willamette River Valley when his son Arthur and several others moved north to Puget Sound.) http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Denny_Party
2 CONT --------------------
