1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Owned farms, worked as a surveyor.
2 CONT
2 CONT Came from Kentucky.  Believed in States Rights but was opposed to slavery, and in fact left Kentucky due to his opposition.  According to the writings of William Ashley Anderson, the family went from Kentucky to Washington County,
2 CONC  Indiana between 1821 and 1826.  William I. walked from Indiana to Dubuque County, Iowa in 1828, returning to Indiana in 1830 to pick up the rest of the family, who relocated to Dubuque in 1832.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2nd of 7 children.  He was born at 7 am on Sunday, 11/18/1814 in Madison County, Kentucky.
2 CONT
2 CONT Data on W.I. Anderson and his ancestors from Arlis Anderson Renfro of Vancouver, WA - she was in contact with Evelyn Howard by snail-mail.
