1 NAME Elizabeth /Feake/
2 GIVN Elizabeth
2 SURN Feake
2 _MARNM Underhill
2 NICK Not Elizabeth Field
1 SEX F
1 BURI
2 PLAC Underhill Cemtery
2 ADDR
3 CITY Mill Neck
3 STAE New York
3 CTRY United States of America
1 BIRT
2 DATE MAY 1633
2 ADDR
3 CITY Watertown
3 STAE Massachusetts Bay Colony
1 DEAT
2 DATE 4 NOV 1675
2 ADDR
3 CITY Oyster Bay
3 STAE Province of New York
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Second wife of John Underhill. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:
2 CONT Deborah b. Sept. 29, 1659, m. Henry Townsend
2 CONT Nathaniel b. Dec 22, 1663, m. Mary Ferris
2 CONT Hannah b. Oct. 2, 1666, m. Richard Alsop
2 CONT Elizabeth b. May 2, 1669, m. Isaac Smith
2 CONT David b. Feb. 1672, m. Hannah, dau. of Moses Forman
2 CONT ----
2 CONT 1182–1183.  Robert Feake was born in London, England, about 1602, and died in Watertown, Massachusetts Bay Colony, on February 1, 1660/1. Elizabeth Fones was born in Groton, England, on Sunday, January 21, 1609/10, and died in ___
2 CONC __ before 1669. They were married in Massachusetts about 1632. She took the name Elizabeth Feake. He is the son of James and Judith (Thomas) Feake. She is the daughter of Thomas and Ann (Winthrop) Fones. They had five children:
2 CONT
2 CONT i.	 Elizabeth Feake was born probably Watertown, Massachusetts Bay Colony, about 1633. She was married to her second husband was John Underhill by 1659.	
2 CONT
2 CONT ii.	 Hannah Feake [#591]: She was born in Watertown, Middlesex, Massachusetts, in June, 1637, and died in London on January 31, 1677/8.	
2 CONT
2 CONT iii.	 John Feake was born probably Watertown about 1639. He married Elizabeth Prior on September 15, 1673, in Killingworth, Oyster Bay.	
2 CONT
2 CONT iv.	 Robert Feake was baptized in New Amsterdam Dutch Church on July 17, 1642, and died probably 1669. He married Sarah _____ to took administration of his estate on June 19, 1669.	
2 CONT
2 CONT v.	 Sarah Feake was baptized in New Amsterdam Dutch Church on April 14, 1647, and died before July 21, 1648. She died in infancy.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT “Field Genealogy: Being the Record of All the Field Family in ..., Volume 1.” By Frederick Clifton Pierce.  Page 91.  [https://books.google.com/books?id=ejAfAAAAMAAJ&lpg=PA569&dq=William%20Hazard%20Field%201833%201888&pg=PA91#v=on
2 CONC epage&q&f=false GoogleBooks]
2 CONT
