1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The Genealogy of Walter Gilbert
2 CONT
2 CONT ANCESTORS: THE SEVENTH GENERATION BACK
2 CONT
2 CONT Job Carr
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah Willets
2 CONT
2 CONT 146–147.  Job Carr was born in Newport, Rhode Island, on Thursday, October 31, 1689, and died in Jericho, Long Island, New York, after 1718. Hannah Willets was born in Flushing, Long Island, New York, on Tuesday, January 24, 1687/
2 CONC 8, and died probably in Flushing on January 27, 1727/8. They were married in New York on Sunday, February 11, 1710/1. She took the name Hannah Carr. He is the son of Samuel Carr. She is the daughter of Richard and Abigail (Bowne) 
2 CONC Willits. They had four children:
2 CONT
2 CONT i.	 Mary Carr was born in New York on August 4, 1712.	
2 CONT
2 CONT ii.	 Samuel Carr was born in New York on November 10, 1714.	
2 CONT
2 CONT iii.	 Hannah Carr [#73]: She was born in New York on July 24, 1716.	
2 CONT
2 CONT iv.	 Caleb Carr was born in New York on November 4, 1719, and died on September 11, 1784. He married first Sarah Ridgway in 1746, b. 11 Jul 1727 d. 16 Apr 1762, he married second Rebecca Bishop before 5 Jun 1764. Their children we
2 CONC re: Mary, Job, Thomas, Samuel, Isaac, Hannah, and Sarah. Much more information is available on this family from Pat Noble.	
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT
2 CONT Hinshaw, William Wade; Encyclopedia of American Quaker Genealogy, vol. III, 1750–1930.
2 CONT
2 CONT Carr, Arthur A.; The Carr Book, 1947
2 CONT
2 CONT Noble, Pat; The Family of Kerr, Karr, & Carr [2003], which contains the Descendants of Rhode Island Governor Caleb Carr, taken from
2 CONT
2 CONT Carr, Arthur; The Carr Book
2 CONT
2 CONT Carr, Edson; Carr Family Records
2 CONT
2 CONT Douglas Hall [unknown to this researcher]
2 CONT
2 CONT [Ancestry of Timothy Titus Robbins assembled by Gayle Ellingsworth]
