1 NAME Hannah /Smith/
2 GIVN Hannah
2 SURN Smith
2 _MARNM Bowne
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 2 JAN 1682
2 PLAC Flushing, Long Island
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE AFT 26 SEP 1720
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ===Biography===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah Smith, daughter of Jasper Smith of Flushing, Long Island, was born about 1682. She married Samuel Bowne, 8 Dec 1709, at Flushing.[1][2][3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Hannah Smith and Samuel Bowne
2 CONT
2 CONT The children of Samuel Bowne by his third wife, Hannah Smith, were:[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah Bowne, b. 30 Jul 1710, Flushing, Queens Co., LI, NY; m. William Burling
2 CONT Joseph Bowne, b. 25 Feb 1712, Flushing, Queens Co., LI, NY; m. Sarah Lawrence
2 CONT Amy Bowne, b. 17 Oct 1715, Flushing, Queens Co., LI, NY; m. Stephen Lawrence
2 CONT Benjamin Bowne, b. 1 Jun 1717, Flushing, Queens Co., LI, NY; m. Mary Rodman
2 CONT Elizabeth Bowne, b. 26 Sep 1720, Flushing, Queens Co., LI, NY
2 CONT Hannah is mentioned in the will of her father, Jasper Smith of Flushing, Long Island, dated 17 January 1695. Samuel Bowne is an executor.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT RECORDED IN NEW YORK SURROGATE'S OFFICE.
2 CONT
2 CONT I. Jasper Smith of Flushing, L. I.
2 CONT
2 CONT My will is that my wife have a comfortable liv- ing out of my estate, during her life If she remar- ries then she is to have only £20. After her death my plantation and all the rest of my real estate to be sold, and the proceeds d
2 CONC ivided among my 3 children John, Judith and Hannah. If my sow John be care- ful and diligent and seeks to please his mother, he is to have £10 more than his sisters. But if he be careless and disobedient, then to have £10 less. I 
2 CONC make my wife Margary, Hugh Copthwaite and Samel Bowne, executors, John Weig and George Langley, overseers.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dated "the 17th day of the nth month called January," 1695.
2 CONT
2 CONT Witnesses. John Ervine Ed. Burrows Wm. Fulor
2 CONT
2 CONT Proved, March 16, 1695/6 Liber i. P. 330.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Smith-189164 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah (Smith) Bowne (abt. 1682 - aft. 1720)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Hannah Bowne formerly Smith===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Born about 2 Jan 1682 in Flushing, Long Island
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of Jasper Smith and [mother unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT [sibling(s) unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of Samuel Bowne — married 8 Dec 1709 (to after 26 Sep 1720) in Flushing, Long Island, New York
2 CONT
2 CONT [children unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT Died after 26 Sep 1720 after about age 38 [location unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ The Fones Family, Page 6; Art Reierson; reprinted by Higginson Book Company, Salem MA.
2 CONT ↑ 2.0 2.1 Thompson, Benjamin Franklin. The History of Long Island, from Its Discovery to the Present Time. Vol. II. Gould, Banks & Co. New York. 1843. Of the Family of John Bowne, pp. 385-90
2 CONT ↑ Long Island Genealogy Samuel Bowne b 1667 2nd marriage Hannah Smith, Pearsal family-accessed June 2019
2 CONT ↑ Pelletreau, William S. (William Smith), 1840-1918. Wills of the Smith families of New York and Long Island, 1664-1794: careful abstracts of all the wills of the name of Smith recorded in New York, Jamaica, and Hempstead, prior t
2 CONC o 1794, with genealogical and historical notes. New York : F.P. Harper. 1898. Wills of the Smith Family : Jasper Smith of Flushing, L.I.
2 CONT Citations from Long Island Genealogy
2 CONT New York Genealogical and Biographical Record, New York Genealogical and Biographical Society, (New York: New York Genealogical and Biographical Society).Vol. 042, No. 2, Apr. 1911, Registration of Pedigrees, p.207
2 CONT American biographical history of eminent and self-made men : Michigan volume, (Cincinnati, OH : Western Biographical Pub. Co., 1878).v.10.p.74
