0 @I6000000000426593606@ INDI
1 NAME Grace /Burling/
2 GIVN Grace
2 SURN Burling
2 _MARNM Cowperthwaite - Browne
1 SEX F
1 BURI
2 ADDR
3 ADR1  Bowne Street
3 CITY Queens
3 STAE NY
3 CTRY United States
1 BIRT
2 DATE 29 OCT 1676
2 ADDR
3 CITY Barking
3 STAE England
1 DEAT
2 DATE 22 JAN 1760
2 PLAC Flushing, Queens County, New York Colonial America
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Grace was a Friend (Quaker)
2 CONT Grace Burling, the second child of Edward Burling and Grace Norrington, was born 29 Oct 1676 at Barking, Essex, England. Grace was about four years old when she immigrated to New York with her parents and two brothers. When her fa
2 CONC ther died in 1697, Grace was 21. She remained unmarried for 13 years, staying with and helping her mother. Her mother remarried in 1706 to John Ferris.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1709, Grace married her first husband, Hugh Cowperthwaite, as his third wife.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT She was 33 and Hugh, a Quaker minister, was 61. Hugh and Grace had no children, neither did he have any from his first two marriages. Hugh died in 1730 at about the age of 82. He left all houses and lands in Flushing to Grace plus
2 CONC  legacies to various members of Grace’s family and to friends, including Samuel Bowne.[1][3] Hugh also remembered his brother:
2 CONT
2 CONT “I leave to my beloved brother, John Cowperthwait, all my wearing apparell, and my riding mare and saddle, and £10, to be paid as soon as convenient.”[3]
2 CONT Hugh Cowperthwait wrote his Last Will and Testament on 28 Apr 1730, probated 3 Jun 1730 at Flushing, Queens, New York.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Grace (Burling) Cowperthwait married her second husband, Samuel Bowne (1667-1745), son of John Bowne, as his third wife, at Flushing, New York on 14 Nov 1734/5. They had no children.[1][4][5]
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel was, like Grace’s first husband, a Friends minister, as well as treasurer of Friends Meeting. She was close to her Bowne step-grandchildren and remembered some of them in her will. Grace lived 15 years after the death of Sa
2 CONC muel. Her will is dated 27 Feb 1759 and proved 13 Mar 1761.[1][6]
2 CONT
2 CONT Grace Bowne died 22 Nov 1760 at Flushing, Queens, New York.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Burling-15
2 CONT
2 CONT Grace (Burling) Bowne (1676 - 1760)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Grace Bowne formerly Burling aka Cowperthwaite===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 29 Oct 1676 in Barking, Essex, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of Edward Burling Jr. and Grace (Norrington) Ferris
2 CONT
2 CONT Sister of Edward Carpenter Burling, William Burling and Jane (Burling) Mott
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of Hugh (Cowperthwaite) Cowperthwait — married Apr 1709 (to 20 May 1730) in Flushing, Long Island, New York
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of Samuel Bowne — married 14 Nov 1735 (to 30 May 1745) in Flushing, Long Island, New York
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 22 Nov 1760 at age 84 in Flushing, Queens, New York
2 CONT
2 CONT Profile last modified 24 Dec 2021 | Created 9 Feb 2011
2 CONT
2 CONT
