1 NOTE Last Will & Testament
2 CONT Page 457.--"To all Christian People, know ye that I, GRACE BOWNE, of Flushing, on Nassau Island, widow, considering the uncertainty of my time
2 CONT here in this world." I direct all debts and funeral charges to be paid. I leave to my sister, Rebecca Ford, œ10, and to her 5 children (not named), œ30
2 CONT each. To my cousin, Sarah Bloodgood, œ10, and to her 3 children (not named), œ30 each. I do give unto 6 of the children of my cousin, William
2 CONT Burling, deceased, viz., Hannah, Sarah, Rebecca, George, William, and Elizabeth, each œ35. I leave to 4 of the children of my cousin, Benjamin
2 CONT Burling, deceased, viz., Peleg, Lancaster, Seneca, and Rebecca, œ35 each. To Samuel Burling, "son of my brother Burling, deceased," œ30. To my
2 CONT cousin, Abigail Bowne, wife of Samuel Bowne, of New York, œ10. To Hannah Vincent, daughter of my cousin, Ebenezer Burling, deceased, œ30. "I
2 CONT do give to my grandchildren-in-law, to wit, Thomas, Mary, John, and Robert Bowne, œ5 each. To my cousin, Phebe Pell, œ20. To my brother-in-law,
2 CONT John Way, and to my friend, Matthew Franklin, each œ5, for being my executors. All the rest of estate I leave to John and Edward, sons of my brother,
2 CONT Edward Burling, deceased, and to James Burling and Hannah Field, children of my brother, William Burling, deceased, and to Samuel Way, son of my
2 CONT sister, Sarah Way. I make my brother-in-law, John Way, and my friend, Matthew Franklin, executors. Dated the 27th of 2d month called February,15,1759.
