1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 9. Elizabeth Thorne was born about 1668 in Long Island, NY. She died between 1737 and 1739 in Hempstead, Long Island, NY.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was married to Richard (Richbell) Mott (son of Adam Mott and Elizabeth Redman) on 14 Oct 1696. Richard (Richbell) Mott was born in 1668 in Long Island, NY. He died in 1734. Philip V. Thorne Notes: According To MOTT Genealogy, 
2 CONC he had a Richbell not Richard. Elizabeth Thorne and Richard (Richbell) Mott had the following children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT +51 i. Edmund Mott. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 52 ii. Margaret Mott died about 1734. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 53 iii. Richbell Mott died about 1724. Unmarried 
2 CONT
2 CONT +54 iv. Richard Mott. 
2 CONT
2 CONT +55 v. Elizabeth Mott. 
2 CONT
2 CONT +56 vi. Mary Mott. 
2 CONT
2 CONT +57 vii. Ann Mott. 
2 CONT
2 CONT +58 viii. Jemima Mott. 
2 CONT
2 CONT +59 ix. Keziah Mott. 
2 CONT
2 CONT +60 x. Deborah Mott.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Adam and Anne Mott By Thomas Clapp Cornell
2 CONT
2 CONT The widow ELIZABETH (THORNE) MOTT left a will dated 7th March, 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1739, and proved l6th April, 1739. She describes herself widow of 
2 CONT
2 CONT RlCHBELL MOTT, and " sick and weak of body," and names the same 
2 CONT
2 CONT children, and indicates marriages as follows : — daughter Jemmima Wood ( 
2 CONT
2 CONT wife of Stephen), daughter Kedzie Jackson, grandson Daniel Kissam, 
2 CONT
2 CONT granddaughter Mary Treadwell, and granddaughter Elizabeth Mott, 
2 CONT
2 CONT daughter of Adam Mott.
2 CONT --------------------
