1 NOTE {geni:about_me} History of Westchester County edited by John Thomas Scharf
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard Cornell, grandson of Thomas Cornell, of 
2 CONT
2 CONT Cornell's Neck, and eldest son of John and Mary (
2 CONT
2 CONT Russell) Cornell, of Cowneck, in Hempstead, was born 
2 CONT
2 CONT about 1670, and died at Scarsdale in 1757. He married
2 CONT
2 CONT in 1701, Hannah Thorne, of Flushing, and brought her
2 CONT
2 CONT and their 10 children to Scarsdale in 1727.
2 CONT
2 CONT children
2 CONT
2 CONT I. Mary, born at Cowneck, 1703, died 1782 ; married Rev. Henry 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sands. 
2 CONT
2 CONT II. Deborah, born at Cowneck, 1705, died 1772 ; married Matthew 
2 CONT
2 CONT Franklin, a Quaker preacher. 
2 CONT
2 CONT III. Richard Cornell, Jr., born 1708 ; married Mary Ferris.
2 CONT
2 CONT IV. Joseph, born in Cowneck, 1708, died 1770 ; married, 1734, Phebe 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ferris, daughter of Peter Ferris.
2 CONT
2 CONT V. Hannah, born 1711 ; married Joshua Quimby.
2 CONT
2 CONT VI. Phebe, born 1715 ; married Ebenezer Haviland. 
2 CONT
2 CONT VII. John, born 1717 ; died 1781, without Issue. 
2 CONT
2 CONT VIII. Rebecca, born 1718 ; married Edward Burling. 
2 CONT
2 CONT IX. Elisabeth, born 1720, died 1795; married 1st, Aaron Palmer; married 2d, Aaron Quimby. 
2 CONT
2 CONT X. Benjamin, born 1723, died 1771 ; married 17th of 9th month, 1742, Abigail Stephenson, daughter of Stephen Stephenson, of Rye, and Jane Clement, of Flushing, his wife
