1 NOTE {geni:about_me}    (I) John Kissam, the founder of the family, was born in July, 1644.  He was of English origin but on the early records his name appears as "Ocasson," "Ockeson," and "Okeson." February 4, 1678, he bought a farm o
2 CONC f John Smith, on Great neck, to which he removed March 26, 1695.  Spelling his name "Kissam," he deeded a part of this farm to his son Daniel.  He married, July 10, 1667, Susanna, daughter of William Thorne, of Jamaica, Long Islan
2 CONC d.  Children, as afar as known:  1. Daniel, referred to below.  2. John (Ockerson), removed to Freehold, New Jersey; married Elizabeth Mott.  3. Thomas, (Okeson), removed to Hunterdon County, New Jersey; married (first) name unkno
2 CONC wn, and (second) Deborah Clayton.
