2 CONC les was the progenitor of a large family of  Johnsons upon Long Island and elsewhere, of which is Hon. Jeremiah  Johnson of Brooklyn.  This is an error.  Gen. Johnson, as clearly  appears from existing records, is a descendant, in
2 CONC  the fourth  generation, of Jan Barentsen van Driest, who came in 1657 from Zuiphen  in Gueiderland, and settled at Gravesend.  See an article on Antony  Jansen van Sales in the Brooklyn Daily Eagle of Feb. 20, 1851.  The  valuabl
2 CONC e work on American Genealogy, by Holgate contains very serious  mistakes respecting the johnson and Rapalye families, which only those  aquainted with the difficulties of genealogical investigation will  know how to excuse.
2 CONT
