1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Will of Isaac Shotwell, of New Jersey, Dated 5 June 1844, Proved 23 Sept. 1848 No. 13762G, Recorded in Book I of Wills for Essex County [New Jersey], on pages 12 and 13.  “Forasmuch as it is appointed for all Men o
2 CONC nce to die, and the time when very uncertain, I, Isaac Shotwell, of Rahway, in the County of Essex, and State of New Jersey, being in health, and of sound and disposing mind and memory, Blessed be the name of the Lord for the same
2 CONC , Therefore do this fifth day of June, in the year of Our Lord One thousand eight hundred and forty four, make and publish these Presents, as and for my last Will and Testament, in manner and form following, that is to say; I do o
2 CONC rder in the first place, that all my just debts and funeral expenses be paid by my Executor, hereinafter named, as soon as conveniently may be after my decease.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Whereas I have advanced to my son Enoch M. Shotwell, from time to time, what I believe to be his full proportion of what might me coming to him from my Estate, which is the reason I do not give him anything in this my last Will a
2 CONC nd Testament.
2 CONT
2 CONT "And I have likewise, in the lifetime of my Daughter, Caty, made similar advances to her, which is the reason why I do not now leave anything to her Children:
2 CONT
2 CONT "Item. I give to my Daughter, Lydia Brokaw, ten full shares of Stock of the Farmers and Merchants Bank of Rahway.
2 CONT
2 CONT "All the residue, overplus, and remainder of my Moveable property of every description, whatsoever, and wheresoever, I do give to my Son, Joel Shotwell, Son of Mary Fagans, Deceased . I also give and Bequeath unto my Son Joel Shot
2 CONC well, Son of Mary Fagens, deceased, All my Lands, Buildings, and Real Estate which I may (unreadable word) of, to be and remain to him, my Son Joel, his Heirs and Assigns forever.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Lastly, I do Nominate, Constitute, and Appoint my son, Joel Shotwell, Son of Mary Fagens, deceased, Executor to this my Last Will and Testament.
2 CONT
2 CONT "In Witness whereof I have hereunto set my Hand and Seal the day and year herein before written.
2 CONT
2 CONT Signed: Isaac Shotwell"
