1 OCCU https://books.google.ca/books?id=Cy88CpankH8C&pg=PA289&lpg=PA289&dq=Ann+Fitz+Randolph,+David+Laing,+NJ&source=bl&ots=C_0YSbZXib&sig=0AxcD1itOzfWS_gEu3G0g2NoM74&hl=en&sa=X&ei=U5quVIW-Mey1sATJ6oKwAg&ved=0CC0Q6AEwBQ#v=onepage&q=Ann%2
2 CONC 0Fitz%20Randolph%2C%20Dav
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} This Old Monmouth Of Ours
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://books.google.ca/books?id=Cy88CpankH8C&pg=PA289&lpg=PA289&dq=Ann+Fitz+Randolph,+David+Laing,+NJ&source=bl&ots=C_0YSbZXib&sig=0AxcD1itOzfWS_gEu3G0g2NoM74&hl=en&sa=X&ei=U5quVIW-Mey1sATJ6oKwAg&ved=0CC0Q6AEwBQ#v=onepage&q=Ann%
2 CONC 20Fitz%20Randolph%2C%20David%20Laing%2C%20NJ&f=false]
2 CONT
2 CONT pg. 289
2 CONT =======================================
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.genealogy.com/forum/surnames/topics/randolph/3569/<br/>
2 CONT <br/>
2 CONT I need to point out a serious error on the part of the compiler or genealogist of this family record because so much work has been done on it.The Joseph Randolph (30) and Joseph Fitz Randolph are not one man but two.
2 CONT
2 CONT  This work was done before we had computers and many sources for documentations. Someone, about in the 70’s, blended these two men together as one. Both men were born in 1750 and had the name Joseph. Other than those coincidences,
2 CONC  they are two distinct people.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Joseph of Virginia was born there in Spotsylvania County in 1750 and served from there in the Revolution in the Continental Army. He enlisted at Chesterfield Court House March 1, 1779, stating his birth place and date. At the tim
2 CONC e his residence is listed as Mecklenburg County.CHESTERFIELD SUPPLEMENT. Page 17.
2 CONT
2 CONT  In 1781, he is living and buying land in Mecklenburg County.In 1782, he is listed in the VIRGINIA EARLY CENSUS INDEX.He is on the MECKLENBURG COUNTY TAX LIST 1784 through 1793.In 1795, he is selling land there.In 1802, he is in A
2 CONC bbeville S. C. witnessing a will. WILL BOOK 1, PAGE 273. In 1803, he is just across the state line on the FRANKLIN COUNTY, GEORGIA, TAX LIST.In 1807, he is in Elbert County, Georgia, signing a deed with his wife, Elizabeth Turman 
2 CONC Randolph, along with other relatives, to dispose of her deceased father’s land.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Joseph of Virginia died about 1810 while visiting his son John in Jackson County, Ga. He was buried on John’s farm as was the custom then. This was confirmed by Annie Howard and James E. Randolph, great grandchildren of Joseph, w
2 CONC hen they visited Capt. Jack’s old home place about 1890 and were shown the grave by the current resident.
2 CONT
2 CONT  On the other hand, Joseph Fitz Randolph was born 16 January 1750 in New Jersey. He married Mary Laing there in 1772. He was a Captain in the Revolutionary War from there. He died 11 November 1801 and is buried in Hillside Cemeter
2 CONC y of Samptown. The address is 1400 New Market Ave., South Plainfield, NJ 07080. He is listed in Middlesex County in 1778 in the NJ EARLY CENSUS INDEX. Other sources for this information are U.S. VETERANS GRAVESITES, ca. 1775-2006,
2 CONC  AMERICAN GENEALOGICAL-BIOGRAPHICAL INDEX (AGBI), and NEW JERSEY CENSUS, 1643-1890. This Joseph also had a large family of children born in New Jersey and in no way can he be the same man as Joseph of Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT  I hope this will clarify that Joseph Randolph of Virginia is a different man than Joseph Fitz Randolph of New Jersey.I also have two signatures of Joseph of Virginia that can be compared with any of Joseph Fitz Randolph’s.
2 CONT
2 CONT  I have been researching the Randolphs since I was a teenager and I am 83 now. I started by helping my grandaunt with her correspondence to the Howards in the 40’s.
2 CONT
2 CONT  I welcome any comments to the above posting.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Edith
2 CONT
2 CONT ==================================================================
