1 NOTE {geni:about_me} >'''[https://www.ancestry.com/discoveryui-content/view/82782619:60525?tid=174604283&pid=132510490426&hid=1036937727215 U.S., Find a Grave® Index, 1600s-Current]''' 
2 CONT >'''Bio''': "John Wickes was one of the original purchasers of Shawomet (later know as Warwick, RI) from Miantonomi, the Narragansett sachem in 1643. On March 17, 1675, after raiding and burning all the local non-stone homes, the 
2 CONC Pequots and Mohegans from eastern Connecticut beheaded Wickes who had ventured out to locate his cows, and placed his head on a pole near his home. When found, the head was buried at the Stone Castle Cemetery. The next day his tor
2 CONC so was found and buried near his head. In 1881 Benjamin Greene Arnold marked his graves with an inscribed sandstone slab which now resides at the Warwick Public Library on Sandy Lane. If you walk in the main door and head down the
2 CONC  corridor, the stone is on the left outside of the building (can be seen through windowed corridor) just before you enter the main part of the building."
2 CONT >'''NOTES''': 
2 CONT >A. FindAGrave ''does not source'' precise birth data (23 Apr 1609) or death data (17 Mar 1675). '''However:'''  
2 CONT >[https://www.ancestry.com/discoveryui-content/view/2545468:1624?tid=174604283&pid=132510490426&hid=1036937727210 Ancestry.com: London, England, Church of England Baptisms, Marriages and Burials, 1538-1812] confirms "Christening (
2 CONC Baptism)" on "23 Apr 1609" at "St Mary, Staines," '''and—'''
2 CONT >HistoricCemeteries.org concurs with FindAGrave. (''See below''.)
2 CONT >B. FindAGrave correctly does not use "Staines-upon-Thames", which Staines was renamed in 1965.
2 CONT >C. His headstone shows only the years of birth and death.
2 CONT >====Find A Grave Historical Errata:
2 CONT >1. Staines was not part of county Surrey until 1963. 
2 CONT >2. "Spelthorne Borough" district did not exist in name or governance at this time. There were no districts in England until 1890, and most were created in 1974. 
2 CONT >3. There were no [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_counties_in_Rhode_Island#Alphabetical_list Rhode Island counties] until two counties were created in 1703. Kent county was created last in 1750.
2 CONT — — — — — — — — 
2 CONT >'''[http://www.rihistoriccemeteries.org/newgravedetails.aspx?ID=293793 Web: Rhode Island, U.S., Historical Cemetery Commission Index, 1647-2008]:'''
2 CONT >Name: John, Esq Wickes
2 CONT >Birth Date: 1609
2 CONT >Death Date: 17 Mar 1676
2 CONT >Burial Place: Rhode Island
2 CONT >Cemetery: STONE CASTLE LOT
2 CONT >Notes: b. Staines England, came to New England 1635. An original purchaser of Warwick 1643. "In King Phillips War after the town was burnt, on going out from Thomas Green's stone castle to look for his cattle on 17 March 1676 he 
2 CONC was slain by Indians and his head set on a pole." Erected by Benjamin Greene Arnold 1881. His head was originally buried separately from his body, but they were later buried together.
2 CONT
