2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage: 1665 as per New England Marriages Prior to 1700 [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Timothy Carpenter was born say 1646. He died at Pawtuxet (Providence) 19 August 1726. Timothy married, probably at Providence 1670–1671, Hannah (Burton) Carpenter (abt.1655-bef.1724)
2 CONT
2 CONT Timothy's age is estimated from the following from Eugene Zubrinsky: "Timothy’s three eldest siblings were minors when they witnessed a deed to their father on 9 February 1657[/8?] (Providence Town Records 80–81). Had Timothy then
2 CONC  been at least 14 (the legal minimum age for witnessing documents), he, as a male, almost certainly would have replaced his sister Lydia in attesting to the document’s legitimacy. Timothy fails to appear on Providence freemen’s li
2 CONC sts (the last dated in 1669) and was not among that township’s householders who swore allegiance to the king between 31 May 1666 and 29 April 1670 (Providence Town Records 3:101–2; 15:104– 5). He evidently became a householder som
2 CONC etime between the latter date and the last Monday in May 1671, when he (along with his brothers Silas and Benjamin and 20 other young men) affirmed his loyalty to the crown (see Providence Town Records 3:199–200). That Timothy app
2 CONC ears first in all documents in which he and his brothers Silas and Benjamin are named in succession (including their father’s will and codicil) implies that he was older than they (Providence Town Records 4:21–22, 5:115–16, 201–2,
2 CONC  6:141, 142, 143, 147, 21:33)."[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Timothy's wife is mentioned in his father in law's will 30 March 1703, where William Burton mentions daughters Hannah Carpenter and Ethlannah Clarke (Providence Town Records 7:170–72).[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Timothy's will dated 1 December 1724 and proved 19 September 1726, names daughters Ethalannah Sweet and Hannah Arnold among his legatees (Providence Probate Records 3:3–5; Austin 36).[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Timothy Carpenter was born in 1646 in Pawtuxet, Providence Plantation. He is the son of William Carpenter and Elizabeth Arnold.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Hannah Burton
2 CONT
2 CONT Together they had 4 children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Ethalanah Carpenter
2 CONT Hannah Carpenter
2 CONT Elizabeth Carpenter
2 CONT Timothy Carpenter
2 CONT He died on 19 Aug 1726 in Providence, Rhode Island. His Will was written on 1 December 1724 and proved 19 September 1726. He mentions his son, Timothy and his daughters, Ethalannah Sweet, Elizabeth Williams, and Hannah Arnold. He 
2 CONC also mentions his granddaughter, Hannah Arnold.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
