2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography===
2 CONT
2 CONT Ethalenah Carpenter, daughter of Timothy Carpenter and Hannah Burton, was born about 1665. Although Ethalenah was her proper name according to History and Genealogy of the Carpenter Family in America,[1] Eleanor was shown as her n
2 CONC ame in the birth records for several of her children.[2] No birth records were found for Ethalenah or any of her siblings in Rhode Island vital records.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ethalenah married Daniel Sweet in Warwick, Rhode Island before 1697.[3] The family lived in Warwick, Rhode Island.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Together she and Daniel had 5 known children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Sweet, b. 1685
2 CONT Daniel Sweet, b. 1692
2 CONT Eleanor Sweet, b. 1696, m. Ezekiel Hunt
2 CONT Timothy Sweet
2 CONT John Sweet, b. 1706
2 CONT Jeremiah Sweet
2 CONT She died on 27 December 1774 in Glocester, Providence, Rhode Island. Jeremiah Sweet is the executor of her Will.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Probate
2 CONT
2 CONT The heading of her inventory records her death as 27 December 1774.
2 CONT
2 CONT Inventory 1774
2 CONT Her will was dated December 1734 and proved on 9 February 1775 in Glocester. She mentioned her father, Timothy Carpenter, decd., and her children, Hannah Sweet, James Sweet, Daniel Sweet, Jeremiah Sweet, and Timothy Sweet. She dev
2 CONC ises to her son Jeremiah, 79 acres of land that was given to her by her honored father. (Researcher's observation: In Timothy Carpenter's will date 1724, she received 20 shillings. No land)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Will of Ethalanah Sweet 1734
2 CONT
2 CONT Research Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT The Carpenter genealogy used as a source says that Daniel Sweet who married Ethalanah Carpenter, father was John Sweet, b. 1657. "She married Daniel, son of John Sweet2d, who was born 1657. (His grandmother, Mary, wife of John 1st
2 CONC , became in 1638, the wife of Ezekiel Holyman. She died in 1681. The family had their home at Sweet's Cove, Warwick, RI." [5]
2 CONT Ethalenah (Carpenter) Sweet (abt. 1665 - 1774)
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Ethalenah "Eleanor, Eloner, Ethilenah" Sweet formerly Carpenter===
2 CONT
2 CONT Born about 1665 in Providence, Rhode Island
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of Timothy Carpenter [uncertain] and Hannah (Burton) Carpenter [uncertain]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sister of William Carpenter, Ellizabeth (Carpenter) Williams, Timothy Carpenter Jr. and Hannah (Carpenter) Arnold
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of Daniel Sweet — married [date unknown] [location unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother of Daniel Sweet, Eleanor (Sweet) Hunt, Jeremiah Sweet, Timothy Sweet and John Sweet
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 27 Dec 1774 at about age 109 in Glocester, Providence, Rhode Island
2 CONT
