2 CONT Hannah Carpenter, was the daughter of Timothy and Hannah (Wickes) Carpenter of Rhode Island. [1] [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Her father Timothy Carpenter, by his will dated December 1, 1724: left bequests to his son Timothy; to daughter Ethalenah Sweet; daughter Elizabeth Williams; daughter Hannah Arnold, and granddaughter Hannah Carpenter alias Hannah 
2 CONC Arnold, among others. [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah married, Elisha Arnold on December 9, 1709 at Warwick, Rhode Island. [3] He was born about 1683, son of Israel and Mary (Barker/Smith) Arnold . [2] [4] [5] [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah died prior to December 12, 1744 when Elisha married second, Patience Hide [3], daughter of Joseph and Mercy (Aldrich) Hide. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Elisha wrote his will on November 8, 1748 and it was proved on February 13, 1749. [5]
2 CONT
2 CONT In addition to his widow Patience, he left bequests to:
2 CONT
2 CONT sons William, Elisha Jr., Joseph, Nathaniel, James, Israel and Thomas
2 CONT daughter Mary Matteson
2 CONT daughter Hannah [5]
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT William born April 11, 1710; died on September 7, 1788; married Phebe Stafford on May 6, 1733. [5] [3] [1]
2 CONT Mary born June 11, 1712 [3] [1]; married John Matteson on July 24, 1729. [5]
2 CONT Elisha Jr. born November 25, 1713 [3] [1]; died in 1775; married ___, had issue. [5]
2 CONT Joseph born March 2, 1716[3] [1]; married Elizabeth ___. [5]
2 CONT Nathaniel born September 15, 1717 [3] [1]; died in 1802; married Elizabeth ___. [5]
2 CONT James born September 30. 1719 [3] [1]; died December 3, 1777; married Freeborne Burlingame c May, 1740. [5]
2 CONT Israel born May 15, 1721. [3] [1] [5]
2 CONT Thomas born May 25, 1724 [3] [1]; died c1779; married Abigail ___. [5]
2 CONT Hannah born March 24, 1727. [3] [1] [5]
2 CONT John born April 27, 1731 [3] [1]; died in 1792; married Deborah Matteson on November 4, 1758. [5]
