1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Samuel Gorton''' III was born on June 29, 1690 in Warwick, Rhode Island. He was the eldest of three children born to Samuel and Susannah (Burton) Gorton of Warwick. Samuel's grandfather was Samuel Gorton, the fo
2 CONC under of Warwick and the immigrant ancestor of this line of the Gorton family in America.
2 CONT
2 CONT On June 1, 1715 at the age of nearly twenty-five, Samuel married Freelove Mason, the twenty-year-old daughter of Elder Joseph and Lydia (Bowen) Mason. [Elder Joseph Mason, of Warren, R. I., mentions in his will, dated March 26, 17
2 CONC 48, his daughter, Freelove Gorton, and his granddaughter, Susannah.] Samuel and Freelove's first child, a son named Samuel (the fourth), was born on March 7, 1716/17. The couple had nine children.
2 CONT
2 CONT In The Life and Times of Samuel Gorton, Adelos Gorton relates that Samuel and Freelove moved from Warwick to Swansey, Mass, where their last five children were born. Samuel died in January, 1784, and was buried in Warwick on Janua
2 CONC ry 23, 1784 near his son, Deacon Benjamin Gorton's house. The funeral sermon was perfromed by Elder John Gorton. The inventory of Samuel's estate was filed on March 8, 1784.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes===
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel moved from Warwick to Swansey, MA where his last five children were born. He was bur., though, from his son's (Deacon Benjamin) house in Warwick, and the funeral sermon was preatch by Elder John Gorton.
2 CONT
2 CONT <Thomas Gorton>
2 CONT
2 CONT 8 Mar 1784 Inventory - shown by administrator Benjamin Gorton, 25 silver coat buttons, and 18 jacket buttons £2, 3s, wearing apparel 30s., warming pan, 2 pair of old cards, a poor old sheep, 2 cows, one of them very poor and diste
2 CONC mpered, 2 nots of hand £50, 9s., 3d., cash in gold £6, 16s., 2 continental bills, one of £80, and one of ¢ £40, out of circulation, &c.<Genealogical Dictionary of Rhode Island; Comprising 3 generations of settlers who came before 
2 CONC 1690. By Joh Osborne Austin published 1978 by Genealogical Publishing Co., Inc.>
2 CONT
