1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Obituary===
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Mr. William I. Wright, an old man and well-known resident of Mount Holly, died suddenly on Monday last, at Berlin, Camden Co., where he had gone on Friday to visit a relative. He had been preaching on Sunday morning, and at the 
2 CONC close of his discourse he sunk down insensible, and did not speak afterwards, dying Monday morning. He had been in feeble health for some time.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Mr. Wright, in early manhood, was extensively engaged in the occupation of a drover, bringing large droves of horses from the West, and disposing of them at public and private sale in Mount Holly and the surrounding country.  Ab
2 CONC out twenty-five years ago he commenced the Dry-goods business, on the West side of High street, in the store now occupied by S. Bowker, baker and confectioner, in which--aided by his wife, a lady of decided business tact and capac
2 CONC ity--he was very successful. He afterwards built the house and store now occupied by E. Holeman & Son, merchant tailors, directly opposite his former stand, where he continued his business for a few years--finally retiring with a 
2 CONC competence.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''The later years of his life were chiefly devoted to transactions in real estate, in which he also met with success. He erected a number of neat and commodious houses and cottages on Garden, Cherry and Pearl streets, in the arran
2 CONC gement of which, and especially in the decoration of the surrounding grounds, he exhibited a marked degree of taste.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''He had been for many years an active member of the Mount Holly M. E. (Methodist Episcopal) Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Parents===
2 CONT
2 CONT William is the first-born son - or at least the first we know of - of Thomas Wright, an Irish immigrant, and Rebecca Inskeep, the last posthumously-born daughter of a prominent Burlington County family.  William's middle name hark
2 CONC s back to Rebecca's birth name.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas married Rebecca in May of 1798, after arriving in February of that year, along with several dozen close relatives from County Monaghan, Ireland.  He bought land for a good price from Rebecca's brother, and he founded a char
2 CONC coal business.  Later he became an innkeeper as well - and was appointed Postmaster General for the town of Berlin.
2 CONT
2 CONT Many other early members of the town were also from Ireland and were on the same boat, including the Johnsons and the Rogers.
2 CONT
2 CONT Irish naming traditions, had they applied for Thomas's family, would dictate that the first son in the family should be named after Thomas's father George.  However, Thomas was married to a woman of English descent, so those rules
2 CONC  may not have applied.  It's also possible that a George was indeed born but did not survive.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Census===
2 CONT
2 CONT William shows up first on the 1850 census, living in Mount Holly.  One possible child living with him at that time: Alice Carr.  In 1860 he and his wife are alone.
