2 CONC r Lahaska Station. In 1709 he traded his farm for 820 acres with Jacob Holcombe. He was thought to be the first white settler in the Buckingham-Solebury valley. Part of his farm was later owned by a third great grandson, Isacc Pea
2 CONC rson Scarborough. John was a farmer and a minister. He and Mary were members of the Middletown and Fall MM. On 3 September 1705 John was condemned by the Fall MM for too much celebrating of so called Christmas the previous year. O
2 CONC n 10-2-1724 he was recorded as a minister. John and Mary were charter members of the Buckingham MM, Bucks County, where he was memorialized: "in his youth somewhat airy... a man of remarkable self-denial and endowed with much mild
2 CONC ness... with loving and kind deportment.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was buried in Buckingham FBG, Bucks County, Pa.<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT It is said he ran away from the family to which he was apprenticed and lived with the Indians for five years, and later served as William Penn's interpreter.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sources:'''
2 CONT *Title: Geneolgy print out; Author: The Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints; Publication: July 1996 (c), data as of 2 January 1996
2 CONT *Repository:  ADDR 35 N West Temple Street CONT Salt Lake City, UT 84150 USA 
2 CONT *Title: International Genealogical Index North America 
2 CONT *Title: International Genealogical Index of England 
2 CONT
2 CONT *John Scarborough II! died at age: 59 
2 CONT *Born: 10 Feb 1667 in: Hosier Lane, London, England 
2 CONT *Baptized: 26 Dec 1669 in: St. Sepulchre, Holburn Parish, London 
2 CONT *Died: 27 Jan 1727 in: Solebury, Bucks Co., Pennsylvania 
2 CONT *Buried: Jan 1727 in: Buckingham FBG, Pennsylvania 
2 CONT
2 CONT *Ref: Occupation: Farmer, Wheelwright, 
2 CONT *Spouse: Mary Pierson b. 20 June 1665 d. 13 Jan 1751 
2 CONT *Married: CA 1690 in: Delaware Co., Pennsylvania 
2 CONT *Ceremony: Divorced/Annulled/Separated: Year: Came to America with his father at Bucks Co., Pa., in 1682. Left behind with friends in 1784 by his father who went to get his wife, but did not return. 
2 CONT *John ran away and lived with the Indians for five yrs. He returned,was used as a interpreter in later years. Will was dated 13 Jan 1726 and proved 2 Oct 1727 
2 CONT *He is the Progenitor of our "Scarborough" line in America! His daughter Sarah was the 4th great grandmother of Herbert Clark Hoover. He was the 1st white man to settle in Solebury, Pennsylvania. He was also a Preacher.  {source: 
2 CONC Ronnie Lee Scarbro}
2 CONT
