1 NOTE {geni:about_me} William Scarborough BIRTH	30 Dec 1691 Middletown, Dauphin County, Pennsylvania, USA DEATH	4 Apr 1727 (aged 35) Doylestown, Bucks County, Pennsylvania, USA BURIAL	 Forest Hills Memorial Park Huntingdon Valley, Montg
2 CONC omery County, Pennsylvania, USA  MEMORIAL ID	45878521 · View Source
2 CONT
2 CONT MEMORIAL PHOTOS 0 FLOWERS 9 Turner and wheelwright. At age ten he moved from Middletown Twp. to Solebury Twp., Bucks Co. Disowned on 1 Feb. 1713 for disunity at Falls MM, Penn. In 1726 he was willed 60 acres of his father's land. 
2 CONC William Scarborough's Will wr. 27 Apr. 1727, naming his 2nd wife, Mary Scarborough, and his children, pv. 24 Sep. 1727 at Doylestown, Bucks Co., Penn. (ref: R. S. Boone, 1991)
2 CONT
2 CONT William Scarborough's sister, Sarah Scarborough married George Haworth and became the founders of the Haworth family in America. Several Haworth descendants later intermarried with Longshore descendants.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family Members Parents John Scarborough 1667–1727
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Pearson Scarborough 1676–1750
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse Alice Longshore Scarborough 1694–1747 (m. 1712)
2 CONT
2 CONT Siblings Sarah Scarborough Hall 1694–1748
2 CONT
