1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Recorded as written:
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Scarborough, b. 10 Aug. 1708; d. 19 Jan. 1805 in Union Co., Va,; inherited from his father a 157 acre farm in Solebury; sold it in 1737 and removed with wife Elizabeth (FISHER) and two children to the Shenandoah Valley, to 
2 CONC what became Hopewell Monthly Meeting. The two children were John (b. 28/11m/1734) and Mary (b. 18/9m/1736).[43] John returned to Bucks County and married Margaret KIRK at Wrightstown MM 8 May 1760. They had 7 children from whom ma
2 CONC ny of the Bucks Co. Scarboroughs are descended. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Letter written by Robert Scarborough to his brother John and wife:
2 CONT
2 CONT This comes with kind love to you and yours, and to our dear mother, and to all brothers and sisters, and to all our relations. hoping that you all are in the enjoyment of health, as we and our children are at present, thanks be to
2 CONC  God for it. We got along pretty well, are settled now on 300 acres of land. We bought ye land, being good, with good meadows, and good water, with the consent of taking up 300 acres more. And a meeting is rent [sic] about a mile 
2 CONC off, and a mill is building about as far off, and we liked ye place very well. We have bought and paid for two cows and we are in a likely way to do well by Divine assistance, yet [that] never fails them yet [that] those who trust
2 CONC  in Him. Intend to come up in the fall if health permits. My wife is desires to be remembered to her friends, which is commendable, and desires thee to get a few lines from her old neighbors, which will be very satisfactory to us.
2 CONC  So we remain your loving and well wishing brother and sister.
2 CONT         Robert Scarborough
2 CONT         Elizabeth Scarborough P.S. I received thy letter a few days ago. I also received a letter from Benjamin Fell sometime before, which said letter gave us great satisfaction to receive all your welfare. This is ye fourth lett
2 CONC er I have sent. 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~paxson/scarborough/Scarborough.index.htm
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Church: BUCKINGHAM MONTHLY MEETING Authorized Marriages, 1730-1810: Bucks County, PA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Pennsylvania Archives.  Second Series.  Vol. IX.   Published under direction of Matthew S. Quay, Secretary of the Commonwealth.   Edited by John B. Linn and Wm. H. Egle, M.D.   Harrisburg: Lane S. Hart, State Printer, 1880.   "Mar
2 CONC riages Authorized by the Buckingham Monthly Meeting of Friends, 1730-1810,"  page 249-268. BUCKINGHAM MONTHLY MEETING.   251
2 CONT
2 CONT Month	Day	Year	Surname		Given		Married
2 CONT
2 CONT 4   	11  	1787       Scarborough 	Robert     		Ann Paxson.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===========================================================
2 CONT
2 CONT  Alternate Information show death as: 19 Jan 1805  Winchester, Greenbrier Co., Shenendoah, Va  
2 CONT
2 CONT ===========================================================
2 CONT Note: Neighbors of Robert on Smith Creek were the Haworth Brothers, Absalom, Stephanua and James. Their mother was Sarah Scarborough, sister to Robert, The survey book of John Bayless gives the location of the lands of (p 191) Sca
2 CONC rboroughs and Haworths on Smith Creek and the Daniel James branch of Smith Creek. With the Haworths came their brother John Hawort, though he did not remain there permanently. This John Haworth was an ancestor to Herbert Clark Hoo
2 CONC ver, 31st President of the United States. George Haworth and Sarah Scarborough had John who with Wife Mary Garner had Rachel who with Husband Aaron Toole had Ann who with Husband Heny Wasley had Mary who with Husband Theodore Mint
2 CONC horn had Huldah who with Husband Jesse Clark Hoover had Herbert. Sources: Title: Geneolgy print out Author: The Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints Publication: July 1996 (c), data as of 2 January 1996 Repository:  Note: N
2 CONC AME Family History Library ADDR 35 N West Temple Street CONT Salt Lake City, UT 84150 USA 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT Robert was born about 1736. <ref>Entered by Bob Fields, Jan 22, 2012</ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT Found on WFT CD's
2 CONT
2 CONT occupation: farmer When Robert and Elizabeth and their family moved to Frederick Co.Virginia in 1737, they were accompanied by their nephews Stephanus, Absolom, and James Haworth. Robert was a widower by 1747 and married Mary Bail
2 CONC ey, daughter of William Bailey, about 1750. He died on 19 January, 1805, probably in Greenbrier Co. Virginia at the age of 97 years. Robert inherited a farm of 127 acres from his father in Solebury PA where he lived until 1737 at 
2 CONC which time he believed the country was becoming too crowded. He sold the farm and took his young family toFrederick Co. Virginia. He next moved to Bedford Co. by 1762 and finally he settled in the Shenandoah Valley in Virginia to 
2 CONC live in what later became Greenbrier Co. and still later, Monroe Co. West Virginia. Two children, John and Elizabeth were born in Pennsylvania. After Robert and Elizabeth arrived in Virginia, they transferred their certificates to
2 CONC  the Quaker Church at Winchester, Virginia. Robert was mentioned several times in Church records and his final location in Monroe Co.is pinpointed by these. He was apparently a friend of the Indians and was frequently asked by the
2 CONC  military for aid during troubled times. In 1762, the court ordered the Church Wardens of Russell Parish in Bedford Co. to "bind out Rachel, William, James, Kiziah and Isaac, children of Rob Scarbrough". According to law, this cou
2 CONC ld be done when parents were too poor to care for their children. In 1768, William Bailey gave a gift of love to his grandson William (1753), and in a separate action, he gave his son-in-law Robert a power of attorney to collect c
2 CONC ertain debts in 1769. Robert was declared tax-free in 1783 because of age <ref> Douglas L. Green 1604 Prince Edward Rd Richmond VA 23225</ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Robert Scarborough and Elizabeth Fisher are: :i. John7 Scarborough, born November 28, 1734. :ii. Elizabeth Scarborough, born September 18, 1736.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Robert Scarborough and Mary Bailey are: :i. Isaac7 Scarborough, born Abt. 1756.:ii. Robert Scarborough, born Abt. 1766 in Bedford Co., VA; died October 06, 1855 in Franklin co., VA. He married Mary McGuire 1785 in Fran
2 CONC klin Co.,VA. :iii. Elizabeth Scarborough.:iv. William Scarborough, born Abt. 1753 in Bedford Co., VA; died June 17, 1830 in Anderson Co., TN. He married Mahala Emily Wood. Neighbors of Robert on Smith Creek were the Haworth Brothe
2 CONC rs, Absalom, Stephanua and James. Their mother was Sarah Scarborough, sister to Robert, The survey book of John Bayless gives the location of the lands of (p 191) Scarboroughs and Haworths on Smith Creek and the Daniel James branc
2 CONC h of Smith Creek. With the Haworths came their brother John Hawort, though he did not remain there permanently. This John Haworth was an ancestor to Herbert Clark Hoover, 31st President of the United States. George Haworth and Sar
2 CONC ah Scarborough had John who with Wife Mary Garner had Rachel who with Husband Aaron Toole had Ann who with Husband Heny Wasley had Mary who with Husband Theodore Minthorn had Huldah who with Husband Jesse Clark Hoover had Herbert.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Research progress ==
2 CONT
2 CONT <b>Scarbeary Family Website</b> : http://www.scarbeary.com/family_tree
2 CONT "5. ROBERT SCARBOROUGH, son of John Scarborough and Mary ?Pierson, was born 10 June 1708, Solebury Township, Bucks County, PA, died 19 January 1805, Union County, VA; buried in what is now WV. He married 1] c 1733 Bucks County, PA
2 CONC , ELIZABETH FISHER (most records show Elizabeth Haworth) daughter of John fisher and Sarah Hutchinson. Elizabeth died c1747. Robert married 2] c1750 Mary BAILEY, daughter of William Bailey.       Robert was a farmer and in 1737 so
2 CONC ld 157 acres of the farm in Solebury Township, Bucks County, PA, which he had inherited from his father, and moved to 5 miles southwest of present New Market, Orange (now Shenandoah) County, VA. He had 400 acres on both sides of S
2 CONC mith’s Creek, joining Absalom Haworth’s land. In 1737 he moved to Winchester, VA, and in 1747/50 (sic) moved to Bedford County, VA. Robert and several of his younger children moved to Greenbrier County, VA and he is believed to ha
2 CONC ve died there in 1805. He was a Quaker with membership at Hopewell MM, Frederick County, VA.  Robert and Elizabeth had issue:  i. JOHN SCARBOROUGH, b 11-28-1734, d 1813, m1] 5 May 1960 MARGARET KIRK, m2] JOHANNA (----) CAHOON. Joh
2 CONC n was a veteran of the Revolutionary War (SQF, vol 1, p24)  ii. ELIZABETH SCARBOROUGH, b 18 Sep 1736 Solebury Township, Buck County, PA. Robert and Mary Bailey had issue: 
2 CONT
2 CONT iii. WILLIAM SCARBOROUGH, 1753-1830, m EMILY WOOD 
2 CONT
2 CONT iv. JAMES SCARBOROUGH, 1755-1809, m RACHEL WOOD 
2 CONT
2 CONT v. SARAH SCARBOROUGH, m JAMES CHRISTY  vi. DAVID SCARBOROUGH, 1760- , m 3 May 1786 Greenbrier, VA (now WV), ELIZABETH ANDERSON  vii. ISAAC SCARBOROUGH, b bef 1762 in VA, m MARY WARD, dau of John Ward  viii. RACHEL (probably KEZIAH
2 CONC ) SCARBOROUGH b bef 1762, m 9 Sep 1791, JAMES KENNEDY  ix. SUSANNAH SCARBOROUGH, b aft 1765, VA, m 22 Mar 1787, Bedford County, VA, JOHN SMITH  x. ELIZABETH SCARBOROUGH, b in VA, m 22 Oct, Bedford County, VA, JAMES JOHNSON  xi. (6
2 CONC ) ROBERT SCARBOROUGH, b c1766 Bedford Co, VA, d c1840 MO; m1] 28 Nov 1785, Bedford Co, VA, MARY McGUIRE, m2] 29 Aug 1793 Franklin Co, VA, CATHERINE BEHELER"
2 CONT
