1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From these entries, one could assume that Isaac and Sidney had marital problems, Isaac was blamed and disowned. He moves out and takes Solomon with him. Sidney appeals to the church for custody of Solomon and gets 
2 CONC it. By the family not reporting Isaac's death, complete alienation, is suggested.
2 CONT Sidney (Rogers) Wright Pickering
2 CONT Her first husband is Isaac Wright and after his passing, she married Isaac Pickering. In her will which is shone here, it names her children and other family members.
2 CONT Her children are:
2 CONT John
2 CONT James
2 CONT Edward
2 CONT Nathan
2 CONT Solomon
2 CONT A minister in Buckingham MM, aged 77 years
2 CONT I found a record from, "Dr· Samuel Worchester Butler" that mentions her as a "minister" and passing in Bucks Co. aged near 85 years
2 CONT In total, 2 records found for 77 years of age and one at 85.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/81622844/sidney-pickering Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Apr 3 20
