2 CONT
2 CONT ==links==
2 CONT * http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=5043148
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT '''Wells/Gunter Family: Information about Benjamin Pickering'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Benjamin Pickering (son of Samuel Pickering and Grace Stackhouse) was born Jul 07, 1752 in Bucks, Pennsylvania, and died Jan 27, 1807 in New Hope, Tennessee.He married Rebeckah Ellis on Oct 18, 1775 in Fredrick, Virginia, daughter
2 CONC  of Enos Ellis and Elizabeth Colson.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Includes NotesNotes for Benjamin Pickering:
2 CONT
2 CONT "In the Name of God Amen; Whereas I Benjamin Pickering of Greene County and State of Tennessee Being weak in health but sound in Memory & understanding thanks be to Almighty God for it, Do make and Constitute this my last will and
2 CONC  Testament my body I Recommend to the Earth to be Buried In a Christian like manner at the Discresion of my Executor and as touching my wordly Estate I give and Demise and disolve in the following Manner first, that all my Just de
2 CONC bts & funeral Charges shall be paid I give to my Several Sons Samuel, Ellis, Enos, Benjamin, Jonathan, and John, the sum of five Dollars to Each & Every of them and to my Daughters Rebeckah, Mary and Elizabeth five Dollars Each to
2 CONC  be paid in two years after my Decease to as many of said Legatees as Shall be then arrived to the Lawful age of an Heir and to be paid to the Rest as they arrive at the age Aforsaid to be Raised and Levied out of my Estate and Di
2 CONC scharged in Good trade. And all the Remainder of my Real and Moveable Estate I give Demise and Beaqueat th my well Beloved wife Rebeckah to be in her actual possession *& after my Decease to Sell & Convey the sam as She Shall See 
2 CONC Cause and also I Constitute make and ordain her my said wife to be my Sole & absolute Executrix of the my Last will and Testament and I do hereby Revoke Disalow and Disanul all & Every other testament, Wills, Legaues, bequests and
2 CONC  Executors by me in any wise Named willed and bequeathed Ratifying and confirming this and not other to be my last will and testament.In witness whereof I have hereunto set my hand and seal this Second Day of the Eight month One t
2 CONC housand Eight hundred and six. Benjamin Pickering Signed Sealed & pronounced by me the said Benjamin Pickering as my last will and testament in the presence of John Jones Ellis Ellis"
2 CONT * illegible
2 CONT
2 CONT More About Benjamin Pickering:
2 CONT
2 CONT Will: Aug 02, 1806 More About Benjamin Pickering and Rebeckah Ellis: Marriage: Oct 18, 1775, Fredrick, Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Benjamin Pickering and Rebeckah Ellis are:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Samuel Pickering, b. Jul 25, 1776, Fredrick, Virginia, d. Apr 30, 1829, Greene County, Tennessee.
2 CONT * Grace Pickering, b. Feb 28, 1778, Fredrick, Virginia, d. date unknown.
2 CONT * Elizabeth Pickering, b. May 07, 1791, Fredrick, Virginia, d. Jul 06, 1857, Greene County, Tennessee.
2 CONT * +Ellis Pickering, b. Jan 23, 1780, Fredrick, Virginia, d. Feb 22, 1836, Rheatown, Tennessee.
2 CONT * Thomas Pickering, b. Dec 15, 1781, Fredrick, Virginia, d. Aug 02, 1806.
2 CONT * Enos Pickering, b. Apr 01, 1783, Berkley, Virginia, d. date unknown.
2 CONT * Rebecca Pickering, b. Mar 10, 1785, Fredrick, Virginia, d. 1826, Greene County, Tennessee.
2 CONT * Mary Pickering, b. Oct 07, 1787, Fredrick, Virginia, d. date unknown.
2 CONT * Benjamin Pickering, b. Jul 28, 1789, Fredrick, Virginia, d. date unknown.
2 CONT * Jonathan Pickering, b. Nov 08, 1793, Fredrick, Virginia, d. date unknown.
2 CONT * John Pickering, b. Oct 05, 1795, Fredrick, Virginia, d. date unknown.
2 CONT * Hannah Pickering, b. Dec 22, 1798, Fredrick, Virginia, d. Sep 18, 1799.
2 CONT
