2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT (Research):«b»Benjamin Pickering«/b» (Samuel, Jr., Samuel, Sr., Jonathan, John) born July 7, 1752 in Bucks County, Pennsylvania; died January 27, 1807 in New Hope, Greene County, Tennessee; married October 18, 1775 at Hopewell Mee
2 CONC ting House, Frederick Co, VA to Rebecca Ellis who was born September 22, 1753 in Bucks County the daughter of Enos and Elizabeth (Coleson) Ellis; died December 22, 1836 Greene County, Tennessee. Benjamin moved with his parents to 
2 CONC Frederick County, Virginia. In 1794, Benjamin and Rebecca moved to Greene County, Tennessee at about the same time as did many of their friends and relatives from the Quaker settlements in Virginia and North Carolina. Much of the 
2 CONC land purchased by the Quakers was part of a 25,000 acre land grant to General Nathaniel Greene for his service in the Revolutionary War. Their settlement was established around New Hope Meeting House, named after the original chur
2 CONC ch in Bucks County. It was located near Rheatown on what was then known as McCartney's Knobbs but soon became better known as the Quaker Knobbs.
2 CONT
2 CONT From a Biography of Benjamin Pickering (1752-1807), it is noted that he was the 3rd of 12 children.
