1 NOTE Quaker notes:
2 CONT 1. The Baltimore Yearly Meeting, which included the Hopewell Meeting, was very anti-slavery. Information from the Baltimore Yearly Meeting webpage, (http://www.bym-rsf.org/quakers/history.shtml#scr).
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Ann Lupton-Udegraff
2 CONT Ann Lupton married Nathan Updegraff who was apparently a strong supporter of rights for African Americans. (http://books.google.com/books?id=NPaBPe6wPfcC&pg=PA226&dq=quaker+slavery+lupton&as_brr=0&sig=McrShMDHSVyvBCy24xXH5D6YVME#P
2 CONC PA227,M1)
2 CONT
2 CONT See: Ohio's Founding Fathers, Fred J. Milligan, FHL 977.1 D3mf
