1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/58610986/isaac-george
2 CONT
2 CONT ''''''Biography'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ISAAC GEORGE, born Apr. 15, 1796, in Hampshire Co., Va. (now West Va.) died Aug. 24, 1829 near Camby, Marion Co., Ind. Married Anna Sumner, born Apr. 1, 1803, at Westfield, Stokes Co., N.C., daughter of Joseph and Abigail Jessup S
2 CONC umner, and the granddaughter of Thomas and Hannah Hiatt Sumner. The Hiatts came to Philadelphia with William Penn on his second voyage. They were supposed to have come to England from France in 1066. Anna Sumner's brother, Martin 
2 CONC Sumner was the great-grandfather of George W. Moore of Seattle, Wash., who has provided all of this information. After the death of Isaac George, Anna married John Cook.Children of Isaac and Anna Sumner George were: Abigail, Sidne
2 CONC y, Evan, and Adin. 
2 CONT ==========
2 CONT Isaac George
2 CONT b. April 15, 1796. m. 1821, Anna Sumner, b. April 1, 1803, Surry Co. N.C., dau. of Joseph & Abigail ( Jessup) Sumner. The family relocated from Fall Creek MM, Ohio to White Lick MM, Indiana in 1824.; Isaac d. September 21, 1829, a
2 CONC ge 33 years, 5 months & 9 days. Burial was at Fairfield Quaker cemetery, Hendricks co., Indiana. Anna m. 2nd., John Cook, November 20, 1824, at Fall Creek MM, Highland co., Ohio. gct White Lick MM, Morgan co., Indiana, rcd Decembe
2 CONC r 11, 1824; charter mbr Fairfield MM, Hendricks co., Indiana. October 16, 1851 granted cert. of transfer to Spring Creek MM, Mahaska co., Iowa. Anna d. September 1, 1869 at home of her son, Martin Cook, at Erlham, Madison co., Iow
2 CONC a. Burial was in the Bear Creek FBG, Dallas, co., Iowa.
2 CONT
