1 OCCU Blacksmith
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Information taken from entry for Adelma Lupton: (Joseph's son)
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the eldest son of Joseph A. and Abagail (Green) Lupton. His father was a native of Highland county Ohio and his mother was born in New Jersey. The family, consisting of five, located in Pennville in 1838. His father followe
2 CONC d his trade, that of blacksmith, being the first blacksmith in the village or in Jay county. His father continued the business until his death in 1870. Adelma Lupton was a lad of seven years when he came with his parents to Jay co
2 CONC unty, hence it may be said that his entire life was spent here except a few years of babyhood and early youth. His earlier years were spent as an assistant in his father's shop and in traveling over the country selling cow bells a
2 CONC nd mattocks made by his father. There being but little money, these commodities were exchanged for hides and furs. In this way the habits of shrewd trading which stood him so well in his dealings with men were early firmly fixed. 
2 CONC He afterward worked by the day or by the month until seventeen when he began a four years apprenticeship to the blacksmith's trade in his father's shop. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Source''': Biographical Memoirs of Jay County, Indiana:Chicago B.F. Bowen Company Publishers; 1901; pg. 330
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Link''': https://books.google.com/books?id=Rk80AQAAMAAJ&printsec=frontcover&dq=biographical+memoirs+of+jay+county&hl=en&sa=X&ved=
2 CONT
2 CONT ____________________________________________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Find A Grave Memorial'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Lupton married Pheobe 29 July 1855 and they had a son named Francis "Frank" Lupton who was born in abt 1857. Francis married Pricilla Lanning and they had 3 children in Jay county Indiana. Francis appears in the 1930 census
2 CONC  in Jay county. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage: 1830, Champaign Co, Ohio to Abigail Green
2 CONT
2 CONT Children from this marriage: Ruth Ann, Adelma, Solomon A, Rachael, John
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage: to Leah Hyatt, 10 Nov 1851, Camden, Jay Co, Illinois; Children: Abigail, Margaret
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage: 1856 to Phoebe Higgins, no children
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: Solomon Lupton 1780-1848 Mother: Rachel Wood 1780-1746 
2 CONT
