1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From LUPTON/DODSON RESEARCH:
2 CONT
2 CONT "Allen Lupton was the only one of his father's family living in Tippecanoe Co., Indiana in 1888, and is numbered among the leading citizens of Sheffield Co. He grew to manhood on the old homestead and was educated in the schools o
2 CONC f Wyandotte. He participated in the raid after the rebel General Morgan. He married Mrs. Sarah (Graham) Peppin, a native of Ind., and this union was blessed with two sons, Mark and Arthur. By her first marriage Mrs. Lupton had fou
2 CONC r daughters, Ella, Nancy, Flora and Lillie. Mr. Lupton lived on the old Peppin homestead of 152 acres, well-improved, a substantial two-story residence, built 1876, a good barn and other valuable improvements. In politics he is a 
2 CONC Democrat. He has served his township as a trustee for four years, which office he filled to the entire satisfaction of his constituents. He was a man of gentle disposition and cordial manners, and honorable in all his dealings, an
2 CONC d has gained the confidence and respect of the entire community where he has spent his entire life."  Allen was a trustee of the Sheffield Methodist Episcopal Church 1878-1882. Siblings of Allen, I have Mary, married Dodson, possi
2 CONC bly Peter, and have seen others listing Emeline.
2 CONT
