0 @I6000000064951891081@ INDI
1 NAME Hannah /Pickering/
2 GIVN Hannah
2 SURN Pickering
2 _MARNM Holmes
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 27 OCT 1827
2 ADDR
3 STAE Virginia
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 15 FEB 1904
2 ADDR
3 CITY Atalissa
3 STAE Iowa
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT per Find A Grave Memorial; Created by: L. Forbes Record added: Sep 16, 2015  Find A Grave Memorial# 152375408
2 CONT
2 CONT In Muscatine County, in 1844, our subject was united in marriage with Hannah Pickering, daughter of Benjamin and Mary ( Lupton ) Pickering, who were both natives of Virginia, and members of the Society of Friends. The family were 
2 CONC of English origin, the founders of the family emigrating to this country prior to the Revolutionary War. Mrs. Holmes was also born in Virginia, but was reared in Ohio. Her father was a millwright by trade, and came to Iowa in 1842
2 CONC , settling upon the farm of our subject. Mr. Holmes soon after erected a house for them, into which the family moved, but later they went to Henry County, Iowa, where Mr. Pickering died some years ago. By the union of Mr. and Mr. 
2 CONC Holmes ten children have been born, seven of whom are living : Sarah Adelaide, now Mrs. Rock, resides in Wapsinonoc Township ; Margaret A., is a graduate of the Female Seminary at Mt. Carroll, Ill., and has for the last ten years 
2 CONC followed the profession of school teacher with marked success. She also possesses natural artistic taste and talent, and, though only an amateur, has produced a number of fine landscapes in oil. 
2 CONT
2 CONT W.G. Jr., is residing with his parents; Mary Bell, who was the wife of Winfield Elliott, died in June, 1886 ; John is single and resides at home ; Lydia Almina, now Mrs. Noble, is living in Monro, Wis.; Frank Byron and Lillie Iren
2 CONC e are also at home ; Benjamin F. died at the age of two years and two months, and Ida died at the age of two years. Mrs. Holmes has two sisters living in Henry County, Mrs. A. Beason and Mrs. C. Tyrrell, and one sister, Mrs. S. Br
2 CONC own, living in Lexington, Ohio.
2 CONT ------------
2 CONT Source: History of Muscatine County Iowa, Volume II, Biographical, 1911, page 334.. EDWARD ROCK.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Link''': https://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=152375408
2 CONT
2 CONT D. Glenn 2017
