2 DATE ABT 1853
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1914
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mrs. Anna Yancey Morris, (1850-1914) beloved wife of H. H. Morris, died at her home in New Castle, on Sunday, September 20, 1914, at 4 p.m., after an illness of eight weeks during which she endured much suffering.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Morris was a  daughter of John Yancey, a member of a leading Kentucky family, but spent the early part of her life in Missouri, to which state her father moved when she was quite young.  Twenty-seven years ago she was married
2 CONC  to Mr. Morris, and during the greater part of the time she has lived in New Castle.  Her age was about 56 years.  She was the mother of only one child, a most devoted daughter, Mrs. Nell Holland, wife of J. A. Holland of this pla
2 CONC ce.  Besides Mrs. Holland, she is survived by her husband and two stepsons, Joseph W. and Mervin L. Morris, both of this place.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services were conducted at the house, Tuesday afternoon at 2 o’clock, by her pastor Mr. W. C. Foster, of the Christian Church, assisted by Mr. B. O. Beck, of the Methodist Church.  Interment was in the New Castle Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry County Local  September 25, 1914
