1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Cantrell-3243
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary (Cantrell) Thomas (abt. 1728 - bef. 1793)
2 CONT Born about 1728 [uncertain] in Pennsylvania 
2 CONT Died before 10 Jan 1793 before about age 65 in Hardy, Virginia, United States
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of Joseph Cantrell  and Catherine (Unknown) Cantrell 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sister of James Cantrell, Hannah (Cantrill) Cantrell, Sarah Cantrell, John Cantrell Sr, Stephen Cantrell, Joseph Cantrell, Zebulon Cantrell, Alice Cantrell, Unknown Cantrell, Benjamin Cantrell and Isaac Cantrell Sr
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of Morris Thomas — married about 1750 in Chester County, Pennsylvania map icon at age 22
2 CONT Mother of Joseph Thomas , Hannah (Thomas) Parsons , John Thomas  , Rachel (Thomas) Denny and David Thomas
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Cantrell married Morris Thomas; She was b. 173 abt. - d. 1790 abt. She was born in Pennsylvania and her death was in Hardy county, Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Morris & Mary (Cantrell) Thomas lived on the Pennsylvania/Delware border county until shortly before Aug 1777 when they moved to Hampshire (now Hardy) Co., Va.(West Virginia)
2 CONT
2 CONT An adjoining land owner in Hampshire Co who bought & sold land with Morris Thomas was Christopher Cantrell. QUESTION - who is he?
2 CONT
2 CONT The only sibling of Mary (Cantrell) Thomas that we can document is Sarah Cantrell b 11 Apr 1736 & bapt David & Sarah (Cantrell) Miles - her sister moved to Hampshire / Hardy Co., Virgina with the Morris Thomas family.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Mary Cantrel alias Thomas" was baptized Oct 6, 1744" at the Welsh Tract Baptist Meeting.[1] It's location is described as "Nestled at the foot of Iron Hill, at the headwaters of the Christiana, is the Welsh Tract Baptist Meeting 
2 CONC House."[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1787, Mary was mentioned in the Last Will and Testament of Morris Thomas (1718-abt.1795) in Hardy County, Virginia.[3][4]
2 CONT
2 CONT From Genealogy.com Message Board Post
2 CONT by Anne Baker 2013
2 CONT
2 CONT Morris married Mary Cantrell, who was baptized in the Baptist faith just after her marriage: 'Welsh Tract Baptist Meeting, Pencader Hundred, New Castle Co., Delaware:
2 CONT p. 52 - Mary Cantrell now Thomas was baptized 6 Oct 1744.'
2 CONT
2 CONT Morris seems to have gotten into a snit with the local Baptist church and moved his family over to what would become Hardy Co., VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Most of the children of Morris & Mary (Cantrell) Thomas moved to Mercer Co., KY., where they became influential Kentucky pioneers. The first to move to KY in the 1780's was son John Thomas, b. 1752 in Chester Co., PA & d. 2 Mar 18
2 CONC 14 in Mercer Co, KY. He was appointed the first surveyor in the then vast Lincoln Co., KY (his home fell in Mercer when it was cut from Lincoln). His surveyor book has survived - his drawn survey plats and the written calls are ab
2 CONC solutely beautiful - showing he had an rigorous and extensive education.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
