1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A Patriot of the American Revolution for VIRGINIA.  [https://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A113105  DAR Ancestor # A113105]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Detached from https://www.geni.com/people/Daniel-Thomas/6000000002759860335?through=6000000041134994570 and https://www.geni.com/people/Catherine-Thomas/6000000006598726688?through=6000000041134994570 based on the following:
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Thomas-23630
2 CONT
2 CONT Morris Thomas (1718 - abt. 1795)
2 CONT Born 23 Apr 1718 in Philadelphia, Philadelphia, Pennsylvania 
2 CONT Died about 1795 [uncertain] at about age 76 in Hardy, Virginia, United States
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Mary (Cantrell) Thomas — married about 1750 in Chester County, Pennsylvania map icon at age 31
2 CONT
2 CONT Father of Joseph Thomas , Hannah (Thomas) Parsons , John Thomas  , Rachel (Thomas) Denny and David Thomas
2 CONT
2 CONT '''This Morris Thomas NEEDS to be removed as a child of Daniel Thomas -'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Morris's father, Rev. Owen Thomas was born Gwrogodlly, Cilmanllwyd, Pembroke, Wales in 1692, he died in Chester Co, PA November 12, 1760.
2 CONT
2 CONT Morris Thomas, the son of Rev. Owen and Eleanor Thomas of Chester County, Pennsylvania, was born in Pennsylvania about 1727.
2 CONT
2 CONT Morris married Mary Cantrell b. 173 abt. - d. 1790 abt. She was born in Pennsylvania and her death was in Hardy county, Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Morris's will was dated September 9, 1795, he died January 13, 1796 in Hardy County, VA. I believe he owned property in Hardy County, VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT All of Morris and Mary's children were born in Pennsylvania. Morris and Mary had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth; Hannah; Owen; Sarah; Susannah;
2 CONT
2 CONT John, died March 2, 1814 in KY.;
2 CONT
2 CONT Rachel born 1758 in PA, married May 14, 1778 Frederick Co., VA died November 12, 1808 in Mercer Co. KY; Rachel married Robert Denny they moved to Lincoln Co, now Mercer, Kentucky about 1790;
2 CONT
2 CONT Elisha, born September 22, 1762, died October 5, 1856, Mercer Co., KY;
2 CONT
2 CONT David, born May 23, 1767, died January 28, 1852 in Clay County, IN;
2 CONT
2 CONT Oswald, born September 10, 1769, died August 12, 1835 in Shelby County, KY."
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT http://genforum.genealogy.com/thomas/messages/19279.html
2 CONT "Owen & wife Eleanor both left wills in the 1760's in Chester Co., Penn naming among others these children:
2 CONT
2 CONT (1) Morris - presumed to be eldest son
2 CONT
2 CONT (2) Elizabeth, wife of Joseph Thomas. (Who were the parents of this Joseph Thomas? Were they first cousins? What happened to Elizabeth Thomas & Joseph Thomas??)
2 CONT
2 CONT (3) Son David Thomas. (Which David is he????)
2 CONT
2 CONT Morris married Mary Cantrell, who was baptized in the Baptist faith just after her marriage:
2 CONT
2 CONT 'Welsh Tract Baptist Meeting, Pencader Hundred, New Castle Co., Delaware:
2 CONT
2 CONT p. 52 - Mary Cantrell now Thomas was baptized 6 Oct 1744.'
2 CONT
2 CONT Morris seems to have gotten into a snit with the local Baptist church and moved his family over to what would become Hardy Co., VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Most of the children of Morris & Mary (Cantrell) Thomas moved to Mercer Co., KY., where they became influential Kentucky pioneers. The first to move to KY in the 1780's was son John Thomas, b. 1752 in Chester Co., PA & d. 2 Mar 18
2 CONC 14 in Mercer Co, KY. He was appointed the first surveyor in the then vast Lincoln Co., KY (his home fell in Mercer when it was cut from Lincoln). His surveyor book has survived - his drawn survey plats and the written calls are ab
2 CONC solutely beautiful - showing he had an rigorous and extensive education.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth & Rachel Thomas (daughters of Morris & Mary) married Dennys from Chester Co., PA. They also became the guardians of their sister Hannah (Thomas) McAchran Parsons' 4 children & brought them to Mercer Co., KY.
2 CONT
2 CONT These Mercer Co., KY children of Morris and Mary always considered David Thomas (1732-1816 Jessamine Co., Ky.) who moved with, them to be the younger Brother of their father Morris. . . .
2 CONT
2 CONT WILL OF MORRIS THOMAS OF HARDY COUNTY, VIRGINIA.
2 CONT In the name of God Amen this 13th Day of February in the year of our Lord one Thousand Seven Hundred and Eighty Seven
2 CONT
2 CONT I, Morris Thomas of the County Hardy in the State of Virginia being aged and weak of Body, but of perfect mind and Memory, thanks be given unto God; Therefore calling unto mind the mortality of my Body and knowing that it is appoi
2 CONC nted for all men once to die do make and ordain this my last Will and Testament: That is say principally and first of all I give and recommend my Soul unto God Almighty that gave it; and for my body I commend it to the earth to be
2 CONC  buried in a Christian like decent manner at the direction of my Executor not douting but at the general resurrection I Shall receive the same again by the mighty power of God - And as touching such worldly estate wherewith it has
2 CONC  pleased God to bles one in this life
2 CONT
2 CONT I give devise and dispose of the estate in the following manner and form -
2 CONT
2 CONT After my Just debts and funeral Expenses are paid I give and bequeath to Mary my Dearly beloved Wife one third of my personal Estate to her, her heirs, and assigns and also one third of the yearly value of what my land and preimes
2 CONC is will Rent for during her life time -
2 CONT
2 CONT Next I give and bequeath to my beloved grand children begoten of the body of my Daughter Hannah deceased the full sum of ten pound Virginia Money to be Equally divided unto them to be paid two years after my Death,
2 CONT
2 CONT Next I give and bequeath to my beloved Daughter Elizabeth Deny [Denny] the full Sum of ten pounds Virginia Money to be paid two years after my Death,
2 CONT
2 CONT Next I give and bequeath to my beloved Daughter Sarah Mars [Marrs] the full sum of five pounds Virginia Money to be paid two years after my Death,
2 CONT
2 CONT Next I give and bequeath to my beloved Daughter Racela Deny [Rachel Denny] the full sum of Seven pounds ten shilling Virginia Money to be paid two years after my Death,
2 CONT
2 CONT Next I give and bequeath to my beloved daughter Susanah Thomas the full sum of Thirty pounds Virginia Money to be paid to two years after my death,
2 CONT
2 CONT Next I give and bequeath to my beloved Son Elisha Thomas the full sum of six shillings Virginia Money to be paid two years after my Death,
2 CONT
2 CONT Next I give and bequeath to my beloved Son John Thomas the full Sum of thirty pounds Virginia Money to be paid two years after my Death with lawful Interest,
2 CONT
2 CONT Next I give and bequeath to my beloved Son David Thomas the full sum of Twenty five pounds Virginia Money to be paid two years after my death,
2 CONT
2 CONT Next I give to my beloved son Oswald Thomas the full sum of Ten pounds Virginia Money to be paid two years after my death,
2 CONT
2 CONT Last of all I give and bequeath to my beloved Son Owen Thomas whom I likewise constitute make and Ordain my only and Sole executor of this my last will and Testament all and and singluar my goods chattels Land and Tanement to him 
2 CONC his Heirs and assigns. he paying the above Legacies and providing for his Mother Diet and Loging and the keeping for her one cow and horse.
2 CONT
2 CONT And I do hereby utterly Revoke and Disanulall and every other former testaments will and Legacies requests and Executors by me in any way before this time named willed and bequeathed ratifying and confirming this and no other to b
2 CONC e my Last will and Testament. In witness whereof I have hereunto set my hand and seal the Day and year above wirtten.
2 CONT
2 CONT Morris Thomas
2 CONT
2 CONT Signed sealed published and declared ye said Morris Thomas as his last will and Testament in ye presence of us ye subscribers:
2 CONT
2 CONT David Miles James Miles Randolph X Buzard
2 CONT
2 CONT Paid and advanced for my son John Thomas to Robert Deny [Denny] the sum of seventeen pound, ten shillings which sum I reduct out of his beguest which I bequeathed to him in this will as witness my hand this 4th day of April 1787.
2 CONT
2 CONT Morris Thomas
2 CONT
2 CONT Testes: Anthony Baker
2 CONT
2 CONT A [????] and a Reform to a Will made and perfected the thirteenth day of February in the year one thousand seven hundred and eighty seven - Whereas I gave and Bequeathed to my then beloved wife who is since Dead therefore the whol
2 CONC e bequest there granted to her I do give and bequeath to my beloved son Owen Thomas and likewise disanul the bequest given and granted unto my beloved son David Thomas being twenty pound five or five and twenty pound and in stood 
2 CONC of that bequest I give and allow his bequest to be Equal to my Executor only one sixth less of the whole Sum of my Executor share of the estate
2 CONT
2 CONT And also I Disanul the bequest given and granted unto my beloved Daughter Susannah Thomas which is thirty pounds and insteed and insteed of that bequest I give grant and bequeath that her share of the estate be equal with my Execu
2 CONC tor only one tenth less than my Executor share of the Estate.
2 CONT
2 CONT I ad also six pounds unto my son John Thomas bequest which ?? the sum of 36 pounds Exceping the sum of seventeen pounds, ten shillings which I advanced for him to Robert Deny -
2 CONT
2 CONT Given under my hand and seal this tenth Day January one thousand seven hundred and ninety three.
2 CONT
2 CONT Morris Thomas
2 CONT
2 CONT Signed sealed and pronounce in the Presence of us
2 CONT
2 CONT David Miles James Miles Randolph X Buzard
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT AT a court held for Hardy County the 13th day of January 1796.
2 CONT
2 CONT This last will and Testament of Morris Thomas dec'd was this day proved by the oath of David Miles, James Miles and Rudolph Buzzard the witnesses thereto, and is ordered to be recorded and on the motion of Owen Thomas who made oat
2 CONC h thereto according to Law the executor therein named certificate is granted him for obtaining a probate thereof in due form Giving Security Whereupon he with security entered unto and acknowledged a bond in the penalty of fifteen
2 CONC  Hundred dollars constituted as the Law Directs."
2 CONT
2 CONT He passed away in 13 January 1796.
2 CONT
