1 NOTE {geni:about_me} James Henry Montgomery BIRTH	7 Oct 1833 Kentucky, USA DEATH	6 Mar 1908 (aged 74) Parke County, Indiana, USA BURIAL	 Adams Cemetery Jessup, Parke County, Indiana, USA 
2 CONT
2 CONT MEMORIAL ID	74786943 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/74786943/james-henry-montgomery
2 CONT
2 CONT Rockville Tribune, March 11, 1908
2 CONT
2 CONT OBITUARY
2 CONT
2 CONT JAMES HENRY MONTGOMERY
2 CONT
2 CONT "Blessed are the dead who die in the Lord from henceforth; and their works do follow them."
2 CONT
2 CONT James Henry Montgomery was born October 7, 1833, near Lexington, Kentucky. He came with his parents and three brothers to Parke county at an early age and located at Jessup, they and two brothers having preceded him to the Great B
2 CONC eyond.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was united in marriage to Rachel Barnes Evans, August 6, 1855, and to this union seven children were born, all of whom, with their mother and one brother survive him. He was a good husband, a loving father and a kind brother. H
2 CONC e was of a jovial and pleasant disposition, always ready to make peace. "Blessed are the peace-makers, for they shall be called the children of God." He united with the Liberty Baptist church, to which he lived a consistent member
2 CONC . He was looking forward in anticipation to the time of only two weeks when he was to be moved to his son John's but was stricken with the fatal malady which ended his earthly career March 6, 1908; aged 74 years, 4 months and 29 d
2 CONC ays. He bore his sufferings with great patience, and was often times heard saying: "Oh, Lord have mercy upon me." He requested that his children all pray for him which they did by kneeling at his bedside. He is gone, but fond memo
2 CONC ries of him shall ever be cherished. He leaves an aged wife, seven children and one brother of his immediately family, besides several grandchildren and a host of relatives and friends to mourn their loss.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services were conducted at the church by Rev. Vancleave and Rev. Adams, Sunday morning, attended by a large concourse of relatives and friends, after which the remains were laid to rest in the Forks of the Creek cemetery, 
2 CONC awaiting the resurrection morn.
2 CONT
2 CONT Tribune, March 11, 1908, page 5
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Joey Hawkins was called to Terre Haute last week to the bedside of her father, James H. Montgomery, who was dangerously sick, and on Friday night his spirit passed away. Mr. Montgomery was formerly a resident of Parke county,
2 CONC  but had resided at Terre Haute for the past sixteen years. He was in every sense a good man and was highly respected by all, and especially loved by his family and friends.
2 CONT
2 CONT His remains were brought to Liberty Baptist church, near Jessup, on Sunday, and Rev. W. H. Vancleave, of Rockville, preached an able funeral sermon, while Rev. Silas Adams, of Jessup, an old friend of the deceased, passed a few wo
2 CONC rds of eulogy which were sincere, beautiful and touching. All that was mortal of James H. Montgomery was then taken to Friendly Grove cemetery nearby and placed at rest. The large crowd in attendance gave evidence of the deepo est
2 CONC eem in which Mr. Montgomery was held. Many handsome floral poieces were received. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The deceased is survived by his wife and seven grown children, all of whom were poresent and administered to him in his last hours. The children are Mrs. Herman Gates, Terre Haute; Mrs. Irwin Stone, Rosedale; Mrs. Joey Hawkins, Br
2 CONC idgeton; Mrs. James H. Pendergast, Terre Haute; Smith Montgomery, Rockville; John Montgomery, Mecca, and M. O. Montgomery, of Dayton, Ohio. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Besides the immediately family, those who accompanied the funeral party to Jessup were: Mrs. Mark Dean and daughter Miss Anna; Mrs. Anna Montgomery and Messrs Cleve and Mason Montgomery, of Eaton, Ohio; Ray Montgomery of Lexington
2 CONC , Kentucky; Tony Pendergast, Fairbury, Ill., and Mrs. Bryce Burton, Danville, Ill.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children Naomi Susan Montgomery Gates* 1855–1942
2 CONT
2 CONT Margaret Belle Montgomery Pendergast* 1858–1946
2 CONT
2 CONT John Henry Montgomery* 1863–1928
2 CONT
2 CONT Minnie Montgomery Stone* 1866–1949
2 CONT
2 CONT Smith E. Montgomery* 1868–1952
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents
2 CONT
2 CONT Caleb Montgomery 1811–1881
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah Hurst Montgomery 1809–1893
