1 NOTE {geni:about_me} possible, but not confirmed
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Born about 1590 (based on date of marriage and date of father's marriage), son of John and Cicely (Reeve) Feake. London Goldsmith  who came to Massachusetts Bay in 1633. First settled in Lynn; moved to Sandwich in 1639, & Newtown 
2 CONC (Long Island) by 1656. Died after 24 September 1657 (date of will) and before 2 April 1658 (date of judgment).  Married: (1) St. Saviour's, Southwark, Surrey, 22 January 1615/6 (lic.) Jane Woolstone; d. after 1633. 
2 CONT    (2) by 1657 Joanna (_____) Wheeler, widow of _____ Wheeler. HENRY FEAKE was second cousin of ROBERT FEAKE of Watertown, and of Robert's brother James, whose children Judith and Tobias also came to New England at a later date. T
2 CONC he gap in the records for Henry Feake from 1623 to 1630 should be a subject for future research; he may have been in a London parish whose records are lost. Since he had a child baptized in London in June 1633, but was made a free
2 CONC man in New England in May 1634, he must have arrived to New England in the fall of 1633, perhaps in the Griffin, which left England in July of that year.
2 CONT * Reference: [https://old.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=35813924 Find A Grave Memorial] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Aug 7 2018, 21:09:01 UTC''
