1 NOTE {geni:about_me} William Hallett, a son of William and Elizabeth (Fones) [Winthrop] 
2 CONT
2 CONT {Feake} Hallett, was born about 1648 in New York and died August 18, 1729 in  Newtown, Queens County, New York. His will is dated September 16, 1727 and Endorsed on August 23, 1729.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Sarah Woolsey December 1, 1669 in Queens County. Sarah, a daughter of George and Rebecca (Cornell) Woolsey, was born August 3, 1650 in Flushing, Queens County, and died after 1700. William's second wife was Mary ---/ He
2 CONC  married Ruth February 1, 1692/93 in New York.
2 CONT
2 CONT William Hallett's Will:
2 CONT
2 CONT In the name of God, Amen. I, WILLIAM HALLETT, of Hellgate Neck, in Newtown, Queens County, being very infirm and weak. 
2 CONT
2 CONT I leave to my son Joseph ''(my eldest son now living),'' all my houses, lands, tenements, and meadows, with all improvements, situate at Hellgate Neck. Beginning at a great Rock in the valley of the southwest of the Ridge, and ran
2 CONC ging from the rock south easterly 40 Degrees, to a certain marked tree in the woods, 300 rods. Ranging from the marked tree North easterly along the Purchase line, 47 Degrees to a stone set in the ground and marked W.H. on the one
2 CONC  side, and S. H. on the other side, 178 rods. Ranging thence along the fence as it now stands to a stone set in the ground on the east side of my gate, at the end of the lane by my orchard. Ranging thence along the orchard 36 rods
2 CONC , thence along the Garden 16 rods. 
2 CONT
2 CONT From thence down to the Purchase line, that comes through Hellgate. From thence to the mouth of the Great Creek, thence to the little creek, from thence to the Great Rock, the first station. And he is to have the equal privilege o
2 CONC f the lane with Samuel Hallett; as it is now fenced, from the stone, by my gate to the water side, so down west to the Purchase line. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Except a certain tract of land and buildings, given to my son, Moses Hallett, by a deed, June 7, 1708. To him, my son, Joseph Hallett, and his heirs male, and in default of such, then to my son, George Hallett, and his heirs male.
2 CONC  And in default to my son Richard and his heirs male, and in default of such to my female heirs, forever. 
2 CONT
2 CONT I also leave to my son Joseph, a negro man, and a negro wench, and a waggon, plough, and my great riding horse, and a cupboard, and the Great Table and great chest, and my silver Tankard. 
2 CONT
2 CONT I leave to my sons, George and Richard, and to my grandson, Joseph Hallett, and to my daughters, Sarah Phillips, Rebecca Jackson, Sarah Blackwell, and Charity Moore, certain negroes. I leave to my true and loving wife, one third o
2 CONC f the remainder of all my movable estate, and the privilege of the chamber in the stone house, during widowhood. And my son Joseph is to furnish her sufficient support and firewood. 
2 CONT
2 CONT I leave two thirds of my movables to my five daughters, Sarah Phillips, Rebecca Jackson, Charity Moore, Mary Blackwell, and Elizabeth Fish. And my son Joseph is to keep for his mother, four head of cattle, winter and summer. I lea
2 CONC ve to my sons, Joseph and George, all my apparell. I make my wife Mary, and my sons, and James Jackson, and Samuel Moore, executors.
2 CONT
2 CONT Dated September 16, 1727.
2 CONT
2 CONT Witnesses,
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel Hallett,
2 CONT Samuel Hallett, Jr.,
2 CONT Samuel Richards.
2 CONT
2 CONT (No probate recorded. Endorsed, August 23, 1729.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of William and Sarah (Woolsey) Hallett.
2 CONT
2 CONT  16.  (1). William III b. December 10, 1670; d. 1708 m. Ruth 
2 CONT  17.  (2). Sarah Elizabeth b. March 19, 1672 m. George Philips
2 CONT  18.  (3). Rebecca Hallett b. August 31, 1675 d. 1730 m. James Jackson, Sr
2 CONT  19.  (4). Joseph b. March  4 1677 m. Lydia Blackwell m. Mary Lawrence in August 22, 1728
2 CONT  20.  (5). Moses b. January 19, 1680 m. Mary Fitch
2 CONT  21.  (6). George b. April 25, 1683 m. Priscilla Allen
2 CONT  22.  (7). Charity b. March 16, 1684 m. Samuel Moore
2 CONT  23.  (8). Mary b. October 22, 1687 m. Jacob Blackwell
2 CONT  24.  (9). Elizabeth b. 1689 m. John Fish
2 CONT  25. (10). Richard b. November 17, 1691 m. Amy Browne
