1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Not the same as https://www.geni.com/people/Deborah-Corson/4225332354880023702
2 CONT *Not the wife of https://www.geni.com/people/Peter-Corson/6000000001691742375?through=6000000000285252011
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ''History and Genealogy of the Cock, Cocks, Cox Family''
2 CONT
2 CONT >DEBORAH (UNDERHILL) TOWNSEND (Capt. John) b. 29/9 mo. (Nov.) 1659; d. 30/1 mo. (Mar.) 1698: m., ante 1686, Henry Townsend, b. about 1654 ; d. Oyster Bay, ante 1703, son of Henry and Ann (Colea) Townsend. (See Townsend Lineage).
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_Townsend_(Oyster_Bay)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Henry Townsend''' (1649-1703) was the son of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_Townsend_(Norwich) Henry Townsend] who emigrated to the colonies from England. Eventually Henry Townsend settled in Oyster Bay, where his son Hen
2 CONC ry Townsend was raised.[1] Townsend Society of America DNA testing project has established that the Oyster Bay family is not related to Thomas Townsend of Lynn, MA. The county of origin in England for Henry, John and Richard Towns
2 CONC end is not known.
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry Townsend married '''Deborah Underhill''' in 1677. Deborah Underhill (1659-1698) was daughter of Captain John Underhill (1597-1672), another important figure in Colonial America who trained the militia of the Massachusetts Ba
2 CONC y Colony and served as magistrate of Flushing for a brief period of time, before settling on 150 acres (0.61 km2) of land outside of Oyster Bay. Captain Underhill was converted to Quakerism by his second wife, thus making the unio
2 CONC n of Henry Townsend and Deborah Underhill the combining of two of the most influential Quaker families in Oyster Bay.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT They had at least four children together: 
2 CONT # Robert Townsend (b. 1687),
2 CONT #  Elizabeth Townsend (1692-1756), 
2 CONT # Henry (d. 1709) and 
2 CONT # Uriah Townsend (1698-1767)
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry Townsend (1670-1709) was the son of Henry Townsend and Deborah Underhill. He bought the mill his grandfather had built from his uncle John Townsend, and when his Uncle John died, he was elected town surveyor, being the third
2 CONC  generation in direct descent engaged in surveying and to operate the mill. He married Eliphal Wright, daughter of his aunt Mary Townsend and John Wright.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Underhill_(captain)
2 CONT
2 CONT John Underhill (ca 1608/1609 – 21 July 1672)[1] was an early English settler and soldier in the Massachusetts Bay Colony, the Province of New Hampshire, where he also served as governor; the New Haven Colony, New Netherland, and l
2 CONC ater the Province of New York, settling on Long Island.  ….
2 CONT
2 CONT Following the death of his first wife and his mother in 1658, Underhill married his second wife Elizabeth Feake on 2 December 1658, in Oyster Bay. Feake was a Quaker and converted John to Quakerism before he died.
2 CONT
2 CONT Captain John Underhill and Elizabeth Feake had five children: '''Deborah''' (1659–1697), Nathaniel (1663–1710), Hannah (1666–1757), Elizabeth (1669–1704), and David (1672–1708).
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Deborah UNDERHILL
2 CONT
2 CONT [NI5757]
2 CONT
2 CONT ____ - ____
2 CONT
2 CONT Father: Capt. John UNDERHILL 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: Elisabeth WINTHROP 
2 CONT
2 CONT Family 1 : Henry TOWNSEND
2 CONT
2 CONT +Henry TOWNSEND
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/219953433/henry-townsend
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry II, son of Henry Townsend I and Anne Coles.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married Deborah, daughter of Capt John Underhill about 1676. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Issue: Henry, Robert, (Elizabeth) a daughter who was married to one of the Ludlams of Hog Island.
2 CONT
2 CONT "He does not appear in the records except for transfer of property. Nor is it known when he died, but it must have been before 1703. " 
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: "A Memorial of John, Henry and Richard Townsend and Their Descendants", New York, W A Townsend, Publisher, 1865, page 185. (aka Townsend Memorial)
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: Date of death listed on this Memorial is After 1709. Henry Townsend II was alive in 1709 because Henry Townsend III calls himself Junior in his Will (which means Henry Senior was living).
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Comments 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/sources/LCT1-BC3
2 CONT
2 CONT AVOID OLD ERRORS. DEBORAH UNDERHILL was daughter of Capt. John Underhill & Elizabeth Feake. Deborah md. Henry Townsend II & had Henry III, Robert & Elizabeth who md. Joseph Ludlam, Jr..See "Three Elizabeth Ludlams of Oyster Bay,' 
2 CONC NYGBR 131:116.
2 CONT
