1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Underhill-9
2 CONT
2 CONT Nathaniel was a Friend (Quaker)
2 CONT
2 CONT Nathaniel was born to John and Elizabeth Feake Underhill in Killingworth, Oyster Bay on 22d 12m 1663 [22 Feb 1664].[1][2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Nathaniel and Mary Ferris announced their marriage intention at the New York (Flushing) Monthly Meeting on 27d 12m 1685 [27 Feb 1686].[3] He married Mary Ferris in Matinecock, Long Island, on February 27, 1685-6.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Nathaniel and his bride sold out his property in Oyster Bay to his half-brother John Underhill in 1686 and removed from Long Island to land in Throgs Neck, Westchester, purchased from John and Sarah Turner.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Nathaniel died in Westchester on November 10, 1710.[1] he was buried in Underhill Cemetery, Williams Bridge, Bronx, New York
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT Nathaniel and Mary had, in Westchester, (in what became in 1898 the Bronx in New York City):
2 CONT
2 CONT # Thomas, b. December 4, 1687.[1]
2 CONT # Nathaniel, b. August 11, 1690.[1] married Mary Honeywell 
2 CONT # Benjamin, b. October__, 1694.[1] married Hannah, and has a son, John Underhill.
2 CONT # Abraham, b. 1697.[1]
2 CONT # John, b. 1700.[1]
2 CONT # Mary, b. 1704, married Joseph Horton.[1]
2 CONT # William, b. April 7, 1707.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
