1 NAME Stephen /Birdsall/ I
2 GIVN Stephen
2 SURN Birdsall
2 NSFX I
2 _MARNM Birdsall
2 NICK Stephen Birdsall
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1656
2 PLAC Oyster Bay, Nassau, New York, United States
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 4 APR 1723
2 ADDR
3 CITY Little Egg Harbor Township
3 STAE NJ
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Birdsall-106
2 CONT
2 CONT Stephen Burdsall (or Birdsell) was born in 1648, the son of Nathan, the son of George Birdsall who emigrated from England circa 1635[1] [2] [3]
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Mary whose maiden name was not found[1] [2]. Their children included:
2 CONT
2 CONT # Mary[1], called "daughter Mabel Grant" in her father's will. She married John Grant of Little Egg Harbour, NJ[3]
2 CONT # Nathan, whose son Nathan married Abigal Willets in 1752[3]
2 CONT # Sarah[1], who married Jeremy Irons of Shrewsbury, NJ March 3, 1730[3]
2 CONT # Phebe[1], who married John Havens in 1727, and then married Mr. Bartlett[3]
2 CONT # Joseph, born 1682, whose son was Benjamin, born 1705[1]
2 CONT # Stephen, Jr, born 1685[1], who married Deliverance Willets in 1738[3]
2 CONT # Elizabeth[1]
2 CONT # Richard[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT He removed to Little Egg Harbor with his brother Nathaniel in 1713
2 CONT
2 CONT Stephen Burdsell died in 1723. The 1723 will of Stephen Burdsall of Litel Egg Harber, Burlington County, New Jersey lists his wife Mary, and children Nathan, Stephen, Phebe, Martha, Mary and Mabel Grant.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes on Spouse
2 CONT
2 CONT His wife's birth name is not known. There is no identified marriage record. In some family trees she is listed as Mary Prior, daughter of John Prior and Elizabeth Bowne. However this Mary Prior was clearly born 1685, which would b
2 CONC e too late for birth of some of Stephen's children. Either Mary Prior was not his wife, or she was his second wife (although then it would seem that based on likely marriage dates in 1700-1710 that there would have been a marriage
2 CONC  record.)
2 CONT
2 CONT STEPHEN2 BIRDSALL (Nathan1) and Mary, he d. 1724, had: 
2 CONT
2 CONT   Stephen3 m. 1738, Deliverance Willets. 
2 CONT
2 CONT   Phebe3 m. 1st a Havens, 2d a Bartlett. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Stephen and Deliverance: 
2 CONT
2 CONT   Mary4 m. Timothy Willets. 
2 CONT
2 CONT   Sarah4 m. Jarvis Hazelton.
