1 NAME Hannah /Carr/
2 GIVN Hannah
2 SURN Carr
2 _MARNM Robbins
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 24 JUL 1716
2 PLAC Oyster Bay, Long Island, New York
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 19 NOV 1762
2 PLAC New Jersey
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The Genealogy of Walter Gilbert
2 CONT
2 CONT ANCESTORS: THE SIXTH GENERATION BACK
2 CONT
2 CONT Jeremiah Robbins
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah Carr
2 CONT
2 CONT 72–73.  Jeremiah Robbins of Oyster Bay, Long Island, New York was born _____, and died in _____ after 1758. Hannah Carr was born in New York on Tuesday, July 24, 1716. They were married about 1732. She took the name Hannah Robbins
2 CONC . Marriage recorded in EQG, vol. III, p. 399, Westbury Monthly Meeting. Marriage recorded in EQG, vol. III, p. 399, Westbury Monthly Meeting. He is the son of Jeremiah Robbins. She is the daughter of Job and Hannah (Willets) Carr.
2 CONC  They had 11 children:
2 CONT
2 CONT i.	 Almy Robbins was born in New York on November 15, 1733.	
2 CONT
2 CONT ii.	 Elizabeth Robbins was born in New York on January 19, 1736/7. On September 10, 1735, she married Henry Cock, son of John and Sarah Cock, in Westbury. Their children were Anna, William, Stephen, Charles, Hannah and four others
2 CONC .	
2 CONT
2 CONT iii.	 Hannah Robbins was born in New York on April 19, 1739, and died in 1778. On March 3, 1762, she married Rees Cock, son of John and Sarah Cock. He was born on January 26, 1738/9, and died on January 9, 1812. The Quaker Meeting
2 CONC  record states that Jeremiah Robbins was of Oyster Bay.	
2 CONT
2 CONT iv.	 Sarah Robbins was born in New York on September 1, 1742, and died probably in Westbury on June 28, 1825. On July 4, 1765, at Matinecock, New York, she married John Titus, son of William (deceased) and Elizabeth of Westbury. H
2 CONC e was born February 30, 1743/4 and died April 24, 1816.	
2 CONT
2 CONT v.	 Samuel Robbins was born in New York on April 26, 1745.	
2 CONT
2 CONT vi.	 Isaac Robbins [#36]: He was born in New York on March 12, 1747/8, and died in _____ on February 15, 1813.	
2 CONT
2 CONT vii.	 Stephen Robbins was born in Long Island on February 26, 1750/1, and died on July 25, 1813. He married Miriam Seaman, daughter of Samuel and Martha Seaman. [EQG, vol. III, p. 495]	
2 CONT
2 CONT viii.	 Phebe Robbins was born in New York on September 17, 1752.	
2 CONT
2 CONT ix.	 Abigail Robbins was born in New York on August 9, 1755.	
2 CONT
2 CONT x.	 Job Robbins was born in New York on April 16, 1758.	
2 CONT
2 CONT xi.	 William Robbins was born in New York after 1758.
2 CONT
2 CONT Vol. III, p. 439 of the EQG has:
2 CONT
2 CONT Jeremiah, s Jere.; m Hannah CARR, dt Job &
2 CONT
2 CONT     Hannah, b 5 Mo (July) 24, 1716 (mo)
2 CONT
2 CONT The "(mo)" indicated that the marriage was outside of the unity of the Quaker community; hence, one of the pair was not a member (in good standing). In this case, since Jeremiah's parentage is given only as "s Jere." while Hannah'
2 CONC s family extends for generations back into the Quaker community, one can speculate that it is Jeremiah who is the outsider.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note that the EQG, vol. III, p. 399, states that Hannah Carr, daughter of Jeremiah (instead of Job) and Hannah, married about 1732, Jeremiah Robbins. Since this is the only reference to a Jeremiah Carr in the entire book, and her 
2 CONC husband was Jeremiah, this is clearly an error; her father is Job. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT
2 CONT Hinshaw, William Wade; Encyclopedia of Quaker Genealogy, vol. III (New York), "Westbury Monthly Meeting", vol. III, p. 439 (children) (CD #192 from Brøderbund)
2 CONT
2 CONT New York Marriage Book, vol. XVI, p. 39
2 CONT
2 CONT Bunker, Mary Powell; Long Island Genealogies, Joel Munsell's Sons, Publishers. Albany, NY, 1895. (as found on CD-ROM: Tracking Down Our Family Heritage)
2 CONT
2 CONT [Ancestry of Timothy Titus Robbins assembled by Gayle Ellingsworth]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
