1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Isaac Horner the 2nd;
2 CONT
2 CONT 	Born 4-17-1678, according to W.S. Hornor, but this record is not included in the present writer’s transcript of Horner data from the Yorkshire Friends’ records; d. 11-24-1760, at White Hill, near Bordentown, N.J., m. (1) 1709, El
2 CONC izabeth Sykes, who d. 4-3-1712 (chesterfield Monthly Meeting records), and (2) 1718, Elenor, daughter of Samuel Bowne, of Flushing, L.I. (N.Y. Geneal. & Biog. Rec., Vol. VI, p. 102).  He was a lifelong member of Chesterfield month
2 CONC ly Meeting and lived at Mansfield, on a plantation bought by his father, John Horner, in 1684.  (West Jersey Deeds, R. p. 272; AAA, p. 187).
