1 NOTE {geni:about_me} THORN, THORNE name variations
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Thorn, Daniel Daniel Thorn m. (1) Mary Frost son of Thomas Thorn & dau. of William Frost & Penelope Coles Susannah Coles b. 1726 b. d. 1765 d. m. (2) Margaret Wright (widow of Noah Townsend )
2 CONT dau. of Zebulon Wright & Clemense Feakes In his will, he wrote: I, Daniel Thorn, of Oyster Bay, in Queens County, this 24 of September, 1765, do make and ordain this my last will and testament."All debts to be paid by my executors
2 CONC . I leave to my wife Margaret £50 and all the household goods that she brought to me. Likewise a mare and a riding chair and two good cows. "Also if my wife Margaret should be turned out of her thirds of the estate which her forme
2 CONC r husband, Noah Townsend, deceased, died seized of, then it is my will that she shall have £100 more."All the rest of my estate, real and personal, I leave to my two sons, Charles and Stephen, equally. If my sons die without issue
2 CONC , then I leave 2/7 of my estate to my brother, William Thorn, and 2/7 to my sister,Athe- lena Baker, and the other 3/7 to my three sisters, Elizabeth Carpenter, Hannah Bowne, and Phebe Cock. I make my friends, Jacob Valentine, Jac
2 CONC ob Carpenter, and Jacob Bowne, executors. Witnesses, John Lawrence, William Lawrence, Jr., William Lawrence. Proved, October 1, 1765. ---children of Daniel Thorn & •
2 CONT Charles Thorne , b. 1755; d. 1818; m. Anne Kirby , dau. of Daniel Kirby & Hannah Latting •
2 CONT Stephen Thorn ---Sources: Pelletreau, William S.,Abstracts of Wills on File in the Surrogate’s Office, City of NewYork , pub. as Collections of the NewYork Historical Society , Vol. VI, 1760- 1766, p. 419 (will of Daniel Thorn); J
2 CONC ones, John H. The Jones Family of Long Island. NewYork: TobiasA. Wright, 1907, p. 259
