2 CONT
2 CONT ===Surname note
2 CONT
2 CONT This surname had many different spellings, including Fitzrandle, Fittsrendolfe, or Fittsrandolfe[3], with FitzRandolph or Fitz Randolph emerging as the most common. Fitz Randolph is being recommended as the standard, recognizing t
2 CONC hough that in later years, Fitz sometimes became used as a middle name for sons and optional for daughters. In Benjamin father's Fitz Randolph family, Fitz appears to have been used by all family members as part of their surname: 
2 CONC the Oris H.F. Randolph genealogy[4] assumes this to be the case when listing the children in the family in which Mary is a child. The current consensus is therefore to use the surname Fitz Randolph. (Need to confirm how Fitz Rando
2 CONC lph was used in legal documents and when births were recorded documents.) Please don't hesitate to contact the profile manager if you think this decision should be reviewed!
