1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Nathaniel Soule Sr.=
2 CONT * BIRTH 1637 Plymouth, Plymouth County, Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT * DEATH 1699 (aged 61–62) Dartmouth, Bristol County, Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT * BURIAL Apponagansett Friends Cemetery, Dartmouth, Bristol County, Massachusetts, USA
2 CONT * PLOT No stone or marker
2 CONT * MEMORIAL ID  45123735 photo added by goose
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Biography==
2 CONT Nathaniel Soule was born say 1637 at Duxbury in the Plymouth Colony, died before 12 Oct 1699 at Dartmouth, Bristol, Massachusetts.  He was the son of George Soule & Mary Becket and his siblings were Zachariah born by 1627, John bo
2 CONC rn circa 1632, George, Jr. born circa 1639, Susanna born circa 1642, Mary born circa 1644, Elizabeth born circa 1645, Patience born circa 1648, and Benjamin born circa 1651.  He married Rose Thorn about 1680 at Dartmouth, Bristol 
2 CONC County, MA. To this union were born four children: Nathaniel Jr, Jacob, Sylvanus, & Miles.
2 CONT
2 CONT On Mar 4, 1674, he was summoned before the courts on a charge of adultery with an Indian woman. On Mar 1, 1675, he and the woman were whipped at the post and he was ordered to pay her 10 bushels of Indian corn towards the support 
2 CONC of her child by him. He was also cited for numerous abuses, such as "lyes, unlawful entry and trespass."   He and his brother, George, inherited land at Dartmouth, MA from their father. They both settled there, owned fishing craft
2 CONC  and were engaged in fishing the "Banks."
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Estate==
2 CONT Nathaniel Soule died without a will. His widow made bond as executrix 12 October 1699. His inventory reported on that day appraised the personal property at 197:16:00 (Bristol County, Massachusetts Probate Court Records, Volume 2,
2 CONC  Page 47, on FHL Microfilm 0,461,882). Debts and charges were in the amount of 23 pounds, 8 shillings and 8 pence. The remaining estate for distribution totaled 174 pounds, 7 shillings, 4 pence.
2 CONT
2 CONT This division was dated 15 May 1702 and approved 10 September 1702. No guardian assignments and no distribution of the real estate that the will of George Soule Sr and the above cited court actions imply have been found. There is 
2 CONC no record of the distribution of widow Rose Soule's undoubtedly substantial estate.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Chronology==  
2 CONT 1667- He was fined 20 pounds for scandalizing his minister, Rev. John Holmes. He avioded the stocks at the request of Rev. Holmes.  
2 CONT 1671- Fined 5 pounds and publically whipped for "telling lyes which tended greatly to the hurt of the Colony."
2 CONT 1674- Again whipped "for adulty with an Indian woman" and ordered to pay 10 bushels of Indian corn "towards the keeping of the child". 
2 CONT 1686, May 24- Took oath of fidelity or Freeman's oath at Dartmouth, MA.
2 CONT 1697, January 22 - Listed in a petition of 20 Proprietors of Dartmouth, MA.
2 CONT 1699, October 12 Probate: Administration granted
2 CONT 1700 October 10 Inventory taken 
2 CONT 1702 September 10 Estate division made
2 CONT
