1 NOTE {geni:about_me} HENDRICK anglicized his surname to DUSENBURY after the Dutch surrendered control of the region to the English in 1667.He married in circa 1680, MARY THORN, born in 1658, in England, the daughter of an English settl
2 CONC er.  Their children were
2 CONT
2 CONT IV.       MARY DUSENBORO, baptized on 15 May 1712, at the Dutch Reform Church in Jamaica, Long Island.She married ARTHUR ALBERTIS, a farmer from Hempstead.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT THOMAS LANGDON II b c1673 d1734 (?) s/o Joseph Langdon & Mary (Osborne) m-1 unknown lady m-2 MARY (maiden surname unknown) ALBURTUS, widow of Arthur Alburtus of Hempstead. Thomas and Mary were married in 1727 at St. George's Churc
2 CONC h, Hempstead, L.I. In 1732 Thomas was living at Jerusalem, L.I. He was doubtless a farmer. At various times he took up large grants of land in the South Woods of Hempstead(HTR 8:327/28, 346,485). His will, dated 1733 and probated 
2 CONC 27 May 1734, mentions his wife, Mary, and the children listed below.
2 CONT ----
