1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Adam and Anne Mott By Thomas Clapp Cornell
2 CONT
2 CONT RlCHBELL MOTT the first born of the second wife, married in 1696, 
2 CONT
2 CONT ELIZABETH THORNE, of 'Flushing. The marriage license in the New 
2 CONT
2 CONT York record is dated the I4th October, 1696, and the name is written 
2 CONT
2 CONT Rigebell Mott. He settled at Mad Nan's Neck (Little Neck), perhaps on 
2 CONT
2 CONT the land mentioned in his father's will, and was a man of standing and 
2 CONT
2 CONT force. His grandmother, ANN RICHBELL, in her will dated April, 1700, 
2 CONT
2 CONT makes "MR. RICHBELL MOTT" one of her executors, the other two 
2 CONT
2 CONT being Col. Caleb Heathcote and Lieut. John Horton.
2 CONT
2 CONT The will Richbell Mott names two sons, Edmond and RICHARD, and six daughters, Elizabeth, Mary, Ann, Jemmima, Kedzie and Deborah, and three sons-in-law, Adam 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mott, of Staten Island, Joseph Mott, of Cowneck, and "Jonathan 
2 CONT
2 CONT Townsend, Esq., of Oyster Bay," the two last named being executors. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The widow ELIZABETH (THORNE) MOTT left a will dated 7th March, 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1739, and proved 16th April, 1739. She describes herself widow of 
2 CONT
2 CONT RlCHBELL MOTT, and " sick and weak of body," and names the same 
2 CONT
2 CONT children, and indicates marriages as follows : — daughter Jemmima Wood (
2 CONT
2 CONT wife of Stephen), daughter Kedzie Jackson, grandson Daniel Kissam, 
2 CONT
2 CONT granddaughter Mary Treadwell, and granddaughter Elizabeth Mott, 
2 CONT
2 CONT daughter of Adam Mott.
