1 NOTE {geni:about_me} RICHARD MOTT, born probably about 1710, died of yellow fever 15th of 
2 CONT
2 CONT 8th mo., 1743, " in unity with Friends;" married 20th of 1st mo., 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1741, SARAH PEARSALL, born 6th of Ilth mo., 1714, died at the house 
2 CONT
2 CONT of her son, John Alsop, in Hudson, N. Y., 9th, mo., 1800, daughter 
2 CONT
2 CONT of THOMAS and SARAH (UNDERHILL) PEARSALL of Hempstead. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The Westbury record of the marriage says: " RICHARD MOTT, late 
2 CONT
2 CONT of Hempstead, now of the City of New York." His will, dated 
2 CONT
2 CONT l0th of 8th mo., 1743, five days before his death, describes him of 
2 CONT
2 CONT Hempstead, and " being very much indisposed in body." He gives 
2 CONT
2 CONT to his wife £loo in addition to one-third of all of his property, and 
2 CONT
2 CONT the remaining two-thirds to his son JAMES (then but little more than 
2 CONT
2 CONT one year old), and in case of his son's death without issue, then to 
2 CONT
2 CONT the three sons of his brother Edmond, viz.: Richbell, Edmond and 
2 CONT
2 CONT John. 
