1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Jemima Mott (1710-1748), daughter of Richbell Mott and Elizabeth (Thorne) Mott.  Wife of Stephen Wood.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Mott-2039
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Excerpt from the 1737 Will of Elizabeth (Thorne) Mott (Mother):
2 CONT
2 CONT "I give my grand Daughter Phoebe Wood Daughter of Stephen Wood ten pounds york Money. I also give her a feather Bed with to Coverlets that are in my Chest with three Sheets and two pair of the best Pillow Cases appertaining to me.
2 CONC  I also give her my Chest.
2 CONT
2 CONT I give my Daughter '''Jemima Wood''' my Crape Gown ? Grey woostead Gown and a Straked Cotton & wool Petty Coat and also a white Cambrick Apron and a home Spun one a Cambrick Handkerchief, three Cape Cotton Gloves my Silk Bonnet.
2 CONT
2 CONT I further give Stephen Wood what is due to me for a year and half keeping of the old Negro Wench named Jenny.
2 CONT
2 CONT I give my Daughter Jemima two Cotton and Linnen Waistcoats and two Shifts that are in my Chest."
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT * The New York Genealogical and Biographical Record, Volume 37.  Records of The Reformed Dutch Church.  Search on Geertje Winter: < [https://books.google.com/books?id=qtUUAAAAYAAJ&lpg=PA372&ots=_zH7IH8Opd&dq=Geertje%20(Winter)%20W
2 CONC ood&pg=PA33#v=onepage&q=Geertje%20(Winter)%20Wood&f=false GoogleBooks] > Search on Jemima Mott: < [https://books.google.com/books?id=qtUUAAAAYAAJ&lpg=PA372&ots=_zH7IH8Opd&dq=Geertje%20(Winter)%20Wood&pg=PA130#v=snippet&q=Jemima%20
2 CONC (Mott)%20Wood&f=false GoogleBooks] >
