3 STAE New York
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Anthony BADGLEY settled at Flushing, Long Island, NY toward the end of the seventeenth century. The destruction of all old town records of Flushing prevents our stating the exact date of Anthony Badgley's arrival t
2 CONC here but we know that he had a plantation there.
2 CONT
2 CONT He petitioned the authorities for a warrant to survey a lot in Flushing called "Hemp Lot" belonging to him in order to end the encroachments of Thomas Hedger and others. The petition was granted 19 Aug 1697. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1698 there was made an exact list of "all ye inhabitants names within ye towne of Flushing and Polntz of old and young freeman and servants white and black," etc. In this list we find the following entry:
2 CONT
2 CONT Anthony Badgley, Elizabeth his wife, Anthony, George, Phebe: 1 negro.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was evidently in comfortable circumstances. At least in 1707 he was one of a company composed chiefly of wealthy men which purchased through its agent, Peter Sonmans, a large tract of land in New Jersey for which it paid the In
2 CONC dians 200 pounds in cash and goods. This tract contained about 170,000 acres called "New Britain" lay about thirty-three miles northwest of Elizabethtown. It had not been laid out and divided among its owners in 1751. The early na
2 CONC me for this tract was "Markseta Colinnge." Among the other proprietors were Nathaniel Bonnell, Richard Townley, William Nickoll, William Urquhart, Ebenezer Wilson, Lancaster Symes and Conningsby Norbury. Badgley's share was one-fo
2 CONC urteenth and that of Townley one-twenty-eighth. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In July, 1711 there was compiled an account of each inhabitant of Flushing provisions as followth "--being the tax rate for the year Anthony Badgley's share was 23 pounds of bacon, 6 bushels of wheat, and one bushel of Indian corn
2 CONC ." 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a Sergeant in Captain Jonathan Wright's company of militia in 1715 and probably died within a few years as no further mention of his name appears. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Anthony BADGLEY married about 1692 Flushing, Queens, NY to Elizabeth <nowiki>-----</nowiki> (surname unknown, possibly THORN(E) or HENDLEY). Their seven children included: 
2 CONT
2 CONT (1) Anthony BADGLEY b. about 1690-5 Flushing, NY, d. 1732 Flushing, NY m. 1719 to Phebe HAIGHT.
2 CONT
2 CONT (2) George BADGLEY (about1693/6-1759) m. 1717 Mary HATFIELD
2 CONT
2 CONT (3) Phebe BADGLEY (about 1696/8-1776) m. 1715 Peter WILCOCKSE (1691-1768)
2 CONT
2 CONT (4) Sarah BADGLEY (about 1698-1785) m. 1721 Joseph DOTY
2 CONT
2 CONT (5) James BADGLEY (about 1700/5-1777) m. Hannah KELSEY
2 CONT
2 CONT (6) John BADGLEY (1700-1759) m. 1719 Euphemia RADLEY
2 CONT
2 CONT (7) Elizabeth BADGLEY (b. after 1700-2) m. Uriah HEDGES
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Settler
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Anthony Badgley BIRTH	1660 England DEATH	1715 (aged 54–55) Flushing, Queens County, New York, USA BURIAL	 Quaker Meeting House Cemetery Flushing, Queens County, New York, USA  PLOT	As a Friend, he was probably buried in this cemet
2 CONC ery without a marker if he died near his home MEMORIAL ID	203291283
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Last documented mention is in 1715 and probably died shortly afterwards. The Quaker Meeting House Cemetery is by far the mostly likely burial location, if he died where he lived in 1715. Given that no records survive and no marker
2 CONC s were used by Quakers at this time, his burial location cannot be confirmed. Note that his son Anthony Badgley does have a documented burial location in the Quaker Meeting House Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was not buried in Gallia, Ohio, as the Anthony Badgley burial there is clearly 19th century and belongs to Anthony Badgley (1849-1863), son of George and Angeline Badgley (see Ohio Burials. "son of ... A. Badgley" on the stone,
2 CONC  and the fact that George Badgley is an adjacent burial).
2 CONT
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/203291283/anthony-badgley Find A Grave Memorial] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Apr 27 2020, 17:35:49 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
