2 CONT ===Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT From http://www-personal.umich.edu/~bobwolfe/gen/mn/m5410x5566.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT 1705 On 11 April, widow Hannah Doughty remarried to Samuel Thorne Jr. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT 1705 On 20 June, Edward, Viscount Cornbury, Captain-General, etc. Whereas Benjamin Doughty, of Flushing, in Queens County, lately died intestate, Letters of administration are granted to Hannah Thorne, his widow. [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT 1705 On 22 August, Inventory of the estate of Benjamin Doughty, of Flushing, Queens County, [New York]. 180 bushels of wheat in stack at 4s. 3d. £38, 5s. Total amount £192. There appeared before me Hannah Thorne, late Hannah Dough
2 CONC ty, relict of Benjamin Doughty and made oathe of the above inventory. Account of debts paid by Hannah Thorne, late widow of Benjamin Doughty, £70, 5s. 2d. [3]
