2 CONT WILL of STEPHEN THORNE     #11035M New Jersey
2 CONT =Lived in Manhattan's Seventh Ward in 1830=
2 CONT ==background==
2 CONT The Seventh Ward was then, in the mid 19th century, a part of Manhattan that included slips on the East River. One of these was Gouveneur's Slip, first known as home to the Walnut St. Ferry to what became the Navy Yards of Brookly
2 CONC n's Wallabout Bay. See [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gouverneur_Street_Ferry Gouveneur St. Ferry], the later name for the same operation. ''titled: "Map from 1847 showing the route of what was then the Navy Yard Ferry"''
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Early Mapping of the Seventh Ward===
2 CONT * 1797 : A New & Accurate Plan of the City of New York in the State of New York in North America.: Published in 1797 Lionel Pincus and Princess Firyal Map Division https://digitalcollections.nypl.org/items/1b995900-0f58-0132-e645-
2 CONC 58d385a7bbd0
2 CONT * 1800 [https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=project&photo_id=6000000218922468913&project_id=4481652 Ward Map of Manhattan 1800]
2 CONT * note the old Gouveneur Farm: https://sites.rootsweb.com/~nynewyo2/history/OldMaps1.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT > By the end of the Civil War and the marriage of Stephen Thorne's son D.C. Thorne, the descendant Thorne family maintained its foothold in the Seventh Ward. Stephen's youngest son [https://www.geni.com/people/Daniel-Thorne/600000
2 CONC 0000760093565 D.C. Thorne (1827-1913)] married Mary Ann Wilson there at a  Gouveneur's St. residence at the end February 1870 but then returned to his home in Prescott AZT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==1850==
2 CONT (last census in which Stephen appears)
2 CONT Living in Shrewsbury with Sarah Kippin (sic) (age 86) = [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/80473042/susan-kippin findagrave] ( c. 1774 - 29 Aug. 1854) ; others in household as well. Sarah seems to have been an aunt.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===remaining work for this profile===
2 CONT
2 CONT # find his wife
2 CONT # find his remaining and unaccounted for children... all seen in the [https://www.geni.com/documents/view?doc_id=6000000218755796827 '''''1830 census of the Seventh Ward Manhattan''''']
2 CONT ## note that Stephen Thorne family hasn't yet been found in any 1840 US census records
2 CONT ### [https://www.geni.com/people/Daniel-Thorne/6000000000760093565 D.C. Thorne] and other Thorne men were prospecting in California by 1850 (Sutter County, CA, 1850 census)
2 CONT ## one possible dau. would be Amanda Thorne who married George Wilkenson in NYC 
2 CONT ==possible daughter or grandchild==
2 CONT https://www.ancestry.com/search/collections/61224/records/54436 Church of the Mediator  Marriage Date	6 Mar 1860
2 CONT > Amanda's husband may have married a 2nd time: https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/15326604/george-wilkinson 
