1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Daughter of Capt. William Piatt and Sarah Shotwell.   Her father Capt. William Piatt, was killed in war when she was a young infant.  Her year of birth indicated on 1850 Federal Census.   
2 CONT
2 CONT Jemima married Elijah Pound Shotwell.  Source: Ambrose Shotwell, Annals of Our Colonial Ancestors, pg. 122: No 5.  (They were cousins).
2 CONT Jemima & Elijah Shotwell's  son:
2 CONT William Piatt Shotwell 1802-1841 m. Harriet Pearce, had son William Piatt Greenleaf Shotwell,
2 CONT
2 CONT On 24 Aug 1853,  Elijah & Jemima  requested that their great grandson, William Piatt Greenleaf Shotwell, a minor ,  be received into membership with Friends. Witnessed by Joseph D Shotwell & Henry Wood.
2 CONT Her grandson Greenleaf, W.P. Shotwell,  upon his death in 1849, appointed his grandmother Jemima; executrix or of his will and caretaker of his son, William P.G.S.  
2 CONT
2 CONT 1850 Federal Census : Elijah was a farmer, age 70y , wife ; Jemima, age 60y, they resided in Westfield, Essex County, N.J.  Jemina 's year of birth about  1790.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jemina was an Orthodox  minister and recorded as such in her MM records, with over 13 pages of  Quaker  miscellaneous notations.  Some of which included appointments as a representative of Friends,  to attend various monthly meeti
2 CONC ngs.  One of these requests came in 21 May 1862,  at the time she would have been  in her seventies.    After the death of her husband in 1857, she removed her certificate from Rahway & Plainfield MM to Philadelphia, Arch Street M
2 CONC M, on June 20, 1860.   
2 CONT
2 CONT Jemina cared for five generations of family; her mother, husband,  son, grandson and great grandson and other family members..  She  held strong to her faith  and spirit  of her 96 years of life.  Surely, a  women of integrity and
2 CONC  inspiration.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Per Ambrose Shotwell, Annals of Our Colonial Ancestors, pg. . 122, she died near Pittsburg, PA, and on pg., 141,  in year 1868.
2 CONT
2 CONT Updated memorial 4-2023, her death and burial records located per Rahway & Plainfield MM Quaker record. Jemima G Shotwell, widow of Elijah died 9m 13 1871, 85y 11m 29ds,  buried West Middlesex, Mercer Co, Pa. Her memorial updated 
2 CONC from unknown to Haywood Cemetery, with date of date from 1868 to 1871.
2 CONT
2 CONT Special thanks to William P. Jones for posting her photo.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/185542692/jemima-green-shotwell Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Oct 2
