2 CONC the farm which was afterward the homestead of Moses Vail. According to records in the Genesee Co. clerks office (liber 28 p. 221 and liber 24 p. 284) he bought land in Elba (now Oakfield) on I May, 1831, and 18 July, 1832; but on 
2 CONC 18 Sept., 1832, he and wife Mercy conveyed land there to Edmond F. Bradly. He afterward dwelt for many years at or near Ottawa, 111., and there d. ;lost one arm in a sorgum grinder in ILL.; dw. Galen, Seneca (now Wayne) Co., N. Y.
2 CONC , when he m. (1) in Junius Friends meeting 31 of 1 mo., 1821, Phebe Laing, b. 7 of 8 mo., 1802, d. Elba, N. Y., soon after marriage, 1824±,dau. of Joseph" and Anna (Smith) Laing of Junius, N. Y., [of John*, Samuel*'?, Wm-., John']
