1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The Descendants of E D W A R D F I TZ R A N D O L P H and E L I Z A B E T H B L O S S O M
2 CONT
2 CONT 1630 - 1950
2 CONT
2 CONT By
2 CONT
2 CONT Louise Aymar Christian and Howard Stelle Fitz Randolph
2 CONT
2 CONT -113. EDWARD5 FJTZ RANDOLPH (45), born Plainfield, Apr. 23, 1749; died in Somerset, Co., N. J., Jan. 3, 1831 [34]; married at Plainfield Meeting Nov. 26, 1782, MARY WEBSTER, born Dec. 13, 1750 a t Plainfield (another authority say
2 CONC s she was b. 10 day, 10 mo., 1750 at Flushing, L. I., N. Y.); died Plainfield, Dec. 2, 1833, dau. of Hugh and Sarah (Marsh) Webster [34]. One morning in the summer of 1777 General Washington and an aide drew rein before the Old Va
2 CONC il Farm, where was gathered quite a group of young men. The General inquired if any of them knew of a place in the nearby hills where he could observe the movements of the British troops without being seen. Edward Fitz Randolph st
2 CONC epped forward, and saluting, assured him he knew every nook and hiding place in the country, and would conduct him to where the entire valley could be seen below. This rocky elevation was later named Washington Rock, and i s not f
2 CONC ar from Plainfield, if not now a part of it. Historians state that this was the turning point of the war. Children, born at Plainfield [34, 611: i. PHEBE,= b. Nov. 20, 1783; mar. JAMES I. COMPTON. NO children. ii. SARAH, b. Feb. 1
2 CONC 8, 1785; mar. JACOB VAIL [17, 341. iii. MERCY, b. Mar. 19, 1786; mar. 1 JACOB LAING; 2, EVY EVANS. iv. HUGH, b. May 18, 1787; d. Plainfield Nov. 3, 1792 [34, 611. v. MARY, b. Aug. 23, 1789; mar. JOSEPH VAIL [34]. vi. EDWARD, b. Oc
2 CONC t. 22, 1792; died Oct. 27, 1792 f34, 611. 203. vii. IRA, b. May 2, 1794 [34]. 204. viii. ASA, b. Oct. 10, 1795 [34, 611. ix. PRUDENCE, mar. BROKAW.
