2 CONT John [MOORE]. m. Nancy ...... <br/>
2 CONT On 22 Jun 1795 a John Moore was administrator of the estate of James Shotwell of Middlesex Co. Fellowbondsman was Joseph D'Camp; inventory made by Samuel Randolph and John Laing (NJ. Arch, 37:318). Wife of James Shotwell was Ann M
2 CONC oore who was called "sister Ann Laing" in the will of John Moore. Ann m/2 John Laing. NOTE: Elizabeth (Fitz Randolph) Moore had a brother Samuel and a nephew Samuel, s/o her brother Jacob Fitz Randolph. 1804, Oct. 15. Moore, John,
2 CONC  Jr. of Rahway Twsp., Essex Co.; will of. Wife Nancy, $ 1,000; all household furniture; also use of my dwelling house, while my widow. Lot of woodland and remainder of moveable estate to be sold, and proceeds put out at yearly int
2 CONC erest and paid to my late brother, Daniel Moore's youngest daughter, Hannah (by his former wife, Mary Frazee), until 18; then said interest to be paid my wife, while my widow. Sister, Ann Laing (late widow of James Shotwell), my r
2 CONC ight to 3 small lots on map number 2-3 and 4 adjoining the highway lot #1 belonging to said Ann Laing.
2 CONT
