2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Richard Townsend and Elizabeth Wicks:
2 CONT
2 CONT III John, b. : d. between 1715 and 1721 in Cape May Co., N. J. ; m. 1st. '''Phebe''' '''Williams''', dau. of Robert and Sarah (Washboume) Williams; m. 2d, Mercy
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT marr: 
2 CONT #1707 plac: Haddonfield, Burlington, New JerseyPhebe Williams birth: ABT 1656 death: 9 AUG 1704
2 CONT # Mary Langdon marr: 1707 plac: Haddonfield, Burlington, New Jersey
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT *Silvanus Townsend:  d: 25 SEP 1711
2 CONT * Sarah Townsend: 1683 deat: 22 SEP 1711
2 CONT * Robert Townsend birt: 1685 deat: 1772
2 CONT * Richard Townsend birt: 7 FEB 1681 plac: Upper Twsp., Cape May Co., New Jersey deat: 30 MAY 1737 plac: Philadelphia, Pennsylvania marr: 16 JUN 1704 place: Dublin Twsp, Phil Co., Philadelphia, Pennsylvania
2 CONT * Phebe Townsend birth 8 SEP 1705
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://minerdescent.com/2010/08/06/robert-williams/
2 CONT
2 CONT Phebe’s husband John Townend was born 1658 in Nassau, Livingston, New York. His parents were Richard Townsend and his second wife Elisabeth Wicks.  After Phebe died, he married Mercy Langdon 1707 in Haddonfield M M Newton, New Jer
2 CONC sey. John died 5 Jan 1721 in Townsends Inlet, Cape May, New Jersey.
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter Phebe Townsend and her husband, John, requested land as indicated in the transaction below, dated 30 Jan 1692:
2 CONT
2 CONT >“Whereas John Townsend ye Husband of my Daughter Phebe having often times requested of me Land in Right of his wife according to ye Last Will and Testament of my Husband Robert Williams deceased, and Consulted w(th) John Bowne on
2 CONC e of my Husbands Overseers concerning ye Matter, wee do Mutally agree in Consideration of ye Necessity of ye Sd John Townsend, And in order to ye ffulfilling of ye Will of ye Sd Robert Williams, according to ye true Intent & Meani
2 CONC ng, as also ye exp(r)sse words of ye Sd Will, We ye Sd Overseers of ye will aforesd, Have Given and Granted unto ye Sd John Townsend Husband of ye aforesd Phebe Townsend daughter of ye Sd Robert Williams Aforesd ffifty Acres of Wo
2 CONC od Land and one Hundred Acres of Plaine Land for him ye Sd John Townsend & his Heires to possesse and enjoy forever, ffor ye Sd John Townsend to take up by ord(r) Und(r) our hands Deputing men to Lay out ye Same where ye Sd John T
2 CONC ownsend Shall Judge Meet near & Convenient for him in any of ye Sd Robert Williams Land untaken up; But if either John or Hope Williams Sons of ye Sd Robert Williams Should obstruct the taking up of ye Sd Land & plaine in ye very 
2 CONC place where ye Sd John Townsend Shall at ffirst Judge ffitt, Meet, Convenient, as Claiming right to take up ffirst, by virtue of a former grant or Gift by their ffathers Will; that then it Shall & may be Lawfull for ye Sd John Tow
2 CONC nsend in pursuance of this our Grant to take up the Sd Wood Land & plaine Land in any place whereever he Shall please throwout the whole Tract of ye Sd Robert Williams Wood & plaine Land whereever he Shall Se Cause it being Land n
2 CONC ot already taken up, To w(ch) wee Set our hands and Seales this thirtyeth Day of ye Eleventh Month, one Thousand Six hundred Ninety and two. Signed Sealed & dd in P(r)sence of us John Bowne, Mare (W) Willitts marke, James Townsend
2 CONC , Richard Willitts” The mark of Sarah (S) Williams
2 CONT --------------------
