2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Mary Townsend
2 CONT * FamilySearch Family Tree
2 CONT * Birth:	1665 - Oyster Bay, New York, British Colonial America
2 CONT * Parents:	Richard Townsend I, Elizabeth Wickes
2 CONT * Husband:	Solomon Coles
2 CONT * Siblings:	Dinah Willets (born Townsend), Leah Williams (born Townsend), John Townsend, Hannah Townsend, Deliverance Townsend, Richard Townsend
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Children:	
2 CONT # Daniel Coles, born Circa 1712.  Married Ann Carpenter (But https://www.geni.com/people/Daniel-Coles-of-Cedar-Swamp/6000000000426726558 is seen as son of https://www.geni.com/people/Joseph-Coles/6000000000490972520?through=600000
2 CONC 0000426726558)
2 CONT # Mary Coles, born Feb 3 1713.  Married 1) Robert Matthews 2) Clement Cherrington
2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/4:1:MKS4-3VR
2 CONT
2 CONT She is referred to in "A Memorial of John, Henry and Richard Townsend," page 214, as one of the three daughters of Richard Townsend I and Elizabeth Weeks.  In her mother's distribution of the father's estate she is mentioned betwe
2 CONC en Hannah and Deliverance.  Her brother Richard II was confirmed to be the youngest, born 8 January 1670/1, as the mother stated, only twelve weeks before Richard I died.  It is difficult to see how Mary could be born after 1665. 
2 CONC  Unfortunately no further mention is made of her in "A Memorial" and no further mention is made in "History and Genealogy of the Cock-Cocks-Cox Family." page 372, the 2 books that probably knew this family best.  Please do not mer
2 CONC ge her or her information with any of her cousins of the same name.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
