2 CONT Profile last modified 30 Jan 2024 | Created 7 Feb 2011
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography===
2 CONT
2 CONT Daniel was born in about 1657; his parents were John Sweet. Daniel married Ethalanah Carpenter[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Daniel and Ethalaneh's known children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Sweet, b. 1685
2 CONT Daniel Sweet, b. 1692
2 CONT Timothy Sweet, b. 1703
2 CONT John Sweet, b. 1706
2 CONT Jeremiah Sweet b. 1700, d. 1 September 1731. In his will, we learn he had a daughter Mary Sweet with Mary Hunt (deceased). He leaves his estate to her and mentions his brothers, John Sweet, Daniel Sweet, and brother-in-law Ezekiel
2 CONC  Hunt.[2]
2 CONT Daniel died on 23 December 1732 in Gloucester, Providence, Rhode Island.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1732 in Glocester, Rhode Island, his wife was granted administrator of his estate.[3] His inventory was taken on 11 Jan 1732/33 in Glocester. His date of death was recorded in the heading of his inventory.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Research
2 CONT
2 CONT Looking at probate records, one Daniel Sweet died on 25 December 1734 in Glocester, Rhode Island. His death date is recorded in the heading of his inventory. His wife Authalanah(Ethalanah) was appointed administratrix of his estat
2 CONC e, as the source above shows.
2 CONT The Carpenter genealogy used as a source says that Daniel Sweet who married Ethalanah Carpenter, father was John Sweet, b. 1657. This may be in err, John may have been his grandfather.
2 CONT There is a second Daniel Sweet who died in Warwick, Rhode Island in 1728, the exact date is not known. His will is dated 16 November 1727 and proved on 24 April 1728. Mentioned, his children, Daniel (received land eastward of the 
2 CONC mill lying next to property of Ezekiel Hunt), Jeremiah, John (both John and Jeremiah receive the Grist Mill) and Ellin Hunt, wife of Ezekiel Hunt [4] His inventory is taken on 17 April 1728. His will mentions no wife, but his four
2 CONC  children are Daniel, Jeremiah, John, and Ellin Hunt, wife of Ezekiel Hunt.
2 CONT Another will that mentions the names of the children of the above Daniel who died in 1728, is that of Jeremiah Sweet whose will is dated 1731. He named his brother John Sweet, his brother Daniel Sweet, and his brother-in-law, Ezek
2 CONC iel Hunt. In this case, Jeremiah who died in 1731 is the son of Daniel who died in 1728. Daniel who married Ethalenah Carpenter died in 1732.
2 CONT Daniel who married Ethalenah is probably the son of Daniel who died in 1728, and the brother of Jeremiah who died in 1731.
2 CONT Many online trees have very few sources and have the same info as this profile.
2 CONT Where does the nickname "The Millet" come from?--Update: The vital records in Warwick record the birth records of Daniel Sweet's (Warwick) children (Daniel, Eleanor, Jeremiah, and John), he is listed as "Daniel Sweet (Miller)"[5] 
2 CONC The children in this listing corresponds to Daniel Sweet's (Warwick) will that is dated 1727.
2 CONT The daughter Elizabeth is not mentioned in any probates of either Daniel Sweet (Glocester) or Daniel Sweet (Warwick).
2 CONT Jeremiah's will is consistent with his father's Daniel Sweet (Warwick)'s will
2 CONT US and International Marriage Records, 1560 and 1900: Daniel Sweet, b. 1657 marries Eleanor Westcott[6] (consistent with Daniel Sweet (Warwick) married to an Eleanor in the Vital Records of Warwick above.
2 CONT Probate of Ethalanah Sweet in 1775 lists Jeremiah Sweet as Executor of her estate. She names her daughter, Hannah, and four sons, James, Daniel, Jeremiah, and Timothy. She give her homestead that was 79 acres that she received fro
2 CONC m her father to her son Jeremiah. Her will is dated (the day is left blank) December 1734 and proved on 9 February 1774.
2 CONT
2 CONT Daniel Sweet (abt. 1657 - 1732)
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Daniel "The Miller" Sweet===
2 CONT
2 CONT Born about 1657 in Warwick, Kent, Rhode Island
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of John Sweet Jr and Elizabeth (Unknown) Wilson
2 CONT
2 CONT Brother of Richard Sweet, John Sweet, James Sweet, Benjamin Sweet, Henry Sweet, William Sweet, Mary Sweet, Jeremiah Sweet and Elizabeth Sweet
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Ethalenah (Carpenter) Sweet — married [date unknown] [location unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT Father of Daniel Sweet, Eleanor (Sweet) Hunt, Jeremiah Sweet, Timothy Sweet and John Sweet
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 23 Dec 1732 at about age 75 in Gloucester, Providence, Rhode Island
2 CONT
2 CONT
