2 CONT ----
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roger_Williams
2 CONT ----https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/First_Baptist_Church_in_America
2 CONT
2 CONT Roger Williams (c. 21 December 1603 – between 27 January and 15 March 1683)[1] was a Puritan minister, theologian, and author who founded Providence Plantations, which became the Colony of Rhode Island. He was a staunch advocate f
2 CONC or religious freedom, separation of church and state, and fair dealings with American Indians, and he was one of the first abolitionists.[2][3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Williams was expelled by the Puritan leaders from the Massachusetts Bay Colony for spreading "new and dangerous ideas", and he established the Providence Plantations in 1636 as a refuge offering what he called "liberty of conscien
2 CONC ce". In 1638, he founded the First Baptist Church in America, also known as the First Baptist Church of Providence.[4][5] He studied the Indian languages and wrote the first book on the Narragansett language, and he organized the 
2 CONC first attempt to prohibit slavery in any of England's North American colonies.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Son of	Daniel Williams and Rebecca (Rhodes) Williams Husband of	Elizabeth (Carpenter) Williams
