1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Direct Descendant of: [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=19715819 Roger Williams] [1602-1683]
2 CONT ----
2 CONT No children! Peleg Williams II was born in 1719 in Johnston, Providence, Rhode Island. He was the fourth of seven children born to Peleg Williams I (1679 to 1766) and Elizabeth Carpenter (1676 to 1766). His great grandfather was R
2 CONC oger William (1603 to 1683), the founder of Rhode Island.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1745 Peleg married Mary Sheldon in Providence, Rhode Island. They were both twenty-six. Mary Sheldon was born in 1719 in Providence, Rhode Island to the parents of Nicholas Sheldon (1670 to 1747) and Abigail Tilinghast (1674 to
2 CONC  1747). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Peleg and Mary were third cousins. Their common ancestors were Richard Carpenter (1577 to 1625) and Susanna Trivilian (1592 to 1625). Peleg and Mary had eight children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Peleg Williams II and Mary Sheldon: 1. Phebe Williams (1746 to 1836) married James Randall 2. Peleg Williams III (1748 to 1821) married Rhoda Windsor 3. Mary Williams (1754) married Captain Edmund Arrowsmith 4. Sarah W
2 CONC illiams (1758 to 1825) married Robert Angell 5. Elisha Williams (1758 to 1831) 6. Edward Williams (1759 to 1830) 7. Elizabeth Williams (1760) 8. Caleb Williams (1764 to 1839) married Tabitha Fenner
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1757, Peleg was listed in the Ratable Rolls for Providence county, Rhode Island as Peleg Jr. At the time his father was still alive.
2 CONT
2 CONT On the 4th of May 1776, Peleg was the representative from Johnson County in the Rhode Island General Assembly. At that time Rhode Island became the first colony to legally leave the British Empire. Peleg William was one of the sig
2 CONC ners of this document, and thus his descendants are eligible for membership in the Sons of the American Revolution.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the 1790 census, the Peleg William family, which consisted of ten individuals, lived in Johnstown, Providence, Rhode Island. There were four white males under sixteen, one male over sixteen, and five females. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In the 1800 census for Johnson, Providence, Rhode Island, Peleg William lived in a family of two. Both members of the family were over the age of forty-five.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Sheldon died on the 24th of November 1802 at the age of eighty-three. She had Peleg had been married for about forty-seven years. Peleg Williams II died on the 31st of January 1809 at the age of ninety.
