1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A Patriot of the American Revolution for RHODE ISLAND with the rank of PRIVATE.
2 CONT [http://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A046313  DAR Ancestor # A046313]
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Joseph Gorton, son of Samuel Gorton III and Freelove (Mason) Gorton of Warwick Rhode Island, was born 1729, in Swansea, Bristol County, Massachusetts.  His father, Samuel Gorton III, had his first four children born in Warwick, R.
2 CONC I., and Joseph and the last four children were all born in Swansea, Massachusetts.  Ref.: < freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/sallycox/samuelgorton3html >
2 CONT
2 CONT On Jan. 1, 1762 Joseph married Mary Barton, sister of American revolutionary war Gen. William Barton who was responsible for the capture of British Major Gen. Richard Prescott.     Ref.: < freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/sallycox
2 CONC /samuelgorton3html >  and also ref. THE LIFE AND TIMES OF SAMUEL GORTON, with supplemental family genealogy thru 9 generations. page 259, by Adelos Gorton, Philadelphia 1907 
2 CONT
2 CONT REVOLUTIONARY WAR VETERAN:
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Gorton was a Private during the revolution, and served in Captain Squire Millard's company, Col. Waterman's Regiment Rhode Island Militia. Served from Nov.1, 1776 - Jan. 9, 1777. (Ref. "Year Book of the Sons of the Revoluti
2 CONC on in the State of New  York" 1909.
