1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "After Martin WILDMAN's first wife, '''Ann WARD''', died, he married '''Sarah BURGESS PEARSON''' (Pierson/Peirson), the widow of Edward PIERSON (Pearson/Peirson). '''Sarah was born in Styal, a village in Wilmslow P
2 CONC arish, Cheshire, and christened in the Church of England 9 June 1650.''' She was the daughter of''' Edward BURGESS'''. Edward PIERSON was born in the same village of Styal about 1651, but there is no record in the parish register 
2 CONC that he was christened. There is good reason to believe his family had already left the Church of England and (to) become very early followers of George Fox, who was soon to become founder of the Society of Friends or Quakers. Edw
2 CONC ard's father was Lawrence PEIRSON, which is the spelling he used in his 1673 will. '''''Two of Edward's brothers emigrated to Chester County in 1683''''', but Edward, who had married Sarah in a Quaker service, 6 March 1672, stayed
2 CONC  in Cheshire and fathered several children there before going to Chester County PA in 1687. After about a year (and another child born) at Darby in Chester Co, they moved on to the Fallsington area in Bucks County, where several o
2 CONC f Sarah's siblings were already established. Edward died there 3 June 1697. Permission for Sarah and Martin WILDMAN to marry was granted by the Falls Monthly Meeting 2 November 1698, and they apparently married within a few days. 
2 CONC Sarah PEARSON had become Sarah WILDMAN before Edward's estate was probated. Martin WILDMAN was buried in '''Bucks County 26 September 1699,''' as a Quaker. I presume some of Martin's children became sufficiently attached to Sarah 
2 CONC and her children that the PEARSON name was used occasionally by Wildmans. Edward PEARSON was the brother of my 6-greats grandfather."
2 CONT
2 CONT Paul C. Palmer
2 CONT
2 CONT source for marriage to martin wildman: Title: Our Children's Kin Author: Jacquelyn (Erhard) Bean Publication: April 15, 2003 Note: Jacquelyn (Erhard) Bean email: jebean13-hotmail.com (use an "@" for the "-") Repository:  Note: Roo
2 CONC tsweb.com Media: Electronic
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT "After Martin WILDMAN's first wife, '''Ann WARD''', died, he married '''Sarah PEARSON (nee Burgess)''' (Pierson/Peirson), the widow of Edward PIERSON (Pearson/Peirson).<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT ===birth===
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sarah was born in Styal, a village in Wilmslow Parish, Cheshire, and christened in the Church of England 9 June 1650.''' She was the daughter of''' Edward BURGESS'''.
2 CONT Her 1st husband Edward PIERSON was born in the same village of Styal about 1651, but there is no record in the parish register that he was christened. There is good reason to believe his family had already left the England and bec
2 CONC ome very early followers of George Fox, who was soon to become founder of the Society of Friends.  Edward's father was Lawrence PEIRSON, which is the spelling he used in his 1673 will. Two of Edward's brothers emigrated to Chester
2 CONC  County in 1683, but Edward, who had married Sarah in a Quaker service, 6 March 1672, stayed in Cheshire and fathered several children there before going to Chester County PA in 1687. After about a year (and another child born) at
2 CONC  Darby in Chester Co, they moved on to the Fallsington area in Bucks County, where several of Sarah's siblings were already established. Edward died there 3 June 1697.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Sarah, now a widow, marries Martin Wildman===
2 CONT
2 CONT Permission for Sarah and Martin WILDMAN to marry was granted by the Falls Monthly Meeting 2 November 1698, and they apparently married within a few days. Sarah PEARSON had become Sarah WILDMAN before Edward's estate was probated.
2 CONT Martin WILDMAN was buried in '''Bucks County 26 September 1699,''' as a Quaker. I presume some of Martin's children became sufficiently attached to Sarah and her children that the PEARSON name was used occasionally by Wildmans. Ed
2 CONC ward PEARSON was the brother of my 6-greats grandfather."
2 CONT
2 CONT notes of'' Paul C. Palmer''
2 CONT
2 CONT ''source for marriage to Martin Wildman'': Title: ''Our Children's Kin'' ; Author: Jacquelyn (Erhard) Bean : Publication: April 15, 2003 Note: Jacquelyn (Erhard) Bean email: jebean13-hotmail.com (use an "@" for the "-") Repository
2 CONC :  Note: Rootsweb.com Media: Electronic
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Birth:  1657 Cheshire, England  Death:  1698 Solebury Bucks County Pennsylvania, USA 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah Burgis [Burgess] married Edward Pearson on 6 Mar 1671 in Pownall Fee, County Chester, England, according to Friends ceremony.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah Burgis Pearson bore Edward Pearson seven children: Mary, Deborah, Lawrence, Sarah, Enoch(I), Phebee [Phoebe], and Martha.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the death of her first husband, Edward Pearson, Sarah married the widowed Martin Wildman in 1698 in Bucks Co., Pennsylvania. 
2 CONT
2 CONT NOTE: Quakers at times did not mark their graves as they thought it was a sign of vanity.
2 CONT
