2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT [[Category:Philadelphia Yearly_Meeting]] [[Category:Falls Monthly_Meeting,_Pennsylvania]]
2 CONT {{Quakers Sticker}}
2 CONT == Biography == 
2 CONT Lawrence Pearson was born 2 Sep 1677 in Pownall Fee, Cheshire, England<ref>Society of Friends' Registers, Notes and Certificates of Births, Marriages and Burials. Records of the General Register Office, Government Social Survey De
2 CONC partment, and Office of Population Censuses and Surveys, RG 6. The National Archives, Kew, Richmond, Surrey, England. Piece 1398: Monthly Meeting of Cheshire, formerly Morley (1654-1776), Frame 29</ref><ref>Society of Friends' Reg
2 CONC isters, Notes and Certificatesof Births, Marriages and Burials. Records of the General Register Office, Government Social Survey Department, and Office of Population Censuses and Surveys, RG 6. The National Archives, Kew, Richmond
2 CONC , Surrey,England. Piece 1035: Quarterly Meeting of Cheshire and Staffordshire:Cheshire (1631-1799), Frame 22</ref> He is the son of [[Pearson-3095|Edward Pearson]] and [[Burgess-764|Sarah Burgess]].  Sarah's name is spelled Burgis
2 CONC  on all English records of the time. 
2 CONT His arrival date is generally thought to be 1687 however a ships register which includes him has not been located. His father Edward was notlisted on the ship ''Endeavor'' which carried his uncles Thomas and John in 1683.   On 4 J
2 CONC ul 1705, Lawrence and Ann Cooper were given permission by the Falls Meeting to proceed in marriage.  The records do not record the parents of Ann or Lawrence<ref>Swarthmore College; Swarthmore, Pennsylvania; Minutes, 1683-1730; Co
2 CONC llection: Philadelphia Yearly Meeting Minutes; Call Number: MR-Ph 177; Ancestry.com. U.S., Quaker Meeting Records, 1681-1935</ref> His Will was dated 27 July 1752 and proved 17 Mar 1756.<ref>Will Book 2, pg 289, Wills 1713-1906 ; 
2 CONC General Index to Wills, 1682-1939; Bucks County (Pennsylvania). Register of Wills; Probate Place: Bucks, PennsylvaniaWills, Vol 1-2, 1713-1759; Ancestry.com. Pennsylvania, Wills andProbate Records, 1683-1993</ref> The abstract<ref
2 CONC >Pennsylvania County, District and Probate Courts. Abstracts of Wills, 1685-1825; Probate Place: Bucks, Pennsylvania</ref> of the Will states that all lands areto be sold and mentions small sums to grandson Lawrence Pearson, grand
2 CONC son Lawrence Shrigley, granddaughter Mary Allen; John Craft. The residue to daughter Hannah Fenton, daughter Priscilla McKinstry; grandsonsArthur Allen and Enoch Allen; Samuel Armitage and son-in-law Samuel McKinstry are the execu
2 CONC tors. Witnesses: Jos. Doan, Israel Doan, Ester Doan.  Given that no definitive death record has been located (see Research Notes) his death could have occurred any time between 27 Jul 1752 and 17 Mar 1756. 
2 CONT
2 CONT === Death ===
2 CONT :: Date:  17 MAR 1756 :: Place:  Plumstead, Bucks, Pennsylvania [needs citation]
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Research note==Regarding his death, [[Stanton-3547 | T Stanton]] has seen an image ofa Quaker meeting death index dated 1754 with other names indicating it might be this Lawrence Pearson however there is no source listed forthe 
2 CONC image.
2 CONT
