1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Biography==
2 CONT
2 CONT Martha Pearson was born 9 Feb 1687 in Delaware, Pennsylvania.
2 CONT
2 CONT Swarthmore College; Swarthmore, Pennsylvania; Births and Burials, 1682-1835; Collection: Quaker Meeting Records; Darby Monthly Meeting, Call Number: MR-PH-139
2 CONT
2 CONT Hinshaw, William Wade. William Wade Hinshaw's Index to Unpublished Quaker Records. Darby Monthly Meeting Swarthmore,Pennsylvania: Friends Historical Library, Swarthmore College.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her marriage to Nathaniel Bye on 2 Aug 1706 is recorded in the Falls Monthly Meeting minutes but the location is uncertain.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hinshaw, William Wade, et al., compilers. Encyclopedia of American Quaker Genealogy. Vol 2:986
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Research Note==
2 CONT Martha was named in the Will of her husband Nathaniel<ref>Wills, 1713-1906 ; General Index to Wills, 1682-1939; Author: Bucks County (Pennsylvania). Register of Wills; Probate Place: Bucks, Pennsylvania, pp 827-828</ref> who died 
2 CONC 1748/1749.A Quaker record dated Jun 1762 [citation needed] stated that the widowMartha Bye and her son Joseph were in need of care and advice, Josephowing his mother money from principal and interest. No other records have been fo
2 CONC und to give an accurate date of death.  Note that the series Colonial Families of the United States, Mackenzie, George Norbury, and Nelson Osgood Rhoades, editors, contains extensive misinformation on this family.
2 CONT
