1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John Scarborough, II BIRTH	1 Mar 1639 Greater London, England DEATH	21 May 1706 (aged 67) Greater London, England BURIAL	 Bunhill Fields Burial Ground London Borough of Islington, Greater London, England  MEMORIAL 
2 CONC ID	130510117 · View Source
2 CONT
2 CONT MEMORIAL PHOTOS 0 FLOWERS 15 The first of our line to come to America was John Sr. who was born in 1646, a son of John and Anne-----?. John Sr., was born in London and married Sarah Ashby (a daughter of William Ashby) on 22 Februa
2 CONC ry, 1663. John Sr., was also a member of the Peel Monthly Meeting. John Sr. purchased 250 acres on 4 July, 1682 from William Penn, to be laid out in Pennsylvania (this land was located in Langhorne, Bucks County, PA). During this 
2 CONC period of turmoil, John Sr., and his oldest son John sailed to Pennsylvania in 1682 on the "Welcome", a vessel owned by William Penn, and the 19th ship to touch the shores of the new World. (The" Welcome" seems to have been a popu
2 CONC lar vessel and our ancestors may well have been on another ship.) John Sr returned to England in 1684 to get his wife. But she was not a Quaker and would not leave England.
2 CONT
2 CONT Upon arrival, John Sr., who was a blacksmith, a whitesmith and a coachsmith, built a rude shelter in the woods of what is now Bucks Co., Pennsylvania and lived there for two years. At this time he departed for England leaving his 
2 CONC son with Quaker friends. His intent was to return to America, but his wife Sarah refused to leave England. In 1696, John Sr., gave his son John a power of attorney for the land in America. He died in England 21 May, 1706. His will
2 CONC , which was made out in 1696 was witnessed by William Penn.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family Members Parents John Scarborough 1620–1706
2 CONT
2 CONT Anne Scarborough
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse Sarah Ashby Scarborough 1648–1706 (m. 1663)
2 CONT
2 CONT Children Anne Scarborough Singfield 1664–1696
2 CONT
2 CONT John Scarborough 1667–1727
2 CONT
2 CONT William Scarborough 1669 – unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT Susanna Scarborough 1672–1674
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah Scarborough 1674–1674
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Scarborough 1675 – unknown
2 CONT
2 CONT Baldwin Scarborough 1679–1679
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard Scarborough 1680–1680
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/130510117/john-scarborough
2 CONT -------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT "Generation No. 1
2 CONT
2 CONT 	1.  John (II)1 Scarborough  (John (1)A, William (2)B, William (1)C, John or Isaac) was born 1645 in Hosier Lane, London, England, and died 11 Apr 1706 in London, England.  He married Sarah Ashby 22 Feb 1662/63 in St. Brides, Flee
2 CONC t St, London, England, daughter of William Ashby and Susannah ?.  She was born Abt. 1646 in London, England, and died 1684 in London, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT More About John (II) Scarborough:
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: 1706, Burnhill Fields, London, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Immigration: Abt. 1682, Bucks co., PA (but back to England)
2 CONT
2 CONT Occupation: Blacksmith & Coachsmith
2 CONT
2 CONT Wedding: 23 Feb 1662/63,  St. Brides, Fleet St, London, Eng.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of John Scarborough and Sarah Ashby are:
2 CONT
2 CONT 	2	i.	Ann2 Scarborough, born 01 Dec 1664 in London, England; died 27 Sep 1696 in London, England.  She married Richard Singfield.
2 CONT
2 CONT More About Ann Scarborough:
2 CONT
2 CONT Baptism: 01 Jan 1663/64, London, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Occupation: Housewife
2 CONT
2 CONT Wedding: 03 Nov 1686, London, England
2 CONT
2 CONT 	3	ii.	John (III) Scarborough1, born 10 Feb 1666/67 in Hosier Lane, London England; died 27 Jan 1726/27 in Solebury Twp, Bucks Co., PA.  He married Mary Ann Pierson Abt. 1690 in Delaware Co., Pennsylvania; born 20 Jun 1665; died 1
2 CONC 3 Jan 1750/51 in PA ?.
2 CONT
2 CONT More About John (III) Scarborough:
2 CONT
2 CONT Baptism: 26 Dec 1669, St. Sepulchre, Holburn Parish, London
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: 27 Jan 1726/27, Buckingham Fbg., Bucks Co.,. Pa
2 CONT
2 CONT Emigration: 1682, From London England
2 CONT
2 CONT Note:: my 8th gr grand (Lorri French)
2 CONT
2 CONT Occupation:  Farmer, Wheelwright,
2 CONT
2 CONT Source (s):: Ronnie Lee Scarbro
2 CONT
2 CONT More About Mary Ann Pierson:
2 CONT
2 CONT Note:: My gggggggg (Lorri French)
2 CONT
2 CONT Residence: Who are her parents and origins?
2 CONT
2 CONT 	4	iii.	William Scarborough, born 04 Jan 1670/71 in London, England.  He married Elizabeth ?.
2 CONT
2 CONT More About William Scarborough:
2 CONT
2 CONT Baptism: 04 Jan 1670/71, London, England
2 CONT
2 CONT 	5	iv.	Susanna Scarborough, born 09 Mar 1671/72 in London, England; died 15 Jun 1674 in London, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT More About Susanna Scarborough:
2 CONT
2 CONT Baptism: 09 Mar 1671/72, London, England
2 CONT
2 CONT 	6	v.	Sarah Scarborough, born 03 Aug 1674 in London, England; died 15 Aug 1674 in London, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT 	7	vi.	Elizabeth Scarborough, born 17 Oct 1675 in London, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT 	8	vii.	Baldwin Scarborough, born 05 Mar 1678/79 in London, England; died 19 Mar 1678/79 in London, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT 	9	viii.	Richard Scarborough, born 25 Aug 1680 in London, England; died 29 Aug 1680 in London, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT More About Richard Scarborough:
2 CONT
2 CONT Baptism: 25 Aug 1680, London, England
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Birth date of 1639 comes from Parish records of St. Sepulchre in London.
2 CONT
2 CONT The following quoted from "History of Pennsylvania" by Robert Proud (1797):
2 CONT
2 CONT "John Scarborough of London, coachsmith, arrived in this country in 1682, with his son John, then a youth, and settled in Middletown in Bucks County, among the first in these parts, where he remained for two years and then embarke
2 CONC d for his native land with the intention to bring his wife and family ... having suffered much, by persecution for his religion in England, being a Quaker. - - - - - John Scarborough, having placed his son under the care of a frie
2 CONC nd sailed for England but he never returned, his wife, who was not a Quaker, being unwilling to leave her native country, and persecution beginning to cease, he afterwards gave his possessions in Pennsylvania to his son, whom he h
2 CONC ad left in the province; with strict charge when it should be in his power to be kind to the poor Indians for the favors he had received from them, which his son faithfully observed and complied with; and he is said to have been a
2 CONC  worthy man, and of good character."
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT John Scarborough II was born in London in 1649. There he married Sarah Ashby on February
2 CONT
2 CONT 22, 1663. Sarah was not a Quaker, but the children were. John was a coachman and blacksmith
2 CONT
2 CONT by trade like his father. He also was a member
2 CONT
2 CONT of the Peel Meeting.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1682, he accepted William Penn's open invitation to come to America where freedom of
2 CONT
2 CONT religion could be found. He took only his eldest child, John III, on this voyage to America. He
2 CONT
2 CONT purchased, for five pounds, 250 acres along Neshaminy Creek near Langhorne in Bucks County.
2 CONT
2 CONT He purchased the land while in England on July 4, 1682 and arrived in Pennsylvania in October
2 CONT
2 CONT of 1682. He stayed in Bucks County, just north of Philadelphia for almost two years.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1684, he returned to England to get the rest of his family and to return to America. His wife
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah was deathly afraid of the long sea voyage, and they never came back to America. John
2 CONT
2 CONT remained in London until his death on April 11, 1706. As far as I know the rest of the family also
2 CONT
2 CONT remained in England, with only his son John remaining in America.
2 CONT
2 CONT INFO FROM OTHER SITE
2 CONT
2 CONT JOHN SCARBOROUGH, bapt. 1638/9, d 21 2nd month 1706 (11 Apr 1706?), bur. Chequer Alley Burial Ground, Bunhill Fields, London England, m 23 Feb 1663, London to SARAH ASHBY (Register of Marriages, St. Bride’s Church, Fleet Street, L
2 CONC ondon, England). Sarah was born c 1648, London and died there.
2 CONT
2 CONT      John was a blacksmith, whitesmith and a coachsmith. He was a member of Peel MM, 65/67 St. John’s Street, one of the earliest Friends Meeting Houses in London, England. Sarah was not a Quaker. They lived on Hosier Lane, London
2 CONC , England. In July 1682 John bought from William Penn for five pounds, 250 acres along Neshaminy Creek, near Longhorne, Middleton Township, Bucks County, PA. In October 1682, he arrived in America with their son John. In 1684, lea
2 CONC ving their son in America, he returned to London to get Sarah, but she was afraid to cross the ocean and refused to leave. By this time the persecutions of Quakers in England had declined, so he stayed there with her. His will was
2 CONC  made in 1696 and was witnessed by William Penn.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Purchased land in Bucks County Pennsylvania  in 1682
