1 NOTE Residence: Shenandoah Valley, Frederick County, Virginia
2 CONT Residence: Bucks County, Pennsylvania
2 CONT Religion: AFT 1739 Quaker, Opeckon or Hopewell Monthly Meeting, Frederick Co., Virginia
2 CONT Reference Number: 3970
1 NOTE James Haworth:
2 CONT
2 CONT !BIOGRAPHY: Robert G Lowry. FOOTPRINTS. (1978)
2 CONT p. 165. "The Haworths, Scarbroughs, Dillons and Ruckmans" (Chapter 24)
2 CONT James Haworth, our ancestor, was born in 1719 in Pennsylvania anddie dat
2 CONT Hopewell in VA in 1757 at the age of 38. He died shortly after heand his
2 CONT wife Sarah Wood Haworth and their six small children were drivenout of thei
2 CONT home near Smith Creek meeting in Frederick County, VA., by theIndians durin
2 CONT the French and Indian War. It was Sarah who was referred to as the"Widow
2 CONT Sarah Haworth" in the account of that period in an earlier chapter.She was
2 CONT "disowned" shortly afterward for some unknown reason, thenreinstated after
2 CONT furnishing "satisfaction", married a Peter Ruble, and then movedfirst to
2 CONT North Carolina and then to Tennessee, where she died at the age of49, June
2 CONT 20, 1769.
2 CONT
2 CONT !RELATIONSHIP: Wm W H Davis. GENEALOGICAL AND PERSONAL HISTORY OFBUCKS CO.,
2 CONT PA. (1905 reprint 1975) [B174]
2 CONT
2 CONT !RELATIONSHIP: Louise Baker, Virginia Schneider and Aletha Thomas,compilers.
2 CONT ANCESTORS AND DESCENDENTS OF JOEL AND SARAH (MCKEE) HAWORTH - PIONEERSTO
2 CONT PRESENT DAY LYON CO., KS. (1978) [B175]
2 CONT
2 CONT !RELATIONSHIP: William W Hinshaw. ENCYCLOPEDIA OF AMERICAN QUAKERGENEALOGY.
2 CONT (Ann Arbor, MI:Author, 1950) [B046]
2 CONT Vol. 6 "Virginia"
2 CONT p. 399. "Hopewell Monthly Meeting"
2 CONT Hayworth
2 CONT 1739, 6, 6. James gct Hopewell MM, Va. by Buckingham MM, Pa."whither he
2 CONT intends to rem"; also something concering his brother,John, who
2 CONT is placed under the care of his brother, Absalom [JamesHaworth]
2 CONT
2 CONT !RELATIONSHIP: Louise Baker & Virginia Schneider & Aletha Thomas,compilers.
2 CONT ANCESTORS AND DESCENDENTS OF JOEL AND SARAH (MCKEE) HAWORTH--PIONEERSTO
2 CONT PRESENT DAY LYON CO., KS. (1978) [B175]
2 CONT In 1739, James and his bro. John left PA and went to VA.
2 CONT
2 CONT !RELATIONSHIP: Elaine Rowlands. WILLIAM HUNT AND SARAH MILLS, THEIRANCESTORS
2 CONT AND OURS, ESSAYS AND GENEALOGIES. [B249]
2 CONT p. 73. James b. Oct 10, 1719, d. 10 Oct 1757, md Mar 11, 1743.
2 CONT
2 CONT !RELATIONSHIP: THE RIDGE RUNNERS.
2 CONT Vol. 15-1. 1982.
2 CONT p. 50.
2 CONT
2 CONT !RESEARCHER: Galen Hinshaw file 1982.
2 CONT FGS of Stephanus Haworth and Rachel Beeson--
2 CONT James Haworth (George & Sarah Scarborough Haworth) m Sarah Wood;
2 CONT their son, James married Mary Rees
2 CONT their son, Jonathan b 1797/98 d 1867 m1 Sarah McPherson; m2 EsterEvans (dt
2 CONT Evan & Patience Evans) in 1827.
2 CONT ch: Isaac Evan m1 Deborah Carey (dt Yenus &Lydia Hawes Carey)
2 CONT m2 Louisa wood
2 CONT Joel Rees m Mahala Mendenhall
2 CONT William P b 6/29/1828; d 11/14/18__; m1 Huldah Carey b 1815 d8/9/1902
2 CONT (dt Yenas and Lydia Haines Carey); m2 7/2/1903 ElizabethAnn Davis
2 CONT Hinshaw (wd of Elias Hinshaw
2 CONT --
2 CONT James Haworth m Sarah Wood
2 CONT Their son, George m Susannah Dillon
2 CONT Their son, James m Rachel Wright
2 CONT Their son, Eli m Lydia Dillon
2 CONT Their son, Wm Perry Haworth (minister, KS Y: Mtg Spt) m AbigailChowner. He
2 CONT grandfather of Gerald Wood - Frnds Univ of Helen Wood's letter
2 CONT 11/20/1980.
1 NOTE From Cecil O'Dell's "Pioneers of Old Frederick Co., VA", Published by Walsworth Publishing Co., Marceline, MO, 1995: p. 198 - "On 17 Nov. 1752, James Hayworth (who moved to Virginia in 1739) received a 227-acre Fairfax grant on Gr
2 CONC eat Spring Branch of
2 CONT Back Creek.  It was surveyed on 26 April 1751.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 4 August 1755, James and wife Sarah sold 227 acres to Thomas Doster for 60 pounds.
2 CONT
2 CONT James was deceased by 1759 and his wife Sarah moved to BUSH RIVER QUAKER MONTHLY MEETING IN NEWBERRY COUNTY SOUTH CAROLINA in 1768.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 10 Oct. 1768, their daughter Jemima and John Wright (son of John--son of James and Rachel Wright) were married in Berkeley County, South Carolina.
2 CONT
2 CONT Absalom Hayworth (a son?) was deceased by 2 June 1752 when his will was proved in Frederick County Court with witnesses John Lewis, BENJAMIN INMAN and John Rubel."
