2 CONT
2 CONT ==Will Abstract==
2 CONT 3.122.  '''John Fisher of Buckingham'''.  12th mo., 15th day, 1756.<br/>
2 CONT    Proved March 13, 1765.<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Son''' Robert (Exr.), Lands in Buckingham and Plumstead.  '''Sons''' Robert, Joseph, Barak and Samuel.  '''Daus.''' Mary Butler, Sarah Michener, Elizabeth Stradling.   '''Hannah Preston''' and Deborah and Katharine Fisher.<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT Wit: Mathew Beans, Jos. Skelton, Paul Preston.
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of:
2 CONT - JOHN FISHER (b. 1671, Barmstone, East Riding, Yorkshire, England; d. 1765, buried Buckingham Burial Ground, Bucks County, PA)
2 CONT - ELIZABETH SCARBOROUGH (b. 1700, Buckingham Twp, Bucks Co., PA, d. 1740, burial Buckingham Burial Ground, Bucks County, PA)
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of John & Elizabeth are believed to be:
2 CONT 1. Robert FISHER, b. 19 Sep 1720, Solebury, Bucks Co., PA, d. 29 May 1784
2 CONT 2. Sarah FISHER, b. 11 Apr 1722, Plumstead, Bucks Co., PA , d. 6 Jun 1812, West Grove, Bucks Co., PA
2 CONT 3. John FISHER, b. 25 Dec 1723, Buckingham Twp, Bucks Co., PA , d. 9 Jun 1752, Buckingham Twp, Bucks Co., PA
2 CONT 4. Elizabeth FISHER, b. 14 Sep 1725, Bucks Co., PA , d. 6 Jun 1812, New Garden, Chester Co., PA
2 CONT 5. Hannah Scarborough FISHER, b. 13 Jun 1727, Buckingham Twp, Bucks Co., PA , d. 13 Jan 1822, Bucks Co., PA
2 CONT 6. Joseph FISHER, b. 29 Sep 1729, Bucks Co., PA , d. 1819, Clarkson, Columbiana Co., OH
2 CONT 7. Deborah FISHER, b. 5 Mar 1733/34, Buckingham Twp, Bucks Co., PA , d. 27 Jun 1822, Fairfield, Highland Co., OH
2 CONT 8. Katherine FISHER, b. 29 May 1740, Solebury, Bucks Co., PA, d. 1827
2 CONT 9. Barak Scarborough FISHER, Sr., b. 19 Apr 1736, Buckingham Twp, Bucks Co., PA , d. 26 Mar 1784, Clearbrook, Frederick Co., VA
2 CONT 10. Samuel FISHER, b. 29 May 1738, Buckingham Twp, Bucks Co., PA , d. 1784, Baltimore, Baltimore Co., MD
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT Below details are from http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=:1175025&id=I0100:
2 CONT
2 CONT ID: I0100
2 CONT Name: Hannah Scarborough FISHER
2 CONT Sex: F
2 CONT Birth: 13 APR 1727 in Bucks Co., Pa
2 CONT Death: 13 JAN 1822 in Bucks Co., Pa
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Bucks County Births, 1682-1800,
2 CONT Hannah Fisher born 13 4 mo 1724
2 CONT Parents: John and Elizabeth Fisher
2 CONT Records of Buckingham Friends Monthly Meeting
2 CONT
2 CONT Roger S. Boone, Some Quaker Families, Scarborough/Haworth, Vol 1, p.21
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah Fisher, daughter of Elizabeth Scarborough and John Fisher lived to be 100 years old.
2 CONT
2 CONT She married 21 Nov. 1753 Paul Preston born circa 1722 Buckingham Twp, Bucks Co., PA, died 1806 at his home 84 years old, Plumstead Twp, Bucks Co., PA, the son of Amor Preston.
2 CONT
2 CONT Paul was a farmer, surveyor, mathematician, and linguist. In 1753 he bought 50 acre farm in Buckingham Twp. where they lived until 1792 when he bought a 130 acre farm on Durham Rd. near Gardenville, Plumstead Twp, Bucks Co., PA. H
2 CONC e was one of the executors of Robert Fisher's estate. Hannah and Paul had issue, all born in Buckingham Twp, Bucks Co., PA:
2 CONT
2 CONT - Deborah Preston, died unmarried, a Quaker
2 CONT - Samuel Preston, born 1756, died 1834 Wayne Co., PA, where he was the first associate Justice. He was a Quaker.*
2 CONT - Ann Preston, died unmarried, a Quaker
2 CONT - Naomi Preston, born 1750, married James Price. She was a Quaker.
2 CONT - Eupemia Price. unmarried, a Quaker.
2 CONT - Paul Preston, a Quaker**
2 CONT - Silas Preston, married Margaret Good
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son, Samuel Preston, land agent for Henry Drinker of Philadelphia, who's most notable efforts was to survey and open the first road by hand (May to September 1789) between the Delaware & Susquehanna Rivers, between Stockport, PA
2 CONC  and what is known today as Lanesboro, PA. Afterwards he established Stockport where he resided the balance of his life.
2 CONT
2 CONT **Son, Paul Preston, born Mar 10, 1767. Bucks County Births, p. 231. Married Sarah Stradling of Plumstead Twp on Nov 19, 1804. Publications of Genealogical Society of Pa. Vol 3, p. 71; Bucks County Patriot, Nov 20 and 27, 1804, Bu
2 CONC cks County Newspaper Marriage Notices, Bucks Co. Gen. Soc.
2 CONT ---
2 CONT Gravesite Details
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah's husband, Paul, has a cemetery record but none for Hannah. She may, or may not be interred within this cemetery. If she was interred here, her grave is unmarked today.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Find a Grave, database and images (https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/169450452/hannah-scarborough-preston: accessed 11 May 2023), memorial page for Hannah Scarborough Fisher Preston (13 Apr 1724–1824), Find a Grave Memorial ID 
2 CONC 169450452, citing Buckingham Friends Cemetery, Lahaska, Bucks County, Pennsylvania, USA; Maintained by NancyM (contributor 47862230). 
