1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT William was born in 1753.
2 CONT In 1762, the court ordered the Church Wardens of Russell Parish to "bind out Rachel, William, James, Kiziah, and Isaac, children of Rob Scarborough."  According to law, this could be done when parents were too poor to care for the
2 CONC ir children. About 1797, William and his brothers, James and David moved to Knox Co., TN. (David was on the tax list for 1805).
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage 1 Mahala "Milly" WOOD b: ABT 1755
2 CONT
2 CONT Children : William SCARBOROUGH b: ABT 1775 : James SCARBOROUGH b: ABT 1777 : Jonathon Lupton SCARBOROUGH b: ABT 1780
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
2 CONT <references/> See also:* http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=demeaux&id=I436 Author: Bob Fields <a href="/wiki/Scarborough-2048" title="Scarborough-2048">Scarborough-2048</a> and Scarborough-222 appear to rep
2 CONC resent the same person because: Same birth date/location and name. Middle names were uncommon in the mid 1700's. Scarborough-2048 contains no other identifying information or sources. Author: Mikaela Renz-Whitmore <a href="/wiki/S
2 CONC carboro-14" title="Scarboro-14">Scarboro-14</a> and Scarborough-222 appear to represent the same person because: Same name, dates, parents. Clear duplicate.
