2 CONT Note from NSDAR Database:  "THE MILITARY SERVICE PROBABLY BELONGS TO MAN RESIDING IN AMELIA CO OR  CHESTERFIELD CO; THIS MAN WAS A QUAKER."
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Many Quakers did fight in the American Revolution - some were 'disowned' by their meetings for it, some were not. A Quaker who had been disowned could still attend meetings - there are no rituals to be denied. It was also possible
2 CONC  to be taken back into the meeting if, after consulting with the Elders, the person admitted "seeing the error of their ways" and promising not to do it again.
