1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Married to Thomas Bills on 03 Oct 1672 in Barnstable, Barnstable Co, MA. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna Twining was born about 1652[1] in Eastham, Massachusetts[1]. Anna was the older sister of Joanna Twining who married Thomas Bills after Anna's death.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the first wife of Thomas Bills whom she married on 3 Oct 1672[2]. They had two children together, Anna (b Jun 1673) and Elizabeth (b 23 Aug 1675)[3][4][5]. It would appear the birth of daughter Elizabeth brought about her 
2 CONC mother's death one week later for Anna Bills died 1 Sep 1725[3][1]. Unverified information states that she is buried in the Cove Burying Ground, Eastham, Barnstable, Massachusetts.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Twining-434
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna Bills formerly Twining
2 CONT
2 CONT Born about 1652 in Eastham, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of William Twining Jr and Elizabeth (Deane) Twining
2 CONT
2 CONT Sister of Elizabeth (Twining) Rogers, Susanna Twining, William (Twining) Twinning III, Joanna (Twining) Bills, Mehitable (Twining) Doane and Stephen Twining
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of Thomas Bills — married 3 Oct 1672 in Eastham, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother of Anna (Bills) O'Killey and Elizabeth (Bills) Andrews
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 1 Sep 1675 [location unknown]
2 CONT
2 CONT Profile last modified 6 Dec 2018 | Created 1 Aug 2018
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna Twining was born about 1652[1] in Eastham, Massachusetts[1]. Anna was the older sister of Joanna Twining who married Thomas Bills after Anna's death.
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the first wife of Thomas Bills whom she married on 3 Oct 1672[2]. They had two children together, Anna (b Jun 1673) and Elizabeth (b 23 Aug 1675)[3][4][5]. It would appear the birth of daughter Elizabeth brought about her 
2 CONC mother's death one week later for Anna Bills died 1 Sep 1725[3][1]. Unverified information states that she is buried in the Cove Burying Ground, Eastham, Barnstable, Massachusetts.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ 1.0 1.1 1.2 Shotwell, A.M., Genealogical Annals of our Colonial Ancestors, Lansing, MI, 1895, https://archive.org/details/annalsourcoloni00shotgoog ↑ Town and City Clerks of Massachusetts. Massachusetts Vital and Town Records. P
2 CONC rovo, UT: Holbrook Research Institute (Jay and Delene Holbrook). Births, Marriages, Deaths, 1643-1714 Town Records, 1736-1855; Vol· 1 ↑ 3.0 3.1 Eastham Massachusetts Vital Records, Vol I, Pt II, p 4 of original record, transcribed
2 CONC  by George Bowman, The Mayflower Society, 1976 ↑ Bill, Ladyard, History of the Bill Family, New York, 1867, https://archive.org/details/historyofbillfam1867bill ↑ Town and City Clerks of Massachusetts. Massachusetts Vital and Town
2 CONC  Records. Provo, UT: Holbrook Research Institute (Jay and Delene Holbrook).Orleans and Eastham Records Erroneous Information
2 CONT
2 CONT Hills, Leon Clark, History and Genealogy of the Mayflower Planters, Vol II, Hills Pub Co, Washington, 1936-41 erroneously lists Anne as having had a second husband following Thomas which would be impossible as she passed away. It 
2 CONC appears he confuses mother Anne with the daughter Anna who married David O'Kelley (O'Killey).
