2 CONT
2 CONT William Twinning III formerly Twining
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 28 Feb 1654 in Eastham, Barnstable, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of William Twining Jr and Elizabeth (Deane) Twining
2 CONT
2 CONT Brother of Elizabeth (Twining) Rogers, Anna (Twining) Bills, Susanna Twining, Joanna (Twining) Bills, Mehitable (Twining) Doane and	Stephen Twining
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Ruth (Cole) Twining — married 21 Mar 1689 in Eastham, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Father of Elizabeth (Twining) Bassett, Thankful (Twining) Mayo, Ruth (Twining) Higgins, Hannah Twining, William Twining IV, Barnabas Twining and Mercy Twining
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 23 Jan 1735 in Eastham, Barnstable, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Profile last modified 30 Jan 2019 | Created 11 Jun 2010
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT William(3) Twining (William2, William1) was born 28 FEB 1654 in Eastham.[citation needed].
2 CONT
2 CONT He married 23 Mar 1689 Ruth Cole, b 1668, d aft 1735, dau of John and Ruth (Snow) Cole of Mayflower stock.
2 CONT
2 CONT While his father and some of his siblings became Quaker and removed to Pennsylvania, William remained in Eastham, devoting his life to agricultural pursuits.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Twining genealogy states that “very little is known of this steadfast Puritan”. I guess they deemed him a steadfast Puritan by the fact that he stayed in Eastham and didn’t become a Quaker and move to Pennsylvania.
2 CONT
2 CONT William made his will in 1725 and gave to his wife Ruth one third of the personal estate during her widowhood. He gave his sons William and Barnabas all his lands and meadows they to comfortably support “my sd wife during the term
2 CONC  of her widowhood”. Ruth and the two boys each got one bed and beding, his daughter Hannah a bed and furniture and one cow and his daughter Mercy one cow. “And forasmuch as my daus Elizabeth, Thankful and Ruth have heretofore had 
2 CONC each a bed and bedding, and each a cow, I therefore give all the rest of my personal estate, in equal proportion unto my natural children namely, my two sons and five daughters”.
2 CONT
2 CONT The inventory included:
2 CONT
2 CONT Land at Smith’s Neck............................................£320 Land of the homestead..........................................800 Dwelling house, barn and shop............................120 Meadow at Boat Meadow & Rock Harb
2 CONC or.............56 Meadow at Poche Flats............................................25 Poche High Flats, 1/3 and 1/2 lots..........................30 Four small wood lots adjacent................................19 Also included wer
2 CONC e an ox, a bull, 2 cows, 4 heifers, one old and one young horse, 14 poor sheep, 3 swine, as well as coopers, joiners and turners tools, a spinning wheel, spokes for cart wheels, coons in a barrel, money scales, beef, pork, molasse
2 CONC s and money was due the estate from Barnabas and William Twining. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Eastham vital records:
2 CONT
2 CONT William Twining Junior and Ruth Cole wear Maried the 21th of March:1688/89 William Twining Junior a daughter borne Named Elizabeth agust: 25th 1690 Thankfull Twining the daughter of William and Ruth Twining was Borne the eleventh:
2 CONC  day: of January in the year: 1696: 7 Ruth: Twining the daughter of William and Ruth Twining was Borne at Eastham: the Seaven and twentieth day of august in the year 1699 Hannah the daughter of William and Ruth Twining was born th
2 CONC e 2d day of April 1702 William Twining the Son of William and Ruth Twining was Born at Eastham the Secund day of September in the year 1704 Barnabas Twining the Son of William and Ruth Twining was Born at Eastham the twenty ninth 
2 CONC day of September in the year of our Lord 1705 Mercy Twining the Daughter of William and Ruth Twining was born at Eastham the 20th day of febuary anno 1707/8 [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Alt Birth from Merge
2 CONT
2 CONT 25 Jan 1654
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth, b 25 Aug 1690; m. Oct 1716 Joseph Merrick Jr; children: Reuben, prob m Abigail Higgins 1733; Mercy July 1717; probably m Ephraim Cook 1735 Thankful, b 11 Jan 1697; d 28 Aug 1779; m Apr 1719 Jonathan Matho, b abt 1694; d
2 CONC  Eastham May 1768. Children. Ruth b 27 Aug 1699; m Oct 1719 Joshua Higgins, Jr. 11 children. Hannah b 2 Apr 1702; m abt 2 Jun 1731 David Young, both of Eastham; she may have m2 Nathanial Snow, Jr 26 Feb 1767. William4 b 2 Sep 1704
2 CONC ; m. 21 Feb 1728 Apphia Lewis (still alive 1776); family tradition states that he was a lawyer and practiced at Orleans, Massachusetts; made will 1769, probated shortly after his death 17 Nov 1769. Barnabus, b 29 Sep 1705; m Hanna
2 CONC  Sweet Mercy, b 20 Feb 1708; m David Higgins of Eastham Oct 15, 1725. Six children. Children of William III Twining and Ruth Cole are: i. Thankful Twining, b. 11 Jan 1696, Eastham, Barnstable Co., MA, d. 28 Aug 1777, Eastham, Barn
2 CONC stable Co., MA. ii. Ruth Twining, b. 27 Aug 1699, d. date unknown. iii. Hannah Twining, b. 02 Apr 1702, Eastham, Barnstable Co., MA, d. date unknown. iv. William Twining IV, d. date unknown. v. Barnabas Twining, b. 29 Sep 1705, Ea
2 CONC stham, Barnstable Co., MA, d. 05 Mar 1766. vi. Mercy Twining, b. 20 Feb 1707, d. date unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
