3 CTRY Colonial America
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Not the same as https://www.geni.com/people/John-Young-Jr/6000000003938327477
2 CONT
2 CONT Colonel John Young Sr 1624-1691
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother: Joan Ann Harris Jentilman (Herington)
2 CONT B:1594 Great Yarmouth, Norfolk, , England
2 CONT D:25 Dec 1632 Southwold, Suffolk, , England.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage: 13 December 1648 Plymouth, Plymouth, Massachusetts Bay, British Colonial America
2 CONT
2 CONT Abigail Howland 1629-1692
2 CONT
2 CONT ====Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Young-400
2 CONT
2 CONT John YOUNG was born in England say 1615 and settled in Plymouth, Massachusetts.  He had a grant of land in Plymouth, October 31, 1638, and November 21, 1639,  as per town of Salem records. His name appears on the list of those abl
2 CONC e to bear arms in 1643. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married, December 13, 1648, Abigail Howland. [...] 
2 CONT
2 CONT He settled in Eastham about 1650, died January 29, 1690/1.  His will, dated January 19, 1688; proved April 21, 1691; bequeathed to wife Abigail and children John, Joseph, Nathaniel, David, Robert (2), Henry and three daughters.  T
2 CONC he widow's estate was divided April 19, 1692.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of John (i) and Abigail (Howland) Young: 
2 CONT
2 CONT # John, born at Plymouth, November 15, 1649, married Ruth Cole; 
2 CONT
2 CONT # Joseph, born November 12, 1651, died December, 1651; 
2 CONT
2 CONT # Joseph, born December, 1654, married Sarah Davis; 
2 CONT
2 CONT # Nathaniel, born April, 1656, married Mercy Davis; 
2 CONT
2 CONT # Mary, born April 28, 1658, married Daniel Smith; 
2 CONT
2 CONT # Abigail, born October, 1660, married Stephen Twining; 
2 CONT
2 CONT # David, born April 17, 1662, married Anne Doane; 
2 CONT
2 CONT # Lydia, born 1664; 
2 CONT
2 CONT # Robert (2), born August, 1667. mentioned below: 
2 CONT
2 CONT # Henry, born July, 1669, died April 30, 1670; 
2 CONT
2 CONT # Henry, born March 17, 1672, married Sarah.
2 CONT
2 CONT Reference:  Page 2684 of the book - [http://books.google.com/books?id=FM8UAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA2684#v=onepage&q&f=false  "Genealogical and personal memoirs relating to the families of the state of Massachusetts" Vol. 4] By William Richar
2 CONC d Cutter, William Frederick Adams Published by Lewis Historical Pub. Co., 1910 Item notes: v. 4 original from Harvard University
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Estate
2 CONT The will of John Young, Senior, of Eastham, was made 19 January, 1688/9, and proved 21 April, 1691. Wife Abigail Young and son Henry Young were to be executors. Bequests were made as follows: To "wife Abigail young my whole estate
2 CONC  Real and personal during ye time of her widdohood" To "my Son John young five acres of upland Lying neare ye south side of ye Cove Comonly Called youngs Cove"; To "my two sons Joseph and Nathaniel young ten shillings a peece" To 
2 CONC "my Son David young all that upland that is mine where he now lives" To "my Son Robirt young that parcel of upland which I bought of Thomas paine except one small field called ye point ffield against Timothy Coles and one Bed and 
2 CONC Beding" To "my son Henry young all my housing and all that upland thatI bought of John mayo and ye point field before excepted Lying against Timothy Coles"; To "my Three Daughters five shillings a peece"; "Capt Sparrow and Daniel 
2 CONC Done Ser and Benjamin Higgins to be my over Seers to be assistent to my executors" The will was signed by a mark. The witnesses were Benjamin Higgins, Richard Higgins, Ichabod Higgins (who made his mark) and Joshua Higgins. Richar
2 CONC d and Ichabod Higgins were the only witnesses present when the will was probated.
2 CONT
2 CONT "An Invintory of ye estate of John young of Eastham deceased on ye 29th of January Last and taken ye 3 of ffebruary 1690:91" by Jonathan Sparrow and Benjamin Higgins. Among the items are: "one Scoue and Canow" "housing and Land" £
2 CONC 55. "Abigail young vid Relict of John young" made oath to the inventory 21 April, 1691. The will and inventory were recorded 30 April 1691, by Joseph Lothrop, Recorder.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Disputed Origins & Merge Warnings
2 CONT
2 CONT Merge Warnings: There are multiple John Young(e)s in early colonial America.
2 CONT
2 CONT This John Young:
2 CONT *was not the son of John Youngs/Yonges and Joan Jentilman.
2 CONT *not the son of John Young and Marie Sharpe
2 CONT *not the son of John YONGES and Joan Herrington, who was born 10 Apr 1623 and died, 12 Apr 1698 in Southold, Suffolk, New York, and married Mary Gardner abt 1653 and Hannah Anne Wines abt 1691.
2 CONT * not a known husband of [https://www.geni.com/people/Elisabeth-Young/6000000089242593903 Elisabeth (Bellamy) Young] (1625 - abt. 1647)
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT *Clarence A. Torrey, [http://jrm.phys.ksu.edu/Genealogy/Needham/d0003/I3423.html "New England Marriages Prior To 1700"]: "YOUNG, John (-1691) & Abigail HOWLAND (1630-1692); 13 Dec 1648, 1647; Plymouth"
2 CONT *George Ernest Bowman, "Plymouth Colony vital records," in Mayflower Descendant, various volumes. Transcribed form marriages appearing in the Court Orders, and from "Marriages, Births and Burials" George Ernest Bowman, "Eastham Ma
2 CONC ss., Vital Records," in Mayflower Descendant, various volumes, Also printed in Leonard H Smith Jr & Norma H. Smith, Vital Records of the Towns of Eastham and Orleans, 1976.
