2 CONT
2 CONT John Young was born on 16 Nov 1649 in Plymouth, Massachusetts to John Young and Abigail (Howland) Young. He is the  brother of George Young, John Young [half], Thomas Young, Joseph Young, Joseph Young, Nathaniel Young, Mary (Young
2 CONC ) Smith, Abigail Young, David Young, Lydia (Young) Murdock, Robert Young, Henry Young and	Henry Young. He married  Ruth Chase (Cole) Bangs on 16 Nov 1669 in Eastham, Barnstable, Massachusetts. He is the father of Benjamin Young, R
2 CONC uth (Young) Brown and Barnabas Young. John died before 19 Jun 1717 in Eastham, Barnstable, Massachusetts.  Profile managers: Jillaine Smith and Kerry Fisher Profile last modified 29 Dec 2018 | Created 1 Mar 2011
2 CONT
2 CONT Categories: Eastham, Massachusetts | Plymouth, Massachusetts.
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT John Young was born November 16, 1649, the son of Reverend John Young, Sr and Abigail Howland of Plymouth, Plymouth Colony[1] [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT He was noted in his father's will, dated April 30, 1691[3] When his mother died in 1692, her portion of the estate was passed to sons John, Joseph and Henry[4] November 16, 1669, he married Ruth Cole, daughter of Daniel and Ruth C
2 CONC ole of Eastham[5] [6][7] [8] [9] [10]
2 CONT
2 CONT John and Ruth Young signed an agreement with Ruth's sibling's to divide her father Daniel Cole's estate on 15 Jan 1694/5 that gave the homestead to Thomas Cole. Ruth had received things in her father's lifetime and after his death
2 CONC  received 12 lbs, 19s[11] John's estate notes his wife Ruth, children, and their Grandfather Daniel Cole[12] He died about 19 Jun 1717 in Eastham, Barnstable Co., Massachusetts. His estate was probated 23 Apr 1718[13]. Administrat
2 CONC ion of estate granted to widow Ruth and son Jonathan. The agreement on the division of his estate was concluded on July 18, 1719[12]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children
2 CONT
2 CONT Some children's dates are earlier than those in Langlais's "Young Family." Eastham is assumed but not proven.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mercy[12], b. 14 Apr 1671, Plymouth, who married Micajah Snow[14], 
2 CONT
2 CONT and who d. Bef 25 Dec 1753, Eastham, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Benjamin[12], b. 1673, Eastham, who married Sarah Snow[8], and who died Sep 1734, Eastham, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Jonathan[12], b. Abt 1680, Eastham, Plymouth Colony d. Abt 1755, Billingsgate (Eastham), Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Israel[12], b. 1686, (Eastham, Plymouth Colony), who married Catherine Frost in 1708[15], and who d. 25 Oct 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1760, Billingsgate (Eastham), Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Ruth[12], b. 1688, Eastham, who married Samuel Brown in 1708[16], and who d. 28 Sep 1768, Wellfleet, Massachusetts Barnabas[12], b. 1690, Eastham, Massachusetts, who married Rebecca Young, daughter of Nathaniel and Mercy (Davis) Y
2 CONC oung, and then married Ann Snow, daughter of John Snow and widow of Leonard Pike[17], and who d. 3 Aug 1772, Wellfleet, Massachusetts Jane[12], b. Abt 1692, Eastham, who married Isaac Perce[18], and who d. Bef Dec 1746, Billingsga
2 CONC te (Eastham), Massachusetts Abigail[12], b. Abt 1693, Eastham, who married John Treat, son of Samuel Treat on December 16, 1716[19], and who d. Yes, date unknown Sources
