2 CONT
2 CONT Sister of George Young, John Young [half], John Young, Thomas Young, Joseph Young, Joseph Young, Nathaniel Young, Mary (Young) Smith, Abigail (Young) Twining, David Young, Robert Young, Henry Young and	Henry Young
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of John (Murdock) Mordoch — married 10 Dec 1686 (to before 1719) in Plymouth, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Mother of Jeremiah Murdock, John Murdock and Thomas Murdock
2 CONT
2 CONT Died about 1719 in Plymouth, Plymouth, Province of Massachusetts Bay] uncertain] ]
2 CONT Profile last modified 15 Jan 2020 | Created 14 Sep 2010
2 CONT
2 CONT Possible Confusion
2 CONT
2 CONT In February of 2017, with the permission of all known stakeholders, Lydia Young, the wife of Samuel Hatch, and Lydia Young, the wife of John Murdock, were merged. As I performed research to revise the merged profile, I discovered 
2 CONC that it represented an impossibility, that the two men must have married two different women named Lydia. Here are some findings:
2 CONT
2 CONT There are near-original records stating that the wife of John Murdock is Lydia Young. The only near-original record that I can find states that the wife of Samuel Hatch is "Lydia ____". Whether the Lydia Young who married John Mur
2 CONC dock is the Lydia Young who was born in 1664 in Eastham is probable but not certain. "Lydia" is a very common name in Plymouth Colony during this period. There was more than one Lydia Young in Plymouth Colony, including a Lydia Yo
2 CONC ung who married a Hatch (but not this Samuel Hatch). Accordingly, in March of 2017, I revised this profile to separate Lydia Young (wife of Murdock) from Lydia ___ (wife of Hatch).
2 CONT
2 CONT JWM, profile manager
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Lydia Young was born in 1664 to John Young and Abigail Howland. [1] [2] [3] [4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Lydia Young married John Murdoch on 10 Dec 1686 in Plymouth, Plymouth Colony. [2] [5] [6] [7] Together they had eight children, during the period from 1687 through 1701, but only three survived to adulthood.
2 CONT
2 CONT Childen born Plymouth:[8]
2 CONT
2 CONT John, b. 13 Dec 1687, d. 8 Jan 1687/8 Janet/Jonat, b. 3 Feb 1689, d. 24 Apr 1697 John, b. 8 Jun 1691 James, b. 13 Jun 1693, d. 11 Mar 1693/4 Robert, b. 14 Mar 1696/7, d. 28 Jul 1699 Robert, b. 8 Oct 1699, d. Nov 1699 James, b. 14 
2 CONC Jan 1694/5 Thomas, b. 19 Nov 1701 Lydia died between 1701 (birth of last child) and 1719 (John's remarriage).[9]
2 CONT
2 CONT An entry on FindAGrave states that Lydia Young Murdock died in 1719 and was buried at Burial, Hill, Plymouth, Massachusetts Bay. [10]
2 CONT
2 CONT Research Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT As mentioned above, Lydia (Young) Murdock is listed in Find-A-Grave and is shown buried at Burial Hill, Plymouth, Plymouth County, Massachusetts. [10] Another entry on Find-A-Grave states that Lydia (Young) Hatch died 10 Apr 1724 
2 CONC and was buried in Falmouth. [11] The confusion is created because both entries claim that each Lydia refers to the daughter of John Young. The second one is incorrect because the daughter of John Young married John Murdock, not Sa
2 CONC muel Hatch. Furthermore, the date of death given by the second would be five years after Murdock remarried.
2 CONT
2 CONT The following comment represents an opinion on how to treat the confusion:
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the name presented on profile, (Lydia (Young) Murdock) should be the only name sourced here. If the other "Lydia (Young) Hatch" entry on Find A Grave Memorial #59390421, is incorrect, then WikiTree profile manager(s) 
2 CONC need to address this issue to the memorial manager on Find A Grave and bring it to their attention. I personally do not know anything about this person nor could not find any other reference source, or I would contact the memorial
2 CONC  manager(s) myself. [12]
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
