2 CONT ↑ Ancestry.com Boards, "Surnames > Howland > wife of Zoeth Howland", post by Roger Howland, 21 Oct 2005, archived 24 April 2017. ↑ Source: #S74 ↑ Source: #S74 Source: S648 Title: Eileen McKinnon-Suggs (suggs1 >at< msn.com), Our Ki
2 CONC ngdom Come (http://awtc.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=emsuggs&id=I39737 Last updated October 10, 2004 Accessed December 2, 2005) Source: S942 Title: RE: wife of Zoeth Howland & early Howland line, Lisarog >at< pacbell.net
2 CONC , http://boards.ancestry.com/mbexec?htx=message&r=an&p=surnames.howland&m=711.1.1.1 Text: The date of the marriage of Abigail to John Young is in dispute. According to Howland's History, this Abigail married Young on 2 9m [Novembe
2 CONC r] 1678, a date not found in any records relating to Abigail and one too late to accord with her being called Abigail Young in her mother's will of 1674. Howland's alleged date is the one found in the Friends Records for the marri
2 CONC age of an Abigail Howland to Richard Keerby (see Abigail, widow of No.2, Zoeth Howland). The names of some of the children born to John Young and wife Abigail (e.g., Joseph, Henry, and possibly Robert) are Howland names and re com
2 CONC patible with a presumption that the mother was a daughter of Henry Howland; but if she were, Abigail was married many years earlier. A likely record of the marriage is the previously cited one in 1684. Extensive information is ava
2 CONC ilable on the family, both published and unpublished. A quick review of the Youngs in Plymouth Colony, made by the the authors Wakefield and Sherman, suggests that this John is the only Young in the colony likely to be Abigail's h
2 CONC usband. Note: This is a decently sourced out report with lots of potential for further study. Source: S74 Title: IGI - International Genealogical Index Subsequent Source Citation Format: IGI - International Genealogical Index Ance
2 CONC stry Family Trees Text: http://trees.ancestry.com/pt/AMTCitationRedir.aspx?tid=4478194&pid=-90599885 Acknowledgments
