2 CONT 4 Acknowledgements
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry Young was born on March 17, 1672 on Cape Cod, on his father's land "Young's Cove," between Eastham and East Orleans, Barnstable, Plymouth Colony, New England. Plymouth and Massachusetts Bay colonies united in 1691, forming t
2 CONC he Province of Massachusetts. Henry's parents were Rev. John Young, b. ca. 1623/24 in England, and his wife, Abigail (Howland) Young, b. 1628 in England.
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry Young married Sarah Snow, b. Feb. 26, 1673, in Eastham, Barnstable, Massachusetts, in about 1694 in Eastham. They had 5 children together before Henry's untimely death on April 26, 1706.[1][2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Martha Young b: 28 Jul 1695 in Eastham, Barnstable, MA
2 CONT Elizabeth Young b: 8 Jan 1697/1698 in Eastham, Barnstable, MA
2 CONT Reliance Young b: 3 Mar 1699/1700 in Eastham, Barnstable, MA
2 CONT Moses Young b: 15 Nov 1702 in Eastham, Barnstable, MA
2 CONT Thomas Young b: 24 Oct 1705 in Eastham, Barnstable, MA
2 CONT Henry Young died in Young's Cove, Eastham (East Orleans), Barnstable County (Cape Cod), Massachusetts, on April 26, 1706. He is buried in the Old Cove Burying Ground, Eastham, Massachusetts.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT "Cape Cod Library of Local History and Genealogy" pg. 477 - 478:
2 CONT
2 CONT John Young came to Eastham before 1659. He was a resident of Plymouth in 1643, and his name appears that year among those liable to do military duty. So far as can be now ascertained, his place of residence was in what was called 
2 CONC by the Indians, Pochet or Poche, and now called East Orleans. He was a planter and had but little to do with town affairs while a resident of Old Eastham. He was not of that class called "Town-purchasers."
2 CONT The old records of Eastham show he was a considerable landholder, and that some of his land was obtained by purchase. He had ten acres at Poche, as early as 1659, adjoining George Crisp's land, the purchase of which was confirmed 
2 CONC by the town. His purchase of five acres between Young's Cove and the highway whyt goeth at the end of Richard Sparrow's ground, this year was also confirmed by the town. In 1676, he bought of Thomas Paine, for f9 [9 Pounds], fifte
2 CONC en acres of upland on the westerly side of "Young's Cove."
2 CONT According to the records, he [John Young] died 25 Jan. 1690, and his wife Abigail, 7 April 1692. No stones with inscriptions mark their resting place. "Goodman" Young died testate and his will is on record at Barnstable. He had el
2 CONC even children, two of whom died in infancy.
2 CONT GENEALOGICAL REGISTER of PLYMOUTH FAMILIES, APPENDIX, PART II, page 295:
2 CONT YOUNG, JAMES, m. Rebecca Shepard, and had Mary, 1723.
2 CONT JOHN, m., 1648, a wife Abigail, and had John, 1649. He removed to Eastham, and had Joseph, 1654; Nathaniel, 1656; Mary, 1658, m. Daniel Smith; Abigail, 1660, m. Stephen Twining; David, 1662; Lydia, 1664; Robert, 1667; Henry, 1669;
2 CONC  and Henry again, 1672.
2 CONT From: Post-em note from Wanda < 6/18/2006 [4]
2 CONT
2 CONT His parents were Henry b. 17 Mar 1671/72, Eastham, m. 1694, Eastham, Sarah Snow, b 26 Feb 1672/73, Eastham. Henry's parents, John Young (came here as a very young man), m. 13 Dec 1648, Plymouth, Abigail Howland, b. abt. 1628 in En
2 CONC gland. Abigail's parents were Henry [Howland] b 25 Nov 1604, Fenstanton, Huntingdonshire, England, and m. abt. 1626 in England and Mary, b Abt. 1609 England. There is no proven last name for Mary no matter how many times you see N
2 CONC ewland. Henry is the brother of John but did not arrive here [New England] till about 1632.
2 CONT Research Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Fitzgerald's family genealogy says:[5]
2 CONT John Young and Abigail Howland (This information is taken from the Bridgewater Vital Records and Barnstable Vital Records MA and the achiever from the Sturgis Library, Barnstable MA). Thomas Young came here as a very young man. Jo
2 CONC hn left all to his wife in his will.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ Ancestry of Carol Austin - Sarah Snow. This family genealogy has 26 primary & secondary source references.
2 CONT ↑ Births, marriages, deaths, 1649-ca.1840; intentions of marriage, 1700-ca.1905, database with images, FamilySearch (https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3QSQ-G979-9XB1 : 3 October 2022), FHL microfilm 007009735, image 154,
2 CONC  Eastham, Massachusetts, Volume 2, Births, & Deaths, 1654-1797, Page 94.
2 CONT ↑ Find A Grave Memorial# 51539366 - Henry Young
2 CONT ↑ BANFILL-BUCK-HAWKINS-PIKE-PERRINE Tree - Thomas Young
2 CONT ↑ Ancestors of Mayflower Descendant, Robert E. Fitzgerald John Young
2 CONT See also:
2 CONT
2 CONT "Cape Cod History of Local History and Genealogy: A Facsimile Edition of 108 Pamphlets Published in the Early 20th Century:" Vol. no. 32, "Early Settlers in Eastham," Book 2, on CD. By Josiah Paine, Esq., of Harwich; compiled by L
2 CONC eonard H. Smith, Jr. Genealogical Publishing, Baltimore MD, 1992, Original Date, 26 Aug 1916.
2 CONT Find A Grave Memorial# 51539366 - Henry Young
2 CONT #S155 Ancestry Family Trees http://trees.ancestry.com/pt/AMTCitationRedir.aspx?tid=4478194&pid=-90599883
2 CONT S942 Abbreviation: RE: wife of Zoeth Howland & early Howland line, Title: RE: wife of Zoeth Howland & early Howland line, , http://boards.ancestry.com/mbexec?htx=message&r=an&p=surnames.howland&m=711.1.1.1 Text: The date of the ma
2 CONC rriage of Abigail to John Young is in dispute. According to Howland's History, this Abigail married Young on 2 9m [November] 1678, a date not found in any records relating to Abigail and one too late to accord with her being calle
2 CONC d Abigail Young in her mother's will of 1674. Howland's alleged date is the one found in the Friends Records for the marriage of an Abigail Howland to Richard Keerby (see Abigail, widow of No.2, Zoeth Howland). The names of some o
2 CONC f the children born to John Young and wife Abigail (e.g., Joseph, Henry, and possibly Robert) are Howland names and re compatible with a presumption that the mother was a daughter of Henry Howland; but if she were, Abigail was mar
2 CONC ried many years earlier. A likely record of the marriage is the previously cited one in 1684. Extensive information is available on the family, both published and unpublished. A quick review of the Youngs in Plymouth Colony, made 
2 CONC by the authors Wakefield and Sherman, suggests that this John is the only Young in the colony likely to be Abigail's husband. CONT Note: This is a decently sourced out report with lots of potential for further study. TMPLT TID 0 F
2 CONC IELD Name: Footnote VALUE RE: wife of Zoeth Howland & early Howland line, , http://boards.ancestry.com/mbexec?htx=message&r=an&p=surnames.howland&m=711.1.1.1 FIELD Name: ShortFootnote FIELD Name: Bibliography Repository: #R73 TMPL
2 CONC T FIELD Name: Page
2 CONT Repository: R73 Name: Ancestry.com
