3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU Miller
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} " Joseph Wood, a native of Chester County, Pa., settled in earlylife in Berkeley County, Va. In 1783 he purchased land on Hogue Creek in Frederick County and there erected a flour mill. In 1787 he removed to one of
2 CONC  the Parkins mills which he operated for some years. In 1804 he purchased land on Red Bud Creek,about four miles northeast of Winchester, where he erected a large mill and lived until his death in 1815. Joseph Wood was much esteem
2 CONC ed amoung Friends and was active in the development of the milling industry in early days."
2 CONT
2 CONT -from Hopewell Friends History, page 169-170
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Link''':http://wc.rootsweb.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=rswayne&id=I4041
2 CONT
2 CONT RESIDENCE: Received at Hopewell from Pipe Creek MM in 1779; Granted certificate from Hopewell to Crooked Run MM in 1798;
2 CONT
2 CONT RELIGION: Joseph and wife Rachel disowned in 1781 at Hopewell; Joseph requested to be reinstated in 1785 at Hopewell. Committee appointed to visit him. He has married contrary to discipline. Request dropped; Reinstated in 1798 at 
2 CONC Hopewell;
2 CONT
2 CONT Hinshaw, Wm. Wade, Ency. of Amer. Quaker Gen. Vol. 6 pg. 416, 457, Hopewell Records.
2 CONT --------------------
