1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Civil War Veteran'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Mustered in: Aug. 17th at Cairo, Ill.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Co.: H
2 CONT
2 CONT * Regiment:: 16th
2 CONT
2 CONT * Division: Illinois Infantry/ Army Corp
2 CONT
2 CONT * Mustered out: August 16, 1864/ Rome Georgia
2 CONT
2 CONT Fredrick Sheetz Allen
2 CONT BIRTH	19 Oct 1839
2 CONT Monticello, White County, Indiana, USA
2 CONT DEATH	11 Jul 1913 (aged 73)
2 CONT Junction, Hampshire County, West Virginia, USA
2 CONT BURIAL	
2 CONT Headsville Methodist Episcopal Church Cemetery
2 CONT Keyser, Mineral County, West Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/21352743/fredrick-sheetz-allen
2 CONT
2 CONT _________________________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Frederick Sheetz Allen served as a soldier in the Civil War. He enlisted at Cario, Ill, August 17, 1861 and discharged at Rome, GA August 16, 1864. In the Union Army was a member of Company H 7th Regiment Illinois Infantry 16th Ar
2 CONC my Corps. His corps including the 13th, 15th, and 17th, corps composed what was designated as the Army of the Tennessee. This army fought in every State of the Southern Confederacy, except Texas, Florida, and Virginia, and did suc
2 CONC ceed in cutting the confederacy twice in two. The following Major Generals commanded (Major US Grant, Major WT Sherman, Major James B McPherson, Generals John A. Logan, General O. O. Howard, General G. M. Dodge. This army had 82 e
2 CONC ngagements from November 7, 1861 to April 9, 1865 (a total of men killed wounded - mortally wounded, captured and missing was 57,413 men in the four years service. As an army the army of The Tennessee never sustained a single defe
2 CONC at during the four years of war. Every fortification which it assailed surrendered, every force arrayed against it was either defeated, captured or destroyed. No officer was ever assigned to the command of that army who had afterw
2 CONC ards to be relieved from it or to be reduced to another command. Such a history is not accident.
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Link''':https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/2:2:33PG-9GK
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: Death date listed as July 18, 1912 on pension payment record; Middle name is sometimes recorded as Shultz due to unusual spelling of mother's maiden name ( Sheetz)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
