1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ''' https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/17359652/anna-cook ''''''Biography'''
2 CONT
2 CONT ANNA SUMNER, born April 1, 1803 at Westfield actually in Stokes County. Died Sept. 1, 1869 and buried at Bear Creek Cemetery near Earlham, Iowa. She married (first) Aug. 24, 1822, near the Fall Creek Friends Meeting, Rainsboro, Pa
2 CONC int Township, Highland County, Ohio to Isaac George. (Anna's brother, Martin Sumner was the great-grandfather of George W. Moore) Second marriage was Nov. 21, 1831, probab1y at the Fairfield Friends Meeting, Camby, Marion County, 
2 CONC Ind., to John Conk, who had formerly married Sept. 11, 1817 to Mary Furnas, horn Nov. 2, 1796, near the Cane Creek Friends Meeting, Snow Camp, Alamance County, N.C. Children of Isaac and Anna George: Sidney, Evan and Adin.  More A
2 CONC bout Anna Sumner and Isaac George: Marriage: 24 Aug 1822, fall Creek Friends Meeting, Rainsboro, Paint Twp., Highland Co., OH.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: Anna married John Cook. Spelled incorrectly on profile.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===========================================
2 CONT
2 CONT From entry for Isaac George:
2 CONT
2 CONT  Married Anna Sumner, born Apr. 1, 1803, at Westfield, Stokes Co., N.C., daughter of Joseph and Abigail Jessup Sumner, and the granddaughter of Thomas and Hannah Hiatt Sumner. The Hiatts came to Philadelphia with William Penn on h
2 CONC is second voyage. They were supposed to have come to England from France in 1066. Anna Sumner's brother, Martin Sumner was the great-grandfather of George W. Moore of Seattle, Wash., who has provided all of this information. After
2 CONC  the death of Isaac George, Anna married John Cook.Children of Isaac and Anna Sumner George were: Abigail, Sidney, Evan, and Adin. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Link''': http://www.genealogy.com/ftm/g/i/l/Margaret-A-Gilmore/WEBSITE-0001/UHP-0212.html
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Link''': http://archiver.rootsweb.ancestry.com/th/read/SC-BUSHRIVERQUAKERS/2009-08/1249766153
2 CONT
2 CONT Added by D.Glenn
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
