0 @I6000000022148438396@ INDI
1 NAME Joseph /Starbuck/
2 GIVN Joseph
2 SURN Starbuck
2 _MARNM Starbuck
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 8 FEB 1811
2 ADDR
3 CITY Barnesville
3 STAE Ohio
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 27 APR 1844
2 ADDR
3 CITY Pennville
3 STAE Indiana
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU Fuller/ Manufacturer of cloth
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Joseph married his wife's sister, Rachel, after Grace died. Marriage to Rachel listed as "after November,1836"
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph and Rachel both died in 1844, leaving their children orphaned. Rachel's family took them to raise.
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Recorded as written:
2 CONT
2 CONT The father of our subject was a native of New Jersey, born February 8, 1811 and died April 27, 1844. By vocation he was a fuller and manufacturer of cloth. He was a man of strong personality and unswerving integrity and a active a
2 CONC nd successful business man. His ancestors were of Welsh origin and were located on the island of Nantucket because of religious persecution in the mother country. They were Quakers, or Friends, in religious belief and this creed o
2 CONC r doctrine has permeated all their American posterity. They have always been active in church work and have been instrumental, in many instances, in the establishment and maintenance of the church of their ancestors. As citizens t
2 CONC hey have been active and progressive, cheerfully lending their aid to worthy enterprises of moral or educational character. Many of the family attained positions of national distinction, though it is not a characteristic of the Qu
2 CONC akers to be aggressive in political life. John G Whittier, the noted Quaker poet, is a direct descendant of the Starbuck family. The founder of the family on American soil was a captain of a ship on the Atlantic who retired from t
2 CONC he ocean in middle life. His posterity have been largely devoted to agricultural or mechanical pursuits The father of our subject was twice married, his wives being sisters. His first was not the mother of our subject. The father 
2 CONC and mother of our subject were married in Highland county, Ohio and all their married life was spent in the Buckeye state. The mother was born about 1819. She died in young womanhood in 1844.and little is known of her chacteristic
2 CONC s except that she was a kind and indulgent mother and a devout Christian lady. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source:Source: Biographical Memoirs of Jay County Indiana; Chicago;: B.F. Bowen Company Publishers; 1901; Page 352'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Link:https://books.google.com/books?id=Rk80AQAAMAAJ&pg=PA352&lpg=PA352&dq=joseph+starbuck+married+rebecca+lupton&source'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Information compiled by D, Glenn
