2 CONT _______________________________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Biography:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT  John M., the second in order of birth, has been a resident of Iowa since he was a youth of sixteen. During the Civil war he enlisted in the Twentieth Iowa Infantry and served three years at the front. Returning from the war, he e
2 CONC ngaged in mechanical pursuits as a contractor and builder. During the early excitement over the finding of gold in Alaska, he joined a party and went to the Klondyke country and was among the first white men to explore the present
2 CONC  site of Nome City.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source:''': Bioigraphical Memoirs of Jay County Indiana; Chicago;: B.F. Bowen Company Publishers; 1901; Page 352
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Link''':https://books.google.com/books?id=Rk80AQAAMAAJ&pg=PA352&lpg=PA352&dq#v=onepage&q&f=false
