1 OCCU Professor of art; American Artist and photographer
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Los Angeles Express, Tuesday, January 12. 1909; pg. 6 
2 CONT
2 CONT The approach of the birthday anniversary of Lincoln brings to light the fact that a historical oil portrait of the martyred president, on which the late Senator John J. Ingalls is said to have placed a value of $10,000, is owned i
2 CONC n Los Angeles. It is the property of Col. T. W. Eckert, who lives at 526 West Avenur Fifty-Three.
2 CONT
2 CONT The portrait was painted by John Lupton in Lebanon, Illinois immediately after Lincoln was assasinated in 1865. Colonel Eckert tells an interesting story of how it came to be painted.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lupton, who has been dead for many years, was proffesser of art in McKendree college at that time, and won a high reputation for his work.
2 CONT
2 CONT "On the day following the assassination of Lincoln," says Colonel Eckert, "I called at Mr. Lupton's studio and round him, like scores of others in that little town, almost prostrated with grief over the calamity which had fallen t
2 CONC he nation. On his easel before him was a large canvas which he gazed upon with more than ordinary interest. Running his long, bony fingers nervously through his hair, which hung well down upon his shoulders, he said, " If the insp
2 CONC iration does not fail me, my masterpiece will be placed upon that canvas.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Who will be your subject?" I asked. "Abraham Lincoln, the martyr," was his reply. "Until this is completed," he added, "no other work will be done in this studio. and no other thoughts shall occupy my mind." 
2 CONT
2 CONT For weeks Mr. Lupton was lost to his former associates, and his recitation room in McKendree college was abandoned for the time. His whole purpose, he said, was to "bring to life the ideal statesman."
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Link''':https://archive.org/stream/artistsofllinc/artistsofllinc_djvu.txt
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT J. Lupton was John Lupton b,. 24 July 1833; d. 9 Nov. 1897 He was the son of Joseph Ambrose Lupton; He was an American artist and photographer; married Louise Dufor and had three children Ralph, Abigail and a dau. Nellie died in i
2 CONC nfancy.His family was part of the LUPTONIAN issue we did on John Lupton the actor. I think it was No.57
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Link''':http://www.genealogy.com/forum/surnames/topics/lupton/654/
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Sale of Bust of Lincoln'''
2 CONT
2 CONT LUPTON, JOHN. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Meserve 87, bust, bearded, 1866.  Once in possession of Thomas W.  Eckert.
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Link'''http://archive.org/stream/artistxx00linc/artistxx00linc_djvu.txt
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ART DEPARTMENT PROFESSOR JOHN LUPTON: This well known artist has been elected to the hall of this de partment. Prof. Lupton has a wide reputation and his election insures the success of the Department. The Prof. is skilled in Flor
2 CONC al Landscape and Portrait Painting, He will give lessons in Oils, Water Colors. Monochromotics &c. He is also prepared to teach Photography and India Ink Portrait Drawing.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source:Catalogue of the Officers and Students; By McKendree College 
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Link''': https://books.google.com/books?id=ryNHAQAAMAAJ&pg=PA87&lpg=PA87&dq=mckendree+college+lebanon+illinois+professor+john+lupton&source=bl&ots=z820buH9v8&sig=NXnc37ViJFoGP4TlS6iqkoO0ByE&hl=en&sa=X&ved
2 CONT
