1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From: http://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/a/y/l/Roger-F-Aylard/WEBSITE-0001/UHP-0013.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Leah Hiatt (daughter of John Hiatt and Margaret Nichols) was born Abt. 1819 in Wayne Co., Indiana, and died March 13, 1855 in Highland Co., Ohio. She married Robert K. Barr on January 17, 1833 in Wayne Co., Indiana, son of John Ba
2 CONC rr and Austin.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Notes for Leah Hiatt: Leah Hiatt was born in North Carolina of English ancestry. She married Robert K. Barr, a son of John Barr by a first marriage to __?__Austin, and stepson of her mother, Margaret (Nickols) (Hiatt) Barr. He wa
2 CONC s born in Pennslyvania. They were married in Wayne Co. Ind. and had three children. (1) John Hiatt Barr (my great grandfather. wfs.) (2) Jezreel Decatur Barr (a) John Barr died at age 21 (b) Opal Barr ( Mother's "cousin Opal"wfs) 
2 CONC (3) Louisa Jane died at five of scarlet fever shortly after her father's death of cholera in 1844 (? 1847) while he was on a business trip to Pittsburg. Leah moved from Wayne Co. to Penn Twp., Jay Co. Ind. in 1949 where she taught
2 CONC  a subscription school and took in sewing. As soon as they were old enough, the boys went to work with Jezreel living with an uncle in Jay Co. She was remarried to a Joseph Lupton on Nov 10, 1851. The Luptons had been very promine
2 CONC nt and wealthy members of the region around Pennville, Indiana. A first child of that marriage died in infancy, and the marriage ended in divorce after a second child, Margaret or Abigail Margaret Lupton, was born. That child was 
2 CONC kept by the father, and was raised by her half sister, Rachel Lupton. Leah died in Highland Co., Indiana soon after the divorce. She had apparently gone there to be with her mother Margaret (Nickols) (Hiatt) (Barr) Stafford.
2 CONT
2 CONT More About Leah Hiatt and Robert K. Barr: Marriage: January 17, 1833, Wayne Co., Indiana.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Leah Hiatt and Robert K. Barr are:  +John Hiatt Barr, b. March 06, 1839, Wayne Co., Indiana, d. October 10, 1907, Old SoldiersHome, Dayton, Ohio.
