1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Civil War Veteran'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Affiliation: Union
2 CONT
2 CONT Enlistmant Rank: Pvt.
2 CONT
2 CONT Discharge Rank: Corp.
2 CONT
2 CONT Co.: B
2 CONT
2 CONT Reg.: 38th Iowa (consolidated with the 34th Iowa)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT From History of Bremer Co., Iowa:
2 CONT
2 CONT Isaac Barrick, son of J.T. Barrick, settled in Bremer County, Iowa, with his family in 1849. Isaac was born in Highland county, Ohio, January 25, 1834. In 1849 he came to Bremer county with his parents, and has since made it his h
2 CONC ome. During the second year of our late rebellion, he enlisted in Company B, 38th Iowa Infantry, and served until its close. He participated in the siege and capture of Vicksburg and also in the charge on Fort Blakesly. During his
2 CONC  term of service he crossed the Gulf of mexico four times. His regiment was consolidated with the 34th Iowa before the close of the war. Mr. Barrick was mustered out at Houston, Texas, and discharged at Davenport, Iowa.  On the 19
2 CONC th day of December, 1865, he was united in marriage with Miss Elizabeth Wagoner of LaPorte, Indiana. They have three children - Emeline, Georgiana, and Edwin. Mr. Barrick owns 160 acres of land, which is under excellent cultivatio
2 CONC n and valued at $50 per acre. He is a member of the Presbyterian Church. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source'':'History of Butler and Bremer Counties, Iowa; Union Publishing Co. Springfield, Ill.; 1883
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Link''': https://books.google.com/books?id=G1A0AQAAMAAJ&q=john+t+barrick#v=snippet&q=john%20t%20barrick&f=false
