1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Joel H. Lewis has Thomas B. Poston listed as Thomas B. Lewis sources are 1870 and 1880 U.S. Federal Census living in household of Joel H. Lewis is Thomas B. Lewis. Should not have been listed as Thomas B. Lewis. Ce
2 CONC nsus takers made mistake or was most likely given wrong information from neighbors. Ellen Catherine Lewis Poston is also reported by well resepected genealogy researchers to be listed as Annie Lewis on those same 1870 and 1880 U.S
2 CONC . Federal Census records. Thomas Benton Poston and his wife Ellen C. Lewis Poston were living with Joel H. Lewis, Ellen's grandfather. Thomas Benton Poston married Joel H. Lewis' grandaughter, Joseph E. Lewis is Joel H. Lewis' son
2 CONC . The daughter of Joseph E. Lewis is Ellen Catherine Lewis Poston, who married Thomas B. Poston. Ellen C. and Thomas B. Poston were staying with Joel H. Lewis when the U.S. Census takers were taking Census in 1870 and 1880. These 
2 CONC are facts. The same facts as Pauline Rash, who was the only Poston family member that would go to Sanford and identify their father, Lewis Erastus Poston.
