1 NOTE {geni:about_me} > Isaac OATES arrived in Highland County as a young boy of fifteen from Hampshire County, Virginia, with his parents Peter and Rachel (LUPTON) OATES. He had seven brothers and one sister with him. His father was a 
2 CONC blacksmith by trade and died at the age of forty-eight. Isaac was married on October 24, 1861 to Catherine M., daughter of Henry and Rebecca (Parker) RHODES. He lived three years in Liberty Township before moving to Washington and
2 CONC  later to Paint Township. He then lived in Ross County until 1891 at which time he purchased a farm consisting of 355 acres lying on the Petersburg Pike eight miles from Hillsboro. Mr. and Mrs. OATES had five children :
2 CONT
2 CONT #  William ;
2 CONT
2 CONT #  Annie, wife of Anderson McKINNEY ;
2 CONT
2 CONT #  Laura, wife of Marion WILLIAMS ;
2 CONT
2 CONT #  Gertie, wife of William TOMPKINS ;
2 CONT
2 CONT #  and Philip.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Marion WILLIAMS taught school in Petersburg for many years and was the town's
2 CONT notary public until his death,. (Wm Schubert farm)
