1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *========================== From [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=56894930 FindAGrave memorial]:  Obituary of John W. Yonally; The Abilene Daily Reflector Saturday, October 5, 1940
2 CONT
2 CONT John W. Yonally was born at Marietta, Ohio, December 9, 1861, and passed away at his home, six miles northwest of Abilene, Kansas, at eleven o'clock Wednesday morning, October 2, 1940, following a short illness.
2 CONT
2 CONT He came with his family to Kansas in the spring of 1871, and came to Abilene, Kansas, April 15 of that year, and has resided in Dickinson county ever since.
2 CONT
2 CONT He united in marriage with Harriet E. Clemence, March 11, 1885, with Elder Clark officiating. His wife passed away December 28, 1907.
2 CONT
2 CONT There were born to this union one son, Frank, who passed away November 16, 1937; two daughters, Mrs. William J. Mauldin of the home, and Mrs. Henry J. Kohler of Arboles, Colorado. He is survived by two grandsons and three granddau
2 CONC ghters; two sisters, Mrs. Louisa Sherman of Lansing, Kansas, and Mrs. Mary Caulk of Abilene, Kansas; two brothers, Charley of Abilene and Fred of Wichita, Kansas; a brother-in-law, Joseph R. Clemence of Abilene; also many nieces a
2 CONC nd nephews living in Kansas an in other states.
2 CONT
2 CONT He purchased the present home in 1899, and lived for 41 years. He farmed his land every year, and was always busy when able to work. He was of a quiet disposition and loved his home, and was always ready to help a neighbor or frie
2 CONC nd. He never said an unkind word about another. He was a kind and loving father, and will be greatly missed by those of his family and immediate neighborhood, and his kind words and deeds will be remembered.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services were held at his home northwest of Abilene, Kansas, Friday afternoon, October 4, 1940, and were conducted by Dr. David Townley, pastor of the First Presbyterian church of Abilene. Music was furnished by Mrs. Charl
2 CONC es E. Hooper and Mrs. Harold Howland. Interment was in the Abilene cemetery.
2 CONT *==========================
