1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Marry Elizabeth Owen, who was born on November 8, 1861, in Robertson County, TN, died on January 28, 1933.  She was married to James P. Morris on June 24, 1879.  To this union was born two children:  Mrs. W. T. Mar
2 CONC tin and B. O. Morris, Sr., both survive her.  She was converted early in life.  She was not long in her Kentucky home until she removed her membership to Pleasant Hill.  It was largely through her energy and liberality that the fi
2 CONC rst Methodist Church of Sulphur was built, of which she became a charter member.  In 1918 she was an untiring worker in erecting the second Sulphur Methodist Church (the first having been destroyed by fire). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Western Recorder Newspaper (Southern Baptist)  January, 1933
2 CONT
2 CONT
