1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Jesse James Coleman, 73, former magistrate of District No. 2, died suddenly at 3:30 p.m.,
2 CONT
2 CONT Thursday, January 1, 1942 at his home near Sulphur.  He had been to Sulphur, where he was shaved, returned home to attend to his cattle, when he suffered a heart attack.  He was a member of the Sulphur Baptist Church, New Castle M
2 CONC asonic Lodge and Sulphur Lodge I.O.O.F.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services were conducted at 10:30 a.m., Sunday, at the Sulphur Baptist Church, with Rev. Tatum, pastor officiating.  Burial was in the Sulphur Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is survived by six daughters: Mrs. Elizabeth Foree, Sulphur, Mrs. Gertrude Colter, Sulphur, Mrs. Mary Willie Garriott, Salvisa, Mrs. Minnie Ruth Morris, Sulphur, Mrs. Darnell Shy, Tyrone and Mrs. Mildred Garriott, Sulphur; two 
2 CONC sons: John O. Coleman and Ellis Coleman, both of Sulphur; one half-sister: Mrs. Ethel Ford, Louisville; twenty-five grandchildren and eight great-grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry County Local  January 9, 1942
