1 NOTE {geni:about_me} W/O Laban Elizabeth Parker Utterback (Mrs. Laban Utterback) 
2 CONT
2 CONT On Wednesday evening, July 31, the angel of death visited the home of David UTTERBACK and claimed his aged mother. Before noon she called her granddaughter, Julia, to her bedside and told her she couldn't stand her suffering much 
2 CONC lonqer. Later in the day she told her daughter-in-law she was nearly dead. At about eight o'clock the final summons came and Aunt Betsy crossed over the dark river to a land beyond the grave. She was nearly 91 years old. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The entire community extend their heartfelt sympathy to the bereaved ones. May they meet her in the shining portals of glory. She had been in a helpless condition for nearly five years, but she bore her great suffering with patien
2 CONC ce and meekness and her every want was supplied with care and pleasure by her son and family. And now they have this consolation--they did their duty. 
2 CONT
2 CONT News, Aug. 8, 1895 
