2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Catharina and Joseph attended the Holy Trinity (Old Swedes) Church in Wilmington, Delaware. Three of their children were baptized at this oldest and quaintest church in the nation. A complete list of the children of Joseph and Cat
2 CONC harina has never been found. The nine children listed were compiled from the court and county records of Orange County, North Carolina. The sixth child (a female, name unknown) was born about 1722.
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: The identity of Catharina Cantrell's parents has never been established: she was not a Heath. Records of her children could not have been compiled by  the Orange County North Carolina Court: she never lived in North Carolina
2 CONC . 
2 CONT
2 CONT Her known children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT James b. circa 1719 Hannah b. circa 1720
2 CONT
2 CONT John 1724 - 1803 DAR Ancestor Number A018946 (reference: dar.org: membership not required to access the DAR GRS.) Note: His named was simply John Cantrell. Miller was his occupation. To distinguish him from the several other men i
2 CONC n the area named John Cantrell, locals called him "Miller John." Reference Find A Grave Memorial Number 110842689.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph  1726 - 1804  DAR Ancestor Number A018949 Zebulon 1728 - 1780 married Sarah Montgomery, DAR Ancestor Number A132693
2 CONT
2 CONT Isaac      1733 - 1805 Birth name: Isaac Cantrell  Occupation: Baptist Minister. Reverend Cantrell's children were documented in a lawsuit. He willed his estate to his third wife, Mary Linder Cantrell, and the children of that uni
2 CONC on. Peter Cantrell, son of a different wife, sued the estate for his portion and named all children fathered by Rev. Cantrell. Reference Find A Grave Memorial 31250529.
2 CONT
2 CONT It is very important that we correct our family trees and any information online so we do not perpetuate misinformation.      
