2 CONT
2 CONT In 1724, John Miller Cantrell entered the world in New Castle, Lawrence, Pennsylvania, United States, born to Joseph Cantrell And Catherine Heath. In 1790, John Miller Cantrell resided in Spartanburg, South Carolina, United States
2 CONC . John Miller Cantrell married Hannah Jane Brittain, and had children including Aaron Cantrell, Abraham Cantrell, Benjamin Cantrell, Brittain Cantrell, Charles Cantrell, Daniel Cantrell, Edward Cantrell, Elijah Cantrell, Jacob Can
2 CONC trell, John James Miller Cantrell, John Cantrell, Joseph Cantrell, Moses Cantrell, Peter Cantrell, Reuben Cantrell, Simon Cantrell, Stephen Cantrell, Susan Cantrell Hannah, Thomas Cantrell, Thomas J Cantrell, William Cantrell. Joh
2 CONC n Miller Cantrell passed away in 1803 in Chesnee, Spartanburg County, South Carolina, USA.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/110842689/john-cantrell
2 CONT
2 CONT John “Miller John” Cantrell
2 CONT Birth
2 CONT 6 Oct 1724
2 CONT New Castle, Lawrence County, Pennsylvania, USA
2 CONT Death
2 CONT 11 Feb 1803 (aged 78)
2 CONT Spartanburg, Spartanburg County, South Carolina, USA
2 CONT Burial
2 CONT Buck Creek Baptist Church Cemetery
2 CONT Chesnee, Spartanburg County, South Carolina, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Message: He had NO middle name. He was a MILLER by trade. His parents were not psychic: they did not name him Miller and then he became a miller.
2 CONT
2 CONT He owned a mill thus was a miller. Since "John Cantrell" was a common name in the area, locals referred to him as "Miller John" to differentiate him from others with the same name. Through the decades, the "Miller John" has morphe
2 CONC d into Miller as a middle name.
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Miss Brittian and Jane. 1st Spouse: Hannah Brittian (1725-1769)
2 CONT
2 CONT "John Cantrell, Sr., was a miller and Baptist Minester. He helped establish the Buck Creek Baptist Chruch in Buck Creek, Sportanburg Co., South Carolina. He served as Pastor from 1800 to 1803. John is burried in Cantrell Family Ce
2 CONC metery. John had a brother by the name of Isaac Cantrell who was also a Baptist preacher at Buck Creek Baptist Church. The Cantrell Cemetery is near the the Buck Creek Baptist Chruch: Information from: Earnest H. Cantrell, Route 1
2 CONC , Box 50, Beaverton, Al. 35544, (1989)'".
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT John was in Rockingham Co NC before the Revolution. He later moved to Spartanburg Co SC, where he owned over 800 acres on Buck Creek in the 96th District. One of the first members of the Buck Creek Baptist Church, son Isaac was a 
2 CONC messenger there. Sons Abraham, Stephen and Moses administered
2 CONT
2 CONT his estate. His first 17 sons were by his first wife, four sons and two daughters by his second. There were supposedly a number of twins in the family, and for the sake of his first wife, let us fervently hope so.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the Cantrell family file folder in the Georgia Archives, "Aaron, Simon and Peter were captured during the Revolution and were condemned to be shot. Tradition says Peter was shot, and Aaron & Peter [sic] escaped." The 
2 CONC three were also supposedly scouts in Gen. Marion's
2 CONT
2 CONT army.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
