1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A Patriot of the American Revolution for NORTH CAROLINA.  [http://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A018949  DAR Ancestor #  A018949]   
2 CONT
2 CONT http://archive.org/stream/cantrillcantrell00chri/cantrillcantrell00chri_djvu.txt
2 CONT
2 CONT '''"The Cantrill-Cantrell genealogy : a record of the descendants of Richard Cantrill, who was a resident of Philadelphia prior to 1689, and of earlier Cantrills in England and America"''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT JOSEPH CANTRILL 4 (John 3 Joseph, 2 Richard 1 ) was  probably born in New Castle county, Pa. (now Delaware), and  was a young boy when his parents moved to North Carolina. We  could not learn the name of his wife, but he married i
2 CONC n North  Carolina and remained there the rest of his life. 
2 CONT
2 CONT It is claimed that he was in the Revolutionary War and that  his record is at Raleigh, N. C. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was executor of the will of his brother, Jacob Cantrill, in  1790, and his own will was probated at Hillsboro, May, 1804. It  is probable that his wife died before he did, as her name is not  mentioned in the will. 
2 CONT
2 CONT WILL OF JOSEPH CANTRILL 
2 CONT
2 CONT "I give and bequeath to my beloved son, Isaac Cantrill, all my  lands and tenement, negroes, horses, cattle, hogs, sheep and  poultry and working tools and all my debts due me and all my  cash, except 
2 CONT
2 CONT "twenty shilling I will and bequeath to Rachel Hensley, my  beloved daughter. 
2 CONT
2 CONT "To Sallie Davis, my beloved daughter, twenty shillings. 
2 CONT
2 CONT "To my beloved son William Cantrill, twenty shillings. 
2 CONT
2 CONT "To my beloved daughter Mary McCooley, twenty shillings. 
2 CONT
2 CONT "To my beloved son, Benjamin Cantrill, twenty shillings. 
2 CONT
2 CONT "I constitute my beloved son, Isaac Cantrill, my sole executor  of this my last will and testament. 
2 CONT
2 CONT "This to be my last will and testament, in witness whereof, I  have hereunto set my hand and seal this 3rd day of January,  1804." 
2 CONT
2 CONT (Signed) " JOSEPH CANTRILL." 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
