1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Family legend says he was born on the ship coming over from England
2 CONT
2 CONT Fought in the American revolutionary war
2 CONT
2 CONT Have conflicting information RE Samual Anderson.In the W.A. Anderson notebook
2 CONT
2 CONT it states that he Sarah Young on Mar 16, 1773.  In the Julia Howard Dawnkins 68
2 CONT
2 CONT book it states that he was born in 1745 d.18 Jul 1852 and was married to
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Gates.  James A. Anderson (his first son) (John Anderson was his
2 CONT
2 CONT second).  James A married Sarah Young on 28 Aug 1814.  However Sarah Young
2 CONT
2 CONT birthdate is 16 Feb 1773.
2 CONT
2 CONT Other facts are that he was born to David Anderson on the trip over from
2 CONT
2 CONT England in 1745 to Virginia.  They settled in Augusta Co. Virginia and lived
2 CONT
2 CONT there at the time of the French & Indian Wars.  Samual Served under Washington
2 CONT
2 CONT at the time of the Revolutionary War. (Not Verified)
2 CONT
2 CONT 9 Jan 2009
2 CONT
2 CONT Seventh of nine children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sourcing: Alta DeCamp, 305 K St, Neleigh, NE 68756
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughters of the American Revolution (DAR) record in posession, research by Dr. Anita Newcomb McGee, et al, in 1930s. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage dates from DAR and Judy Cannon, 2201 Parkway Ave, Salt Lake City UT, 84109
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel is supposed to have died in Indiana - but unable to locate him in Greene County.
2 CONT
2 CONT Death info from Judy Cannon records; Samuel died in Greene co IN while visiting a granddaughter.
2 CONT
2 CONT Baptism in Augusta Stone Meeting House, recorded in "The Tinkling Spring Meeting House", Headwater for Freedom, Appendix F, record of Baptisms, 1740-1749 by Rev. John Craig.  Old Craig parish wich was included both Stone and Tinkl
2 CONC ing Spring Meeting Houses.
2 CONT
2 CONT Executor of father's (James) will, as oldest surviving son was left the whole estate.
2 CONT
2 CONT More information is in the Google:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://homepages.rootsweb.com/~anderson/va/trees/augusta.html
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.twinwolf.net/~tsb/ged-html/g735.html
2 CONT
2 CONT From an article that W.A. Anderson had saved in the family papers:
2 CONT
2 CONT "John [James?] Anderson emigrated from Scotland to Virginia in the year 1746.   Samuel Anderson was born on board ship druing the voyage.  Little or nothing is known about any other members of the family.  Samuel Anderson and his 
2 CONC father became wealthy planters and lived near Richmond in Hanover County, Virginia.  Here John Anderson was born October 16, 1779.   the other children left the home and very little is known of their life.  Following the trend of 
2 CONC the times, Samuel Anderson and his son sold their plantation in Virginia and moved to Kentucky in 1797.  they purchased 1400 acres of land in Maison County near the city of Lexington.  The other members of the family settled in th
2 CONC e southern states.  John Anderson married Elizabeth Haggard, a relative of the father of Sir Rider Haggard, the famous English author.  Samuel Anderson was also the grandfather of Robert Anderson, the commander at fort Sumter of C
2 CONC ivil War fame.
2 CONT
2 CONT "
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------Mabel writes of her family history<nowiki>--------------------</nowiki>
2 CONT
2 CONT David Anderson and his family took passage for Virginia in America. On the voyage over, Samuel Anderson was born in 1745 and was the head of the present Anderson family [Evelyn writes: the above birth is disputed by later facts]
2 CONT
2 CONT The family settled in Augusta County, VA and there at the time of the French and Indian war were living in VA. When the war of the revolution began, Samuel Anderson joined the army and under Washington and fought until Independenc
2 CONC e was secured [Evelyn writes: Archives in Washington DC can give us no such record of his service.]
