3 STAE District of Columbia
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU Geologist and Anthropologist
1 TITL Dr.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Born April 17, 1853, Dubuque, Iowa
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 	September 4, 1912
2 CONT
2 CONT Nationality:American
2 CONT
2 CONT Fields:geology, anthropology, and ethnology
2 CONT
2 CONT William John McGee, LL.D. (April 17, 1853 - September 4, 1912) was an American geologist, anthropologist, and ethnologist, born near Dubuque, Iowa. He devoted his early years to reading law and to surveying. In 1877-81, he execute
2 CONC d a topographic and geological survey of 17,000 square miles (44,030 km²) in northeastern Iowa.[1][2][3] He was appointed geologist for the United States Geological Survey in 1881.
2 CONT
2 CONT McGee was ethnologist in charge of the Bureau of American Ethnology from 1893 to 1903. In 1895, he explored the Isla del Tiburón, Gulf of California, home of the Seri Indians.[4] In 1904 he was chief of the department of anthropol
2 CONC ogy at the St. Louis Exhibition. His other prominent positions were: acting president of the American Association for the Advancement of Science (1897-98); president of the American Anthropological Association (1902-12); and presi
2 CONC dent of the National Geographic Society (1904-05). His publications include:
2 CONT
2 CONT     * The Pleistocene History of Northeastern Iowa (1889)
2 CONT
2 CONT     * The Geology of Chesapeake Bay (1888)
2 CONT
2 CONT     * The Siouan Indians (1895)
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Primitive Trephining (1897)
2 CONT
2 CONT     * The Seri Indians (1899)
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Primitive Numbers (1901)
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Soil Erosion (1911)
2 CONT
2 CONT     * Wells and Subsoil Water (1913)
2 CONT
2 CONT Works by William John McGee at Project Gutenberg
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] References
2 CONT
2 CONT    1. ^ McGee, W.J. and Call, R.E. 1882. On the löss and associated deposits of Des Moines, Iowa. The American Journal of Science, 3rd Series, Whole no. 124, 24(141):202-223.
2 CONT
2 CONT    2. ^ McGee, W.J. 1884. The drainage system and the distribution of loess of Eastern Iowa. Bulletin of the Philosophical Society of Washington 6:93-97.
2 CONT
2 CONT    3. ^ McGee, W.J. 1891. The Pleistocene history of northeastern Iowa. In: Powell, J.W. (ed), Eleventh Annual Report of the Director of the United States Geological Survey, Part 1: 1889-1890, pp. 199-577.
2 CONT
2 CONT    4. ^ McGee, W.J. and Johnson, W.D. 1896. Seriland. The National Geographic Magazine 7(4):125-133.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.geni.com/people/Mary-Ann-Edwards/6000000001702049778
