1 NAME Emily M. /McClure/
2 GIVN Emily M.
2 SURN McClure
2 _MARNM Chaffee
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1842
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1908
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ---- Obit:
2 CONT
2 CONT The Cedar Rapids Evening Gazette, Mon., May 11, 1908, p. 8, col. 4.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral Of Mrs. Chaffee. __The funeral services of Mrs. Emily McClure Chaffee, which were private, were held this afternoon at 12:30 o'clock from the home of Rev. A. R. Paul, 606 South Second street west. Rev. DeWitt Clinton, past
2 CONC or of the Methodist church at Vinton, officiating. __Emily M. McClure was born in Erie county, Pennsylvania, March 20, 1842. At the age of 14 she was united with the Presbyterian church, of which she was a member until her marriag
2 CONC e, when she became a member of the Methodist church and had been a member of that church until her death. At the age of 15 her parents removed to Warren county, Illinois, where she resided until her marriage, Nov. 5, 1863, to Rev.
2 CONC  W. N. Chaffee. Of this union seven children were born, two of whom died in infancy. The surviving members of the family are Frank M. and Will N., both of Chicago; Dr. O. L. of Waverly, Iowa; Mrs. Dr. C. T. Brown of Waverly, Iowa,
2 CONC  and Mrs. A. R. Paul, wife of Rev. A. R. Paul of this city. __For four years after her marriage the family resided in Illinois, when they removed to eastern Iowa. In 1869 her husband became a member of the Upper Iowa conference of
2 CONC  the Methodist Episcopal church, and has in the years intervening served many charges in this district. For the last five years of her life she was an invalid and her death in a sanitarium at Lincoln, Neb., where she had gone for 
2 CONC treatment. Interment was at Linwood cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT
