2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.archive.org/stream/chaffeegenealogy01chaf/chaffeegenealogy01chaf_djvu.txt
2 CONT
2 CONT 91 James ^ Chaffee (Joseph, 3 Joseph,^ Thomas i) was born probably in Swansea, Mass., about 1713, and died in Monson, Mass., May 22, 1799. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married (1) in Woodstock, Conn., June 16, 1737, by John Chandler, Esq., Justice of the Peace, to Beriah Hayden of Woodstock, born February 10, 1715-16, died June 24, 1758. Her name is found on a list of the members of the W
2 CONC oodstock Congregational Church as early as October 30, 1743. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married (2) in Killingly, Conn., August 8, 1759, Rhoda Cady of that place. At this time he was living in Woodstock. She died May 22, 1799, and was buried in the same grave with her husband. 
2 CONT
2 CONT *November 4, 1747, Beriah Chaffe, an heir of Reverend John Child of Woodstock, and James Chaffee, her husband, of the same town, with other heirs of John Child, sold land to Jacob Child of Woodstock for £415. 
2 CONT *James Chaffee, a voter of Woodstock, was made a Freeman, September 12, 1749. 
2 CONT *The records of the First Congregational Church of Woodstock, where he lived, show that December 12, 1763, James "Chaffe" did a day's work for the church for which he was paid 3s. 6d. 
2 CONT *He was drafted during the Revolution, but said that he could not leave such a large family. His son Abial, aged 15, stepped forward and, offering to take his father's place, was accepted. 
2 CONT *James Chaffee was a farmer. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children, by first wife, born in Woodstock: 
2 CONT *281 i Nathan^ Chaffee, died October 8, 1750; baptized in the First Congregational Church, Woodstock, September 23, 1739. 
2 CONT *+ 282 ii Zebediah Chaffee, born April 11, 1741; married Mehetabel Preston. 
2 CONT *283 iii Dorothy Chaffee, born May 6, 1743; died October 27, 1823; baptized in the First Congregational Church, Woodstock, May 22, 1743. 
2 CONT *284 iv Sarah Chaffee, born April 27, 1746 ; married Samuel Chaffee (See 320.) 
2 CONT *+ 285 V James Chaffee, Jr., born March 22, 1748; married Sarah Howlett. 
2 CONT *+ 286 vi Nathan Chaffee, born November 17, 1750; married Priscilla Wedge. 
2 CONT *287 vii Abigail Chaffee, born January 2, 1753; died; baptized in the First Congregational Church, Woodstock, March 11, 1753. 
2 CONT *+ 288 viii Chester Chaffee, born April 6, 1755; married Caroline Walker. 
2 CONT *289 ix Calvin Chaffee, born May 12, 1757; died April 25, 1758; baptized in the First Congregational Church, Woodstock, May 29, 1757. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children, by second wife, born in Woodstock: 
2 CONT *+ 290 X Calvin Chaffee, born February 3, 1760; married Ruth Evidon. 
2 CONT *+ 291 xi Abial Chaffee, born August 13, 1761 ; married Hannah Seargent. 
2 CONT *+ 292 xii Charles Chaffee, born June 14, 1763; married Deborah . 
2 CONT *293 xiii Lucy Chaffee, born August 18, 1765; died; baptized in the First Congregational Church, Woodstock, October 20, 1765. 
2 CONT *294 xiv Martha Chaffee, born June 22, 1768; died April 13, 1772; baptized in the First Congregational Church, Woodstock, July 3, 1768. 
2 CONT *+ 295 XV Chadwick Chaffee, born March 16, 1771; married Abigail Moulton. 
2 CONT *+ 296 xvi Stephen Chaffee, born September 25, 1773; married Ruth Underwood. 
2 CONT *297 xvii Fatty Chaffee, born April 17, 1776; died in 1845. 
2 CONT *298 xviii Jemima Chaffee, born May 30, 1778; died. 
2 CONT *+ 299 xix Joseph Chaffee, born June 30, 1780; married Clarissa Dunham. 
2 CONT *+ 300 XX Leonard Chaffee, born April 11, 1782; married Betsey Needham. 
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT  JAMES CHAFFEE (1713–1799) was born in Swansea, Bristol, Massachusetts, and died in Monson, Massachusetts. “He was married (1) in Woodstock, Conn., June 16, 1737, by John Chandler, Esq., Justice of the Peace, to Beriah Hayden of W
2 CONC oodstock, … Her name is found on a list of the members of the Woodstock Congregational Church as early as October 30, 1743. He married (2) in Killingly, Conn., August 8, 1759, Rhoda Cady of that place. At this time, he was living 
2 CONC in Woodstock. She died May 22, 1799, and was buried in the same grave with her husband.” He had nine children (including Abigal) with Beriah, and eleven children with Rhoda. He lived 86 years, and is buried in Moulton Hill Cemeter
2 CONC y, Monson, Hampden County, Masssachusetts.
2 CONT ----
