2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT James Chaffee was born around 1713 in Swansea, Massachusetts.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Beriah Hayden of Woodstock on 16 June 1737 in Woodstock, Connecticut.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT James was made a Freeman on 12 September 1749.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Rhoda Cady on 8 August 1759 in Killingly, Connecticut.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT The records of the First Congregational Church of Woodstock show that 12 December 1763, James Chaffe did a day's work for the church for which he was paid 3s. 6d. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT James was drafted during the Revolution, but said that he could not leave such a large family. His son, Abial, aged 15, stepped forward and offered to take his father's place. Abial was accepted.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Both James and his wife Rhoda passed away on 22 May 1799, and they are buried together.[1]
