1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Dr. Charles Chaffee
2 CONT
2 CONT From the Chaffee Genealogy:
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.archive.org/stream/chaffeegenealogy01chaf/chaffeegenealogy01chaf_djvu.txt
2 CONT
2 CONT 292 Charles ^ Chaffee (James,* Joseph, 3 Joseph, 2 Thomas 1) was born in Woodstock, Conn., June 14, 1763, and died November 29, 1825. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Deborah. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was baptized in the First Congregational Church of Woodstock, July 17, 1763. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the first physician in Alexander, N. Y., where he was living as early as 1810. He bought land there December 23, 1814, and his widow sold 50 acres of land there March 16, 1832. He was a very outspoken man. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The pension claim of "Charles Chafey of Bennington, N. Y." is thought to refer to Doctor Chaffee. It states that he enlisted in the War of 1812 in Captain Matteson's company, New York Militia, in May, 1812. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children : 
2 CONT *780 i Ruby " Chaffee, married Abel McKane. 
2 CONT *781 ii Jerusha Chaffee, married Martin McKane. 
2 CONT *782 iii Abigail Chaffee, married J. M. Riddle. 
2 CONT *783 iv Polly Chaffee, married Charles Raymond. 
2 CONT *784 V Bethia Chaffee, married Riddle. 
2 CONT *+ 785 vi Thomas J. Chaffee, married. 
2 CONT *786 vii Jefferson Chaffee. 
2 CONT *+ 787 viii James Sullivan Chaffee, born in 1808; married Sarah Jenkins. 
2 CONT *788 ix Maria Chaffee, residence, 1828, Alexander. 
2 CONT *+ 789 x Charles Chaffee, Jr., born March 3, 1818; married Naomi Roberts. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT 295 Chadwick Chaffee (James,* Joseph, 3 Joseph, 2 Thomas 1) was born in  Woodstock, Conn., March 16, 1771, and died in Monson, Mass., September 6, 1848. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married there, Abigail, daughter of Freeborn Moulton of that place. She was born April 23, 1773, and died in Monson, March 17, 1838, where she was buried. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Chadwick Chaffee was baptized in the First Congregational Church of Woodstock, March 24, 1771. He had a light complexion and was five feet, eight inches in height. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He lived in Monson, where he was a farmer. He died while out driving. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children, the first ten born in Monson: 
2 CONT *+ 790 i Freeborn Moulton « Chaffee, born August 9, 1794; married Mrs. Betsey (Leonard) Squire. 
2 CONT *+ 791 ii James Austin Chaffee, born December 7, 1796; married (1) Susan Thresher; (2) Martha Dunham. 
2 CONT *+ 792 iii Ira Chaffee, born August 2, 1798; married (1) Anna Davis; (2) Anna Ladd Chaffee (3525) ; (3) Eunice Butler. 
2 CONT *793 iv Lotheta Chaffee, born June 29, ISOO; died in Stafford, Conn., November 24, 1869; married, November 12, 1843, Erasmus Rood of that place, their marriage intention being published in Monson, October 13, 1843; they lived in S
2 CONC tafford and had no children; she was buried in Staffordville, Conn. 
2 CONT *+ 794 V Orinda Chaffee, born February 14, 1802; married Gad Davis. 
2 CONT *+ 795 vi Stephen Chaffee, born January 26, 1804; married Betsey Davis. 
2 CONT *+ 796 vii Annis M. Chaffee, born May 22, 1806; married Heustis. 
2 CONT *797 viii Rhoda Cady Chaffee, born May 14, 1808; died June 25, 1844; married in South Wilbraham, Mass., May 27, 1832, Hiram Merrick of Ellington, Conn., and had two children; the family moved to Iowa and were all thought to be dea
2 CONC d in 1890. 
2 CONT *+ 798 ix Calvin Chaffee, born June 12, 1810; married Betsey A. Morgan. 
2 CONT *+ 799 X Julius Chaffee, born January 13, 1813; married Polly Ellis. 
2 CONT *+ 800 xi Almond Chaffee, born ]\Iay 29, 1815; married Melissa R. F. Washburn. 
2 CONT *+ 801 xii Abigail Rebecca Chaffee, born June 12, 1817; married EH M.Smith. 
