1 NOTE Jonathan Kingsley Underwood was recorded in the Woodstock records under that name but as a man dropped the first name and was always known to his family as Kingsley Underwood. Kingsley Underwood was the best read man of his town a
2 CONC  "man of original force of mind, wit, and poetic feeling." Some of his poetical compositions still remain in the possession of the family of his grandson, Francis H. Underwood. He wrote some articles for the press, one or more of 
2 CONC which appear in Garrison's Emancipator. He was a strong anti-slaver, anti-masonic, and anti-alcohol advocate. The character of the blacksmith in "Quabbin" by Frances H. Underwood which is a  picture of Enfield, Mass., was based on
2 CONC  Kingsley Underwood. 
2 CONT Some of his rhymes wer spontaneous, made up naturally on the spur of the moment. We give one or two quaint samples of these of the spontaneous sort.
2 CONT
2 CONT ON THE MARRIAGE OF ARIEL PARRISH AND ANNA WOODS
2 CONT Of Aladdin's great lamp we have all heard the story
2 CONT How it rose  in one night in full splendor and glory;
2 CONT But that is a fiction no mortal can swallow
2 CONT Shile a fact comes from Enfield which beats it all hollow,
2 CONT How a small piece of Woods, sure, the deuce must be in it,
2 CONT Was changed to a Parrish inless that a minutel
2 CONT
2 CONT In working the roads between Enfield ad Ware there was once a dispute berween the road-repairers of the two towns which let to considerable chaffing. On this occasion Kingsley Underwood gave vent to the following:
2 CONT
2 CONT "Dame Nature once in makin' land, 
2 CONT Hed refuse left o' stones an' sand
2 CONT She viewed it o'er, then flung it down
2 CONT Between Coy's Hill and Belchertown.
2 CONT said she, "Yeou paltry stuff, lie there!,
2 CONT An' made a town and called it Ware."
2 CONT Among his more extended rhymes was a long Essay on Melchisedek in shich he attenpted to prove that that personage was the second person of the Trinity. An account of his Literary habits and writings but with no mention of name may
2 CONC  be seen in "Quabbin" 
2 CONT pp. 66-67.
1 CHAN
2 DATE 01 MAY 2022
3 TIME 19:11:37
