2 CONT Besides the daughters she leaves one brother, James Thomas Barnes, age 82, of Washington, Ia.; six grandchildren, three great-grandchildren and a large number of nieces and nephews. The community has lost a long revered and respec
2 CONC ted citizen, the church a faithful member and the family a loving, devoted sister, moth and grandmother. Words are inadequate to pay proper tribute to one who for more than three-quarters of a century was so constant in her faith.
2 CONC  To family and friends her memory will remain a blessed benediction thru life. "Blessed are the dead who die in the Lord. They rest from their labors and their works do follow them."
