1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Thomas, citizen and Draper of London. Died 8 June 1610, buried 26 same month. Judith Fisher, daughter of William Fisher, 1st wife. Ellen Muffett, 2nd wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children by first wife:
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Humphrey - b. c1567; d. bef 12 Feb 1615; married about 1592 to Jane Cotton. He was buried on 12 February 1615/6, St Nicholas Acon, London, England.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Mentioned in the Will of Robert Thomas, of St. Nicholas Acons, dated 14 Feb. 1609/10, proved 18 Oct. 1610: 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * Upon my son Humfrey's marriage I assured and made over to him the house he now lives in and £500 stock, which house and stock cost me  £1000 and did also enter into bond with one Mr. Sillyard to leave my son  £1000 more. 
2 CONT * Also to his (Humfrey's) son Robert  £100. And also further to him all my lands in Essex called Dagman with 12 acres of Marsh by the Thames side, which one John Hardwood now holds. … 
2 CONT * Probate: 12th Oct. 1610 to George Southcott, Knight and Humfrey Thomas, Executors.
2 CONT ----
