1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Tobias Feake
2 CONT * Birth Aug 1624   Whitechapel, London, England
2 CONT * Christening Church of St. Mary White Chapel 1624   London, London, England
2 CONT *Son of James Feake and Audrey Crompton
2 CONT * Marriage to: Anna Feake (born van Beyeren) After 1645  Greenwich, Fairfield, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT * Marriage to: Mary Feake (born Patrick) 1656  Flushing, Queens, New York, United States
2 CONT * before Oct 8 1672  Wapping, Middlesex, England
2 CONT ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT His wife, Anna, died in April 1656, at age 46 years, leaving him a widow. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Tobias was authorized by the Orphan Masters to travel to collect the inheritance that belonged to his first wife. 24 1662  Netherlands (her aunt https://www.geni.com/people/Elizabeth-Van-Beyeren/6000000169009346639 estate)
2 CONT
2 CONT Legal
2 CONT
2 CONT He carried a remonstrance to New Amsterdam and was arrested and jailed for lodging Quakers in his home. He was fined 299 guilders. 29 1659   New Amsterdam, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Residence
2 CONT
2 CONT Tobias & Anna were residing in Flushing on Long Island. 14 1649
2 CONT
2 CONT Will
2 CONT
2 CONT In his Will he stated he was a mariner, he mentioned no wife or child but stated he was indebted to Ann Faraway of the same place, widow. 07 1669 Wapping, Middlesex, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Residence
2 CONT
2 CONT He never returned from his trip abroad. Instad of returning to his home in Flushing, he returned to his home in England, deserting his wife and children., Wapping, Middlesex, England 24 1662
2 CONT
2 CONT Probate
2 CONT
2 CONT His will was probated on 8 October 1672. "In a good and valuaable sum of money and also for divers good causes and considerarions". He named Ann Faraway his sole heir and exectris. 08 1672 Wapping, Middlesex, England
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Notes 
2 CONT
2 CONT From McCurdy Family Lineage: Tobias was the s/o Feake-47 and Crompton-129. Born circa 1622 and christened at White Chapel, London, Aug., 1624. As young children Tobias and his sister Judith were sent to live w/ his Aunt Alice Feak
2 CONC e Dickson and Tobias Dickson (Dixon). They lived in Germany for a time and by 10 May 1639 both were under the guardianship of Robert Feake-4 in Mass. Bay Colony. He was schout (sheriff) Flushing, New Netherlands and a signer of th
2 CONC e Flushing Remonstrance in Dec. 1657. Was arrested for this action and fined 299 guilders (per this narrative). He marr. 2nd Mary Patrick after 1656, may have had children. On 24 June 1662 Tobias was authorized by the Orphan Maste
2 CONC rs to go to Holland to collect the inheritance that belonged to his first wife. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT https://mccurdyfamilylineage.com/ancestry/p7170.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Tobias never returned from his trip abroad. Instad of returning home to Flushing, he returned to his home in England, deserting his wife & children. Mary & the children were left with no income & to fend for themselves.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT It is possible that Elizabeth the wife of Charles Morgan was Mary Patrick's daughter with Mary's first husband; his name is unknown. But Elizabeth might be a daughter with the second husband of Mary, Tobias Feake.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT * https://mosergenealogy.wordpress.com/my-paternal-ancestors/captain-daniel-patrickc-1605-1643/
2 CONT *Torrey, Volume Title: New England Marriages Prior to 1700 [https://www.ancestry.com/imageviewer/collections/3824/images/gpc_newenglandmarriages-0277?pId=148794 AncestryImage]
2 CONT * https://mccurdyfamilylineage.com/ancestry/p7195.htm
2 CONT * [S971] Patricia L. Haslam, Captain Daniel Patrick of the 1630 Winthrop Fleet & Some of His Descendants, page 475 - Anneken’s four children with her first husband, Daniel Patrick and her son with Tobias Feake were named in a docu
2 CONC ment dated 19 May 1662:;”Anna Patrick, wife of Bartholomew Applegate living in Gravesend; Patientia Patrick, wife of Arent Cornelius of Flushing, Zeeland, and living in Flushing, Long Island; Daniel Patrick living in Middleburg; S
2 CONC amuel Patrick living in Gravesland (all villages in the jurisdiction of New Netherland); and James Feackx. Daniel and Samuel were under age on 24 June 1662 when Martin Kresjier (Creiger) and Pieter Kowenhoven, Orphan Masters at th
2 CONC e Court at New Amsterdamn, were appointed their guardians in papers filed in the Orpans Court at The Hague, Holland. The children were to gain possession of the inheritance of their maternal grandparents.“
2 CONT * Great Migration Begins, Vol 3, P-W.  “Daniel Patrick.” Page 1405.  [https://www.ancestry.com/imageviewer/collections/2496/images/42521_b158320-00093?treeid=&personid=&rc=&usePUB=true&_phsrc=ffA4&_phstart=successSource&pId=67800 
2 CONC AncestryImage]. ii. Patience b say 1636 married by 24 June 1662 [NS] Arent Cornelis of Flushing.  [NYGBR 113:150-152]
