1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Update
2 CONT
2 CONT According to WikiTree Ref to: Richard Lyon Jr. b. o/a 1625 in England or Scotland d. 17 Oct 1678 in Fairfield, CT Colonial America, and married Margaret Winthrop. See link to WikiTree. https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Lyon-74  Also h
2 CONC is tree goes from Richard Lyon Sr. married to Margaret Hopwood, William Lyon married to Isabel Wightman, John Lyon II and married to Jean "Joan",  John Lyon I and married to Emma Hedde. Is Richard Lyon tree correct?
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT http://dgmweb.net/Resources/GenLin/Gen-LyonHenry.html
2 CONT
2 CONT UPDATE (25 May 2010):  Y-DNA testing has proven that https://www.geni.com/people/Richard-Lyon-of-Fairfield/6000000004647456492?through=6000000128684367129 and https://www.geni.com/people/Henry-Lyon-of-Newark/6000000007938368730?th
2 CONC rough=6000000004647456492 were closely related.  Rather surprisingly, it also appears https://www.geni.com/people/William-Lyon-of-Roxbury/6000000002641636055 is closely related to them, while https://www.geni.com/people/Thomas-Lyo
2 CONC n-of-Rye/6000000003942693369 is not.  At last, some solid evidence on the relationships of these four men! 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Came to Connecticut from England
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Richard Lyon (b. 1624, d. Oct 17, 1678) Richard Lyon was born 1624 in Glen Lyon, Scotland, and died Oct 17, 1678 in Fairfield, CT..He married Margaret.
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for Richard Lyon: Richard Lyon, along with his brothers Henry and Thomas, emigrated to the colonies in 1648 from Glen Lyon, Tayside, Scotland. ' The story is that these three who were Scotch soldiers in Cromwell's army, were
2 CONC  on guard before the banqueting house at Whitehall, January 31, 1648, and witnessed the execution of King Charles I. Immediately after the regicide they fled to America. Henry Lyon went to Milford, Connecticut; Richard Lyon settle
2 CONC d in Fairfield as early as May, 1649' It appears that Richard was one of the gaolers or 'keepers' of Goody Knapp who was accused and hung as a witch in 1653. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In his will Richard Lyon gave 7 pounds sterling to his 'cousin Mary Fitch.' Although she is thought somehow to have been a descendant of Thomas Fitch and Anne Reeve Fitch of Bocking, Essex, England, that link has not been document
2 CONC ed; nor has the relationship between her and Richard. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The Lyon Memorial reports that Henry, Thomas and Richard Lyon belonged to one of the five families who descended from John de Lyon, Feudal Baron of Fortevolt, 'but the name of their Scottish ancestor is lost out of tradition '
2 CONT Richard conveyed to sons Richard and Moses in 1677/1678. The will of Richard Lyon of Fairfield is dated 12 April 1678. It names son Moses, who was to pay "to my Cosen Mary fitch" L7; sons Richard, William, Samuel, Joseph; daughter
2 CONC  Hester Perry; son-in-law Nathaniel Perry; wife Margaret Executriz; daughters Betty, Hannah and Abigail, all under 19. Witnesses: Nathan Gold and Mary Murwin. Inventory was taken 17 October 1678.  Distribution of commonage was mad
2 CONC e on 10 March 1723/1724 to heirs of Richard Lyon, who left five sons: Moses (eldest, deceased without heirs; Richard, Samuel, William deceased (children: Nathaniel, deceased, left children; William and Benjamin), Joseph deceased (
2 CONC sons Joseph; and David, deceased, left children), and four daughters: Hannah, Esther deceased (children Joseph Perry; Esther, deceased, wife of Daniel Burr, left children; Mary, deceased, wife of John Downs, left children; and Sam
2 CONC uel Grumman), Elizabeth deceased (children Benjamin and Joseph Banks; and Elizabeth, deceased, wife of Samuel Davis, left children), Abigail deceased (left daughter, wife of William Odell.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Richard Lyon and Margaret are: +Esther Lyon, b. Abt. 1658, of Fairfield CT, d. Abt. 1699, Fairfield, CT..
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT !"The Families of Old Fairfield" Will, 12 Apr 1678, inv. 17 Oct 1678
2 CONT
2 CONT !"Lyon Memorial"  FHL 927.273 L994l Vol.2 Settled in Fairfield, Connecticut as early as May 1649. Freeman, 13 Oct 1664. "The compilers of this family history regard it as very highly probable that Henry, Thomas and Richard lyon we
2 CONC re brothers. They do not accept as of historic value the tradition that these brothers came direct from Scotland, although they have no doubt that they were of the same Lyon family of which the Earls of Strathmore are a branch.
2 CONT
2 CONT !Also AFN NP8J-K3
2 CONT
2 CONT !Will:son Moses to pay "to my cosen Mary Fitch"; sons Richard, William, Samuel, Joseph; dau. Hester Perry; son-in-law Nathaniel Perry; wife Margaret; dau. Betty, Hannah and Abigail (all under age 19) Distribution 10 Mar 1723/4 of 
2 CONC commonage to heirs of Richard Lyon, who left five sons, Moses(eldest, dec'd without heirs), Richard, Samuel, William dec'd, Joseph dec'd, and four daus., Hannah, Esther dec'd, Elizabeth dec'd, Abigail dec'd.
