1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Rebecca Hallett 
2 CONT *Born 31 Aug 1675 in Hallett's Cove (now Astoria), Yorkshire, New York
2 CONT * Died 12 Apr 1730 in Rocky Hill, Flushing, Queens County, New York
2 CONT * Daughter of William Hallett Jr. and Sarah (Woolsey) Hallett
2 CONT * Wife of James Jackson Sr — married 1694 (to 12 Apr 1730) in Halletts Cove, now Astoria, Long Island, New York
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Hallett-133
2 CONT
2 CONT Descendant of Elizabeth Fones.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rebecca was born on 31 August 1675 in Hallett's Cove (now Astoria, Queens County), New York [Queens County was formed in 1683][1]
2 CONT
2 CONT On 1 July 1694 in Halletts Cove (now Astoria), Long Island, New York[2] when she was about twenty years old, she married James Jackson, Sr., the second of eight known children and the oldest of three known sons of Col. John and El
2 CONC izabeth Seaman Jackson, at  Halletts Cove, now Astoria, Long Island, New York. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Over the next quarter-century, Rebecca bore her husband 20 children; all were single births.
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/99970689/rebecca-jackson
2 CONT
2 CONT * (1) Thomas Jackson b Dec 4, 1694 d April 12, 1730 m Mary Townsend.
2 CONT * (2) Mary Jackson b Jan 20, 1696/1697 d Sept 27, 1735 m Jacob Willetts.
2 CONT * (3)Sarah Jackson b Dec 11, 1697 
2 CONT * (4) Rebecca Jackson b Feb 20, 1698/1699 m Sylvanus Seamon. 
2 CONT * (5) John Jackson Sr b March 9, 1700/1701 d 1768/1772 m Sarah Doty. 
2 CONT * (6) Charity Jackson b Feb 26, 1701/1702 m John Dingey 
2 CONT * (7) Elizabeth Jackson b March 20, 1703 m Nathaniel Field 
2 CONT * (8) James Jackson Jr b July 4, 1704 d 1750 m Sarah Thorne, m Mary Fitzrandolph.
2 CONT * (9) William #1 Jackson b Jul 6, 1705 d May 1706 
2 CONT * (10) Hannah Jackson b Aug 5, 1706 d Sept 27, 1735, m. John Hicks m. John Hewlett
2 CONT * (11) William #2 Jackson b Oct 4, 1707 d Oct 9,1746
2 CONT * (12) Martha Jackson b Jan 26, 1709 d 1735 m. William Green Jr 
2 CONT * (13) Gen'l Joseph Jackson b Feb 9, 1710 d 1769 
2 CONT * (14) Richard Jackson b March 20, 1711 d 1739 m Mary Townsend 
2 CONT * (15) Phoebe Jackson b May 3, 1712 d 1777 m Edward Fitz Randolph Jr 
2 CONT * (16) Robert Jackson b May 15, 1713 
2 CONT * (17) Jemima Jackson b Nov 25, 1714 m Mr Hicks 
2 CONT * (18) Samuel Jackson b July 21, 1716 m Sarah Carpenter 
2 CONT * (19) Stephen Jackson b Aug 17, 1717 m Mary Lewis 
2 CONT * (20) Benjamin Jackson Sr. b July 26, 1719 d 1805 m Mary Lively Rushing, m Amanda "Amy" Forrest.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Rebeca died in Rocky Hill, Flushing, Queens County, New York[3] on, 12 April 1730 at the age of fifty-four, when her youngest child was ten years old. She was buried in Hallett's Cove, Queens County, New York[4] Her husband remarr
2 CONC ied less than two months after her death.[5] At a later time her remains were removed to Mount Olivet Cemetery, Maspeth, Queens County, New York, USA. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.jacksonfamilygenealogy.com/pafg03.htm#8.
2 CONT
2 CONT James Jackson-(John , Robert ) was born 7, 8 about 1670 in Hempstead, Long Island, New York. He died 9, 10 in Oct 1735 in Flushing, Long Island, New York. He was buried in Rocky Hill Cem, Flushing, L.I., New York. James resided in
2 CONC  Flushing, Queens Co., New York.
2 CONT
2 CONT James married 5 (1) Rebecca Hallett-9 1, 2, 3, 4 daughter of William Hallett Jr.-272 and Sarah Woolsey-853 in 1694 in Halletts Cove, now Astoria, Long Island, New York. Rebecca was born on 31 Aug 1675 in Hallett's Cove (now Astori
2 CONC a), Queens Co., New York. She died 12d 2m (Apr) 1730 in Rocky Hill, Flushing, Queens Co., New York. She was buried in Hallett's Cove, Queens Co., New York.
2 CONT
2 CONT They had the following children:
2 CONT
2 CONT * +	64	M	i	 Thomas Jackson-10 
2 CONT * +	65	F	ii	 Mary Jackson-11
