2 CONT ===Origins 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1st Gen. John Browne of Wigham in com. Essex; Will Arch. Colchester, 9 March 1562; probate 19 April 1563; names Elizabeth Raven, his daughter, and Margery, Anne, Joan and Anne, the four daughters of Henry Browne his son. 
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===References 
2 CONT # Muskett, Joseph James. "Evidences of the Winthrops of Groton, Co. Suffolk, England, and of families in and near that county with whom they intermarried." 1894-1896. Page 3. “Winthrop of Groton, co. Suffolk” < [https://books.goog
2 CONC le.com/books?id=7dYKAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA25&dq=henry+hoskins+winthrop&hl=en&sa=X&ved=0ahUKEwi43fLpxNTcAhUSHqwKHUCAAogQ6AEIJzAA#v=onepage&q=henry%20hoskins%20winthrop&f=false GoogleBooks] >
2 CONT # Muskett, Joseph James. "Evidences of the Winthrops of Groton, Co. Suffolk, England, and of families in and near that county with whom they intermarried." 1894-1896. Page 77.  “Will of John Browne of Witham, 1562.”  “Will of Henr
