2 TITL Adam Winthrop, III 1548-1623  Husband of Alice Still and Anne Browne Winthrop is your 11th great grandfather.
2 NOTE WPI: 140 
3 CONT Severus, Alexander, Image of Government translated from Greek to English by Sir Thomas Eliot (London, 1540) 
3 CONT -- note on Eliot and his father in hand of AW: Sir Thomas Eliot knight was the sonne of Sir Rich: Eliott knight one of the Justices of the common plees anno 12 H 8 and was borne in Suffolke as Mr Bale reporteth: he died at Carleto
3 CONC n in Cambridshir the 25 day of Marche anno 1546 and in 37 yere of the reigne of Kinge Henry the eight. And lyeth buried in the churche of Carleton aforesaid. Ex cen 8. D Balaei 
3 CONT NYS: 136 
3 CONT Smith, Thomas, De Republica Anglorum, The maner of Government or policie of the Realme of England (London, 1584) 
3 CONT -- on reverse of title page is "Plebs sine lege ruit. Adam Wintrop"; also marginal notes and a full page in Latin on leaf facing first page of text: "Epistola D. Thoma Smithe ad D Gualterum Haddo[num] de huius Libri argumento & ut
3 CONC a. Quia [inram] rempub: absens desedero de eadem tres libros Tholosa conscipso quibus titula feci de repub Anglorum In quibus totam fere formionis eius [explicum]: praeser[ ] ibus rebus ubi a caeteris dissert dissert antem ferem o
3 CONC mnibus. Ita utop longuis progressum sit quam putabam. Scripsiantem sermoni nostrati stilo inter historicum & philosophicum medio ad cum forma, qua scripsisse connectabam Aristotolem de multis greciae rebus pub: qui libri nunc exci
3 CONC derat. Prebui argumentum ubberrimum illis, qui di putare philosophico more desingulis quastionibus volunt: & problemata facere, [aqunncan] iniquum sit; & utrum sit melius a quod istic teneatur in Anglia pro lege, an quod hic & mil
3 CONC lis [proumeiis] qua romano jure [reaunter]. Libri quos D. Th: Smithus Literis mandatos reliquit hi sunt De greca lingua orthographia De repubica Anglorum. Denumismatis. Epistola aliquot latina. In eudem distichon. Polluit ingemo d
3 CONC octrina moribus, arte deum, requiem, Sprevit am[ ] habet. 
3 CONT AW 
3 CONT Dignum laude virum Musa vetat mori" 
3 CONT NYS: 232 
3 CONT Stevens, Charles and John Liebault, translated by Richard Surflet, Maison Rustique or the Countrie Farme (London, 1600) 
3 CONT -- AW notes (including reference to Henry Macham) 
3 CONT MHS: WL 
3 CONT Stubbes, John, The Discoverie of a Gaping Gulf, whereinto England is like to be swallowed by an other French Maraige, if the Lord forbid not the Banes, by letting her Majestie see the sin and punishment thereof (1579) 
3 CONT -- information re: Stubbes in handwriting of AW on fly-leaf before title page: "Made by John Stubbes a gentleman of Lincolnes Inne: for the wch he was committed to the Tower, & from thence was brought to Westminster, and had jugem
3 CONC ent to have his right hand cutte of, the wch was executed, in kinges street uppon a Scaffolde, the thirde day of November, anno D 1579, & Elizabeth Reginae anliae vicesimo primo. 
3 CONT Mr Canden in his history of the annales of Queene Elizabeth, pag: 324. 325 & 326, very modestly & wisely maketh mention of Mr Stubbes, & of the contents of this booke. And how grivously her Majesty tooke the writing & publishing o
3 CONC f it, wch she commanded to be burned & the Author to be severely punished. 
3 CONT MHS Proceedings vol X, 482: RW report with details 
3 CONT Vives, Joannes Ludovicus, De ratione dicendi (Louvain, 1533) 
3 CONT -- has AW signature; it belonged originally to Daniel Wythipoll (his signature, with the date 1560 is on the flyleaf), who was of the Ipswich Wythipolls; it is said to have passed from him to Henry Foljambe and then to AW; some no
3 CONC tes on flyleaf in AW hand 
3 CONT AC 
3 CONT Gualter [Walther], Rodolph, Certaine Godlie Homilies, or Sermons upon the Prophets Abdias and Jonas, translated into English by Robert Norton (London, 1573) 
3 CONT -- extensive annotation by AW, including list of other books which also deal with explication of these scriptural books: " Mr Wm Tindal made a long prologue of the Prophet Jonas, wch is printed amonge his woorkes. Pag: 23. 24. 25.
3 CONC  26. 27 
3 CONT Mr John Hooper made sermons before King Edwarde the sixte, wch are in printe 
3 CONT Mr Francis Junius wrote analyses in Latine of this prophet wch I have 
3 CONT Dr. Kinge nowe B. Of London expounded this prophet in divers sermons wch are printed 
3 CONT Dr Baro a french man red upon the prophet in Cambridge, whose lectures are in print 
3 CONT Mr Francis Quarles metaphrased him in meeter 
3 CONT Mr. Hen: Sandes preached upon Jonas in Groton churche divers sermons, anno 1620. 1621 
3 CONT In the Doctrine of the Bible by Questions & Answeres, this booke is unfolded. Fol: 142 
3 CONT Mr Calvin made Commentaries upon al the smal Prophetes 
3 CONT And Mr Gualter wrote Homilies" 
3 CONT -- at the end of the Epistle to the reader by John Walker, AW writes: " Dr Walker was Archdeacon of Essex in the reigne of Q. Eliz: & was one of them that disputed with Campion the Jesuite in the Tower of London. Mr Norton that tr
3 CONC anslated these 2 Homilies out of latine into English was the publicke preacher in Ipswiche & a Doctor of divinitie"; next to the remark in the dedictaory epistle commenting on the "godly and reformed household of good master Drue 
3 CONC Druries", AW writes "Sr Drue Drurye" in the margin to draw attention to it 
3 CONT NYS: 122 
3 CONT Wilson, George, The Commendation of Cockes, and Cock-fighting (London, 1607) 
3 CONT -- quite a few pages of notes (some references to classic allusions to cocks, another reference to Roger Ascham and what he wrote on the subject) and marginal annotations -- [transcribe these here] 
3 CONT MHS: WL 
3 CONT Wotton, Edward, Ni Oxoniensis de differentiis animalium libri decem (Paris, 1552) 
3 CONT -- notes (AW?) 
3 CONT MHS:WL 
3 CONT B. Books probably owned based on dates or other reasons 
3 CONT Alabaster, William, Apparatus in Revelationem Jesu Christi Nova & admirabilis ratio investigandi Prophetiarum mysteria ex Scriptura Seipsam Interpretante (Antwerp, 1607) 
3 CONT -- no notes or signature; possible because of interest AW took in his nephew Alabaster and its presence in a family collection 
3 CONT AC 
3 CONT Almasoris, Exponentis Curandi Morbos, et Aben Hali de Curandis Febribus (Venice, 1521) 
3 CONT -- notes on title page not in AW's hand, some marginal notes could be 
3 CONT NYS: 9 
3 CONT Ausonius, Burdigadlensis, Opera, Recognita a J. Scaligero, et Ausoniarum Lectionem (Heidelberg, 1588) 
3 CONT -- some notation on reverse of title page could be in AW's hand 
3 CONT NYS: 24 
