3 CONT -- in his notes in Walther's Homilies above AW writes "Dr Baro, a frenchman red upon the prophet in Cambridge, whose Lectures are in print"; AW was familiar with it even if he didn't own it 
3 CONT see NYS: 122 
3 CONT Bright, Thomas, A Treatise of Melancholie (London, 1586) 
3 CONT -- marginal notes that appear to be in the hand of AW 
3 CONT MHS: WL 
3 CONT Calvin, John, ?Sermons of Master John Calvin upon the Booke of Job? (1574) 
3 CONT -- in his notes in Walther's Homilies above AW writes "Mr Calvin made Comentaries upon al the smal Prophets" -- his father-in-law, Henry Browne evidently owned and copied from the volume above 
3 CONT see NYS: 122 
