2 CONT VITAL: A twin.
1 NOTE Little is known of Adam Winthrop's early life except to note that his father died when he was 14 and his mother died three years later.  Family traditions, as perpetuated by Cotton Mather, represent him to have been a lawyer; and 
2 CONC he has sometimes been recorded as a sergeant-at-law.  He seems to have resided almost altogether at Groton, and to have occupied himself mainly with agricultural pursuits.  He became "Lord of the Manor" at some point and there are
2 CONC  abundant proofs that he was a man of good education and of high social standing.  He was also a poet, his verses having been thought worthy of preservation in a miscellany of the poetry of the time.  
2 CONT
2 CONT There are in existence many of the old "Winthrop Almanacs" containing memoranda.  Adam Winthrop kept a diary from 1594 until 1610.  He was an auditor of Trinity College, Cambridge, for 16 or 17 years.  He held other offices, as we
2 CONC ll - "in 1602, the xvth of Aprill I kept a Court for my brother Snelling at Shimplinge."  "The xxviith I kept a Court at Groton Hall."  "1602.  On Wednesdays the xxiiii of Marche Queen Elizabeth died & James the vith Kinge of Scot
2 CONC land was proclaymed the next day at London & on Saturday & Sudbury with the great rejoycings of all men."
2 CONT
2 CONT In one entry, he mentions the Fones connection:  "1608.  The i of November my Daught'r Fones' daught'r was christened.  Sr Robert Crane & his Lady were present & she witness with Mres. Sampson & mres. Bronde & myselfe.  She named 
2 CONC the childe Dorothey."
2 CONT
2 CONT his death, a stone replaced the bronze plate covering his father's grave and it was carved with the following:
2 CONT
2 CONT Heaven the Country:  Christ the Way
2 CONT
2 CONT Here lies the body of Adam Winthrop Esq., son of Adam
2 CONT Winthrop Esq. who were patrons of this church
2 CONT and lords of the manor of Groton.
2 CONT The above named Adam, the son, married Anna, the daughter
2 CONT of Henry Browne of Edwardston, by whom he had one son
2 CONT and four daughters.
2 CONT He departed this life in the year of our Lord 1623.
2 CONT And of his own age 75.  But Anna his wife died in 1628.
2 CONT She is also buried here with him.
2 CONT Blessed are the peacemakers, for they shall be called
2 CONT The sons of God.
