2 CONT
2 CONT FROM History of York by Banks, page 179:...Emanuel Downing, a wealthy lawyer of London, brother-in-law of Winthrop, and the "friend at Court" of the Massachusetts Colony
2 CONT
2 CONT •*¨*•☆•*¨*•
2 CONT
2 CONT Winthrop family John Winthrop (1588–1649): governor of Massachusetts Bay Colony
2 CONT
2 CONT Lucy Winthrop Downing, mother of diplomat Sir George Downing, 1st Baronet, founder of New York, of Downing Street, London, and ultimately of Downing College, Cambridge UK. Lucy's letter to her brother Governor Winthrop provided th
2 CONC e impetus for the founding of Harvard College. 
2 CONT
2 CONT John Winthrop the Younger (1606–1676): governor of Connecticut Fitz-John Winthrop (1637–1711): governor of Connecticut
2 CONT
2 CONT John Winthrop: married Anne Dudley, granddaughter of Thomas Dudley John Winthrop (1714–1779): acting president of Harvard, pioneer of American science
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Lindall Winthrop (1760–1841): lieutenant governor of Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert Charles Winthrop (1809–1894): lawyer, politician, philanthropist
2 CONT
2 CONT Winthrop Rockefeller (1912–1973): governor of Arkansas, philanthropist
