1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Notes: New Windsor History
2 CONT 3em>The earliest recorded patent was issued to Patrick McGregorie in 1685. Others were as follows: 1,000 acres to William Chambers and William Southerland, September 2, 1709.
2 CONT 3em>The Chamber and Southerland patents were divided November 7, 1723, into three equal parts. Chambers occupying the northern part, Matthews the central Part and Southerland the southern part, on the death of the latter in 1738, 
2 CONC his portion passed to his two sons, William and John.
2 CONT 3em>The central portion held by Matthews was purchased by [https://www.geni.com/people/John-Alsop/6000000009967714809], 1724, whose son John Alsop, Jr., was prominent in the Revolution, and grandfather of Governor [https://www.gen
2 CONC i.com/people/John-Alsop-King/6000000000986027584], in 1749. He also sold that portion on which the village of New Windsor stands to the company called the "Proprietors" of New Windsor, September 9, 1749. Their names were Vincent M
2 CONC atthews, [https://www.geni.com/people/Ebenezer-Seely/6000000006823749299], Michael Jackson, Joseph Sackett, David Marvin, Evan Jones and [https://www.geni.com/people/Brant-Schuyler/6000000210418492874].
