1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 2/3. William Townsend, born February 13/1715, died May 5/1777 of
2 CONT
2 CONT      smallpox.  He married in 1741, Elizabeth Cock, born December
2 CONT
2 CONT      14/1715, died November 30/1794, twin daughter of Henry and Mary
2 CONT
2 CONT      (Feake) Cock: they lived at Duck Pond. He was a man of unquestioned
2 CONT
2 CONT      integrity and was executor of many estates. In the Revolution, he
2 CONT
2 CONT      was a warm Whig and in consequence had his house filled with both
2 CONT
2 CONT      troops and refugees, to his great loss and annoyance.
2 CONT
2 CONT      Issue:-
2 CONT
2 CONT      3/1. James Townsend, born April 25/1742, died December 12/1798.
2 CONT
2 CONT         He married on February 4/1762, Freelove Townsend Wilmot, born
2 CONT
2 CONT         February 25/1744, died July 21/1809, daughter of the Reverend
2 CONT
2 CONT         Walter and Freelove (Townsend) Wilmot, see subject 616, page 3.
2 CONT
2 CONT         They had seven children.
2 CONT
2 CONT      3/2. Rosanna Townsend, born September 4/1751, died April 10/1831.
2 CONT
2 CONT         She married on December 20/1768. her cousin Daniel Cock, born
2 CONT
2 CONT         March 26/1747, died October 22/1804, son of James and Deborah
2 CONT
2 CONT         (Feake) Cock, see subject 306, page 3. They had no children.
