1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.longislandgenealogy.com/ligwhitson.html
2 CONT
2 CONT HENRY1 WHITSON was resident of Hempstead, L. I. in 1647, his wife was a Foster. They removed to Huntington about 1653, where he died in 1669, leaving a widow and minor son, Thomas, who afterwards m. Martha, dau. of Thomas Jones an
2 CONC d Catharine (Estes), dau. of Jeffrey, he d. 1657, the first death in Huntington. Thomas Whitson purchased 1-3 of the Bethpage Purchase in 1700, died there in 1742, aged 90 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of THOMAS2 and Martha Whitson:
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas3 b. 1689, m. 1716, Deborah Feeks, b. 1695, 
2 CONT
2 CONT he d. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Martha3 b. 1691. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ruth3 b. 1694. 
2 CONT
2 CONT John3 b. 1697, m. 1722, Esther Seaman. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Rebecca3 b. 1699, m. 1719, Amos Willets, son of 
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas and Dinah. 
2 CONT
2 CONT David3 b. 1701, m. Clement Powell, dau. of John 
2 CONT
2 CONT and Margaret. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry3 b. 1705, m. 1739, Hannah Powell, dau. of 
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas,2 he d. 1790. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah3 b. 1707, she d. 1789.
2 CONT
2 CONT THOMAS3 WHITSON (Thomas2 Henry1) and 
2 CONT
2 CONT     Deborah (Feaks) had: 
2 CONT
2 CONT   John4 b. 1718, m. 1744, Deborah Powell, b. 1715, 
2 CONT
2 CONT     dau. of Thomas,2 he d. 1804. 
2 CONT
2 CONT   Thomas4 m. went to N. Jersey or Penn'a. 
