1 NOTE {geni:about_me} History and Genealogy of the Cock, Cocks, Cox Family By George William Cocks, John Cox
2 CONT
2 CONT HANNAH (COCK) COLES (Samuel", James*, James1) b. Beaver Swamp Hollow near Susco's Wigwam, now (1912) Brookville, L. I. 4/2 mo (Apl) 1731 ; d. ; m. ist about 1750, Joseph Coles, carpenter, son of Joseph and Temperance (Albertson) C
2 CONC oles of Musketa Cove, L. I. m. 2d 1789, Matthew Prior, son of Matthew and Hannah1' (Cock) Prior. No issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT Issue (Coles) :
2 CONT
2 CONT  i Samuel, b. 5/9 mo. (Nov.) 1750, was impressed on a British Vessel and probably lost at sea. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ii Rhoda, b. 3.26.1752; m. 7.12.1769, Adolph De Grove, son of Adolph and Sarah (Lawrens) De Grove, 
2 CONT
2 CONT iii Martha, b. 2.3.1754; m. John Bailey or Bayles. 
2 CONT
2 CONT iv Anne, b. 12.6.1756; ?died young.
2 CONT
2 CONT v Esther, b. 12.3.1759; d. 8.12.1847; m. 3.13.1782, Jonathan Carpenter b. 9.7.1749; d. 5.12.1812, son of Benedict and Abigail (Hor- ton) Carpenter.
2 CONT
2 CONT vi Barak, b. 3.19.1762; d. 2.9.1817 ; m. 3.8.1784, Abigail Colwell, dau. of Harvey and Hannah (Tillot) Colwell.
2 CONT
2 CONT vii James, b. 7.15.1767 ; d. 1852 ; m. ist., Oct., 1790, Mary Fisher; m. 2d 10.19.1826, Phebe Pearce; m. 3d 5.15.1839. Edna Carpenter.
2 CONT
2 CONT viii Joseph, b. 9.25.1768; m. Susan Shute of Eastchester, Westches- ter Co., N. Y.
2 CONT
2 CONT ix Temperance, b. 11.30.1770; d. 5.25.1818; m. Charles Weeks, b. 5.15.1763, son of Charles and Anna (Longworth) Weeks of Matinecock, L. I.
2 CONT
2 CONT x Rachel, b. 8.20.1775; m. 5.24.1792 Noah Tompkins, b. 1771, d. 1820, of Rye, Westchester Co., N. Y.
