1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John Searing IV1
2 CONT
2 CONT M, b. December 1743, d. 20 May 1822
2 CONT
2 CONT      John was born in December 1743 at Hempstead Town, Nassau County, Long Island, New York. He was the son of John Searing III and Elizabeth (?). On 13 October 1744, John was christened at St. George's Anglician Church in the Tow
2 CONC n of Hempstead, Queens County, Long Island, New York. John married Mary Prior on 5 January 1764 at the Quaker Meeting House, Westbury, Hempstead Town, Queens County, Long Island, New York.2 John & Mary had children: Mary [12/12/17
2 CONC 64], John [2/11/1766], Amey [2/23/1768] & Phebe. John departed this life on Monday, 20 May 1822 at Hempstead Town, Nassau County, Long Island, New York, at age 78 years and 5 months.3
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT
2 CONT [S79] William Wade Hinshaw, Encyclopedia of American Quaker Genealogy, Volume III [Westbury Monthly Meeting]: page 446 - John Searing, son of John deceased Hempstead, died 5/20/1822 age 48 years and about 5 months; married 1/05/17
2 CONC 64 Mary Prior, d/o Samuel & Mary. Children Mary b, 12/12/1764, John b. 2/11/1766, Amey b. 2/23/1768 & Phebe. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Volume III [New York Meeting]: page 283 - John Searing Jr. & Mary children: Sarah b. 8/24/1790, Phebe. [not sure if same John & Mary]
2 CONT
2 CONT Volume III [Westbury Meeting]: page 474 - Phebe Searing, d/o John & Mary of North Hempstead, m. Thomas Silas, s/o Fry & Anne Silas of Jericho.
2 CONT
2 CONT Volume III [Jericho Meeting]: page 508 - Thomas Willis, b. 11/20/1771 & d. 9/11/1864 age 92.10,0 years, s/o Fry & Anne [Seaman] Willis of Jericho, m. 1795 Phebe Searing b. 1/06/1773 d. 6/20/1804. d/o John & Mary.
2 CONT
2 CONT [S79] William Wade Hinshaw, Encyclopedia of American Quaker Genealogy, [FR:Oakwood Cemetery:FR].
2 CONT
2 CONT [S396] Death Record: record stated age 48 & about 5 months - probably should have read 78 - (transcribed by Larry & Kathy McCurdy).
