1 NOTE {geni:about_me} . Miriam4 Seaman (Samuel3, Nathaniel2, John1) was born December 25, 1751 (Source: Hinshaw, William Wade "Encyclopedia of American Quaker Genealogy"[Compiled by Thomas W. Marshall] [Genealogical Pub. Co., Baltimore,
2 CONC MD:1977] Vol. III p. 444 ), and died July 2, 1826 (Source: Hinshaw, William Wade "Encyclopedia of American Quaker Genealogy"[Compiled by Thomas W. Marshall] [Genealogical Pub. Co., Baltimore,MD:1977] Vol. III p. 498). She married 
2 CONC Stephen Robbins October 30, 1773 in St. George's [Episcopal] Church, Hempstead, Long Island, NY (Source: Haight, John Sylvanus "Adventures for God: a history of St. George's Episcopal Church, Hempstead, Long Island" [Vail-Ballou P
2 CONC ress, Binghamton, NY:1932]), son of Jeremiah Robbins and Hannah Carr. He was born June 26, 1750 (Source: Hinshaw, William Wade, Encyclopedia of American Quaker Genealogy, (Baltimore: Genealogical Publishing Co., 1991), 3:439.), an
2 CONC d died Unknown. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for Miriam Seaman:
2 CONT
2 CONT Miriam Seaman disowned by the Westbury Meeting of the Quakers on Aug. 25, 1773. 
2 CONT
2 CONT More About Miriam Seaman:
2 CONT
2 CONT Fact 4: February 16, 1780, mentioned in father's will, Samuel Seaman of Oyster Bay, Queens [now Nassau] Co. (Source: Heritage Books Inc., New York Abstracts of Wills, 1665-1801 (CD #9), (Bowie, MD: Heritage Books, 1997), "CD-ROM,"
2 CONC  10:100, "...my daughter Meriam Robens...")
2 CONT
2 CONT Fact 12: gravestone: ae 74y (Source: Hinshaw, William Wade "Encyclopedia of American Quaker Genealogy"[Compiled by Thomas W. Marshall] [Genealogical Pub. Co., Baltimore,MD:1977] Vol. III p. 498)
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage Notes for Miriam Seaman and Stephen Robbins:
2 CONT
2 CONT Church records at the time of the marriage list Miriam Seaman "of Oyster Bay" and that the couple were married in Hempstead. [Haight, John Sylvanus "Adventures for God: a history of St. George's Episcopal Church, Hempstead, Long I
2 CONC sland" [Vail-Ballou Press, Binghamton, NY:1932] 
2 CONT
2 CONT More About Stephen Robbins and Miriam Seaman:
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage: October 30, 1773, St. George's [Episcopal] Church, Hempstead, Long Island, NY (Source: Haight, John Sylvanus "Adventures for God: a history of St. George's Episcopal Church, Hempstead, Long Island" [Vail-Ballou Press, Bi
2 CONC nghamton, NY:1932])
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Miriam Seaman and Stephen Robbins are: 
2 CONT
2 CONT  	881	i.	 	Stephen5 Robbins, died Unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT  	882	ii.	 	Samuel Robbins, died Unknown.
