1 NAME Sarah /Ridgway/
2 GIVN Sarah
2 SURN Ridgway
2 _MARNM Carr
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 11 JUL 1727
2 PLAC Little Egg Harbor, Burlington, New Jersey, USA
2 ADDR
1 BURI
2 DATE AFT 16 APR 1762
2 PLAC Friends Burial Ground, Tuckerton, Ocean, NJ
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 16 APR 1762
2 PLAC Little Egg Harbor, Burlington, New Jersey, USA
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Birth: 	Jul. 11, 1727 Little Egg Harbor Ocean County New Jersey, USA Death: 	Apr. 16, 1762 Little Egg Harbor Ocean County New Jersey, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah married Caleb Carr, in October of 1746, in Little Egg Harbor, NJ. They had 7 children.
2 CONT
2 CONT -Mary Carr (1747-1831) -Job Carr (1750-1784) -Thomas Carr (1753-1753) -Samuel Carr (1754-1832) -Isaac Carr (1757-1814) -Hannah Carr (1759-1778) -Sarah Carr (1762-1824)
2 CONT
2 CONT According to "The Carr Book", pg. 50: Caleb and Sarah were both earnest Quakers and possessed of considerable ability and education.
2 CONT
2 CONT Caleb and Sarah are buried among many other Ridgeway family members in the Friends Burial Ground, including Sarah's parents, Thomas and Mary Ridgeway, according to "The History of Little Egg Harbor, NJ," by Leah Blackman, pg. 206.
2 CONC  Also nearby are many Willits, which was Caleb's mother's maiden name.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah likely died from complications from child birth, passing away two days after the birth of their youngest daughter Sarah. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Family links: 
2 CONT  Parents:
2 CONT   Thomas Ridgway (1701 - 1786)
2 CONT   Mary Ong Ridgway (1704 - ____)
2 CONT
2 CONT  Spouse:
2 CONT   Caleb Carr (1719 - 1783)*
2 CONT
2 CONT  Children:
2 CONT   Samuel Carr (1754 - 1832)*
2 CONT
2 CONT *Calculated relationship
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Friends Burial Ground  Tuckerton Ocean County New Jersey, USA
2 CONT
