1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Birth: 	Oct. 22, 1754 Little Egg Harbor Ocean County New Jersey, USA Death: 	Jun. 29, 1832 Mount Holly Burlington County New Jersey, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel married Ann French, 20 Dec 1781, in Evesham, NJ. They had 8 known children.
2 CONT
2 CONT -Hannah Carr (1782-1870) -Caleb Carr (1784-1842) -Jeremiah Carr (1786-1786) -Samuel Carr (1788-1873) -Mary F. Carr (1791-1839) -Isaac Carr (1793-1873) -Robert Carr (1795-1844) -Thomas Carr (1798-1798)
2 CONT
2 CONT Samuel and Ann were devout Quakers. A complete recitation of their wedding certificate can be found in the book "The Carr Family Records", pgs. 88-89.
2 CONT
2 CONT A complete version of his will is available as well, recorded in Book D of Wills page 395 in the Surrogates Office of the County of Burlington. 
2 CONT
