1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Effingham Lawrence, son of John, who was the son of Richard, who was the son of Joseph, who was the son of the first William, and Elizabeth Smith, afterwards Lady Carterett, before mentioned, was born June 6, 1760;
2 CONC  married Elizabeth, daughter of Thomas Watson. He was a gentleman of some wealth for the time in which he lived. His name is among those who formed an association in 1794, for the purpose of erecting the well-known building in the
2 CONC  city of New York, called the Tontine Coffee-house. The Lawrence Genealogy (1858)
