1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John Thorn was the son of Joseph Thorn and Charity Underhill. He married Hannah Hicks 24 Oct 1774. Children are Sarah, Jacob, Steven, Margaret, Joseph, William, Phebe, Mary, Elizabeth, Martha
2 CONT
2 CONT "John Thorn came from Dutchess Co in 1785 to the Albany Area of Saratoga, NY. He had been a soldier in the Revolutionary army. He settled on what is still (1885) Thorn place. His first house was on the site of the present one. He 
2 CONC had four sons and six daughters. Three of the latter are still living." (Schuylerville)
2 CONT
2 CONT Posted by the surrogate court in the Albany Evening Journal posted January 12 1841 "The people of the State of New York to William Thorn, Sarah Smith, Thomas N Dillingham and Margaret his wife, of the town of Saratoga, in the coun
2 CONC ty of Saratoga, Samuel Hewit and Betsey his wife, of Halfmoon, in said county; Jacob Thorn of Cohocton, Steuben County; Lewis Judson and Mary his wife, of Mobile, in the state of Alabama; William R Slocum and Phoebe, his wife, of 
2 CONC Greenwich, Washington county; Garret W Van Vegthen and Martha his wife, and Charles Nelson, of albany; Elias Hewit and Sally his wife of West Troy, Albany county; John Nelson, jun. and Hamilton Nelson, of Prairie, in the territory
2 CONC  of Wisconsin; William Nelson whose residence cannot be ascertained; and Thomas B Sherwood of Ballston Spa, special guardian to George Nelson, Eliphalet Nelson and Mary Nelson; minors, heirs and next of kin of John Thorn, late of 
2 CONC the town of Saratoga, in the county of Saratoga and state of New York, deceased, greetings..." 
