1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 722. John5 Jackson (John4, John3, Elizabeth2 Seaman, John1) was born 1733 (Source: (1) Bunker, Mary Powell, Long Island Genealogies, (Reprint. Originally published: Albany, NY: J. Munsell's Sons, 1895), 222., (2) S
2 CONC eaver, J. Montgomery, Jackson Family Records, (Philadelphia, PA: American Historical-Genealogical Society, 1929), 27.), and died January 1, 1821 (Source: Hinshaw, William Wade, Encyclopedia of American Quaker Genealogy, (Baltimore
2 CONC : Genealogical Publishing Co., 1991), vol. 3, p. 486.). He married (1) Charity Smith Treadwell February 13, 1756 in St. George's [Episcopal] Church, Hempstead, Long Island, NY (Source: (1) Haight, John Sylvanus, Adventures for God
2 CONC : a History of St. George's Episcopal Church, Hempstead, Long Island, (Binghamton, NY: Vail-Ballou Press, 1932)., (2) Bunker, Mary Powell, Long Island Genealogies, (Reprint. Originally published: Albany, NY: J. Munsell's Sons, 189
2 CONC 5), 222.). She died Unknown. He married (2) Margaret Wright Aft. 1763 (Source: Bunker, Mary Powell, Long Island Genealogies, (Reprint. Originally published: Albany, NY: J. Munsell's Sons, 1895), 222.). She died Unknown. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for John Jackson:
2 CONT
2 CONT Hinshaw's Quaker Records: John received by request 1-20-1791 [to Jericho, NY Meeting] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary, [his child], received by request 3-17-1791 
2 CONT
2 CONT More About John Jackson and Charity Treadwell:
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage: February 13, 1756, St. George's [Episcopal] Church, Hempstead, Long Island, NY (Source: (1) Haight, John Sylvanus, Adventures for God: a History of St. George's Episcopal Church, Hempstead, Long Island, (Binghamton, NY: 
2 CONC Vail-Ballou Press, 1932)., (2) Bunker, Mary Powell, Long Island Genealogies, (Reprint. Originally published: Albany, NY: J. Munsell's Sons, 1895), 222.)
2 CONT
2 CONT More About John Jackson and Margaret Wright:
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage: Aft. 1763 (Source: Bunker, Mary Powell, Long Island Genealogies, (Reprint. Originally published: Albany, NY: J. Munsell's Sons, 1895), 222.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of John Jackson and Charity Treadwell are: 
2 CONT
2 CONT  	1500	i.	 	Mary6 Jackson, died Unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT +	1501	ii.	 	Thomas Tredwell Jackson, died Unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT  	1502	iii.	 	John Jackson, died Unknown. He married Sarah Udal Treadwell (Source: Bunker, Mary Powell, Long Island Genealogies, (Reprint. Originally published: Albany, NY: J. Munsell's Sons, 1895), 222.); died Unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT  	More About John Jackson and Sarah Treadwell:
