1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Descendant of Mayflower passenger George Soule
2 CONT ----
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Soule-215
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography===
2 CONT
2 CONT Nathaniel Soule, son of Sylvanus and Sarah (Slade) Soule, was born about 1709, probably in Swansea, Massachusetts. [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Lydia Gifford on 15 March 1732/3 in Tiverton, Rhode Island.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Nathaniel was a blacksmith, and his father sold him 2.5 acres of land in Tiverton, 10 June 1734. Nathaniel and his wife Lydia sold the same land on 20 March 1746/7[1].
2 CONT
2 CONT Appointed hogviewer in Tiverton on 24 March 1745/6.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Nathaniel moved to Nine Partners, New York, where he was taxed as early as June 1747[1] and as late as 1775.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Children probably born in Tiverton.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Nathaniel b. ca. 1734; d. prob. after 1800 (census);[2]
2 CONT Ebenezer b. c. 1736 [1]
2 CONT Child?? Soule b. c 1738[1]
2 CONT Child?? Soule b. c 1740[1]
2 CONT Child?? Soule b. c. 1742[1]
2 CONT Daniel?? Soule b. c. 1744.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Nathaniel Soule (abt. 1709 - 1760)
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Nathaniel Soule===
2 CONT
2 CONT Born about 1709 in Swansea, Bristol, Massachusetts
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Sylvanus Soule and Sarah (Slade) Soule
2 CONT
2 CONT Brother of William Soule, Edward Soule, Jonathan Soule, Sarah (Soule) Davis and Sylvanus Soule Jr
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Lydia (Gifford) Soule — married 15 Mar 1733 in Tiverton, Newport, Rhode Island
2 CONT
2 CONT Father of Nathaniel Soule, Ebenezer Soule Sr., Unknown Soule and Daniel Soule
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 28 Mar 1760 at about age 51 in Nine Partners, Dutchess, New York [uncertain]
2 CONT
2 CONT Profile last modified 28 Feb 2023 | Created 27 Mar 2011
2 CONT
