2 CONT William Soule, son of Sylvanus Soule and Sarah Slade, was born in Swansea, Bristol, Massachusetts, around 1710[1] .
2 CONT
2 CONT William was a joiner. A joiner is a specialized carpenter, who cuts and then fits together the joints between two pieces of wood, without using nails, or screws etc[1].
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in Tiverton, Rhode Island between 1777, when he was on a military census and before 6 Sep 1778, the date his estate was inventoried[1].
2 CONT
2 CONT William married twice, first, 20 Sep 1733 in Swansea, "William Soul of Tivertown and Jemima Baker of Swanzey", daughter of Joseph and Martha Baker[2][1].
2 CONT
2 CONT William next married Keziah Gifford, daughter of Stephen and Mary Gifford[1]. We know this marriage was after 24 Oct 1735, when Jemima was involved with a sale of land and before 24 April 1747, when William's wife Caziah was invol
2 CONC ved with a sale of land[1], but this date is most likely earlier.
2 CONT
2 CONT There is some disagreement over which children belong to which wife.
2 CONT The Mayflower Society, in it's 2006 "Pink Book", lists Edward, Jemima, Joseph, Lillie?, and Silas as children of Jemima[1]. They do not seem to have taken into consideration the fact that only Edward and Jemima, appear to have por
2 CONC tions from their grandfather Baker's estate. They have also added some speculative daughter's to their list: Lillie, Mary, Hannah, Eleanor. Their names are followed by ??
2 CONT
2 CONT Children:[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward b. ca. 1734
2 CONT Jemima b. ca. 1736
2 CONT Joseph b. ca 1738
2 CONT Lillie/Lillis?? b. ca. 1740 (based on age at death). She has been listed as d/o Jonathan, but is more likely to be daughter of William
2 CONT Silas b. ca. 1742
2 CONT Jacob b. ca. 1745
2 CONT Mary/May ?? b. ca. 1747 She also has been listed as d/o Jonathan, but is more likely to be daughter of William
2 CONT Nathaniel b. ca. 1753, (based on age at death)
2 CONT Samuel b. May 1756 (based on pension record)
2 CONT Job b. 28 Aug 1757
2 CONT Hannah ?? b. ca. 1761 (evidence is circumstantial)
2 CONT Eleanor ?? b. ca. 1763 (evidence is circumstantial)
2 CONT Recompense b. ca. 1765 (from 1830 Census)
2 CONT William and Jemima (Baker) Soule married in 1733 and had the following (5) children:[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward Soule, born 1734
2 CONT Jemima Soule, born 1736
2 CONT Joseph Soule, born 1738
2 CONT Lille Soule, born 1740
2 CONT Silas Soule, born 1742
2 CONT William and Keziah (Gifford) Soule married in 1744 had the following (11) children:[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob Soule, born ca. 1745
2 CONT Mary Soule, born ca. 1747
2 CONT Unnamed Soule, born ca. 1749
