1 NAME Oliver /Booth/
2 GIVN Oliver
2 SURN Booth
2 _MARNM Booth
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1520
2 ADDR
3 STAE Derbyshire
3 CTRY England
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1586
2 ADDR
3 CITY Whitfield
3 STAE England
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Booth-516
2 CONT
2 CONT Oliver Booth was of Derbyshire and of the family from Barton Lancashire. He married Elizabeth Hatfeild of Whitfeild in Derbyshire [1] Note his father is not named.
2 CONT
2 CONT Booth of Handsworth Woodhouse Oliver Booth of Derby, son of John Booth and Ann Brereton of Tatton, Cheshire, was born about 1517, he married Elizabeth Hatfield from Whitfield, Derbyshire, about 1547.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Oliver and Elizabeth Booth:
2 CONT
2 CONT Nicholas
2 CONT Charles
2 CONT John (1553-1613)
2 CONT Thomas
2 CONT Oliver
2 CONT John Booth (1553-1613) was servant to Gilbert, Earl of Shrewsbury.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Booth was born at Ballifield, Handsworth. On 15th January, 1576 he married Ann Revel (buried 24/06/1597), daughter of Thomas Revel (b1529) and Ann West(Nee More) of Treeton.
2 CONT
2 CONT He had three daughters and co-heirs, who carried considerable property to their husbands and their descendants:
2 CONT
2 CONT Anne (b1579), the eldest married Thomas Stacye (1574-1632) of Ballifield on 18th May, 1597 at Handsworth. Thomas Stacye was the son of John Stacye (about 1539-1594) and Anne(about 1543-1609) nee Parker.
2 CONT Elizabeth (1582-1665) married 1. William Castleford of Worsborough and 2. Gervase Hanson, gentleman
2 CONT Catherine (b1583) married John Nodder (1580-1665) of Handsworth-Woodhouse.
2 CONT The will of John Booth, dated 1613, was proved at Laughton-en-le-Morthen.. He gives to the poor of Handsworth, Sheffield, Attercliffe, Darnall, Rotherham, Whiston, Treeton, Catcliffe and Orgreave. He leaves the Manor of Worsboroug
2 CONC h to his son-in-law William Castleford and after some family - remainders to Charles Cavendish, second son of Sir Charles Cavendish, knight.
2 CONT
2 CONT Attested copy will of John Bouthe of Handsworth Woodhouse (Y.), gent. 12 June 1613. To poor of Handsworth, 40s. To churchwardens there 'a33 6s. 8d. for good church books. To poor of Sheffeld, 20s., of Attercliff, 10s., of Darnell,
2 CONC  10s., of Rotherham, 20s., of Whiston, 10s., of Treeton, 10s., of Cattcliff, 10s., and of Orgrave, 6s. 8d. After death of wife Elizabeth, then to grandson John Nodder in house in Handsworth Woodhouse, glass, seeling, irons and iro
2 CONC n ranges, brewing lead, great board in kitchen, 2 great tables in hall and 1 in parlour with all their seats and forms, and all bedsteads, except 1 for wife absolutely. To Thos. Newbould of Mosburgh, Eckington (Db.), yeoman, copyh
2 CONC old Morehall Close there. To Thos. Hobson of Westwell, Eckington, all other copyhold there. To daughter Elizabeth Castleford, 1 messuage at Darley Cliff Edge in manor of Worsburghe Yorkshire. To grandson John Castleford 1 messuage
2 CONC  and premises in Worsburgh and Worsburgh Dale for rest of term. Testator being lord of Worsburgh, and brother-in-law Rob. Elmhirst holding 2 copyhold messuages called Houndhill and Elmehirst for 19s. 10d. p.a., now he quit of 17s.
2 CONC  10d. thereof, 2s. and other manorial incidents to remain. Manor of Worsburgh to son-in-law William Castleford and wife Elizabeth for lives, then to son John, with entail; in default to daughter Isabell; in default to Charles Cave
2 CONC ndish, esq., 2nd son of Sir Chas. Cavendish. To wife Elizabeth, 1 messuage called Netherhouse in Handsworth Woodhouse, close adjoining and 1a. meadow in Mylnefield, for rest of term from St. John's College, Cambridge, paying 20s. 
2 CONC p.a. to brother-in-law John Nodder, and son John; at her death premises to these. Wife executrix. Francis West of Rotherham and Rob. Elmehirst supervisors, having 20s. each. Parch..
2 CONT
2 CONT In the will of George, 6th Earl of Shrewsbury , he left his servant John Booth all lands in Wodhowse, Hansworth for life. There is a memorial stone to him in Handsworth Church: 'Here lyeth the body of John Booth late of Hansworth-
2 CONC Woodhouse gentleman; servant to the right honourable Gilbert Earl of Shrewsbury. He was ... in the profession of the gospel of Jesus Christ, and the same John died in the same Christian faith, the sixty first yere of age, the 16 d
2 CONC ay of June anno Domini 1613. And Ann his wife'
2 CONT
2 CONT Research Notes
2 CONT This person has been detached as son of John Booth (1527-bef.1564), due to his birth date being before his supposed father's birth. The Visitation source does not name his father. It states that he was of Derbyshire (presumably th
2 CONC e north of the county), not the borough of Derby.
2 CONT
2 CONT Suggested sources:
2 CONT
2 CONT England, Select Deaths and Burials, 1583-1991. Birth, Marriage & Death
2 CONT Derbyshire, England, Church of England Baptisms, Marriages and Burials, 1538-1812. Birth, Marriage & Death
2 CONT Yorkshire, England, Church of England Parish Records, 1538-1873. Birth Marriage & Death
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT ↑ Treswell R, Vincent A., Camden W.,ed Rylands ; Booth of Shifnall The Visitation of Shropshire, 1623 ,(London 1889)p 59 archive books
