1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Biography 
2 CONT
2 CONT “ Gathered Fragments of the Past and Present History of Woodhouse and Its ...” By William James Le Tall.  Page 7.  [https://books.google.com/books?id=TKg3gkzK6JUC&lpg=PA7&ots=xqeH0Lo100&dq=Catherine%20(Booth)%20Nodder&pg=PA7#v=one
2 CONC page&q=Catherine%20(Booth)%20Nodder&f=false GoogleBooks]
2 CONT
2 CONT John Booth, of Handsworth Woodhouse, was a man of large property: he was the son of Oliver Booth, of county of Derby. His will is dated 12th June, 1618. He left something to the poor of Handsworth, Attercliffe, Darnall, Rotherham,
2 CONC  Sheffield, Whiston, Treeton, Catcliffe and Orgreave, and left the manor of Worsborough to William Castleford, and after some family remainders, to Charles Cavendish, Esq., son of Sir Charles Cavendish, Knight. Sir Charles Cavendi
2 CONC sh's son William was born at ..Handsworth Hall, 16th of xii. mo., 1593. William was afterwards Earl, Marquis and Duke of Newcastle. John Booth, being servant of Gilbert Earl of Shrewsbury, may account for his leaving Charles, the 
2 CONC son of Sir Charles Cavendish some interest in his estate, for Charles was the Earl's nephew. 
2 CONT
2 CONT John Booth, of Handsworth Woodhouse, died in 1613, and left three daughters: 
2 CONT *Ann, the oldest, who married Thomas Stacye, of Ballifield ; 
2 CONT *Elizabeth, who married William Castleford, of Worsborough, to whom he left Worsborough Manor; 
2 CONT *and Catherine, who married John Nodder, of Handsworth Woodhouse. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===References
2 CONT *” The Publications of the Harleian Society, Volume 38”.  “Nodder.”  Page 689.  [https://books.google.com/books?id=EuEyWOCNEjYC&lpg=PA689&ots=5V1BOnOw2y&dq=Catherine%20(Booth)%20Nodder&pg=PA689#v=onepage&q=Catherine%20(Booth)%20No
2 CONC dder&f=false GoogleBooks]
