1 NOTE Name: Thomas LANGDON Given Name: Thomas Surname: Langdon Sex: M Birth: Abt 1673 in Hempstead, Nassau, Long Island, New York Death: Abt 1732 in Jerusalem, New York Event: Occupation  Father: Joseph LANGDON b: 23 Mar 1649 in New Hav
2 CONC en, New Haven, Connecticut  Mother: Mary OSBORNE b: Abt 1653  Marriage 1 Mary DUSENBORO b: Abt 1682 in Hempstead, Nassau, Long Island, New York
2 CONT Married: Abt 1698 in St. George's Episcopal Church, Hempstead, Long Island, New York
2 CONT Change Date: 15 Aug 2003
2 CONT Children
2 CONT Children of Mary DUSENBORO and Thomas LANGDON are:
2 CONT 	i.	Joseph LANGDON was born Abt 1700 in Hempstead, Nassau, Long Island, New York, and died Abt 1751 in Hempstead, Nassau, Long Island, New York. He married Keziah LANGDON1725 in St. George's Episcopal Church, Hempstead, Long Islan
2 CONC d, New York. She was born Abt 1702 in Hempstead, Nassau, Long Island, New York, and died Bef 16 Oct 1736 in Hempstead, Nassau, Long Island, New York. He married Abigail LEE  16 Oct 1736 in St. George's Episcopal Church, Hempstead,
2 CONC  Long Island, New York, daughter of Joseph LEE and Abigail PRICE. She was born Abt 1711 in Hempstead, Nassau, Long Island, New York, and died 1748 in Hempstead, Nassau, Long Island, New York.
2 CONT 	ii.	Elizabeth LANGDON < was born Abt 1702 in Hempstead, Nassau, Long Island, New York, and died Unknown. She married John BURWELL  Abt 1722, son of Benjamin BURWELL and Mercy FORMAN. He was born Abt 1696 in Hempstead, Nassau, Lon
2 CONC g Island, New York, and died 1764.
2 CONT 1.	iii.	Deborah LANGDON was born Abt 1704 in Hempstead, Nassau, Long Island, New York, and died Unknown. She married Cornelius LOSEY  Abt 1724. He was born Abt 1700 in Hempstead, Nassau, Long Island, New York, and died Unknown.
2 CONT 	iv.	Thomas LANGDON was born Abt 1710 in Hempstead, Nassau, Long Island, New York, and died Unknown in Dutchess, New York.
2 CONT 	v.	Jonathan LANGDONwas born Abt 1711 in Hempstead, Nassau, Long Island, New York, and died Unknown in Dutchess, New York.
