1 NOTE {geni:about_me}  439. Mary4 Seaman (Richard3, Richard2, John1) died Unknown. She married Richbell Mott April 1, 1736 (Source: Hinshaw, William Wade, Encyclopedia of American Quaker Genealogy, (Baltimore: Genealogical Publishing Co
2 CONC ., 1991), 3:444, 429.), son of Adam Mott and Elizabeth Mott. He was born Bet. 1717 - 1718 (Source: (1) Seaman, Mary Thomas, The Seaman Family in America..., (New York: TA Wright, 1928), 66., (2) Hinshaw, William Wade, Encyclopedia
2 CONC  of American Quaker Genealogy, (Baltimore: Genealogical Publishing Co., 1991), vol. 3, p. 429, b. abt. 1710.), and died Unknown. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for Mary Seaman:
2 CONT
2 CONT Hinshaw's Quaker Records: Mary acknowledged marrying outside the faith 6-8-1761 [vol. 3, p. 429] 
2 CONT
2 CONT More About Mary Seaman:
2 CONT
2 CONT Fact: May 15, 1751, mentioned in father's will, Richard Seaman of Herricks, Hempstead Twp., NY (Source: Heritage Books Inc., New York Abstracts of Wills, 1665-1801 (CD #9), (Bowie, MD: Heritage Books, 1997), "CD-ROM," 4:388.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes for Richbell Mott:
2 CONT
2 CONT Richbell Mott and his father Adam Mott, III removed from Long Island to Kent Co., Deleware. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary [Seaman, dau. of Richard Seaman] and her son Richard left Richbell and returned to Long Island. They left the other three children with their father (Sarah, Elizabeth, and Seaman Mott). It 
2 CONT
2 CONT must have been very messy for Mary's father to make such a stiipulation in his will. Elizabeth m. Solomon Seaman Jr. of Sassafras, Kent Co. MD. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Solomon was the brother of my ancestress Rebecca Seaman Clothier. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Richbell Mott was a member of St Peter's Anglican Church, Kent Co. DE. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [from Lee Guerra] 
2 CONT
2 CONT More About Richbell Mott:
2 CONT
2 CONT Will: in Deleware
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage Notes for Mary Seaman and Richbell Mott:
2 CONT
2 CONT Hinshaw's Quaker Records: married per bond dated 1 June 1736 [Vol. 3, p. 429] 
2 CONT
2 CONT More About Richbell Mott and Mary Seaman:
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage: April 1, 1736 (Source: Hinshaw, William Wade, Encyclopedia of American Quaker Genealogy, (Baltimore: Genealogical Publishing Co., 1991), 3:444, 429.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Mary Seaman and Richbell Mott are: 
2 CONT
2 CONT  	1028	i.	 	Elizabeth5 Mott (Source: Seaman, Mary Thomas, The Seaman Family in America..., (New York: TA Wright, 1928), 66, Mary Seaman, married April 1, 1736, son of Richbell Mott. (He was born 1717/18) They had one daughter: Eli
2 CONC zabeth Mott, married Solomon Seaman of Maryland.), died Unknown. She married Solomon Seaman (Source: Lee Guerra, Elizabeth m. Solomon Seaman Jr. of Sassafras, Kent Co. MD.); died Unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT  	Notes for Solomon Seaman:
2 CONT
2 CONT Solomon Seaman of Maryland... Mary Thomas Seaman, "The Seaman Family in America" p. 66 
2 CONT
2 CONT  	Marriage Notes for Elizabeth Mott and Solomon Seaman:
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Mott married Solomon Seaman of Maryland. 
2 CONT
2 CONT  	More About Solomon Seaman and Elizabeth Mott:
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage: (Source: Lee Guerra, Elizabeth m. Solomon Seaman Jr. of Sassafras, Kent Co. MD.)
2 CONT
2 CONT  	1029	ii.	 	Richbell Mott (Source: Harris, Edward Doubleday, The Descendants of Adam Mott of Hempstead, Long Island, NY, (Lancaster, PA: New Era Printing Co., 1906), 2, Richbell [4], who mar. 1736 Mary Seaman, dau. of Richard and
2 CONC  Sarah, and died before July 11, 1745, leaving a sone Richbell [5].), died Unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT  	Notes for Richbell Mott:
2 CONT
2 CONT Hinshaw's Quaker Records: minor 1777 [vol. 3, p. 429] 
2 CONT
2 CONT  	1030	iii.	 	Seaman Mott (Source: Lee Guerra.), died Unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT  	1031	iv.	 	Richard Mott, died Unknown.
