1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Adam and Anne Mott By Thomas Clapp Cornell
2 CONT
2 CONT SARAH PEARSALL, born 6th of Ilth mo., 1714, died at the house 
2 CONT
2 CONT of her son, John Alsop, in Hudson, N. Y., 9th, mo., 1800, daughter 
2 CONT
2 CONT of THOMAS and SARAH (UNDERHILL) PEARSALL of Hempstead. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The widow, SARAH (PEARSALL) MOTT, was a great-granddaughter 
2 CONT
2 CONT of Capt. JOHN UNDERBILL, her mother, SARAH (UNDER- 
2 CONT
2 CONT HILL) PEARSALL, being a daughter of Capt. JOHN'S son, JOHN UN- 
2 CONT
2 CONT DERHILL, Jr., and MARY, daughter of MATTHEW and MARY PRYOR. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Nearly four years after the death of her first husband, on the 3d of 
2 CONT
2 CONT 4th mo., 1747, according to the Westbury records, Richard Alsop, 
2 CONT
2 CONT Jr., of Newtown, Queens County, married SARAH MOTT, widow of 
2 CONT
2 CONT RICHARD MOTT, of Hempstead.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Richard Alsop of Oyster Bay and SARAH ALSOP, his wife : 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. Sarah, born 3d of 11th mo., 1747 ; married 7th of 5th mo., 1767, 
2 CONT
2 CONT William Loines, son of William and Ann Loines, of Hempstead. 
2 CONT
2 CONT JAMES MOTT, then himself married, was one of the many witnesses 
2 CONT
2 CONT to this marriage of his half-sister. РнЕИЕ DODGE another, &c., &c. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Phebe, born 2d of l0th mo., 1749. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. John, born 27th of 2d mo., 1753 ; married first, about 1780, Mary ' , 
2 CONT
2 CONT and had Robert, born 1783 ; Thomas Jenkins, born 1787 ; 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah, born 1792 ; Hannah, and Mary ; and married, second, Avis (
2 CONT
2 CONT Slocum-Folger) Barnard, born 1759, died 1819 ; daughter of John 
2 CONT
2 CONT and Martha Slocum, and widow, first of Sylvanus Folger, second of 
2 CONT
2 CONT Matthew Barnard. She brought with her her daughter, Martha Barnard, 
2 CONT
2 CONT born about 1790, died 1827, who became as an own daughter 
2 CONT
2 CONT to her stepfather, John Alsop. John Alsop went to Providence, R. I., and then, before 1777, to Mamaroneck, N. Y., whence, in 1783, he went to Hudson, N. Y., then just founded and he being one of the original proprietors ; and on t
2 CONC he incorporation of the city in 1785, he was made Chamberlain. He subsequently removed across the river to Athens, where he lived many years, and thence, in 1827, he removed to his son's house in Scipio, where he died some years l
2 CONC ater. 4. Hannah, born 7th of 2d mo., 1755 ; died l8th of gth mo., 1757. 5. Hannah, born I8th of I2th mo., 1757 ; married, first, Carpenter; married, second, I5th of 6th mo., 1785, Job Webb, son of John Webb, of Pennsylvania. 
2 CONT
2 CONT JAMES MOTT, born 8th of 8th mo., 1742 ; died, 7th of 5th mo., 1823 ; only son of RICHARD and SARAH (Pearsall) Mott ; married, 5th of 9th mo., 1765, MARY UNDERHILL, born 31st of 1st mo., 1745, died of , 1776, daughter of SAMUEL and
2 CONC  ANN (Carpenter) Underbill, "both of Oyster Bay," according to Westbury records.
