1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Adam and Anne Mott By Thomas Clapp Cornell
2 CONT
2 CONT JAMES MOTT, born 8th of 8th mo., 1742 ; died, 7th of 5th mo., 1823 ; only son of RICHARD and SARAH (Pearsall) Mott ; married, 5th of 9th mo., 1765, MARY UNDERHILL, born 31st of 1st mo., 1745, died of , 1776, daughter of SAMUEL and
2 CONC  ANN (Carpenter) Underbill, "both of Oyster Bay," according to Westbury records.
2 CONT
2 CONT JAMES MOTT found his wife in his second cousin, Mary Underhill, 
2 CONT
2 CONT daughter of SAMUEL and ANN (Carpenter) Underhill, and 
2 CONT
2 CONT they were married, as above stated, in 1765.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of James and Mary (Underhill) Mott ; 
2 CONT
2 CONT I. Richard Mott, born in New York 10th of 1st month, 1767, died at 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mamaroneck 29th of 7th month, 1856, in his 90th year, married 
2 CONT
2 CONT I7th of 1st month, 1787, Abigail Field, born 20th of l0th month, 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1766, died at Burlington, New Jersey, 8th of 8th month, 1851, daughter 
2 CONT
2 CONT of Uriah and Mary Field, of Purchase.
2 CONT
2 CONT II. ANNE MOTT, born in New York, 31st of 7th month, 1768, died of 
2 CONT
2 CONT Asiatic cholera, at the house of her son-in-law, Silas Cornell, at 
2 CONT
2 CONT Rochester, 5th of 8th month, 1852, in her 85th year, married at 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mamaroneck 19th of 5th month, 1785, in her I7th year, Adam Mott, 
2 CONT
2 CONT of Cowneck, born in " the old place," nth of l0th month, 1762, died 
2 CONT
2 CONT at Rochester in the house of his son-in-law, Lindley M. Moore, l0th 
2 CONT
2 CONT of 1st month, 1839, in his 77th year, son of Adam and Sarah (Willis) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mott, and grandson of the " younger son Adam." 
2 CONT
2 CONT The children of Adam and Anne Mott will be given in the account 
2 CONT
2 CONT of Adam Mott, the husband. 
2 CONT
2 CONT III. Robert Mott, born in New York, 1771, died 21st of 3d month, 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1805, of consumption, married July, 1795, Lydia Philadelphia Stans- 
2 CONT
2 CONT bury, born in Philadelphia 23d February, 1775, died , 1862, 
2 CONT
2 CONT youngest daughter of Joseph and Sarah Stansbury. He was a paymaster 
2 CONT
2 CONT in the British Army in Philadelphia, during the American 
2 CONT
2 CONT Revolutionary War. 
2 CONT
2 CONT IV. Samuel Mott, born in New York, 2oth of 9th month, 1773, died 
2 CONT
2 CONT 8th of 10th month, 1843, married at Newport, Rhode Island, 31st of 
2 CONT
2 CONT 7th month, 1794, Elizabeth Barnard, born about 1775, died , 
2 CONT
2 CONT daughter of Matthew Barnard, who after her mother's death married 
2 CONT
2 CONT about 1783, Avis Slocum, daughter of John and Martha Slocum, 
2 CONT
2 CONT and widow of Sylvanus Folger, and after Matthew Barnard's death, 
2 CONT
2 CONT Avis Slocum married third time, John Alsop, half-brother of James 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mott, bringing her daughter, Martha Barnard, who became like an 
2 CONT
2 CONT own daughter to her step-father. Samuel and Elizabeth (Barnard) 
