1 OCCU Cordwainer
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Note about wives and marriage dates===
2 CONT
2 CONT For Stephen, we have the Dutch Reformed Church records on Staten Island we can refer to (available online [https://archive.org/details/recordsofdutchre00wrig/page/n3/mode/2up here]).  These describe some of the children of Stephen
2 CONC , and the names of their mothers.  Stephen's early children from Jannetje (1725) through Stephen and Obadiah (twins) (1727) are the children of Geertje Winter, who was Stephen's first wife.  A son Richard was born in 1731 to Steph
2 CONC en and Jemima Mott.  This sets the rough date of when Stephen's first wife died and when Stephen remarried.
2 CONT
2 CONT The third wife comes from Stephen's will, described below.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Will===
2 CONT
2 CONT From "Abstracts of Wills Vol VI 1760-1766," New York Genealogical and Biographical Society Record
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Page 323.--In the name of God, Amen, May 10, 1763. I, STEPHEN WOOD, SR., of Staten Island, cordwainer, being in good health. I leave to my wife Sarah £60 and my best bed and furniture and a cow. I leave to my son Stephen 25 acre
2 CONC s of the land I bought of John Van Tell, from the road in front upward, except the highways, and a road to and from the woodland for my sons. I leave to my sons, Joseph and John, the remainder of the said tract, and they are to pa
2 CONC y to my grandson, Stephen Wood, son of my daughter, Mary Wood, each £20 when he is of age. I leave to my son Timothy 10 shillings. To my daughter Phebe £10. To my daughter Elizabeth £50. To my daughter Sarah £50. I leave to my two
2 CONC  sons, Joseph and John, 15 acres of wood land which I bought of the executors of my son James, lying in the Manor of Castleton, bounding upon Richard Cannon and Lawrence Hillyard, to the clear land, "and in a square." Also a road 
2 CONC to and from it. And my son Joseph is to pay to my grandson, James Wood, £60, and John is to pay to my grandson, Abraham Wood, £60, when they are of age. The remainder of the tract and 20 acres of fresh meadow adjoining are to be s
2 CONC old, and after paying debts, I leave the surplus to my son Richard. I make John Morgan, Henry La Tour and my son Joseph, executors.
2 CONT
2 CONT Witnesses, Stephen Mesereau, Abraham Yates, Mathias Sweene. Proved, February 4, 1764.
2 CONT
2 CONT
