1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=34507260&ref=wvr
2 CONT
2 CONT Cornelius Van Wyck was a surveyor and in 1735 built a house with three rooms on 959 acres he had acquired from Catheryna Rombout Brett, daughter of Francis Rombout, who with Stephanus Van Cortlandt and Jacobus Kip, received a land
2 CONC  grant from King James II, the Rombout Patent, consisting of 85,000 acres. Rombout was the 12th mayor of New York City. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The house Cornelius Van Wyck built in 1735 was extended some time before 1757 and stands today, known as the Van Wyck Homestead Museum. 
