2 CONT
2 CONT Virtual Lecture: Cornelius Van Wyck House Preservation Project
2 CONT
2 CONT On Wednesday September 24th at 11:00am EST, Zaskorski & Associates Architects will present a Zoom lecture about the restoration of the historic Cornelius Van Wyck House, located in Douglaston Manor, Queens.  Overlooking Little Nec
2 CONC k Bay, it was designated as a landmark by the NYC Landmarks Preservation Commission in 1966 and added to the National Register of Historic Places in 1983.
2 CONT
2 CONT Built in the early 18th century, the Cornelius Van Wyck House is one of the few remaining examples of Dutch colonial-era architecture in Queens. Its significance lies both in its architectural design and its connection to the earl
2 CONC y history of New York City. The Van Wyck family, prominent in the area’s development, originally constructed the house as a rural estate fronting Little Neck Bay, where trade with native peoples took place.
