1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Birth: 	1728 Elizabeth Union County New Jersey, USA Death: 	Jun. 10, 1794 Elizabeth Union County New Jersey, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Their days are number'd, and their spirits fled Their gone, the husband and the wife are dead Nor weeping friends nor healing art could save Their bodys from the cold and silent grave.
2 CONT
2 CONT Will made June 21, 1794. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sons Abner and William received: 
2 CONT
2 CONT All my house and lands where I now live with all improvements and appurtenances thereunto and all my personal estate of every nature and kind so ever to be divided between them, share and share alike.
2 CONT
2 CONT He ordered them to pay his other sons, Edward, Matthias, Andrew, James, Jacob and Isaac, the sum of ten shillings for their legacy. 
2 CONT
2 CONT His daughters, Margery, Mary, Rachel, Sarah and Jane were to be paid forty shillings each. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Note the date of the will is AFTER the date shown as his death on his tombstone. 
2 CONT
2 CONT BADGLEY HISTORY from Newark, New Jersey Evening News  July 23 to Nov 11, 1906 by Wheeler Thurston 
2 CONT
2 CONT "Cornelius Badgley son of George and Mary Hatfield Badgley was born at Elizabethtown NJ about 1728. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married to Elsey, daughter of James and Mary (Garthwait) Townsley who was born at Elizabethtown between 1728-1733. They lived at Elizabethtown and were members of St. John's Episcopal Church although both Mr. and Mrs. Badgl
2 CONC ey are buried in the Presbyterian Cemetery. Mrs. Badgley died of a fright on July 21, 1809 when she was informed of the suicide of her son the day before. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The children of Cornelius and Elsey (Townsley) Badgley: 1. Margery, baptized September 16, 1753 married Abner Price in 1784 and died before 1808; 2. William baptized August 10, 1755, died in infancy; 3. Mary baptized May 8, 1757; 
2 CONC 4. Abner baptized October 15, 1758 married Sarah <nowiki>----</nowiki> and died May 2, 1797; 5. Rachel born June 28, 1760 married Thomas Price in 1778 and died January 17 1839; 6. Sarah baptized April 15, 1762 married Joseph Mann 
2 CONC of Elizabethtown; 7. Jane baptized August 5, 1764; 8. Edward baptized August 31, 1766, died July 20 1809; 9. William born October 13, 1767, married Rebecca Abbott and died November 11, 1825; 10. Matthias baptized September 11, 177
2 CONC 1 married <nowiki>-----</nowiki> Abbott and moved to Canada; 11. Andrew baptized December 1, 1771; 12. James baptized July 10, 1773."  Note his two youngest sons, Jacob and Isaac are not mentioned in the above article but are list
2 CONC ed in his Will
2 CONT
