2 CONT ==Last Will & Testement==
2 CONT Wife, Elizabeth, remainder of movable estate, during her lif e. Aft er her decease it is to be divided between my daughters, Latitia Redden, Sarah French and Rachel Willcocks and my grandaughters, Mary Vrelandt and Rhoda Lacy; the
2 CONC  daughters, one share each and grandaughters, each 1/2 share. Whereas I have already given my sons, Levi and Benjamin, de eds for la nd of some considerable value; they are to pay my grandaughter, Mary Willcocks (daughter of my so
2 CONC n Cornelius, dec'd) L12.10, when she is 18. Son, William, 5 shillings. Daughter, Elizabeth Hasel, 5 shilligs. Daughter, Latetia Redden, use of house she lives in with 1 3/4 acr es of land, during her life; after her decease the sa
2 CONC me to my grandson, William Redden. Sons, Levi and Benjamin, all my right and title to out lands, to be divided between them; Also each L12. Executors --- sons, Levi and Benjamin. Witnesses -- William Stewart, Henry Jennings, Willi
2 CONC am Coles. Proved Nov.11, 1800
2 CONT
