1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Inscription on Original Stone:
2 CONT In Memory Of M.
2 CONT John Willcocks
2 CONT He Deceas'd November
2 CONT The 22nd 1776
2 CONT Aged 49 Years
2 CONT
2 CONT Inscription On Later Marker:
2 CONT JOHN WILLCOCKS Sr
2 CONT LT HORSE CO
2 CONT NJ MILITIA
2 CONT REV WAR
2 CONT November 22 1776
2 CONT
2 CONT Revolutionary War - Jersey Troops at Fort George, Colonel Wind's First Regiment, [https://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A216525 DAR Ancestor A216525]
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT On November 22, 1776, patriot John Willcocks, a member of “Captain Marsh’s Light Horse Troop” died at age 49. He was shot and wounded in General Washington’s army on November 10. He died twelve days later at home in what is now th
2 CONC e Watchung Reservation. He is buried in the Willcocks and Badgley family cemetery at the Deserted Village of Feltville in Berkeley Heights
2 CONT
2 CONT * https://www.familysearch.org/tree/person/details/LVGN-66X
2 CONT
