1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A Patriot of the American Revolution for NEW JERSEY (Teamster).  [http://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A004490  DAR Ancestor # A004490]
2 CONT
2 CONT buried in First Pres. Cem., Westfield, NJ grave #258
2 CONT
2 CONT * son of Hannah Kelsey and James Badgley
2 CONT
2 CONT * CNW II p 214
2 CONT
2 CONT * Magie Family History p 7, 18, 19
2 CONT
2 CONT * Family Records or genealogies of the first settlers of Passaic 
2 CONT
2 CONT Valley and Vicinity above Chatham, with their ancestors and 
2 CONT
2 CONT descendants, as far as could be ascertained in 1851. By John Littell, 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1851.
2 CONT
2 CONT ANTHONY BADGLEY, (3rd child of James Badgley,) [possibly d. June 30, 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1803 age 40 Presbyterian Church in Westfield NJ] and Anna Woodruff
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Served in the Revolutionary War as a Lieut. 1st Reg., Essex Co. Militia. Husband of Anna Badgley. Inscription: "The months of affliction are over. The days & the nights of distress. We see him in anguish no more. He's gained his h
2 CONC appy release."
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: Lt. 1st Reg. Essex Co. Militia Rev War 70y
