1 NAME James John /Shreve/
2 GIVN James John
2 SURN Shreve
2 _MARNM Shreve
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC Shreve Family Cemetery
2 ADDR
3 CITY Rehoboth
3 STAE Ohio
3 CTRY United States
1 BIRT
2 DATE 13 OCT 1754
2 PLAC Springfield Township, Burlington County, New Jersey, USA
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 18 APR 1839
2 PLAC Rehobeth, Perry, Ohio, United States
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} James son of Caleb and Hannah Thorn Shreve was their seventh child and third son.James married Mary Williams in Virginia, the children born around Loundon County. The family came to the Rehoboth Hills around 1809.
2 CONT
2 CONT The 1983 stone reading: died April 18, 1839 aged 81y6m5d done by C. Guy and Beth Summanen is in agreement with L. P. Allen's History of the Shreve family, the source of all three stones. 
2 CONT
2 CONT CEMETERY NOTES:This place could use some maintenance. It looks as if the plot has slid towards the very close by drainage ditch for Essex Lake. It looks big enough for 4 stones, but only 3 are visible. The stones surrounding the c
2 CONC emetery have square cut holes where the gate posts used to be. (Written by Mary Ireton) 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT JAMES SHREVE, the seventh child and third son of Caleb Shreve and Hannah Thorn, was b. Oct. 13th, 1754, in Springfield, Burlington Co., N. J. ; m. Mary Williams, of Va. He died in Perry Co., O., aged nearly one hundred years. Jame
2 CONC s Shreve moved from Loudon Co., Va., in 1792 to Bedford Co., Pa.; thence in 1809 to Perry Co., O., where the fam- ily settled in the Rehoboth Hills near Rehoboth. All his family excepting his son John left Pennsylvania at the time
2 CONC . J. M. Doty writes : 'T was informed by my mother that her grand- father, James Shreve, served in the American Army in the Revo- lutionary War ; he came out all right, and refused to accept a pension, saying that the Government n
2 CONC eeded it at that time worse than he did. He crossed the Delaware with Washington, and was in the battles of Trenton and Princeton."
2 CONT
2 CONT https://dn790004.ca.archive.org/0/items/genealogyhistory00alle/genealogyhistory00alle.pdf
