1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ''[http://www.geni.com/people/Andy-McMahan/6000000000036146003 Andy McMahan] writes:''
2 CONT
2 CONT Most family trees in the "genealogy world" agree that John is the son of Henry; however, there seems to be no consensus on who might have been his mother.
2 CONT
2 CONT My general feeling is that, although Rebecca could have technically borne a child at 42, chances are that John was a bastard child of Henry or could have possibly been adopted (from either inside or outside the family.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Of course, there are some folks that list John's birth date as c. 1745.   If this were to be closer to the truth, then there would be a greater possibility that he was a natural born son of Henry and Rebecca.
1 FAMC @F6000000008441562919@
1 RFN geni:6000000013709075363
1 SUBM @S285894111400006134@
