2 CONT Liber 31, folio 219 3 May 1758 BLACKISTON, BENJAMIN, Kent Co.     To my wife, Sarah Blackiston, for life, Reserve, the plntn. I live on & a brown horse Nobb.     To my son John Blackiston, Illises Industry, which he lives on.     
2 CONC To my son Wm. Blackiston, my part of Benjaman Park, in Queen Anns Co., on the d. of my wife, Reserve, & 170a of Deer Park, on the main rd. to Duck Crk     To my dau. Sarah Comegys, 300a on the W line of Deer Park, where John Beck 
2 CONC lived.     To my dau. Ann Spearman, 300a of Deer Park, on the S side the land where John Layton lives.     To my dau. Priscillah Blackiston, 300a on the E line of Deer Park, where William Heath lives.     To my son George Blackist
2 CONC on, 400a of Deer Park near the rd. to Duck Crk. at a place called My New Design, my part of Williams Virtue, & the lands I lately took up.     To my grdson Benjn. Blackiston, s. o. John Blackiston, 200a of Deer Park.     To my 2 g
2 CONC rdsons, Richard & Ebenezer Blackiston, s. o. John Blackiston, the rest of Deer Park.     If John Beck or Jean, his wife, d. & the survivor mar., it will be at the discretion of my heir or extrs. whether to turn he or she from thei
2 CONC r place.     Upper Landing, in Queen Anns Co., is to be sold & the money equ. div. betw. my 2 sons, William & George, George to have his share at age 18.     If the money for the 200a of Deer Park I have sold to Jacob & Isaac Hurl
2 CONC ik is pd. after my d., it is to be equ. div. among my 3 sons John, William, & George.     To my son William, a bed, & he is to be grdn. to my son George till he is 18     To my dau. Priscillah Blackiston, a bed, L 5, a cow & calf,
2 CONC  & a roan mare called hers.     To my son George, 3 negroes - a boy Jem & 2 girls, Rachell & Cate - a horse worth L 10, a bed, a cow & calf, & L 5.     Extrs: my sd. wife & my son William Blackiston.     Witn: Jeremiah Semans, Dan
2 CONC iel Semans, Samuell Davis.     23 Dec. 1760, sworn to by all 3 witn.
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Liber 31, folio 219 3 May 1758 BLACKISTON, BENJAMIN, Kent Co.     To my wife, Sarah Blackiston, for life, Reserve, the plntn. I live on & a brown horse Nobb.     To my son John Blackiston, Illises Industry, which he lives on.     
2 CONC To my son Wm. Blackiston, my part of Benjaman Park, in Queen Anns Co., on the d. of my wife, Reserve, & 170a of Deer Park, on the main rd. to Duck Crk     To my dau. Sarah Comegys, 300a on the W line of Deer Park, where John Beck 
2 CONC lived.     To my dau. Ann Spearman, 300a of Deer Park, on the S side the land where John Layton lives.     To my dau. Priscillah Blackiston, 300a on the E line of Deer Park, where William Heath lives.     To my son George Blackist
2 CONC on, 400a of Deer Park near the rd. to Duck Crk. at a place called My New Design, my part of Williams Virtue, & the lands I lately took up.     To my grdson Benjn. Blackiston, s. o. John Blackiston, 200a of Deer Park.     To my 2 g
2 CONC rdsons, Richard & Ebenezer Blackiston, s. o. John Blackiston, the rest of Deer Park.     If John Beck or Jean, his wife, d. & the survivor mar., it will be at the discretion of my heir or extrs. whether to turn he or she from thei
2 CONC r place.     Upper Landing, in Queen Anns Co., is to be sold & the money equ. div. betw. my 2 sons, William & George, George to have his share at age 18.     If the money for the 200a of Deer Park I have sold to Jacob & Isaac Hurl
2 CONC ik is pd. after my d., it is to be equ. div. among my 3 sons John, William, & George.     To my son William, a bed, & he is to be grdn. to my son George till he is 18     To my dau. Priscillah Blackiston, a bed, L 5, a cow & calf,
2 CONC  & a roan mare called hers.     To my son George, 3 negroes - a boy Jem & 2 girls, Rachell & Cate - a horse worth L 10, a bed, a cow & calf, & L 5.     Extrs: my sd. wife & my son William Blackiston.     Witn: Jeremiah Semans, Dan
2 CONC iel Semans, Samuell Davis.     23 Dec. 1760, sworn to by all 3 witn.
