1 NAME Josiah /Quimby/
2 GIVN Josiah
2 SURN Quimby
2 _MARNM Quimby
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 31 MAR 1692
2 ADDR
3 CITY Northcastle
3 STAE Province of New York
1 DEAT
2 DATE 15 MAR 1735
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Genealogical History of the Quinby (Quimby) Family in England and America By Henry Cole Quinby
2 CONT
2 CONT Josiah 4 (Josiah*, John*, William1) born 31 May ("31, 3 mo.") 1692. The Friends' Meeting in Westchester granted him a "certificate of clear," or permission to remove, 3 mo. 23, 1728, from Westchester. The records do not state his 
2 CONC proposed new destination.
2 CONT
2 CONT Josiah4 married Hannah6 Cornell (Richard4, John3, Thomas1, Richard1), of Scarsdale, Westchester county, N. Y. She was born 1711, say the records; it is therefore likely tht she was a second wife. The only recorded child is by wife
2 CONC  Hannah:
2 CONT
2 CONT II. Mary' Quinby, born 5 May, 1730, says John Cox, Jr., custodian of Friends' records; married 15 July, 1748, at Mamaroneck, Westchester county, N. Y., William, son of Joshua and Charity Cornell of Greenwich, Conn. ("Rev. Joseph H
2 CONC ull," etc. p. 46).
2 CONT
2 CONT Hannah Cornell's sister Eliza, married Aaron4 Quinby, brother of Josiah4. Hannah (Cornell) Quinby's will, proved 7 Jan. 1765, is on record at New York city, N. Y. (lib. 26 p. 39). She is described as of New Rochelle, Westchester c
2 CONC ounty; left a brother John Cornell; a daughter, Mary Cornell; and seven Cornell grandsons, the eldest being Quinby Cornell.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT === Life Sketch ===
2 CONT from:
2 CONT https://archive.org/details/cu31924085658379/page/n143/mode/1up?view=theater
2 CONT
2 CONT Josiah* married Hannah* Cornell (^Richard*, John^, Thomas^, Richard^), of Scarsdale, Westchester county, N. Y. She was born 1711, say the records; it is therefore likely tht she was a second wife. The only recorded child is by wif
2 CONC e Hannah:
2 CONT
2 CONT II. Mary' Quinby, born 5 May, 1730, says John Cox, Jr., custodian of Friends' records; married 15 July, 1748, at Mamaroneck, Westchester county, N. Y., William, son of Joshua and Charity Cornell of Greenwich, Conn. ("Rev. Joseph H
2 CONC ull," etc. p. 46).
2 CONT
