0 @N6000000002248181109@ NOTE Noted by Philip V. Thorne, as ref'd. by website of jdmount@cox.net (http://members.cox.net/mountgen/baldwin.html): 
1 CONT Susannah Booth Thorne's exact parentage is unknown. There was an Ensign John Booth who came with Reverend John Youngs to New Southold on Long Island. He resided on Shelter Island. Youngs was a militant puritan with strong anti Qua
1 CONC ker feelings. In more than one instance Booth sided with the quakers against Youngs. Given this bent towards religious tolerance and given the fact the Reverend Youngs group was from Southold in Suffolk County, England (next to Li
1 CONC ncolnshire) we have some circumstantial evidence tying the Booths and Thornes to the same general area. There was a very large and very ancient Booth family in Great Grimsby an old seaport and military site at the mouth of the riv
1 CONC er Humber, Lincolnshire. Travelling inland from Grimsby, not far from the Humber River lies the City of THORNE. Thorne is located in South Yorkshire and is less than 35 miles from Grimsby and is less than 60 miles from where Gunby
1 CONC  was formerly situated. Further it's only about 80 miles south towards London to Southold (John Youngs and John Booth).
