1 CONT Is listed as having been born in Bucks Co, PA, but her parents were married in England only 6 years previously.
1 CONT
1 CONT This marriage may have some genealogical problems.  It is agreed that John Scarborough and Mary Pierson married in 1689 in Bucks County, PA.  However, it is unclear if Mary was the daughter of Edward Pierson b. 1651, or his sister
1 CONC .  At present, I have her as getting married at 13, which is a little young.
1 CONT
1 CONT I've read some criticism of the thought that John Scarbough's wife could have been Mary Pierson -- but in that reading, Mary was 10 or so years older than John, and John's last child was born when Mary was 53.  In addition, they h
1 CONC ad the rumor that John Scarborough married an Indian woman.
1 CONT
1 CONT However, John and Mary Scarborough's daughter Sarah first married a Matthew Hall, and their daughter Sarah Hall married a grandson of Edward Pierson.
