1 CONT
1 CONT According to Mary Powell Bunker, in LI Genealogies, James was also a Goldsmith of London. As per her notes: Lieutenant Robert Feke, of Watertown, New England, and William Palmer of Yarmouth, and Judith his wife, son and daughter o
1 CONC f James Feke, late of London, Goldsmith, deceased, and Tobias Feke, aged 17, make Tobias Dixon, of London, their attorney in the settlement of the estate of James, 1638 to 41.
1 CONT Frank Edgar Weeks states in Genealogy of the Weeks Family......that Bunker also gives "Tobias Feke, son of Robert, born at Watertown, came to Long Island 1650, died 1668." He believes this is an error, as Tobias was possibly a nep
1 CONC hew, not a son of Lieutenant Robert.
1 CONT Two other notes from Bunker are puzzling:
1 CONT 1669. Robert Feaks d. wife named Sarah.
1 CONT 1670. James Feke gave release to Mary, widow of Tobias Feke, she having paid him all his claims the estate of Tobias, deceased.
