1 CONT 4. ROBERT3 FEAKE was born in Killingworth, Long Islansd 22 Jun2 1683, and died in Locust Valley Long Island April 1773. He married about 1704 the widow CLEMENCE LUDLAM. He was a farmer, blacksmith, mill owner and specially was pas
1 CONC tor of the Baptist Church at Oyster Bay, having been converted to that faith by a traveling minister. "According to tradition John Feake came to the water's edge and protested against Robert's baptism while the ceremony was being 
1 CONC performed. (LIF)." This Robert was also the father of another Robert Feake a celebrated portrait painter.
