0 @N6000000001034247767@ NOTE QUAKER-ROOTS-L Archives
1 CONT
1 CONT From: "DeMarco" <demarco@ix.netcom.com>
1 CONT Subject: Re: BAKER and HORNOR families
1 CONT http://archiver.rootsweb.com/th/read/QUAKER-ROOTS/1998-07/0901855555
1 CONT
1 CONT I would suggest for your HORNOR side that you look into New Jersey
1 CONT HORNOR/HORNER families who were Quakers and some of these families
1 CONT moved to Canada because they were Loyalists.
1 CONT
1 CONT In particular, look into the following family:
1 CONT
1 CONT Isaac HORNER was born April 1, 1732, the son of Isaac HORNER and
1 CONT Eleanor BOWNE. At various times Isaac lived in Kingwood, Hunterdon
1 CONT County, NJ, Mansfield, Burlington County, NJ, and Trenton, Mercer
1 CONT County, NJ. He married Mary POTTS, daughter of Thomas POTTS of
1 CONT Trenton, NJ. Isaac HORNER was a Loyalist and moved to Canada. He died
1 CONT February 7, 1822. Isaac and Mary HORNER had a large family. Their
1 CONT children were: Samuel (1758-1778), Elizabeth (1760-1765), Sarah
1 CONT (1763-1765), Isaac (1765-1849), Thomas (1767-?), Stacy (1769-?), and
1 CONT Mary (1771-1776).
1 CONT
1 CONT Margaret
1 CONT
1 CONT http://www.magma.ca/~ekipp/thornor.htm
1 CONT Col. Thomas Hornor
1 CONT Accomplishments and events in the life of
1 CONT the first white settler of
1 CONT Blenheim Twp., Oxford Co., Ontario Canada
1 CONT
1 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1 CONT April 17, 1678 - His grandfather Isaac Hornor Sr. was born in Tadcaster, England.
1 CONT February 6, 1732 - His father Isaac Hornor Jr. was born near Princeton, New Jersey.
1 CONT
1 CONT March 17, 1767 - Col. Thomas Hornor was born at Mansfield, near Bordentown, south of Princeton, New Jersey U.S.A.
1 CONT
1 CONT 1773 - The Hornor?s were a Quaker family and Thomas attended with his parents the new Quaker Meeting House near Bordentown.
1 CONT
1 CONT 1783 - His father Isaac decided to give up his job working for a local newspaper, moved to New York City, and with his partner commenced publishing his own paper ?The New York Morning Post.?
1 CONT
1 CONT 1785 - Thomas Hornor now 18 years of age, was allowed by his reluctant Quaker parents to attend a military college to further his education.
1 CONT
1 CONT 1793 - At the invitation of John Graves Simcoe, the Governor of Upper Canada, Thomas Watson Jr. of the State of New Jersey, arrives in Blenheim Twp., accompanied by his first cousin Thomas Hornor. (Watson?s mother was Elizabeth Ho
1 CONC rnor, a sister of Isaac Hornor the father of Thomas Hornor.)
1 CONT
1 CONT May 22, 1794 - The two cousins return to New Jersey where Watson plans to remain. Thomas Hornor encouraged at the prospect of soon owning Blenheim Twp., as promised by John Simcoe if a saw and griss mill were built, purchased equi
1 CONC pment at Albany, N.Y., hired millwrights and mostly by water traveled back to what is now Princeton, Ontario. Here they built their first saw mill on the main stream of the creek which now bears his name.
1 CONT
1 CONT http://search.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/sse.dll?db=njwills&gsfn=isaac&gsln=hornor&gspl=33%2cNew+Jersey&prox=1&ti=0&gss=angs&sx=&submit.x=45&submit.y=6&ct=27104
1 CONT Calendar of New Jersey Wills, Vol. III 1751-1760
1 CONT
1 CONT Name: Isaac Hornor
1 CONT Date: 21 Sep 1759
1 CONT Location: Mansfield Township, Burlington Co.
1 CONT yeoman; will of. Son, Samuel, has had his share. Son, Joseph to have my plantation, he paying my son, Benjamin, £50, and my daughter, Amy, £50. Daughter, Rachel Taylor, to have use of a room while widow. Son, Isaac, had his share.
1 CONC  Son, Benjamin, to have my house and lot in Bordentown. Daughter, Elizabeth Watson, £10, which her husband stands charged with in my book. Daughter, Amy Horner, to have my negro, Fanny. Sons Joseph and Benjamin to have my meadow l
1 CONC and in Nottingham Township. Rest of personal estate given to four daughters, Rachel Taylor, Mary Field, Elizabeth Watson and Amy Hornor. Executors--sons Samuel and Joseph Hornor. Witnesses--Richard Potts, Samuel Field, John Bliss.
1 CONC  Proved Dec. 5, 1760.
1 CONT Lib. 10, p. 558.
1 CONT 1760, Dec. 5. Inventory, £210.11.6, by Aaron Watson and Richard Potts.
1 CONT
1 CONT http://search.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/sse.dll?db=jersey%2c&gsfn=isaac&gsln=horner&sx=&year=&yearend=&gskw=&gsco=1&gspl=1%2c+&prox=0&rank=0&ti=0&ti.si=0&gss=angs&submit.x=38&submit.y=11&ct=27283
1 CONT New Jersey Marriages, Colonial Era, 1665-1800
1 CONT HORNER, Isaac, of Mansfield Township, and Elizabeth Sykes, of Chesterfield, at Chesterfield.
1 CONT 19th 3d mo. 1709
1 CONT Witnesses?John and Frances Horner, John, Joanna Sykes, Thomas Folkes, Peter Fretwell, John Bunting, Daniel Farnsworth, Joseph Reckless, John Warren, Daniel Smith and others.
1 CONT
1 CONT http://awt.ancestry.com/cgi-bin/igm.cgi?op=GET&db=teincnj&id=I054258
1 CONT Families of Burlington Co., NJ
1 CONT Entries: 122463    Updated: 2005-02-17 14:49:42 UTC (Thu)    Contact: Bill Abrams     Home Page: Abrams Family of Burlington Co., NJ
1 CONT
1 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1 CONT
1 CONT Index | Descendancy | Register | Pedigree | Ahnentafel | Add Post-em
1 CONT
1 CONT --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1 CONT
1 CONT ID: I054258
1 CONT Name: Isaac Horner
1 CONT Sex: M
1 CONT Birth: 17 APR 1678 in Tadcaster, York, England
1 CONT Death: 24 NOV 1760 in White-Hill, Bordentown, Burlington Co., NJ
1 CONT Burial: 24 NOV 1760 Bordentown, Burlington Co., NJ
1 CONT
1 CONT Father: John Horner b: ABT. 1635 in Tadcaster, Yorkshire, England
1 CONT Mother: Mary Pearson b: ABT. 1655 in Tiffenthwaite, Cumberland, England
1 CONT
1 CONT Marriage 1 Agnes Sesan
1 CONT
1 CONT Marriage 2 Elizabeth Sykes b: ABT. 1688
1 CONT Married: 19 MAR 1708/09 in Chesterfield Mm, Burlington Co., NJ
1 CONT Children
1 CONT Isaac Horner b: 1 APR 1732 in New Hanover, Burlington Co., NJ
1 CONT
1 CONT Marriage 3 Eleanor Esther Bowne b: 20 FEB 1694/95 in Flushing, NY
1 CONT Married: 4 SEP 1718
1 CONT Children
1 CONT Elizabeth Horner b: 18 MAR 1728/29
1 CONT
1 CONT http://archiver.rootsweb.com/th/read/NJBURLIN/2000-10/0970442338
1 CONT From: Lemuel Allison <lemmela@home.com>
1 CONT Subject: [NJBurlin] Abstract of Isaac Horner's Will 1763
1 CONT Date: Sun, 01 Oct 2000 19:18:58 -0400
1 CONT
1 CONT This is an Abstract of Isaac Horner's will of 1763 that some of you
1 CONT might have an interest in.
1 CONT
1 CONT 28 July 1763, Isaac Hornor, of New Hanover Twp, Burlington Co.; Wife,
1 CONT house where I live and 5 acres of plow land, and 2 acres of meadow. Son,
1 CONT William, house at Crosswicks Creek, he paying the legatees hereafter
1 CONT mentioned; otherwise the legatees, Isaac Horner and Content, (alias
1 CONT John) Horner, to enter the plantation if he refuse to do so. Daughter,
1 CONT Mary, wife of John Clevenger, 10 pounds. Sons, William and Joshua, 20
1 CONT pounds each more than the rest. Residue to my children, William Horner,
1 CONT Joshua Horner, Hannah (wife of James Garwood), Isaac Horner and Content
1 CONT (alias John) Horner; but as Hannah, wife of James Garwood, is dead, her
1 CONT share shall go to her children when 21. Executors - William Horner,
1 CONT Isaac Horner and Content (Alias John) Horner. Witness - James London,
1 CONT John Emley, William Potter. Will proved 27 August 1763.
1 CONT
1 CONT Cheers,
1 CONT Barbara
