1 CONT by Elizabeth Quinby and witnessed by James Quinby, Anna Quinby, and Josiah 
1 CONT Quinby. [Note: originally assigned D-0361-039 by Julia Clark.]
0 @N6000000002315676518@ NOTE Enlisted re-Enlisted as volunteer? At time of death apparently res  Locke twp?, Cayuga (co?), NY. Samuel JOHNSON served 13 months as a Gunner & 11 months as a Bombardier during Revolutionary War in Company commanded by Capt (? LOC
1 CONC KWOOD) of NY Artillery Regiment commanded by Col. (?LAMB) 
1 CONT
1 CONT Acted as Captain and Commander of a Whale Boat in Long Island Sound...Captain Samuel JOHNSON captured a British Gunboat and brought it into Long Island Sound....Aug or Sep 1781. 
1 CONT
1 CONT was at Battle of Ticonderoga. Marched through state of New York. served also under Col ? Jabez FITCH 
1 CONT
1 CONT Was in Battle at Troys Pointe on American Roll.
1 CONT
1 CONT Enlisted circa 1st Sep 1775 (Roll of New York, Albany)...served through the war. 
1 CONT
1 CONT Pension #W16619
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT ----------------------- There was a Rev. Samuel FIELD (nobody knows if is this person or a relative or who ???) who organized a church at Batavia, NY circa 1817. ---------------------------------------------------------- (book at 
1 CONC Tucson LDS:  974.721 H29L) Long Island Source Records P377: Federal Census, 1800 Queens co, Long Island, New York, Town of Oyster Bay: Inglehart HUSTED P347: 1800 Census, Queens co, Long Island, Town of Hempstead: Samuel JOHNSON p
1 CONC 25: 13 Aug 1819 Samuel JOHNSON, Juner (sic) to Martha BEDELL, both of Hemp., Section J 1817-1819 Marriages performed by Justice William MOTT, of town of Hempstead, Long Island NY 1793-1827 -------------------------------- (book at
1 CONC  Tucson LDS: 973.M28g v.2) Genealogical Abstracts of Revolutionary War Pension Files vol II F-M abstracted by Virgil D. White p1856: JOHNSON, Samuel, Elizabeth, W16619, Cont & NY Line wid appl 17 Jul 1837 Cayuga Co NY aged 85 sol 
1 CONC & wid had m 03 Sept 1768. sol d 10 June 1821 wid d 05 Dec 1837 Elsie HUSTED one of surviving children ...rec'd final payment on 19 June 1839. 
1 CONT
1 CONT ------------------------------------------------- Vic told me he saw in IGI that Samuel JOHNSON m Elizabeth FIELD --------------------------------------------------- 
1 CONT
1 CONT I am sorry to admit but the following notes are ones I summarized from microfilm...think it was ... LDS reel #0971428: 
1 CONT
1 CONT #W16619 JOHNSON, Samuel  (Elizabeth) service: Continental-New York Samuel JOHNSON, of Cayuga co, New York,  died 16 June 1821 Bombadier 13 months Gunner 11 months Bombardier in Company commanded by Capt (??might be LOCKWOOD???...h
1 CONC ard for me to make out) of Regt commanded by Col. (LAMB ?)  NY, New York Inscribed in the Roll of New York (Alby) at rate of 106 dollars 25 Cents per annum to commence on 4th Day of March 1831. Certificate of Pension issued 19th d
1 CONC ay of July 1838 and sent to S(M/U?) CROFT, Esqr, Locke, Cayuga co, NY Arrears to the 4th of March 1838 $743.75 Semi-an allowance ending 4 Sept 1838  $53.12 rec'd by G (?F) RHODES, Clerk  $796.87 Book A, Vol 2, p111. 
1 CONT
1 CONT Treasury Dept Second Comptroller's Office July 19th, 1839 Sir, Under the act of the 6th of April 1838 entitled "An ...."   Elsie HUSTED one of the children of Elizabeth JOHNSON a Pensioner on the Roll of the Albany, NY Agency at t
1 CONC he rate of one hundred & six Dollar and twentyfive Cents per annum, under the law of 4th July 1836, has been paid 1/2 of her pension at this Department, from 4th of March 1831, to the 5th December, 1837, the day of her death. 
1 CONT
1 CONT V2388 Elizabeth JOHNSON, widow of Samuel  N York married in '68. Capt LOCKWOOD LAMB- enlisted gunner 1 Apl 77- Bombardier 1 May 78 on roll of June 79 ------------------------------------ 
1 CONT
1 CONT have 6 zeroxes of pages on microfilm above notes were gleaned from... -------------------------------- 
1 CONT
1 CONT following is what is on 2 zeroxed sheets of Vic's notes:
1 CONT
1 CONT Certificate of pension sent 19 July 1838, sent to Samuel CROFT, Locke, Cayuga 
1 CONT
1 CONT 79618 arrears Paid to Elsie HUSTED one of the children  1/2 of the pension of Elizabeth JOHNSON  from 4 March 1831 to 5 Dec 1837 
1 CONT
1 CONT married Elizabeth FIELD Sept 3, 1768 by John GOLDSMITH, pastor Presby Church Newton Long Island 
1 CONT
1 CONT Samuel JOHNSON of Genoa, Cayuga co. July 17, 1837 said he knew Elizabeth JOHNSON, the widow of Samuel JOHNSON who died 16 day June 1821 in Cayuga Co. Samuel JOHNSON (above) and Ebenezer HOW of Genoa knew Samuel JOHNSON from 1805 u
1 CONC ntil his death. 
1 CONT
1 CONT July 19, 1839-- In 1800 - a Samuel JOHNSON in Greene Co in 1830 a Samuel JOHNSON at Elba in 1840- Samuel JOHNSON     at Cayuga Co at Jenoa 
1 CONT
1 CONT 1850 Seth at Mentz, Cayuga
1 CONT
1 CONT Seth HIGLEY-father-in-law to Peter HUSTED ( a son of David (LT of Lee, Oneida Co, NY) HUSTED Higley (mentioned in French's 1860 Gazeteer) page 203 Comfort, Tyler - one earliest settlers Montezuma., Cayuga. 
1 CONT
1 CONT Samuel JOHNSON 971,428 1790 Samuel JOHNSONs p60 Columbia Co, Canaan Town p90 Dutchess at Poughkeepsie 133 New York City and County, West Ward 156 Queens, South Hempstead town 182 Ulster co, Newburgh. 
1 CONT
1 CONT -----------------
1 CONT
1 CONT this is all I have aside from what's in Vic's manuscript, if anything. 
