0 @N6000000000491150619@ NOTE [Himes.Core.FTW]
1 CONT
1 CONT [143983.GED]
1 CONT
1 CONT Occupation:  Blacksmith
1 CONT Baptized 24 Feb 1639
1 CONT Buried: Burnhill, Chequer Alley, London
1 CONT
1 CONT Came to America in 1682 with son John.  Returned to England in 1784 to get his wife, but she was not Quaker and would not leave England.  John bought 250 acres of land from William Penn.  This land located in Langhorne, Bucks Co.,
1 CONC  Pa.  John did not return to America either after he left in 1684.  William Penn witnessed his will.  He gave son John power of attorney.  He was a Blacksmith, Whitesmith and Coachmaker.  He came over on the ship WELCOME, the 19th
1 CONC  to reach the shore of the Americas.
1 CONT Narrative from Mark Law  at   mark.law@umich.edu
1 CONT found at: http:..www-personal.umich.edu/~mlaw
1 CONT
1 CONT He followed the same trade as his father, William Scarborough, and lived i the same Parish of St. Sepulchr and belonged to the same Peel's Monthly Meeting of Friends, where as early as 1677 he is referred to as a Member.
0 @N6000000003077169968@ NOTE In 1684 he returned to England, leaving his young son in care of friends, intending to bring back his wife to America.  When he arrived in London, he found that the "persecution of Friends or Quakers" had somewhat relaxed and his 
1 CONC wife refused to leave her home and friends for a life in the new world.  John remained and never saw his son again
