0 @N6000000004558286759@ NOTE Records for Joseph Cantrell are from the Holy Trinity (Old Swedes) Church Registry, Wilmington, Delaware. Joseph was living 1738 in Orange Co, VA., died abt. 1753 in Orange (now Rockingham) Co, N Carolina. He is possibly buried in
1 CONC  Orange Co., N. C. Primary sources are from contributors to the Cantrell Cousins Project.......
1 CONT
1 CONT More info. from the Cantrell Cousins Project, Descendants of William Cantrell..........
1 CONT
1 CONT Joseph Cantrell was born abt. 1695 in Phil., PA., and spent his early boyhood in that city. He married Catharina ............... They were living in New Castle Co, PA., on or near the site of the present city of Wilmington, Delawa
1 CONC re, and were attendants at Holy Trinity (Old Swedes) Church before 1720. It is probable that Catharina was a daughter of one of the Old Swedes, first settlers of this section but we could not verify this. Their first three childre
1 CONC n were baptized at the old historic church still used and known as Old Swedes, which is one of the oldest and quaintest churches in this country.
1 CONT Christina parish was mostly situated on both sides of Christina creek, partly on both sides of Brandywine creek in New Castle Co, and in the Hundreds of New Castle, Christina and Brand-wine. It stretched two Swedish miles in lengt
1 CONC h and one in breadth. The most remote families of the parish were not more than six and a half English miles distant from the church. The city of Wilmington is built on the Swedish "church land" and the charter for the town was gr
1 CONC anted in 1735. At the time Joseph Cantrill went there it was known as Christina.
1 CONT Many of the earliest records of this locality have been lost, or destroyed, and at best are very incomplete. There is evidence, however, from scattered records in New Castle Co today, that descendants of Richard Cantrill lived the
1 CONC re from before 1720 until 1797, though the majority moved south during this period.
1 CONT
1 CONT From Carol Cantrell ...... "Acquired records: Holy Trinity (Old Swedes) Church. Wilmington, Del., from 1697-1773. There are three references there for Joseph Cantrell :
1 CONT 1. Joseph Cantrel & wife Catharina's child Hanna, b. March 20, baptized April 15, 1720.
1 CONT 2. Joseph Cantrill & wife Catharina's child John, one & one-half year old, bap. March 25th, 1726.
1 CONT 3. Jospeh Cantrill & wife Catharina's child Joseph, a half yr. old, baptized Dec. 10, 1726.
1 CONT From this we do know that Joseph married Catharina and we know birthdate for three of the children,
