1 CONT
1 CONT Horace Bonney died during a flu epidemic in 1918, leaving his wife with three young daughters.  His father, Fred Bonney, obtained power of attorney to take custody of them.  His wife wasn't eager to take on three more children and
1 CONC  kept them separated through most of their childhood. The youngest daughter, Grace Bonney,  was adopted by her father's sister, Lila Bonney Pierce, became known as "Lila Grace Bonney Pierce" and was raised as an only child.  Horac
1 CONC e's wife, Lola, after giving away her three little daughters, went on to remarry, adopt more children, gave them away, had her own son - who died, and reportedly allowed her own daughter, Rosa, to be mistreated by one of her "husb
1 CONC ands".
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT Information downloaded from Don Dickenson's GedCom version 1/1/2003.
