1 CONT Buried in Berlin cemetary - section 14 lot 1 along with Jessue Watson, age 17, d. 12/22/1882 and Howard C. Watson, Age 1, d. 04/22/1885 (w18)
1 CONT
1 CONT 1905 census for West Berlin,waterford twp shows Harry R. Watson... both parents are shown as being born in NJ. (W20)
1 CONT
1 CONT 1850 census, Camden County, NJ, Gloucester Township, (page 262).  Mark (age 9) is living with his parents and Hannah Ann (age 17), George (age 15), Peter R. (age 13), Chirstopher (age 11), James ? (age7) and Richard (age 5) and Ph
1 CONC ilip ? (age 3).  Mark is shown as having attened school in the last year.
1 CONT
1 CONT 1860 census, Camed County, NJ, Waterford Township, (page 184).  Mark (age 20) and his brother Richard (age 14) are living with another family, Samuel and Sarah Potel ?.  Mark's occupation is listed as "boxmaker".
1 CONT
1 CONT 1870 census Mark is in Gloucester Township, Camden County, NJ (page 57).  Many of the Watson's are living around him; Aaron (age 68), Peter D. (age 44), Peter S. (age 22), Aaron C. (age 35), Frederick (age 66), Joseph (age 48), Wi
1 CONC lliam (age 46 )and Josiah (age 33).  This is more than likely the Watson framlands in Watsontown, NJ (Clementon).  Mark's occupation is listed as "Candle and Box Manufacture".   Other than William (Farmer) and Josiah (Lawyer) all 
1 CONC the Watson men have the same occupation.  Almost every other family listed on the four pages on the census are "farmers".   Mark is living with his wife Mary (age 25) and children Thomas (age 8), Sarah (age 6), Mary (age 4), Anna 
1 CONC (age 3) and Mark (age 1).  Value of his personal estate is $150.00.  (W35 to Ws38)
1 CONT
