0 @N6000000004548156515@ NOTE Source: Public Library Peru, Clinton County, New York. A  Collection of Articles on Local History of Peru, New York - Volume II  (Page 91)
1 CONT Samuel Keese, married the granddaughter of Benjamin Franklin.  This Keese family settled in Clinton County, NY and many are buried in the Quaker Cemetery near Keese's Corners, outside of Keeseville, NY.  The Keese homestead was an
1 CONC  Underground Railroad stop on the way north to Canada.  This was in the same time period that "Abolitionist" John Brown was establishing Timbuctoo in Lake Placid, New York.
1 CONT
1 CONT From Jean Thwait of Flower Memorial Library, Watertown, NY, 10/27/2003:
1 CONT I do know that Benjamin Franklin was introduced to my Eells ancestors, per Eells Family History. Seems Benjamin Franklin was a surveyor for mail delivery, and would go out and measure the distances mail had to travel so they would
1 CONC  know how much to charge for mailing. He bought a horse, and as he was passing through the area from whence the horse had been purchased, the horse realized where he was and took Benjamin Franklin to the door of the Eells househol
1 CONC d, his former home. Eells Family History says the joke was always that this was the only time they had been introduced to new people by a horse.
