1 CONT  The information below was extracted from microfilms of the records of the Probate Court of Dutchess County, New York. The records are arranged alphabetically by surname. My apologies for any transcription errors -- the handwritin
1 CONC g is often difficult to read.
1 CONT
1 CONT The volume and page number is listed in the last column; the films are available through the Family History Centers of the Church of Latterday Saints. Vols AA-A (1751-1796) are on film #913659, Vol. B (1796-1806) Film #913660, Vol
1 CONC . C-D (1806-1815) Film #913661, Vol. E-F (1814-1824) Film #913662, Vol. G-H (1824-1832) Film #913663. Further films go to 1905. See Library catalogue on www.familysearch.org.
1 CONT
1 CONT Surname: Badgley
1 CONT Given: Anthony
1 CONT Name(s)
1 CONT Date of will: Apr. 20, 1809
1 CONT Probate Granted: Nov. 24, 1810
1 CONT Location in Dutchess: Clinton
1 CONT Spouse: Elizabeth wife of Thomas Barker, George, Stephen
1 CONT Children: Granchildren: Sarah wife of Jacob Freligh, Dorothy Boid, Phebe Peters, Elizabeth wife of Peter Welling, Ann Wicks, Joshua Badgley, 6 sons of George are John, Anthony, Jonathon, Stephen, George, Elisha
1 CONT Other beneficiaries: Grandson Jonathon and friends Cort Dubois & Isaac Albertson
1 CONT Executors	Witnesses: William Lawrence, Zaccheus Marshal, M??? Albertson
1 CONT Vol (page): C (517)
1 CONT
1 CONT
1 CONT     Dutchess Co. tax lists show Anthony, George and Stephen Bad gley in the Town of Clinton, prob. dated 1787; and in Nin e Partners/Crum Elbow, Anthony Beb 1756-1778, Anthony Jr. 1 773-79, George Feb 1753-1779, and Samuel Jun 175
1 CONC 8-1779.
1 CONT
1 CONT     Anthony died age 89y, 3m, 10?d. Anthony's will was dated 2 0 Apr 1809 - Anthony Badgley of Clinton. He made bequests to his dau., Elizabeth, wife of Tho. Barker; son George ; son Stephen; gr. dau. Sarah, wife of Jacob Freligh;
1 CONC  gr. dau. Dorty Bois; Gr. dau. Phebe Peters; gr. dau. Elizabeth Welling, wife of Peter; gr. dau. Ann Wickes; gr. son Joshua , and George's six sons, John, Anthony, Jonathan (named as executor), Stephen, George, and Elisha. The wil
1 CONC l was proved 24 Nov 1810.
1 CONT
1 CONT     References: Cheska Wheatley; Old Gravestones of Dutchess Co ., pp. 207-208; Ulster Co. Probate Records, Anjou - Bk C, p . 517; Dutchess Co., NY Tax Lists - Buck, pp. 66, 131.
1 CONT
1 CONT     Was a Captain with the Dutchess County Militia, Fourth Regiment.
1 CONT     Revolutionary War Veteran
1 CONT
1 CONT     In 1790 he owned one slave.
1 CONT
1 CONT     He became an orphan at the age of nine. He lived with his cousin Hannah Haight and her husband Isaac Thorn. Sometime in the 1740's Isaac and Hannah Thorn left Long Island and moved to what is now Dutchess County, New York. By 
1 CONC 1769 he is found in Clinton Township, Dutchess County, New York. He owned a considerable amount of land in Clinton and set aside 1/4 of an acre to be used as a cemetery where he, his wife and many descendants are buried.
